July 11, 2023
MINUTES
WINNETKA VILLAGE COUNCIL
STUDY SESSION
(Approved: August 15, 2023)
 
A record of a legally convened meeting of the Council of the Village of
Winnetka, which was held at Council Chambers on Tuesday, July 11, 2023, at 7:
00 PM.
1)   Call to Order.
President Chris Rintz called the meeting to order at 7:00 PM. Manager Bahan
called the roll of the Village Council. Present: Trustees Rob Apatoff, Tina
Dalman, Bob Dearborn, Kim Handler, and Bridget Orsic. Absent: Kirk Albinson.
Also present: Village Manager Robert Bahan, Assistant Village Manager Kristin
Kazenas, Deputy Village Clerk Berina Gradjan, Village Attorney Courtney
Willits, Water & Electric Director Brian Keys, Finance Director Tim Sloth, and
4 persons in the audience.
 
2)   Public Comment.
a)   Ted Wynnychenko addresses Council regarding the Bertling-Hill-Woodland
Pathway Vacation.
b)   Tom Brown expresses concerns regarding the Hubbard Woods Train Station
patch work. Village Manager Rob Bahan confirms that the Village has been
working with representatives from Metra regarding the construction and
addresses conflict due to Union Pacific obtaining permits.
c)   Patrick Hanley extends the Environmental and Forestry Commission’s support
regarding the Electric System & Power Plant discussion.
3)   Winnetka Electric System & Power Plant Overview.
Water and Electric Director Brian Keys provides an overview of the Village’s
wholesale power supply contract with IMEA through September 20, 2035 noting
various terms and conditions. Brian Keys provides an additional detail
regarding the power supply encompassing Northfield Substation, the Electric
Generating Plant and ComEd tie lines. He explains the distribution system,
including how power gets distributed through the Village and the peak system
electrical demand.
 
Brian Keys provides the Council with an overview of the Electric Generating
Plant. His remarks include an explanation of steam generation, a review of
historical plant capacity additions, and a summary of the existing generation
assets and their respective installation dates.
 
Brian Keys provides information on IMEA Generation Contract. In addition,
Council is informed of various expenses such as fuel costs, reimbursements,
IMEA related costs, and costs associated with maintenance, repair, and labor.
Brian Keys provides an overview the capacity credit payments, annual operating
hours, and testing requirements.
 
Council discusses matters related to operating hours, market conditions, IMEA
benefits, electric and power plant operations, conditions, and emergency action
plans. Furthermore, Council discusses various financial components related to
cost projections, staffing, and maintenance, and speculation of long-term
operations.
 
While no policy direction is requested from Council, Brian Keys advises that at
a future meeting, staff will provide additional details on generating
components, capital investment, and financial considerations related to
maintaining current generating capacity through the existing IMEA contract
period.
 
Public Comment.
Marcus Wedner addresses Council on public education regarding emissions.
Tom Brown addresses Council regarding the remaining life of generators.
Ted Wynnychenko addresses Council regarding efficiency of diesel generators and
storage capacity.
4)   Closed Session
for the Purpose of Discussing pending litigation pursuant to Section 2(c)(11)
of the Open Meetings Act and discussion of minutes of closed session meetings
Pursuant to Section 2(c)(21) of the Open Meetings Act.
Trustee Handler, seconded by Trustee Dalman, moved to adjourn to Closed Session
for the Purpose of Discussing pending litigation pursuant to Section 2(c)(11)
of the Open Meetings Act and discussion of minutes of closed session meetings
Pursuant to Section 2(c)(21) of the Open Meetings Act and to adjourn the Open
Meeting automatically and immediately upon the conclusion of the Closed Session
without the conduct of any further business or comments. By roll call vote, the
motion carried. Ayes: Trustees Apatoff, Dalman, Dearborn, Handler, and Orsic.
Nays: None. Absent: Trustee Albinson.
The Council adjourned into Closed Session at 8:45 p.m.
5)   Adjournment.
The Closed Session meeting ended at 9:27 p.m.
 
/s/ Berina Gradjan, Deputy Village Clerk 
Recording Secretary
