Realty - 564 Lincoln Avenue (Introduction)
Community Development Director David Schoon addresses Council regarding an
application for a special use permit submitted by Compass Realty for 564
Lincoln Avenue. The subject property is approximately 4,500 square feet, with
1,500 square feet in the commercial overlay district. The Plan Commission
recommended approval of the request by a vote of 4-2.
The applicant’s attorney Cal Bernstein addresses Council regarding the feedback
received from the Plan Commission, and introduces Jen Epstein, Hoffman
Commercial Real Estate Property Manager for 564 Lincoln who provided a summary
of the efforts to lease the space, noting various homeowner association
restrictions. Johnny Satts, Compass Director of Corporate Real Estate addresses
Council affirming that the Applicant has provided updated information regarding
the proposed use of the retail area, focusing on a long-term art gallery tenant
rather than a pop-up approach.
Terry Dason, Executive Director of the Winnetka Northfield Glencoe Chamber of
Commerce expresses support for the special use application.
Council discusses various aspects of the application including signage,
accessibility of the space, continuity of the overlay district, pop up versus a
long-term tenant in the retail space, vibrancy of the retail space, and
creation of foot traffic in the district.
Trustee Dearborn notes that the Ordinance refers to a pop-up retail use and
should be updated before adoption if a long-term tenant is secured.
Trustee Dearborn, seconded by Trustee Apatoff, moved to introduce Ordinance No.
M- 13- 2023 with the modifications noted above. By roll call vote, the motion
carried. Ayes: Trustees Albinson, Apatoff, Dalman, Dearborn, and Handler. Nays:
None. Absent: Trustee Orsic.
6)   Old Business. None.
