February 13, 2024
MINUTES
WINNETKA VILLAGE COUNCIL
STUDY SESSION
(Approved: March 21, 2024)
 
A record of a legally convened meeting of the Council of the Village of
Winnetka, which was held at the Council Chambers on Tuesday, February 13, 2024
at 7:00 PM.
1)   Call to Order.
President Rintz called the meeting to order at 7:01 PM. Village Manager Bahan
called the roll of the Village Council. Present: Trustees Kirk Albinson, Rob
Apatoff, Tina Dalman, Bob Dearborn, Kim Handler and Bridget Orsic. Absent:
None. Also present: Village Manager Robert Bahan, Assistant Village Manager
Kristin Kazenas, Village Attorney Peter Friedman, Deputy Village Clerk Berina
Gradjan, and approximately 3 persons in the audience.
2)   Public Comment.
i)    Ted Wynnychenko addresses Council on matters related to steep slope, the
Bertling-Hill-Woodland pathway vacation, and closed session meeting minutes.
Trustee Albinson enters 7:03 pm.
3)   Turbine and Steam Generation.
Water & Electric Director Brian Keys briefs Council on the overview of steam
generation, specifically regarding turbine #4 and boiler #4. With turbine #4
currently out of service and in need of a repair plan, previous inspections
have led staff to identify the root cause of the damage. Mr. Keys provides
information related to the turbine and boiler history, functions, required
repairs and reassembling, and estimated repair costs.
Additionally, Mr. Keys provides an overview of boiler #4 history regarding
manufacturing, primary functions, repair needs, and estimated repair costs and
duration of repairs.
Council is provided a summary of repair costs for turbine #4 and boiler #4,
cost escalations, budgeting, funding, and CIP, capacity credits from the
Illinois Municipal Electric Agency, and historical expenses.
Village staff indicated financial projections based on presented planned, and
unplanned repairs, the operation of steam generation facilities, and short term
and long term outcomes of turbine #4 and boiler #4.
Council discusses various matters related to the future of the electric
distribution system, repairs such as compensation regarding the Northfield
transformer, contract extensions, IMEA credits, concerns regarding the future
of turbine operations and functions, and replacement of the turbine and diesel.
Furthermore, Council discusses placement of the generators, Winnetka’s power
use generated by the plant, condition of electric distribution system, impacts
on resident utility bills, prioritization of other Water & Electric projects,
and matters related to dual fuel usage.
Staff is provided Council consensus to retire turbine #4 in 2024, not retubing
boiler #4 in 2025 and retiring the remaining steam generation facilities on
December 31, 2026.
4)   Closed Session
for the Purpose of Discussing Probable or Imminent Litigation pursuant to
Section 2(c)(11) of the Open Meetings Act.
Trustee Handler, seconded by Trustee Apatoff, moved to adjourn to Closed
Session for the purpose of discussing probable or imminent litigation pursuant
to Section 2(c)(11) of the Open Meetings Act and to adjourn the Open Meeting
automatically and immediately upon the conclusion of the Closed Session without
the conduct of any further business or comments. By roll call vote, the motion
carried. Ayes: Trustees Albinson, Apatoff, Dalman, Handler, and Orsic. Nays:
 None. Absent: None.
The Council adjourned into Closed Session at 8:22 p.m.
5)   Adjournment.
The Closed Session meeting ended at 9:27 pm.
 
 
/s/ Berina Gradjan, Deputy Village Clerk 
Recording Secretary
