A record of a legally convened regular meeting of the Council of the Village of Winnetka, which
was held at the Council Chambers on Tuesday, March 5, 2024, at 7:00 PM.
1)   Call to Order. 
President Rintz called the meeting to order at 7:01 PM. Village Manager Rob
Bahan called the roll. Present: Trustees Kirk Albinson, Rob Apatoff, Tina
Dalman, Robert Dearborn, Kim Handler, and Bridget Orsic. Absent:
None. Also present: Assistant Village Manager Kristin Kazenas, Deputy Village
Clerk Berina Gradjan, Village Attorney Peter Freidman, Community Development
Director David Schoon, and approximately 19 persons in the audience.
2)   Pledge of Allegiance. President Rintz led the group in the Pledge of
Allegiance.
3)   Quorum.
a)   March 12, 2024 Study Session
All of the Council members present said they expect to attend.
b)   Thursday, March 21, 2024 Regular Meeting
All of the Council members present said they expect to attend with the
exception of Trustee Dalman.
4)   Public Comment.
i.   Ted Wynnychenko addresses Council regarding the Bertling-Hill-Woodland
pathway vacation and lakefront access.
ii.   Rocky Flinterman and Terry Dason provide information regarding the 2024
Winnetka Farmer’s Market including specification and vendors.
5)   Reports.
a)   Landmark Preservation Awards Presentation .
Each Spring, the Landmark Preservation Commission accepts nominations for the
annual preservation award program, honoring construction projects preserving
the history and charming characteristics of the Village. LPC Chairman Jack
Coladarci presents the awards for restoration; 500 Maple Street, 656 Ardsley
Road, 740 Ardsley Road, and rehabilitation; 1100 Pelham Road.
b)   Trustees. No report.
c)   Attorney. No report.
d)   Manager. No report.
e)   Village President. No report.
