Trustee Albinson seconded by Trustee Apatoff,
moved to approve the foregoing items on the Consent Agenda by omnibus vote. By
roll call vote, the motion carried. Ayes: Trustees Albinson, Apatoff, Dalman,
Dearborn, Handler, and Orsic. Nays: None. Absent: None.
7)   Ordinances and Resolutions.
a)   Ordinance No. MC-04-2024: Amending Chapter 15.60 of the Winnetka Village
Code Concerning Window Sign Regulations (Introduction/Adoption)
The Design Review Board unanimously recommended that Village Council amend the
Village Code to permit staff to administratively approve the placement of
window signage applied to both the interior and exterior of a window.
Trustee Dearborn, seconded by Trustee Albinson, moved to waive introduction
of Ordinance No. MC-04-2024. By voice vote, the motion carried unanimously. 
Trustee Albinson, seconded by Trustee Handler, moved to adopt Ordinance No. MC-
04-2024. By roll call vote, the motion carried. Ayes: Trustees Albinson,
Apatoff, Dalman, Dearborn, Handler, and Orsic. Nays: None. Absent: None.
b)   Resolution No. R-24-2024: Approving an Outdoor Dining Agreement with
Paradise Food Italia LLC D/B/A Tocco (Adoption)
While key provisions of the outdoor dining agreement for Tocco are consistent
with last year, Assistant Village Manager Kristin Kazenas reviews changes to
the agreement that address concerns regarding customer access to street
parking, volume of music, and musical acts impacting both sides of Chestnut
Court.
The agreement will permit music in the outdoor seating area on Wednesdays,
Saturdays, and Sunday, however, the music levels must comply with Village Code
and may not cause a public nuisance. Additionally, the agreement provides
updates regarding parking concerns and elimination of street closure during
April and October due to weather conditions.
Public Comment.
Bruno Abate, owner of Tocco, expresses gratitude for working in the Village and
hopes that he and neighboring businesses can cordially work alongside one
another.
Marie, Tocco employee, commends Council for granting accommodations regarding
parking and ensures that Tocco will monitor noise levels while the agreement is
in effect.
Bella Kaminsky, owner of Bellas Day Spa, addresses Council regarding concerns
related to parking, noise level, and disruption of business operations as a
result of outdoor dining.
Teresa Lucas expresses concerns regarding Tocco and its outdoor dining
agreement.
Council discusses parking concerns specific to Tocco, Bellas Day Spa, Good
Grapes, and neighboring Chestnut Court businesses, and agreement terms and
conditions.
Trustee Dearborn suggests memorializing expectations regarding the outdoor
dining agreement, incorporate protection of impacted Chestnut Court businesses,
further consideration of parking, musician setup, and permitted window of
outdoor setup.
Council defers the item to the March 21st meeting. Without objection, the item
is deferred.
c)   Resolution No. R-25-2024: Approving an Outdoor Dining Agreement with Good
Grapes, LLC (Adoption)
Good Grapes has submitted a request for an outdoor dining agreement consistent
with the previous year’s agreement. Assistant Village Manager Kristin Kazenas
informs Council of updates such as allowing music during permitted times while
ensuring the music must comply with Village Code and not create a public
nuisance, reduction of parking spaces, elimination of street closure during
April and October due to weather conditions.
Teresa Lucas addresses Council regarding the benefits of street closure,
business scheduled events, and matters related to parking.
Council discusses the agreement terms and conditions.
Trustee Orsic, seconded by Trustee Apatoff, moved to adopt Resolution No. R-25-
2024. By roll call vote, the motion carried. Ayes: Trustees Albinson, Apatoff,
Dalman, Dearborn, Handler, and Orsic. Nays: None. Absent: None.
d)   Resolution No. R-27:2024: Approving a Non-Exclusive Agreement for Use of
Winnetka Property for the Winnetka Music Festival (Adoption)
Trustee Handler recused herself from the discussion.
Assistant Village Manager Kristin Kazenas addresses Council regarding the
approval of an agreement for the Winnetka Music Festival co-sponsored by the
Village of Winnetka and the Winnetka-Northfield-Glencoe Chamber of Commerce.
The agreement is consistent with the prior year agreement with the exception of
the date update scheduled for Friday, June 14, 2024, and Saturday, June 15,
2024.
Scott Myers presents information about the Music Fest and Village wide provided
support.
