May 14, 2024
(Approved: June 4, 2024)
A record of a legally convened meeting of the Council of the Village of
Winnetka, which was held at the Council Chambers on Tuesday, May 14, 2024 at 7:
00 PM.
1)   Call to Order.
President Rintz called the meeting to order at 7:02 PM. Village Manager Bahan
called the roll of the Village Council. Present: Trustees Kirk Albinson, Rob
Apatoff, Tina Dalman, Bob Dearborn, Kim Handler and Bridget Orsic. Absent:
None. Also present: Village Manager Robert Bahan, Assistant Village Manager
Kristin Kazenas, Village Attorney Peter Friedman, Deputy Village Clerk Berina
Gradjan, Water & Electric Director Nick Narhi, Strategic Development Manager
Brian Keys, and approximately 5 persons in the audience.
2)   Public Comment
a)    John Root addresses Council regarding future lakefront ordinances and
litigation matters related to the adoption of the steep slope ordinance.
3)   Discussion.
a)   Illinois Municipal Electric Agency (IMEA) Contract Renewal Discussion –
Policy Direction
The Village’s current power sales contract and capacity purchase agreement is
set to expire on September 30, 2035, and in order to plan for the transition to
a net zero generation portfolio and to meet the future power needs, the
Illinois Municipal Electric Agency has requested that the Village and the other
thirty-one members consider extending their contracts with the agency. Members
of the IMEA are currently considering the terms and conditions of the proposed
contracts.
Staci Wilson, Director of Government Affairs, reviews the agency’s partnership
with Winnetka, its boards, benefits of joint actions, its costs and
efficiencies, and the various services provided to its members. Additionally,
Ms. Wilson provides the proposed contract terms and conditions, regulations,
affordability, cost, and the IMEA’s financial state, market fluctuations, power
supply resources, and an overview of the sustainability report, a roadmap of
the anticipated transition to a net-zero vision.
Rakesh Kothakapu, Vice President of Engineering & Energy Markets, provides
information regarding key dates for the transition to the net zero generation
portfolio, matters related to the resource agreements, and rate projections.
Troy Fodor, Vice President & General Counsel, addresses Council regarding the
history of the contract, provides information related to the extension of the
contract and duration, partnership with outside vendors, rates and charges,
added benefits to the proposed agreement, and generator capacity credits and
its benefits to IMEA members.
Council discusses power needs, power systems utilized by various other
communities not part of the IMEA, anticipated debt related to carbon neutral
transition, utilization of alternate power agencies other than the IMEA,
production and cost increases, the future of net-zero vision, replacements and
additions of resources, and the benefits of ownership of IMEA resources.
Public Comment
Craig Woody comments on Winnetka’s unique assets that can be utilized to
generate power.
Patrick Hanley, Environmental & Forestry Chair, addresses IMEA representatives
regarding updates to rules related to Prairie State and its impacts, and the
IMEA member contract.
John Root addresses Council regarding Winnetka’s power plant once transitioned
to net zero generation portfolio.
4)   Closed Session for the Purpose of Discussing Closed Session Minutes
pursuant to Section 2(c)(21) of the Open Meetings Act.
Trustee Albinson , seconded by Trustee Apatoff, moved to adjourn to Closed
Session for the purpose of discussing closed session minutes pursuant to
Section 2(c)(21) of the Open Meetings Act and to adjourn the Open Meeting
automatically and immediately upon the conclusion of the Closed Session without
the conduct of any further business or comments. By roll call vote, the motion
carried. Ayes: Trustees Albinson, Apatoff, Dalman, Dearborn, Handler, and
Orsic. Nays: None. Absent: None.
The Council adjourned into Closed Session at 8:41 p.m.
5)   Adjournment.
The Closed Session meeting ended at 9:03 pm
/s/ Berina Gradjan, Deputy Village Clerk 
Recording Secretary
