8)   Ordinances and Resolutions.
a)   Ordinance No. MC-05-2024: Amending the Winnetka Village Code to Increase
the Village Manager’s Purchasing Authority for Purchase Orders, Contracts, and
Change Orders (Introduction/Adoption)
The Village Manager may authorize purchases and promote efficient purchasing
and procurement processing.
Finance Director Tim Sloth confirms the Village Manager’s purchasing authority
at $25,000, since 1999, with an authority to delegate $10,000 to the Finance
Director. Due to accumulated inflation, the Village Manager’s purchasing
authority has been eroded and staff is proposing to increase the purchasing
authority of the Village Manager to $50,000 and raise the delegation authority
to the Finance Director to $20,000.
Village Manager Bahan advises Council that the increase in purchasing authority
will allow staff to handle purchases more efficiently and decrease the amount
of items on Council’s agenda for approval.
Trustee Orsic, seconded by Trustee Apatoff, moved to waive introduction
of Ordinance No. MC-05-2024. By voice vote, the motion carried unanimously. 
Trustee Albinson, seconded by Trustee Orsic, moved to adopt Ordinance No. MC-
05-2024. By roll call vote, the motion carried. Ayes: Trustees Albinson,
Apatoff, Orsic, and President Rintz. Nays: None. Absent: Trustees Dalman,
Dearborn, and Handler.
9)   Old Business. 
None.
10)   New Business. 
None.
