December 10, 2024
MINUTES
WINNETKA VILLAGE COUNCIL
STUDY SESSION
(Approved: January 21, 2025)
A record of a legally convened meeting of the Council of the Village of
Winnetka, which was held at the Council Chambers on Tuesday, December 10, 2024
at 7:00 PM.
1)   Call to Order.
President Rintz called the meeting to order at 7:02 PM. Village Manager Bahan
called the roll of the Village Council. Present: Trustees Kirk Albinson, Rob
Apatoff, Tina Dalman, Bob Dearborn, Kim Handler, and Bridget Orsic. Absent:
None. Also present: Village Manager Robert Bahan, Village Attorney Peter
Friedman, Deputy Village Clerk Berina Gradjan, and approximately 8 persons in
the audience.
2)   Public Comment 
3)   Discussion.
a)   IMEA Contract Renewal Follow Up – Winnetka Future Energy Supply
Considerations
President Rintz states that during the October Future Energy Forum, Mark
Pruitt, former Director of the Illinois Power Agency, and current Principal for
the Power Bureau, presented about power purchasing and the PJM Transmission
Area.
Water & Electric Director Nick Narhi introduces Mark Pruitt, stating he has
more than 30 years of experience in the Illinois energy sector and provides
Council Mr. Pruitt’s employment history.
Mark Pruitt, Principal at the Power Bureau, provides information regarding the
electricity market conditions; demand, supply, capacity prices, volatility, and
reliability projections. Because energy systems are interconnected, Mr. Pruitt
advises on how these systems affect one another and how electricity is
efficiently distributed with shared power plants. Additionally, Mr. Pruitt
provides information related to PJM supply and demand and the demand for
electricity by region as well as the hourly output of all power assets that
make up the PJM system.
Mr. Pruitt provides information regarding solar and natural gas resources
posing various challenges also referred to as the effective load carrying
capability due to the uncontrollable fluctuating circumstances. Mr. Pruitt
provides information regarding the outlook of less nuclear, coal, and gas,
measurement of reliability based on reserve margins, generating capacity of
various fuels, Commerce Commission Forecasts, and projected costs.
Mark Pruitt provides Council information regarding grid supply options such as
operating as a municipal utility, requirements of a load serving entity to
supply electricity to end users, grid supply services options as in-house or
contracted, trade-offs between different grid supply services, and information
regarding renewable energy and carbon-free supply.
Council discusses individual contracts with various suppliers, supplier costs
related to electricity usage, technological advancements regarding battery
storage, production of energy from coal-fired and gas-fired power plants,
matters related to resources and capacity, and transitioning to greener
resources, reduction of carbon footprint, and costs related to greener options.
Additionally, Council discusses matters related to the proposed IMEA contract
renewal extension.
Public Comment
Brenden Andrew addresses Council regarding working within the constraints of
the IMEA contract and various forms of energy that can be utilized
King Poor addresses Council regarding concerns on the Village’s reliance upon
coal from Prairie State and the IMEA contract renewal extension.
Patrick Hanley addresses Council regarding various energy supplies and matters
related to capacity and supply costs.
Roger Hawkschild addresses Council regarding sustainability, costs, options,
and the IMEA contract renewal extension.
Terry Cross addresses Council regarding supplier options and concerns related
to the IMEA contract renewal extension.
President Rintz suggests Village staff continue discussions with the IMEA
regarding negotiations.
Council discusses solar contracts as part of a sustainability plan, continued
discussions with IMEA, Winnetka’s distribution system and policies, and matters
regarding negotiations.
4)   Adjournment.
Trustee Orsic, seconded by Trustee Dalman moved to adjourn the meeting. By
voice vote, the motion carried. The meeting adjourned at 9:16 pm.
/s/ Berina Gradjan, Deputy Village Clerk     Recording Secretary
