The public hearing opened at 7:10pm
Community Development Director David Schoon advises Council of the refined One
Winnetka proposed final planned development including changes to building
height, parking, exterior building design, use of Village parking lot, location
of streetscape transformer and lightning controller, and parking matters during
construction. Economic Development Coordinator Liz Dechant and Mr. Schoon will
provide notices regarding parking.
Additionally, Council is advised of the One Winnetka construction schedule
between April 2025 through October 2026. The construction schedule consists of
demolition, foundation, vertical construction, interior buildout, public
improvements, and substantial completion.
Council discusses concerns related to parking restrictions during construction
and the expansion of parking into residential neighborhoods. Mr. Schoon
confirms that the Village will utilize Safebuilt, a service that provides
additional assistance with overseeing the construction activity and monitoring
contractor parking as well as general public parking.
Additionally, Council discusses the location of the transformer and lighting
controller, contractor parking, access to handicap parking spaces, matters
related to leasing, proposed refinements to the development, and construction
notices to neighboring residents and businesses.
Trustee Dalman suggestion that construction updates and alerts be shared via
the Winnetka e-newsletter.
Public Comment
Frank Petrek addresses Council regarding obtaining an easement for a retaining
wall at 711 Oak Street.
Kelly Corley addresses Council regarding construction concerns, rodent and pest
control, air quality control, asbestos control, residential traffic, and safety
for pedestrians.
Jim Torvik expresses concerns regarding construction traffic and parking.
Carolina Polo addresses Council regarding rodent and pest control and traffic
concerns.
Lexis Serot expresses concerns regarding rodents, matters related to traffic
control, and designated handicap parking spaces.
The public hearing closed at 7:58 pm.
Trustee Albinson, seconded by Trustee Dalman, moved to waive introduction
of Ordinance No. M-01-2025. By voice vote, the motion carried unanimously. 
Trustee Albinson, seconded by Trustee Dalman, moved to adopt Ordinance No. M-
01-2025. By roll call vote, the motion carried. Ayes: Trustees Albinson,
Apatoff, Dalman, Handler, and Orsic. Nays: None. Absent: Trustee Dearborn.
b)   Resolution No. R-07-2025: Approving a Final Plat of Subdivision (511-515
Lincoln Avenue and 714-740 Elm Street – One Winnetka Subdivision) (Adoption)
Trustee Dalman, seconded by Trustee Apatoff, moved to adopt Resolution No. R-
07-2025. By roll call vote, the motion carried. Ayes: Trustees Albinson,
Apatoff, Dalman, Handler, and Orsic. Nays: None. Absent: Trustee Dearborn.
