9)   Ordinances and Resolutions. 
a)   Ordinance No. MC-01-2025: Amending Title 9 of the Winnetka Village Code to
Prohibit the Sale of Illicit THC Products and Kratom (Introduction/Adoption)
In recent years, there has been an increase in availability and marketing of
synthetic or chemically altered forms of tetrahydrocannabinol (THC) and kratom
products. While these products are being found at local convenience stores, gas
stations, vape shops, and online, there are increasing concerns that these
products are associated with addiction, withdrawal, and in some cases, death.
Police Chief Brian O’Connell provides information regarding THC and kratom
products, information regarding illicit drugs, various chemical effects, health
risks, testing, consumption, sales, marketing and legality.
Council discusses the availability of products and sales in surrounding
communities and within the Village, product marketing, age restrictions,
possible benefits, and various cons of the product. Additionally, Council
discusses concerns regarding marketing to the younger residents of the Village.
Public Comment
Heidi Sykora provides information regarding kratom health benefits and
encourages Council to reconsider the ban of the product.
James Hemmings addresses Council regarding Kratom health benefits and urges
Council to continue researching the product.
Jim Pratt addresses Council regarding the safety and health benefits of kratom
and encourages Council to reconsider approving a ban.
Council opted to defer the item to a later date in order to conduct further
research.
b)   Ordinance No. MC-02-2025: Amending Chapter 6.08 of the Winnetka Village
Code Regarding Limited Public Off Leash Dog Areas on Lake Michigan
(Introduction/Adoption)
This item is deferred to a later meeting.
 
10)   Old Business. None.
11)   New Business. None.
12)   Appointments: None.
 
 
13)   Closed Session for the Purpose of Discussing Specific Personnel and
Municipal Utility Contracts relating to the Purchase, Sale, or Delivery of
Electricity or Natural Gas Pursuant to 2(c)(1) and 2(c)(23) of the Open
Meetings Act.
 
Trustee Albinson, seconded by Trustee Dalman, moved to adjourn to Closed
Session for the purpose of discussing specific personnel and municipal utility
contracts relating to the purchase, sale, or delivery of electricity or natural
gas pursuant to 2(c)(1) and 2(c)(23) of the Open Meetings Act
and to adjourn the Open Meeting automatically and immediately upon the
conclusion of the Closed Session without the conduct of any further business or
comments. By roll call vote, the motion carried. Ayes: Trustees Albinson,
Apatoff, Dalman, Dearborn, and Orsic. Nays: None. Absent: Trustee Handler.
The Council adjourned into Closed Session at 8:33 p.m.
