May 6, 2025
 
(Approved: June 3, 2025)
A record of a legally convened regular meeting of the Council of the Village of Winnetka, which
was held at the Council Chambers on Tuesday, May 6, 2025, at 7:00 PM.
1)   Call to Order. President Rintz called the meeting to order at 7:02 PM.
Village Manager Rob Bahan called the roll. Present: Trustees Kirk Albinson, Rob
Apatoff, Tina Dalman, Robert Dearborn, Kim Handler and Bridget Orsic. Absent:
 None. Also present: Deputy Village Manager Kristin Kazenas, Deputy
Village Clerk Berina Gradjan, Village Attorney
Peter Friedman, and approximately 34 persons in the audience.
Following the tragic accident on May 2, 2025, involving Sediqeh Samadi and
Raziyeh Sigary, President Rintz called for a moment of silence in their memory.
2)   Pledge of Allegiance. President Rintz led the group in the Pledge of
Allegiance.
3)   Quorum.
a)   May 13, 2025 Study Session
All of the Council members present said they expect to attend.
b)   May 20, 2025 Regular Meeting
All of the Council members present said they expect to attend with the
exception of Trustee Dalman due to work obligations.
4)   Public Comment:
a)   Irene Smith expresses concern related to outreach emails from Our Town
Winnetka and commends President Rintz for his service.
b)   Ted Wynnychenko urges Council to govern cautiously.
c)   Theresa Lucas urges Council to reconsider amplification of music during
the outdoor dining season including revisions to the noise ordinance.
5)   Reports :
a)   Trustees.
i.   Trustee Handler encourages those attending the Winnetka Farmers’ Market to
stop by and engage with members of Council and members of the various Village
boards and commissions.
ii.   Trustee Orsic emphasizes the value of public service and the vital role
those that serve have in the community.
iii.   In response to the tragic accident on May 2nd, Trustee Apatoff commends
Police and Fire first responders for their tremendous professionalism
responding to the scene.
b)   Attorney. No report.
c)   Manager. No report.
d)   Village President.
i.   President Rintz addresses matters related to the Village’s relationship
with IMEA, the Village’s revenue as a result of being a member of the IMEA,
generation of electricity, and the importance of the Village being a power
generator.
 
6)   Establishment of the Consent Agenda.
Trustee Albinson seconded by Trustee Dalman moved to approve the Establishment
of the Consent Agenda. By voice vote, the motion carried.
7)   Approval of the Consent Agenda
a)    Approval of Village Council Minutes
i.   April 8, 2025 Study Session
b)    Approval of Warrant List Dated April 11, 2025 – May 1, 2025, in the
amount of $617,621.48.
c)    Resolution No. R-41-2025: Approving a Contract with Power Line Supply
Company for the Purchase of 600 Volt Underground Cable (Adoption)
d)    Resolution No. R-43-2025: Waiving Bidding and Approving a Purchase of
Software Licenses from Liftoff LLC (Adoption)
Trustee Albinson seconded by Trustee Handler,
moved to approve the foregoing items on the Consent Agenda by omnibus vote. By
roll call vote, the motion carried. Ayes: Trustees Albinson, Apatoff, Dalman,
Dearborn, Handler, and Orsic. Nays: None. Absent: None.
8)   Village Clerk’s Report: Election Results
Village Manager Bahan reported the results of the April 1, 2025 election:
Robert Dearborn was elected Village President; and Kirk Albinson, Scott Myers,
and Bridget Orsic, were elected Village Trustees.
9)   Recess for Swearing In
10)   Village Clerk to Administer Oath of Office to President-Elect Robert
Dearborn, Trustee Kirk Albinson, Trustee Bridget Orsic, and Trustee-Elect Scott
Myers
Village Manager Bahan administered the Oath of Office to the newly elected
Village officials.
President Dearborn introduces and extends appreciation to the Village Council,
the Village’s department heads and staff led by Village Manager Rob Bahan and
Deputy Village Manager Kristin Kazenas, and the boards and commissions.
Additionally, President Dearborn promises that residents, community members,
and members of the public will be treated with respect and their voices will be
heard.
11)   Call the New Council to Order and Roll Call
President Dearborn called the meeting to order at 7:35 PM. Village Manager Rob
Bahan called the roll. Present: Trustees Kirk Albinson, Rob Apatoff, Tina
Dalman, Kim Handler, Scott Myers, and Bridget Orsic. Absent: None. Also
present: Deputy Village Manager Kristin Kazenas, Deputy
Village Clerk Berina Gradjan, Village Attorney
Peter Friedman, and approximately 34 persons in the audience.
12)   Ordinances and Resolutions
a)   Resolution No. R-44-2025: President Rintz Commendation (Adoption).
President Dearborn read aloud the Resolution honoring former President Rintz
for his exceptional service, compassion, unwavering dedication and leadership
to the Village of Winnetka.
Mr. Rintz reflects on his time as not only the longest serving Village
President since 1929, but also as Village Trustee, expressing deep gratitude
for the opportunity to serve the community, alongside exceptional past and
present trustees, Village staff, and residents of the community. Mr. Rintz
expressed heartfelt gratitude to his wife, Kathy Rintz, for her support and
sacrifices during his time serving. Mr. Rintz urges Council and community
members to be kind, listen, respect one another, and work collaboratively to
make Winnetka a special place.
Members of Council express deep appreciation, emphasize the value of working
alongside former President Rintz, and commend his lasting impact on each
trustee.
Trustee Orsic, seconded by Trustee Dalman, moved to adopt Resolution No. R-44-
2025. By roll call vote, the motion carried. Ayes: Trustees Albinson, Apatoff,
Dalman, Handler, Myers, and Orsic. Nays: None. Absent: None. Abstain: None.
13)   New Business. None.
14)   Appointments:
