M-ORDINANCES
These ordinances are complete through M-09-2025
1998
ORDINANCE NO. M-515-98
AN ORDINANCE AUTHORIZING THE VACATION OF THE ALLEY RIGHT-OF-WAY AT THE REAR OF
333 FAIRVIEW AND ACCEPTING A PLAT OF CONSOLIDATION
   WHEREAS, pursuant to Section 11-91-1 of the Illinois Municipal Code (65 ILCS
5/11-91-1), the Council of the Village of Winnetka are authorized to vacate any
street or alley or part thereof within the corporate limits of the Village if
the corporate authorities determine that the public interest will be served by
the vacation; and
   WHEREAS, the property commonly known as 333 Fairview (the “Adjoining
Property”) is legally described as follows:
Lot 7 (except the North 1 Foot thereof) in Block 3 in Dale’s Addition to
Winnetka, a Subdivision of the North 7 Chains and 50 Links of the Southeast
Fractional ¼ of Section 21, Township 42 North, Range 13, East of the Third
Principal Meridian, in Cook County, Illinois; and
   WHEREAS, the Council of the Village have considered whether it should vacate
all or portions of the 10-foot alley right-of-way adjoining the east lot line
of the property commonly known as 333 Fairview Avenue; and
   WHEREAS, the alley adjoining the east property line of the Adjoining
Property was formerly part of a 20-foot wide dedicated alley, which east 10
feet has previously been vacated by the Village; and
   WHEREAS, the Council of the Village of Winnetka have determined that it is
in the public interest that the 10-foot alley right-of-way adjoining the east
lot line of the Adjoining Property be vacated and consolidated with the
Adjoining Property; and
   WHEREAS, the Council of the Village of Winnetka have determined that the
reasonable value of the alley is $12,500 and the owner of the Adjoining
Property has agreed to pay the Village that amount if the alley is vacated and
consolidated with the Adjoining Property; and
   WHEREAS, on February 3, 1998, pursuant to duly published notice thereof, the
Winnetka Village Council conducted a public hearing regarding the proposed
vacation; and
   WHEREAS, the vacation of the above-described right-of-way will result in the
consolidation of the vacated alley to the Adjoining Property, resulting in the
reconfiguration of that lot, as depicted in the plat of subdivision entitled
Thompson’s Consolidation, which is attached hereto as Exhibit A; and
   WHEREAS, pursuant to Section 21.04(f) of Chapter 21 of the Winnetka Village
Code, “Land Subdivisions,” the Director of Community Development has reviewed
the plat of subdivision and has recommended that the consolidation be approved,
subject to the condition that an easement for water and electrical utilities be
reserved along the 10-foot wide vacated alley and that a 5-foot easement for
water and electrical utilities be reserved along the north side lot line and
the west (front) lot line; and
   WHEREAS, the Department of Water and Electric has determined that the needs
of the Department will be adequately met if the easement along the north side
lot line is for ingress and egress for the purpose of maintaining existing
overhead utility lines, and has recommended that the easement along the north
side lot line be reserved accordingly; and
   WHEREAS, the President and the Board of Trustees have determined that the
public interest will be served by vacating the above-described alley right-of-
way, which is legally described as follows:
The West Half (1/2) of the Alley lying South of the North Line of Lot 7,
extended, and North of the South Line of Lot 7, extended, except the North 1
Foot thereof) in Block 3 in Dale’s Addition to Winnetka, a Subdivision of the
North 7 Chains and 50 Links of the Southeast Fractional ¼ of Section 21,
Township 42 North, Range 13, East of the Third Principal Meridian, in Cook
County, Illinois; as depicted on the plat of subdivision entitled Thompson
Consolidation, which is attached hereto as Exhibit A; and
   WHEREAS, the corporate authorities of the Village of Winnetka have
determined that it is in the best interests of the public for the vacation of
the alley right-of-way to be subject to the reservation of easements as
recommended by the Director of Community Development, subject to the
modification recommended by the Director of Water and Electric.
   NOW, THEREFORE, the Council of the Village of Winnetka do ordain:
   SECTION 1 : The foregoing recitals are hereby adopted by the Council as its
findings and are incorporated herein by reference as if fully set forth herein.
   SECTION 2: That the alley right-of-way adjoining the east property line of
the Adjoining Property, as depicted in the attached Plat of Subdivision and
legally described as follows (the “Vacated Alley”):
The West Half (1/2) of the Alley lying South of the North Line of Lote 7,
extended, and North of the South Line of Lot 7, extended (except the North 1
Foot thereof), in Block 3 in Dale’s Addition to Winnetka, a Subdivision of the
North 7 Chains and 50 Links of the Southeast Fractional ¼ of Section 21,
Township 42 North, Range 13, East of the Third Principal Meridian, in Cook
County, Illinois; is hereby vacated, subject to the conditions hereinafter set
forth.
   SECTION 3 : The vacation of the Alley shall be subject to: (1) the
reservation of a 10-foot water and electric utility easement along the Vacated
Alley, the reservation of a 5-foot water and electric utility easement along
the west (front) lot line of the parcel of land to be formed by the
consolidation of the Vacated Alley with the Adjoining Property, and the
reservation of a 5-foot easement for ingress and egress along the north side
lot line for the purpose of operating, maintaining, repairing and replacing
existing overhead utilities; (2) the receipt by the Village of the full payment
of $12,500.00 from the Adjoining Owner; and (3) the payment by the Adjoining
Owner of all costs related to the vacation of the alley and the preparation and
recording of the plat.
   SECTION 4: Provided that the conditions set forth in Section 3 of this
ordinance are met, the Vacated Alley shall be consolidated with the Adjoining
Property into a single parcel of land, as depicted on the attached plat,
entitled “Thompson’s Consolidation,” said consolidated parcel from thereafter
to be legally described as:
Lot 1 of Thompson’s Consolidation, being a resubdivision in the Southeast
Fractional Quarter of Section 21, Township 42 North, Range 13, East of the
Third Principal Meridian, in Cook County, Illinois,
   SECTION 5 : The corporate authorities of the Village of Winnetka do hereby
authorize the Village President and Village Clerk to execute the plat entitled
"Thompson’s Consolidation," and to take all other steps necessary to effectuate
the vacation of the alley right-of-way and the recording of the Thompson’s
Consolidation plat, provided that all of the conditions set forth in Section 2
of this ordinance have first been met.
   SECTION 6 : Upon the execution of the plat, and the Adjoining Owners’ full
performance of all of the conditions set forth in this ordinance, the Village
Clerk of the Village of Winnetka is hereby authorized and directed to cause a
certified copy of this Ordinance and the Thompson’s Consolidation plat to be
recorded in the Office of the Cook County Recorder of Deeds.
   SECTION 7 : This ordinance shall be in full force and effect from and after
its passage, approval, and posting.
   PASSED and approved this  3rd day of  March , 1998.
