ORDINANCE NO: M-523-98
ORDINANCE AUTHORIZING THE SALE OR OTHER DISPOSITION OF CERTAIN PERSONAL
PROPERTY OWNED BY THE VILLAGE OF WINNETKA
WHEREAS, the Village of Winnetka owns the items of personal property
(hereinafter the “Personal Property”) described in Exhibit A, which exhibit is
attached to this ordinance and incorporated herein by reference; and
WHEREAS, the Computer Equipment listed in Exhibit A has been or is in the
process of being replaced by the Village’s upgraded computer system and the
prompt sale of the individual pieces of Computer Equipment as they are retired
from service and replaced is in the Village’s best interests because the value
of such Computer Equipment depreciates significantly as newer, upgraded
equipment becomes available on the market; and
WHEREAS, the Chief of Police has requested that two of the computers and two
monitors be donated to the North Regional Major Crimes Task Force (NORTAF), an
intergovernmental organization, in order to aid that organization in
accumulating data and conducting its correspondence; and
WHEREAS, the Finance Director and Village Manager have recommended that two
computers and two monitors be donated to NORTAF and that the remaining Computer
Equipment listed in Exhibit A be disposed of by sealed bid as soon as they are
no longer used by the Village; and
WHEREAS, the Council of the Village of Winnetka have determined that
Miscellaneous Property and Communications Equipment listed in Exhibit A are no
longer necessary or useful to the Village of Winnetka and that, upon the
installation of replacement Computer Equipment, the items of Computer Equipment
listed in Exhibit A will no longer be necessary or useful to the Village of
Winnetka; and
WHEREAS, the Council of the Village of Winnetka have further determined that
the cost of storing the Personal Property exceeds its value to the Village and
that the Personal Property should be disposed of in the manner hereinafter
provided, pursuant to Section 11-76-4 of the Illinois Municipal Code (65 ILCS
5/11-76-4), so as to avoid incurring additional costs for storing the Personal
Property and unnecessary costs in disposing of the Personal Property.
NOW THEREFORE, the Council of the Village of Winnetka do ordain as follows:
SECTION 1 :   Pursuant to Section 11-76-4 of the Illinois Municipal code (65
ILCS 5/11-76-4), the Council of the Village of Winnetka find that the items of
Personal Property listed in the attached Exhibit A (the “Personal Property”),
are either no longer necessary or useful to the Village of Winnetka or are
scheduled to be replaced and will no longer be necessary or useful to the
Village when that replacement occurs, and that the best interests of the
Village of Winnetka will be served by the sale or other disposition of the
Personal Property.
SECTION 2: The Council of the Village of Winnetka further find that, based on
prior experience in disposing of similar items of property, the cost of
conducting a public sale of such items of property, including the costs of
advertising and publishing, and the costs of personnel needed to maintain
security and to conduct the public sale exceeds the value of such items.
SECTION 3: Pursuant to Section 11-76-4 of the Illinois Municipal Code, the
Village Manager is hereby authorized and directed to donate two 486 computers
and two computer monitors to NORTAF, and to determine the value and dispose of
the remaining Personal Property listed in Exhibit A in any manner he deems
reasonable under the circumstances, including but not limited to: (a) the
outright disposal or donation of the Miscellaneous Property; (b) the trade-in
or outright disposal of the Communications Equipment and the Digital Micro VAX
2000 computer and the 13 Digital terminals; (c) and the sale of the remaining
Computer Equipment listed on Exhibit A, with or without advertising, after
determining the value of the equipment at the time it is replaced or retired
from service.
SECTION 4: The authority set forth in the preceding Section 3 to dispose of the
computer equipment, shall also apply to any other computer equipment that is
replaced or retired from service during the 1998-1999 fiscal year, the Council
having determined that such equipment will no longer be necessary or useful to
the Village and that it is in the best interests of the Village to dispose of
such equipment as soon as it is no longer necessary or useful to the Village.
SECTION 5: That this ordinance shall be in full force and effect from and after
its passage, approval and posting.
   ADOPTED this 2nd day of June, 1998, pursuant to the following roll call
vote:
   AYES:      Trustees Derning, Duhl, Lanphier, Lien and Meuer
   NAYES:   None
   ABSENT:   Trustee Hilton
   APPROVED this 2nd day of June, 1998.
   Signed
   ss/Louise A. Holland
   Village President
Countersigned:
Douglas G. Williams
Village Clerk
