ORDINANCE NO. M-525-98
AN ORDINANCE GRANTING A VARIATION IN THE APPLICATION OF THE ZONING ORDINANCE OF
THE VILLAGE OF WINNETKA COOK COUNTY, ILLINOIS (653 BLACKTHORNE)
WHEREAS, there has been presented to the Council of the Village of Winnetka,
Cook County, Illinois, the request of the owner of the following described real
estate (the “Subject Property”):
The North 75 feet of Lot 7 and the South 3 feet of Lot 4 in Burling’s
Resubdivision of Block 2 in Nelson’s Subdivision in the Southwest ¼ of the
Southeast ¼ of Section 17, Township 42 North, Range 13, East of the Third
Principal Meridian, in Cook County;
commonly known as 653 Blackthorne Road, Winnetka, Illinois, and located in the
“A-2” (One-Third Acre) Single-Family Residential Zoning District provided in
the Winnetka Zoning Ordinance, Chapter 22, Winnetka Village Code, for
variations from the rear yard setback requirements of Section 22.06(j) of the
Winnetka Zoning Ordinance, to allow a rear yard setback of 4.75 feet instead of
the minimum required rear yard setback of 25 feet, resulting in a variation of
20.25 feet (81%), for the purpose of allowing the relocation of window and door
openings in the existing exterior walls of the single family home on the
Subject Property; and
WHEREAS, on May 11, 1998, on due notice thereof, the Zoning Board of Appeals
conducted a public hearing on the requested variation and, by the unanimous
vote of the five members then in attendance, has reported to the Council
recommending that the requested variation be granted; and
WHEREAS, there are practical difficulties and particular hardships associated
with carrying out the strict application of the Zoning Ordinance with respect
to the Subject Property because the single family residence on the Subject
Property, which was constructed in 1916, before any zoning regulations were
enacted, is located at the rear of the lot, with the entire rear portion of the
residence now being located within the 25 foot rear yard setback; and
WHEREAS, the Subject Property cannot yield a reasonable return if the requested
variation is not granted because, due to the location of the rear portion of
the house within the rear yard setback, any renovation of the kitchen, laundry
and powder room, and of portions of the dining room and a study, all of which
are in nonconforming locations, would not be permitted; and
WHEREAS, the requested variation will not alter the essential character of the
neighborhood because the proposed work merely reorients doors and windows
within the existing walls at the rear of the house, is consistent with the
design and scale of the existing home and the scale of homes in the
neighborhood, does not increase the building footprint and replaces a roof
overhang with a canopy that is set farther back from the lot line; and
WHEREAS, the requested variation will not impair an adequate supply of light
and air because the footprint of the residence will not be increased and the
existing roof overhang will be removed, with a canopy being placed over the
proposed new French doors, which are set back farther from the lot line than
the existing overhang; and
WHEREAS, the requested variation will not increase the hazard from fire and
other dangers to the Subject Property; and
WHEREAS, the requested variation will not diminish the taxable value of land
and buildings throughout the Village, and the taxable value of the Subject
Property may be increased because of the proposed addition; and
WHEREAS, the proposed addition will not contribute to congestion on the public
streets, as the structure will continue to be used as a single family
residence; and
WHEREAS, the proposed addition will not otherwise impair the public health,
safety, comfort, morals and welfare of the inhabitants of the Village.
NOW, THEREFORE, the Council of the Village of Winnetka do ordain:
SECTION 1:   That the foregoing recitals are incorporated herein as the
findings of the Council of the Village of Winnetka, as if fully set forth
herein.
SECTION 2:   That a variation is hereby granted with respect to the Subject
Property, commonly known as 653 Blackthorne Road, which is located in the “A-2”
(One-Third Acre) Single-Family Residential District provided in the Winnetka
Zoning Ordinance, Chapter 22, Winnetka Village Code, from the rear yard setback
requirements of Section 22.06(j), to allow a rear yard setback of 4.75 feet
instead of the minimum required rear yard setback of 25 feet, resulting in a
variation of 20.25 feet (81%), for the purpose of allowing the relocation of
window and door openings in the existing exterior walls of the single family
home on the Subject Property, in accordance with the plans dated March 31,
1998, which were submitted with the application.
SECTION 3:   That the variation hereby granted is conditioned upon the
commencement of the proposed construction within 12 months after the effective
date of this Ordinance.
SECTION 4:   This Ordinance shall take effect immediately upon its passage,
approval and posting.
Passed and approved this 16th day of June, 1998:
AYES:    Trustees Derning, Duhl, Hilton, Lanphier, Lien and Meuer
NAYS:    None
ABSENT:    None
