ORDINANCE NO. M-526-98
AN ORDINANCE GRANTING A VARIATION IN THE APPLICATION OF THE ZONING ORDINANCE OF
THE VILLAGE OF WINNETKA COOK COUNTY, ILLINOIS (731 PROSPECT)
   WHEREAS, there has been presented to the Council of the Village of Winnetka,
Cook County, Illinois, the request of the owners of the following described
real estate (the “Subject Property”):
   Lot 3 in resubdivision of block 8 in park addition to Winnetka in township
42 North, Range 13, East of the Third Principal Meridian, described January 11,
1889 in Book 32 on Page 33 as Document 1049627 (excepting from said Lot 3, that
part lying East of a line drawn at right angles to the North line of said Lot 3
at a point 198.21 feet West of the Northeast corner of said Lot 3; also
excepting from the said Lot 3 that portion described as follows: beginning at
the Northwesterly corner of said Lot 3; thence Southeasterly along the
Southwesterly line of said Lot 3, being the easterly line of Prospect Avenue
70.00 feet; thence North line of said Lot 3, 55.83 feet to said North line;
thence west along said North line 42.22 feet to the angle in the Northerly line
of said Lot 3; thence Southwesterly along the Northwesterly line of said Lot 3,
205.00 feet to the place of beginning, in Cook County, Illinois;
commonly known as 731 Prospect Avenue, Winnetka, Illinois, and located in the
"A-3" (One-Half Acre) Single-Family District provided in the Winnetka Zoning
Ordinance, Chapter 22, Winnetka Village Code, for a variation of 1,614.92
square feet (11.40%) from the maximum building size of 14,164.26 square feet
permitted by Section 22.07(g) of the Winnetka Zoning Ordinance, to allow a
gross floor area of 15,779.18 square feet, and a variation from the maximum
height of 35 feet and two and one half stories permitted by Section 22.07(c) of
the Winnetka Zoning Ordinance, to allow a maximum building height of 35.88 feet
and three stories, said variations being requested for the purpose of
constructing a dormer addition at the third floor level of the existing
residence on the Subject Property; and
   WHEREAS, the owners of the Subject Property have also applied for a
variation of 2.57 feet (21.41%) from the minimum side yard of 12.0 feet
required by Section 22.07(i), to allow air conditioning condensers which they
have placed in the north side yard to observe a setback of 9.43 feet; and
   WHEREAS, on May 11, 1998, on due notice thereof, the Zoning Board of Appeals
held a public hearing on the requested variations, with the five members of the
Board then present unanimously voting to recommend that the Council grant the
requested variations from the maximum building size and maximum building height
limitations, and unanimously voting to recommend that the Council deny the
requested variation from the minimum required side yard setback; and
   WHEREAS, there are practical difficulties and particular hardships
associated with carrying out the strict application of the Zoning Ordinance
with respect to the proposed dormer addition, because the home was built before
any zoning regulations were enacted, it has a legal, non-conforming floor area
and building height, and adding the dormer will not increase either the floor
area or the building height, although the addition of the dormer increases the
degree on non-conformity by increasing the building volume; and
   WHEREAS, the Subject Property cannot yield a reasonable return if permitted
to be used only under the conditions allowed by the Zoning Ordinance, in that
the proposed dormer addition will increase the natural light on the third
floor, without which the area of the home on which it is proposed to be
constructed would have little utility; and
   WHEREAS, the requested variation for the dormer addition will not alter the
essential character of the neighborhood, because the proposed addition is a
small dormer that will match the existing dormers on the building without
increase the building height, the gross floor area or the visible bulk of the
building; and
   WHEREAS, the proposed dormer addition will not impair an adequate supply of
light and air because of its minimal size and its location away from the
buildings on adjoining properties; and
   WHEREAS, the requested variation for the dormer addition will not increase
the hazard from fire and other dangers to the Subject Property as it will
comply with all applicable building and fire protection codes; and
   WHEREAS, the requested variation for the dormer addition will not diminish
the taxable value of land and buildings throughout the Village, and the taxable
value of the Subject Property may be increased because of the proposed
addition; and
   WHEREAS, the proposed dormer addition will not contribute to congestion on
the public streets, as the structure will continue to be used as a single
family residence; and
   WHEREAS, there is no evidence that the proposed dormer addition will
otherwise impair the public health, safety, comfort, morals, and welfare of the
inhabitants of the Village; and
   WHEREAS, the variation requested for the air conditioners has been
withdrawn.
   NOW, THEREFORE, the Council of the Village of Winnetka do ordain:
   SECTION 1: That the foregoing recitals are hereby incorporated as the
findings of the Council of the Village of Winnetka, as if fully set forth
herein.
   SECTION 2: That a variation is hereby granted with respect to the Subject
Property, commonly known as 731 Prospect Avenue, which is located in the "A-3"
(One-Half Acre) Single-Family Residential District provided in the Winnetka
Zoning Ordinance, Chapter 22, Winnetka Village Code, for variations from the
maximum building size (Gross Floor Area) limitations of Section 22.07(g) of the
Winnetka Zoning Ordinance, to allow a gross floor area of 15,779.18 square
feet, whereas 14,164.26 square feet are permitted, resulting in a variation of
1,614.92 square feet (11.40%), and from the building height limitations of
Section 22.07(c) of the Winnetka Zoning Ordinance to allow a building height of
35.88 feet and three stories, whereas a maximum building height of 35 feet and
2 ½ stories is permitted, said variations being requested for the purpose of
allowing a dormer addition the east end of the existing roof, all in accordance
with the plans and application submitted on April 8, 1998.
   SECTION 3: That the variation hereby granted is conditioned upon the
commencement of the proposed construction within 12 months after the effective
date of this Ordinance.
   SECTION 4: That this Ordinance shall be in full force and effect from and
after its passage, approval, and posting.
   Passed and approved this 16th day of June, 1998.
   AYES:      Trustees Meuer, Lanphier, Lien, Hilton, Duhl and Derning
   NAYS:   None
   ABSENT:   None
               Signed:
                  ss/Louise A. Holland
                  Village President
Countersigned:
Douglas G. Williams
Village Clerk
