ORDINANCE NO. M-529-98
AN ORDINANCE GRANTING A VARIATION IN THE APPLICATION OF THE ZONING ORDINANCE OF
THE VILLAGE OF WINNETKA COOK COUNTY, ILLINOIS (2 Golf Lane)
   WHEREAS, there has been presented to the Council of the Village of Winnetka,
Cook County, Illinois, the request of the owners of the following described
real estate (the “Subject Property”):
Lot 8 in Indian Hill Subdivision No. 2, being a subdivision of parts of
Sections 20 and 29, Township 42 North, Range 13 East of the Third Principal
Meridian, according to plat recorded as Document #5772391 in Recorder's Office
of Cook County, Illinois (except that part of said Lot 8 lying south of a line
drawn from a point in the east line of said Lot 8, 247.56 ft. south of the
northeast corner of said Lot 8) to a point in the westerly line of said Lot 8,
128.23 feet southerly from the Northwest corner of said Lot 8) (said exception
being a portion of said Lot 8 heretofore conveyed by Florence Joys Fairman to
Mary F. Hicks by deed dated March 4, 1950 and recorded in Recorder's Office by
Cook County, Illinois, in Book 45285, at page 480, as Document No. 14750017 in
Cook County, Illinois;
commonly known as 2 Golf Lane, Winnetka, Illinois, and located in the "A-3"
(One-Half Acre) Single-Family District provided in the Winnetka Zoning
Ordinance, Chapter 22, Winnetka Village Code, for a variation from the front
setback provisions of Section 22.07(h) of the Winnetka Zoning Ordinance, from
50 feet to 18 feet in the front yard adjoining Hill Road, resulting in a
variation of 32 feet (64%), and from 50 feet to 20.15 feet in the corner yard
adjoining Golf Lane, resulting in a variation of 29.85 feet (59.7%), to permit
improvements to an existing enclosed porch located within the required front
setback, and to permit the construction of a full basement entirely below
grade; and
   WHEREAS, there are unique circumstances and practical difficulties
associated with carrying out the strict application of the Zoning Ordinance
with respect to these premises in that: the Subject Property is an irregularly
shaped, trapezoidal, corner lot, which requires 50-foot setbacks along both
street frontages; the house on the Subject Property was built in 1924 with 20-
foot setbacks, pursuant to a variation from the then-applicable 30-foot
setbacks, and is oriented so that the Hill Road frontage of the Subject
Property functions as part of the rear yard; and Hill Road is classified as a
primary street, making such orientation reasonable; and
   WHEREAS, in addition to the variation granted for the construction of the
residence in 1920, variations were granted in 1930 and 1996 to allow
improvements to be made to the Subject Property; and
   WHEREAS, the proposed variation will neither impair the essential character
of the locality nor impair an adequate supply of light and air, because the
proposed enclosure of the screened porch will be located entirely within the
existing building footprint at the rear of the house, the height of the
screened porch roof will not be increased, and the proposed basement will be
located entirely below grade; and
   WHEREAS, the proposed enclosure of the screened porch and proposed
construction of a full basement will not increase the hazard from fire and
other damage to the Subject Property, because it will comply with all
applicable building and fire protection codes; and
   WHEREAS, the proposed variation will not increase congestion on the public
streets, as the building will continue to be used as a single family,
residence; and
   WHEREAS, the proposed variation will not otherwise impair the public health,
safety, comfort, morals, and welfare of the inhabitants of the Village; and
   WHEREAS, the proposed enclosing of the porch and construction of a full
basement will not diminish the taxable value of land and buildings throughout
the Village because they will be improvements to the Subject Property and are
therefore likely to increase the taxable value of the Subject Property without
negatively impacting on other properties in the immediate vicinity; and
   WHEREAS, on June 8, 1998, on due notice thereof, the Zoning Board of Appeals
conducted a public hearing on said requested variation and, on the unanimous
vote of the six members then present, has reported to the Council recommending
that the requested variations be granted.
   NOW, THEREFORE, the Council of the Village of Winnetka do ordain:
   SECTION 1: That the foregoing recitals are hereby incorporated as the
findings of the Council of the Village of Winnetka, as if fully set forth
herein.
   SECTION 2: That a variation is hereby granted with respect to the Subject
Property, which is commonly known as 2 Golf Lane and is located in the "A-3"
(One-Half Acre) Single-Family Residential District provided in said Zoning
Ordinance, for a variation from the front setback provisions of Section 22.07
(h) of the Winnetka Zoning Ordinance, Chapter 22, Winnetka Village Code, from
50 feet to 18 feet in the front yard adjoining Hill Road, resulting in a
variation of 32 feet (64%), and from 50 feet to 20.15 feet in the corner yard
adjoining Golf Lane, resulting in a variation of 29.85 feet (59.7%), to permit
an existing screened porch to be enclosed and to permit the construction of a
full basement, all in accordance with the application and plans submitted with
the application for said variation.
   SECTION 3: That the variation hereby granted is further conditioned upon the
commencement of the proposed construction within 12 months after the effective
date of this Ordinance.
   SECTION 4: That this Ordinance shall be in full force and effect from and
after its passage, approval, and posting.
   ADOPTED this 21st day of July, 1998, pursuant to the following roll call
vote:
   AYES:      Trustees Duhl, Derning, Lien, Hilton and Meuer
   NAYES:   None
   ABSENT:   Trustee Lanphier
   APPROVED this 21st day of July, 1998.
   Signed
   ss/Louise A. Holland
   Village President
Countersigned:
ss/Douglas G. Williams
Village Clerk
Introduced:   July 7, 1998
Posted:   July 8, 1998
Passed and Approved: July 21, 1998
Posted:   July 22, 1998
ORDINANCE NO. M-530-98
AN ORDINANCE GRANTING A VARIATION IN THE APPLICATION OF THE ZONING ORDINANCE OF
THE VILLAGE OF WINNETKA COOK COUNTY, ILLINOIS (984 HILL ROAD)
   WHEREAS, there has been presented to the Council of the Village of Winnetka,
Cook County, Illinois, the request of the owner of the following described real
estate (the “Subject Property”):
   Parcel 1: Lots 1 to 4 both inclusive and Lot 5 (except the westerly 15 feet
thereof) all in Block 1 in Bradford and Porter’s Addition to Kenilworth, a
subdivision of the west ½ of the west ½ of the northwest ¼ of the northeast ¼
section 29, Township 42 North, Range 13 East of the Third Principal Meridian,
in Cook County, Illinois.
   Parcel 2: The North ½ of the vacated alley south and adjoining parcel 1 in
Cook County, Illinois commonly known as 984 Hill Road, Winnetka, Illinois, and
located in the "A-4" (One Acre) Single-Family District provided in the Winnetka
Zoning Ordinance, Chapter 22, Winnetka Village Code, for variations from the
rear yard setback requirements of Section 22.07A(j) of the Winnetka Zoning
Ordinance, to allow a rear yard setback of 18.37 feet instead of the minimum
required rear yard setback of 50 feet, resulting in a variation of 31.63 feet
(63.26%), for the purpose of allowing the construction of a family room
addition to the single family home on the Subject Property; and
   WHEREAS, on July 13, 1998, on due notice thereof, the Zoning Board of
Appeals conducted a public hearing on the requested variation and, by the
unanimous vote of the six members then in attendance, has reported to the
Council recommending that the requested variation be granted; and
   WHEREAS, there are practical difficulties and particular hardships
associated with carrying out the strict application of the Zoning Ordinance
with respect to the Subject Property because the Subject Property, which was in
existence before its annexation into the Village in 1989, has a legal,
nonconforming lot area of approximately one-third of an acre, although the
minimum lot size in the A-4 Zoning Districts is one acre, and the original
house has nonconforming front and rear yards; and
   WHEREAS, the Subject Property cannot yield a reasonable return if the
requested variation is not granted because the setback requirements in the A-
4 Zoning District limit the building area to 1,984 square feet, approximately
half of the permitted lot coverage of 3, 923 square feet; and
   WHEREAS, the requested variation will not alter the essential character of
the neighborhood as it is consistent with the design and scale of the existing
home and the scale of homes in the neighborhood; and
   WHEREAS, the requested variation will not impair an adequate supply of light
and air because the proposed addition has only one story, and will be aligned
with an existing bay window at the rear of the house; and
   WHEREAS, the requested variation will not increase the hazard from fire and
other dangers to the Subject Property as it will comply with all applicable
building codes; and
   WHEREAS, the requested variation will not diminish the taxable value of land
and buildings throughout the Village, and the taxable value of the Subject
Property may be increased because of the proposed addition; and
   WHEREAS, the proposed addition will not contribute to congestion on the
public streets, as the structure will continue to be used as a single family
residence; and
   WHEREAS, there is no evidence that the proposed addition will not otherwise
impair the public health, safety, comfort morals, and welfare of the
inhabitants of the Village.
   NOW, THEREFORE, the Council of the Village of Winnetka do ordain:
   SECTION 1: That the foregoing recitals are incorporated as the findings of
the Council of the Village of Winnetka, as if fully set forth herein.
   SECTION 2: That a variation is hereby granted with respect to the Subject
Property, commonly known as 984 Hill Road, which is located in the "A-4" (One
Acre) Single-Family Residential District provided in the Winnetka Zoning
Ordinance, Chapter 22, Winnetka Village Code, from the rear yard setback
requirements of Section 22.07A(j), to allow a rear yard setback of 18.37 feet
instead of the minimum required rear yard setback of 50 feet, resulting in a
variation of 31.63 feet (63.26%), for the purpose of constructing a one-story
family room addition to the single family home on the Subject Property, in
accordance with the plans submitted with the application.
   SECTION 3: That the variation hereby granted is conditioned upon the
commencement of the proposed construction within 12 months after the effective
date of this Ordinance.
   SECTION 4: That this Ordinance shall be in full force and effect from and
after its passage, approval, and posting.
   Passed and approved this 18th day of August, 1998.
   AYES:      Trustees Meuer, Derning, Lien and President Holland
   NAYS:   None   ABSENT:   Trustee Lanphier, Duhl and Hilton
               Signed:
                  ss/Louise A. Holland
                  Village President
Countersigned:
ss/Douglas G. Williams
Village Clerk
