ORDINANCE NO. M-531-98
AN ORDINANCE GRANTING A VARIATION IN THE APPLICATION OF THE ZONING ORDINANCE OF
THE VILLAGE OF WINNETKA COOK COUNTY, ILLINOIS (466 POPLAR)
   WHEREAS, there has been presented to the Council of the Village of Winnetka,
Cook County, Illinois, the request of the owner of the following described real
estate (the “Subject Property”):
   The north 30 feet of the east 25 feet of Lot 8 and the north 60 feet of Lots
9 and 10, in Sherlock’s Subdivision of Block 40 in Winnetka, according to the
map of the subdivision of said block recorded April 24, 1871, as document
number 93665, in Book 173, of maps, page 29, in Cook County, Illinois;
commonly known as 466 Poplar Street, Winnetka, Illinois, and located in the "A-
5" (One-Quarter Acre) Single-Family District provided in the Winnetka Zoning
Ordinance, Chapter 22, Winnetka Village Code, for a variation from the maximum
building size (Gross Floor Area) limitations of Section 22.05A(g) of the
Winnetka Zoning Ordinance, to allow a gross floor area of 3,928.37 square feet,
whereas 3,645 square feet are permitted, resulting in a variation of 283.37
square feet (7.8%), said variation being requested for the purpose of allowing
a 5 foot by 28 foot, one story breakfast room addition on the west side of the
existing kitchen of the single family residence on the subject property; and
   WHEREAS, July 13, 1998, on due notice thereof, the Zoning Board of Appeals
conducted a public hearing on the requested variation and by the affirmative
vote of four of the six members then present, has reported to the Council
recommending that the requested variation be granted; and
   WHEREAS, there are practical difficulties and particular hardships
associated with carrying out the strict application of the Zoning Ordinance
with respect to the Subject Property in that the existing residence became
nonconforming in size when the previous owner sold 750 square feet of the lot
to an adjoining owner, and the minimal size of the addition will add only 140
square feet to the residence, although the total nonconforming area is 283.37
feet; and
   WHEREAS, the Subject Property cannot yield a reasonable return if permitted
to be used only under the conditions allowed by the Zoning Ordinance, in that
the proposed addition will allow the renovation of the existing condition, the
creation of a new breakfast room, and more direct access to the family room
from the kitchen, all of which are typical elements of single family residences
in the area; and
   WHEREAS, the requested variation will not alter the essential character of
the neighborhood because the proposed addition is at the rear of the house and
is within the perimeter of an existing patio; and
   WHEREAS, the proposed addition will not impair an adequate supply of light
and air because of it will have a low profile that will extend only 5 feet from
the rear of the existing house; and
   WHEREAS, the requested variation will not increase the hazard from fire and
other dangers to the Subject Property as it will comply with all applicable
building and fire protection codes; and
   WHEREAS, the requested variation will not diminish the taxable value of land
and buildings throughout the Village, and the taxable value of the Subject
Property may be increased because of the proposed addition; and
   WHEREAS, the proposed addition will not contribute to congestion on the
public streets, as the structure will continue to be used as a single family
residence; and
   WHEREAS, there is no evidence that the proposed addition will otherwise
impair the public health, safety, comfort, morals, and welfare of the
inhabitants of the Village.
   NOW, THEREFORE, the Council of the Village of Winnetka do ordain:
   SECTION 1: That the foregoing recitals are incorporated as the findings of
the Council of the Village of Winnetka, as if fully set forth herein.
   SECTION 2: That a variation is hereby granted with respect to the Subject
Property, commonly known as 466 Poplar Street, which is located in the "A-5"
(One-Quarter Acre) Single-Family Residential District provided in the Winnetka
Zoning Ordinance, Chapter 22, Winnetka Village Code, for a variation from the
maximum building size (Gross Floor Area) limitations of Section 22.05A(g) of
the Winnetka Zoning Ordinance, to allow a gross floor area of 3,928.37 square
feet, whereas 3,645 square feet are permitted, resulting in a variation of
283.37 square feet (7.8%), said variation being requested for the purpose of
allowing a breakfast room addition onto the west side of the existing kitchen
of the single family home on the Subject Property.
   SECTION 3: That the variation hereby granted is conditioned upon the
commencement of the proposed construction within 12 months after the effective
date of this Ordinance and upon the applicants’ having paid all applicable fees
and charges within 30 days after the adoption of this ordinance.
   SECTION 4: That this Ordinance shall be in full force and effect from and
after its passage, approval, and posting.
   Passed and approved this 15th day of September, 1998.
   AYES:      Trustees Lanphier, Meuer, Derning and Hilton
   NAYS:   Trustees Lien and Duhl
   ABSENT:   None
               Signed:
                  ss/Louise A. Holland
   Village President
Countersigned:
ss/Douglas G. Williams
Village Clerk
