ORDINANCE NO. M-532-98
AN ORDINANCE GRANTING A VARIATION IN THE APPLICATION OF THE ZONING ORDINANCE OF
THE VILLAGE OF WINNETKA COOK COUNTY, ILLINOIS (1311 SCOTT AVENUE)
   WHEREAS, there has been presented to the Council of the Village of Winnetka,
Cook County, Illinois, the request of the owner of the following described real
estate (the “Subject Property”):
   Lot 8 except the west 50 feet thereof in Block 8 in Lloyd’s Subdivision of
Blocks 1 to 5 of Taylor’s Second Addition to Taylorsport, being a part of the
northwest ¼ of Section 17, Township 42 North, Range 13, East of the Third
Principal Meridian, in Cook County, Illinois;
commonly known as 1311 Scott Avenue, Winnetka, Illinois, and located in the "A-
1" (One-Sixth Acre) Single-Family Residential District provided in the Winnetka
Zoning Ordinance, Chapter 22, Winnetka Village Code, for a variation from the
maximum building size (Gross Floor Area) limitations of Section 22.05(g) of the
Winnetka Zoning Ordinance, to allow a gross floor area of 3,773.58 square feet,
whereas 3,197.39 square feet are permitted, resulting in a variation of 576.19
square feet (18.02%), for the purpose of constructing four new dormers on the
upper floor of the single family home on the subject property; and
   WHEREAS, on July 13, 1998, on due notice thereof, the Zoning Board of
Appeals conducted a public hearing on the requested variation and by the
unanimous vote of the six members then present, has reported to the Council
recommending that the requested variation be granted; and
   WHEREAS, there are practical difficulties and unique hardships associated
with carrying out the strict application of the Zoning Ordinance with respect
to the Subject Property in that the Subject Property is larger than the minimum
lot size, is improved with a single family residence that was constructed in
1928, and has less than one half of the allowable lot coverage, although it
exceeds the maximum permitted floor area by 485.78 square feet, of which 376.8
square feet are unusable attic space without natural light and ventilation; and
   WHEREAS, the Subject Property cannot yield a reasonable return if permitted
to be used only under the conditions allowed by the Zoning Ordinance, in that
the existing attic area is more than 11.5% of the home’s total floor area,
although it is unusable without the proposed improvements, which will add only
another 90.41 square feet of floor area; and
   WHEREAS, the requested variation will not alter the essential character of
the neighborhood because the proposed dormers are consistent with the style of
the house and add only 90.41 square feet of floor area without increasing
either the height or the footprint of the house; and
   WHEREAS, the requested variation will not impair an adequate supply of light
and air because of the proposed new dormers change a small portion of the roof
line on three sides of the house without adding to the building height or to
the building footprint; and
   WHEREAS, the requested variation will not increase the hazard from fire and
other dangers to the Subject Property as it will comply with all applicable
building and fire protection codes and bring the nonconforming attic stairway
into compliance; and
   WHEREAS, the requested variation will not diminish the taxable value of land
and buildings throughout the Village, and the taxable value of the Subject
Property may be increased because of the proposed improvements; and
   WHEREAS, the proposed new dormers will not contribute to congestion on the
public streets, as the structure will continue to be used as a single family
residence; and
   WHEREAS, there is no evidence that the proposed addition will otherwise
impair the public health, safety, comfort, morals, and welfare of the
inhabitants of the Village.
   NOW, THEREFORE, the Council of the Village of Winnetka do ordain:
   SECTION 1: That the foregoing recitals are hereby incorporated as the
findings of the Council of the Village of Winnetka, as if fully set forth
herein.
   SECTION 2: That a variation is hereby granted with respect to the Subject
Property, commonly known as 466 Poplar Street, which is located in the "A-1"
(One-Sixth Acre) Single-Family Residential District provided in the Winnetka
Zoning Ordinance, Chapter 22, Winnetka Village Code, for a variation from the
maximum building size (Gross Floor Area) limitations of Section 22.05(g) of the
Winnetka Zoning Ordinance, to allow a gross floor area of 3,773.58 square feet,
whereas 3,197.39 square feet are permitted, resulting in a variation of 576.19
square feet (18.02%), for the purpose of constructing four new dormers on the
upper floor of the single family home on the Subject Property, in accordance
with the application for variation and plans submitted with the application.
   SECTION 3: That the variation hereby granted is conditioned upon the
commencement of the proposed construction within 12 months after the effective
date of this Ordinance.
   SECTION 4: That this Ordinance shall be in full force and effect from and
after its passage, approval, and posting.
   Passed and approved this 18th day of August, 1998.
   AYES:   Trustees Lien, Meuer,Derning and President Holland
   NAYS:   None
   ABSENT:   Trustees Lanphier, Duhl and Hilton
               Signed:
                  ss/Louise A. Holland
   Village President
