ORDINANCE NO. M-533-98
AN ORDINANCE GRANTING A VARIATION IN THE APPLICATION OF THE ZONING ORDINANCE OF
THE VILLAGE OF WINNETKA COOK COUNTY, ILLINOIS (821 FOXDALE AVENUE)
   WHEREAS, there has been presented to the Council of the Village of Winnetka,
Cook County, Illinois, the request of the owners of the following described
real estate (the “Subject Property”):
Lot 17 in Block 4 in Winnetka Park Bluffs, being a subdivision by William H.
Cairnduff of part of Sections 16, 17 and 20, Township 42 North, Range 13 East
of the Third Principal Meridian, in Cook County, Illinois;
commonly known as 821 Foxdale Avenue, Winnetka, Illinois, and located in the
"A-1" (One-Sixth Acre) Single-Family Residential District provided in the
Winnetka Zoning Ordinance, Chapter 22, Winnetka Village Code, for a variation
from the side yard setback provisions of Section 22.05(i) of the Winnetka
Zoning Ordinance, to allow a north side yard of 4.29 feet instead of the
required 6 feet, resulting in a variation of 1.71 feet (28.5%), for the purpose
of constructing a second floor addition above an existing one story sunroom;
and
   WHEREAS, there are unique circumstances and practical difficulties
associated with carrying out the strict application of the Zoning Ordinance
with respect to these premises in that the single family residence on the
Subject Property was built in 1915, before the adoption of the Zoning Ordinance
and has a nonconforming north side yard, there is no conforming alternative
location for the proposed addition, and setting the second floor back 1.71 feet
from the first floor building line would create structural problems or
reconstructing the first floor would be prohibitively expensive; and
   WHEREAS, the proposed variation will not impair the essential character of
the locality in that the addition will vertically extend the walls of the
sunroom below, which is located at the rear of the house, and will not be
visible from the street; and
   WHEREAS, the proposed addition will not impair an adequate supply of light
and air in that it will not encroach any further into the required side yard
than the existing floor below, and will be more than 10 feet less than the
maximum allowable building height; and
   WHEREAS, the proposed construction of a second floor addition will not
increase the hazard from fire and other damage to the Subject Property, as it
will comply with all applicable building and fire protection codes; and
   WHEREAS, the proposed variation will not increase congestion on the public
streets, as the building will continue to be used as a single family,
residence; and
   WHEREAS, the proposed variation will not otherwise impair the public health,
safety, comfort, morals, and welfare of the inhabitants of the Village; and
   WHEREAS, the proposed construction of a second floor addition will not
diminish the taxable value of land and buildings throughout the Village and the
taxable value may be increased because of the improvement to the Subject
Property; and
   WHEREAS, on July 13, 1998, on due notice thereof, the Zoning Board of
Appeals conducted a public hearing on the requested variation and, on the
unanimous vote of the six members then present, has reported to the Council
recommending that the requested variations be granted.
   NOW, THEREFORE, the Council of the Village of Winnetka do ordain:
   SECTION 1: That the foregoing recitals are hereby incorporated as the
findings of the Council of the Village of Winnetka, as if fully set forth
herein.
   SECTION 2: That a variation is hereby granted with respect to the Subject
Property, which is commonly known as 821 Foxdale Avenue and is located in the
"A-1" (One-Sixth Acre) Single-Family Residential District provided in the
Winnetka Zoning Ordinance, Chapter 22 of the Winnetka Village Code, for a
variation from the side yard setback provisions of Section 22.05(i) of the
Winnetka Zoning Ordinance, to allow a north side yard of 4.29 feet instead of
the required 6 feet, resulting in a variation of 1.71 feet (28.5%) for the
purpose of constructing a second floor addition above an existing one story
sunroom, all in accordance with the application for variation and the plans
submitted with the application.
   SECTION 3: That the variation hereby granted is further conditioned upon the
commencement of the proposed construction within 12 months after the effective
date of this Ordinance.
   SECTION 4: That this Ordinance shall be in full force and effect from and
after its passage, approval, and posting.
   ADOPTED this 15th day of September, 1998, pursuant to the following roll
call vote:
