ORDINANCE NO. M-534-98
AN ORDINANCE GRANTING A VARIATION IN THE APPLICATION OF THE ZONING ORDINANCE OF
THE VILLAGE OF WINNETKA COOK COUNTY, ILLINOIS (955 OLD GREEN BAY ROAD)
   WHEREAS, there has been presented to the Council of the Village of Winnetka,
Cook County, Illinois, the request of the owner of the following described real
estate (the “Subject Property”):
   Lot 3 in Knode’s Resubdivision of Lot 2 in the subdivision of block 11,
except the east 1-1/2 acres, in Hubbard Estates Subdivision in the northeast
fractional ¼ of Section 17, Township 42 North, Range 13 East of the Third
Principal Meridian, in Cook County, Illinois;
commonly known as 955 Old Green Bay Road, Winnetka, Illinois, and located in
the "A-3" (One-Half Acre) Single-Family Residential District provided in the
Winnetka Zoning Ordinance, Chapter 22, Winnetka Village Code, for a variation
from the rear yard setback requirements of Section 22.07(j) of the Winnetka
Zoning Ordinance, to allow a rear yard setback of 13.26 feet instead of the
minimum required rear yard setback of 25 feet, resulting in a variation of
11.74 feet (46.96%), for the purpose of allowing the existing detached garage
located in the rear yard setback, to be connected to the existing single family
home on the Subject Property; and
   WHEREAS, on July 13, 1998, on due notice thereof, the Zoning Board of
Appeals conducted a public hearing on the requested variation and, by the
unanimous vote of the six members then in attendance, has reported to the
Council recommending that the requested variation be granted; and
   WHEREAS, there are practical difficulties and unique hardships associated
with carrying out the strict application of the Zoning Ordinance with respect
to the Subject Property because the existing detached garage which is permitted
as an accessory structure in the rear yard, will be in a nonconforming location
upon its connection to the residence, which is the principal use, although the
location of the garage will not change ; and
   WHEREAS, the Subject Property cannot yield a reasonable return if the
requested variation is not granted because the Subject Property is an
irregularly shaped lot with ravines along the rear and the east side, and the
only other accessible, conforming locations for an attached garage would
require reconfiguring the interior plan of the house to avoid connecting the
garage to the more formal living areas; and
   WHEREAS, the requested variation will not alter the essential character of
the neighborhood as the garage will remain in its existing location, while its
roofline will be modified to match the pitch of the roof of the house; and
   WHEREAS, the requested variation will not impair an adequate supply of light
and air because the garage will remain in its existing location along the
ravine, maintaining the existing distance between the garage and the residence
on the other side of the ravine; and
   WHEREAS, the requested variation will not increase the hazard from fire and
other dangers to the Subject Property as the proposed work will comply with all
applicable building and fire protection codes; and
   WHEREAS, the requested variation will not diminish the taxable value of land
and buildings throughout the Village, and the taxable value of the Subject
Property may be increased because of the proposed improvement to the Subject
Property; and
   WHEREAS, the proposed addition will not contribute to congestion on the
public streets, as the structure will continue to be used as a single family
residence; and
   WHEREAS, the proposed addition will not otherwise impair the public health,
safety, comfort morals, and welfare of the inhabitants of the Village.
   NOW, THEREFORE, the Council of the Village of Winnetka do ordain:
   SECTION 1: That the foregoing recitals are hereby incorporated as the
findings of the Council of the Village of Winnetka, as if fully set forth
herein.
   SECTION 2: That a variation is hereby granted with respect to the Subject
Property, commonly known as 955 Old Green Bay Road, which is located in the "A-
3" (One-Half Acre) Single-Family Residential District provided in the Winnetka
Zoning Ordinance, Chapter 22, Winnetka Village Code, from the rear yard setback
requirements of Section 22.07(j), to allow a rear yard setback of 13.26 feet
instead of the minimum required rear yard setback of 25 feet, resulting in a
variation of 11.74 feet (46.96%), for the purpose of constructing an addition
that will connect the existing detached garage to the single family home on the
Subject Property, in accordance with the application for variation and the
plans submitted with the application.
   SECTION 3: That the variation hereby granted is conditioned upon the
commencement of the proposed construction within 12 months after the effective
date of this Ordinance.
   SECTION 4: That this Ordinance shall be in full force and effect from and
after its passage, approval, and posting.
   Passed and approved this 18th day of August, 1998.
   AYES:   Trustees Lien, Meuer, Derning and President Holland
   NAYS:   None
   ABSENT:   Trustees Hilton, Lanphier and Duhl
               Signed:
               ss/Louise A. Holland
               Village President
Countersigned:
ss/Douglas G. Williams
Village Clerk
