ORDINANCE NO. M-535-98
AN ORDINANCE GRANTING A VARIATION IN THE APPLICATION OF THE ZONING ORDINANCE OF
THE VILLAGE OF WINNETKA COOK COUNTY, ILLINOIS (562-572 LINCOLN AVENUE)
   WHEREAS, there has been presented to the Council of the Village of Winnetka,
Cook County, Illinois, the request of the owners of the following parcels of
real estate (the “Subject Property”):
   Parcel 1:
   Lot 5 (except that part lying west of a line 50 feet northeasterly of and
parallel with easterly line of Chicago and Northwestern Railroad company right-
of-way) in Block 13 in Winnetka Park Bluffs, being a subdivision by William
Cairnduff of parts of Sections 16, 17 and 20, Township 42 North, Range 13, east
of the Third Principal Meridian, in Cook County, Illinois.
   Parcel 2:
   Lot 11 (except westerly 50 feet thereof) in Block 12 in Park Addition to
Winnetka Subdivision by William H. Cairnduff of part of Sections 16, 17 and 20
Township 42 North, Range 13, east of the Third Principal Meridian, in Cook
County, Illinois.
   Parcel 3:
   The south 5 feet of Lot 6 in Lewis D. Webster’s Resubdivision of Block 11
(except the north 75 feet thereof) and of Lots 6, 8, 9 and 10 in Block 12 in
Park Addition to Winnetka aforesaid, all in Cook County, Illinois;
commonly known as 562-572 Lincoln Avenue, Winnetka, Illinois, and located in
the "C-2" (General Retail) Commercial District provided in the Winnetka Zoning
Ordinance, Chapter 22, Winnetka Village Code, for a variation from the maximum
building height of 35 feet and 2 1/2 stories permitted by Section 22.11(c) of
the Winnetka Zoning Ordinance, to allow the construction on the Subject
Property of a 3-story building with a height of 35 feet; and
   WHEREAS, on July 13, 1998, on due notice thereof, the Zoning Board of
Appeals held a public hearing on the requested variation and by the affirmative
vote of four of the six members of the Board then present has reported to the
Council recommending that the requested variation from maximum building height
limitations be granted; and
   WHEREAS, on May 19, May 29 and August 13, 1998, on due notice thereof, the
Design Review Board considered the proposed building and has provided favorable
comment to the Council on the proposed building materials and the general
appearance of the building; and
   WHEREAS, there are practical difficulties and particular hardships
associated with carrying out the strict application of the Zoning Ordinance
with respect to the Subject Property in that the upper floor of the proposed
building is designed as and looks like a 2 ½ story building, and does not
exceed the lot coverage limitations for the upper floor, but is considered to
be a 3-story building because the area with a height of 7 feet or more is
greater than 50% of the area of the floor below; and
   WHEREAS, the Subject Property cannot yield a reasonable return if permitted
to be used only under the conditions allowed by the Zoning Ordinance, in
retaining the square footage and outside balconies and terraces are an
essential element of the building design and modifying the roof line to bring
the upper floor into conformity with the definition of half story, would
request in the loss of the balcony details, while increasing the visual bulk of
the building, which will negatively impact on the economics of the proposed
development of the Subject Property because the residential units will lose
value as the result of losing exterior living space; and
   WHEREAS, the requested variation will not alter the essential character of
the neighborhood, because the visual appearance of the proposed building is
consistent with the Zoning Ordinance’s height limitations of 35 feet and 2 ½
stories; and
   WHEREAS, the proposed building will not impair an adequate supply of light
and air because the upper floors are set back from the street and the actual
measured height of the proposed building will comply with the 35-foot maximum;
and
   WHEREAS, the requested variation will not increase the hazard from fire and
other dangers to the Subject Property as the proposed building will comply with
all applicable building and fire protection codes; and
   WHEREAS, the requested variation will not diminish the taxable value of land
and buildings throughout the Village, and the taxable value of the Subject
Property may be increased because the proposed building will replace an
existing, deteriorating commercial building with a new building that will
contain both residential and commercial units; and
   WHEREAS, the proposed building will not contribute to congestion on the
public streets, as the proposed building will provide more off-street parking
than is required by Village Code; and
   WHEREAS, there is no evidence that the proposed building will otherwise
impair the public health, safety, comfort, morals, and welfare of the
inhabitants of the Village; and
   NOW, THEREFORE, the Council of the Village of Winnetka do ordain:
   SECTION 1: That the foregoing recitals are hereby incorporated as the
findings of the Council of the Village of Winnetka, as if fully set forth
herein.
   SECTION 2: That a variation is hereby granted with respect to the Subject
Property, commonly known as 562-572 Lincoln Avenue, which is located in the "C-
2" (General Retail) Commercial District provided in the Winnetka Zoning
Ordinance, Chapter 22, Winnetka Village Code, for a variation from the building
height limitations of Section 22.11(c) of the Winnetka Zoning Ordinance to
allow the construction of a new, mixed use building at a height of 35 feet and
3 stories, all in accordance with the application for variation and the plans
submitted with the application.
   SECTION 3: That the variation hereby granted is conditioned upon the Village
Council’s adoption of Resolution R-1433-98 and the completion of the sale of
the property described therein, and upon commencement of the proposed
construction within 12 months after the effective date of this Ordinance.
   SECTION 4: That this Ordinance shall be in full force and effect from and
after its passage, approval, and posting.
   Passed and approved this 18th day of August, 1998.
   AYES:      Trustees Derning, Meuer, Lien and President Holland
   NAYS:   None
   ABSENT:   Trustees Duhl, Lanphier and Hilton
               Signed:
                  ss/Louise A. Holland
                  Village President
Countersigned:
ss/Douglas G. Williams
Village Clerk
