ORDINANCE NO. M-536-98
AN ORDINANCE GRANTING A SPECIAL USE PERMIT TO ALLOW EXPANSION OF THE CHRIST
CHURCH FACILITIES AT 784 SHERIDAN ROAD AND 739 HUMBOLDT AVENUE
   WHEREAS, the Rector, Churchwardens and Vestrymen of Christ Church, Winnetka,
an Illinois religious corporation is the owner of the following described real
estate:
Lot 1 & 2 in Christ’s Church Resubdivision, being a resubdivision of Block 42
in Garland’s Lake View subdivision of the southwest quarter of Section 17 and
the southeast quarter of Section 16, all in Township 42 North, Range 13 east of
the Third Principal Meridian; according to the plat thereof recorded July 13,
1857 as Document No. 88987 in Book No. 133 of Plats, Page No. 76 Therein – also
– all of Lot 1 and parts of Lots 5 and 7 in the subdivision of Blocks 26 and 41
in said Garland’s Lake View Subdivision; according to the Plat of said Christ’s
Church Resubdivision recorded July 25, 1980 as Document No. 25526668, all in
Cook County, Illinois;
which is commonly known as 784 Sheridan Road and 739 Humboldt Avenue, Winnetka,
Illinois (collectively referred to as the “Subject Property”), and which is
located in the "A-2" (One-Third Acre) Zoning District provided in Section 22.06
of the Winnetka Zoning Ordinance, Chapter 22 of the Winnetka Village Code; and,
   WHEREAS, the portion of the Subject Property at 784 Sheridan Road is
improved with a church building known as the “Church on the Hill”, driveways, a
cemetery, and other church-related uses; and
   WHEREAS, the portion of the Subject Property at 739 Humboldt Avenue is
improved with a single family residence known as the “Humboldt House,” a
detached garage and a swimming pool; and
   WHEREAS, the Church on the Hill has been in continuous operation as a church
since the 784 Sheridan Road location was acquired in 1869; and
   WHEREAS, the Humboldt House, which previously served as the Church rectory
up until the 1980’s, when it was subdivided and sold by the Church, was
reacquired by the Church in 1997; and
   WHEREAS, church buildings are permitted as special uses in the A-2 (One-
Third Acre) Single Family Residential District, subject to the conditions and
requirements pertaining to special uses, as set forth in Section 22.13 of the
Winnetka Zoning Ordinance; and,
   WHEREAS, the Christ Church has filed an application for a special use permit
under Section 22.13 of the Winnetka Zoning Ordinance, to permit the
construction of a one-story addition to be constructed on the northwest portion
of the church building and an additional two-story structure to connect the
church and the existing residence at 739 Humboldt, in accordance with the plans
accompanying the applications for special use permit; and
   WHEREAS, on June 18, 1998, the Design Review Board considered the proposed
improvements and has unanimously determined that a certificate of
appropriateness would issue for the proposed additions; and
   WHEREAS, pursuant to due notice thereof, the Plan Commission met on June 24,
1998, and voted unanimously that the Special Use Permit request is consistent
with the Comprehensive Plan and recommended that the special use permit be
granted; and
   WHEREAS, on July 16, 1998, on due notice thereof, the Zoning Board of
Appeals conducted a public hearing on the proposed special use and, by the
affirmative vote of the five members then present, has reported to the Village
Council, recommending that the special use permit be granted; and
   WHEREAS, the building additions are necessary for Christ Church to allow
church functions to expand into the existing residence and to increase the size
of the church facilities, which will enable it to consolidate its worship and
religious education programs at a single location, rather than dividing the
activities of its congregation between the Subject Property and its parish
house location at Maple and Elm Streets; and
WHEREAS, the special use, if granted, will not alter the essential character of
the locality, in that the Christ Church and the buildings on the Subject
Property are established uses and structures in the neighborhood and the
proposed additions represent a minimal increase to the existing buildings; and
   WHEREAS, the proposed additions will not be detrimental to or endanger the
public health, safety, comfort, morals and welfare of the inhabitants of the
Village, because Christ Church is an established use and because the
consolidation of the Church’s activities in a single location will enhance the
morals and general welfare of the Village; and
   WHEREAS, the proposed special use will not be substantially injurious to the
use and enjoyment of other property in the immediate vicinity, since the impact
of the additional cars from the consolidated services will be minimal; and
   WHEREAS, the Christ Church is an established element of the residential area
in which it is located and will not impede the orderly development or
improvement of other property in the immediate vicinity because both the Church
on the Hill and Humboldt House are existing structures for which only minor
additions are proposed; and
   WHEREAS, adequate parking facilities, utilities, access roads, drainage and
other facilities necessary for the operation of the special use exist or will
be provided; and
   WHEREAS, adequate measures have been or will be taken to provide ingress and
egress in a manner which minimizes pedestrian and vehicular traffic congestion
in the public ways; and
   WHEREAS, the special use, when constructed in accordance with the terms and
conditions of this ordinance, will conform to the applicable regulations of the
Zoning Ordinance and the Winnetka Village Code;
   NOW, THEREFORE, the Council of the Village of Winnetka do ordain:
   SECTION 1:   That the Village Council hereby adopts by reference the
foregoing recitals as its findings as if those recitals were fully set forth
herein.
   SECTION 2: That the special use permit in accordance with Section 22.13 of
the Winnetka Zoning Ordinance is hereby granted with respect to the Subject
Property, which is located in the "A-2" (One-Third) Acre Zoning District, and
which is commonly known as Christ Church, 784 Sheridan Road and Humboldt House,
739 Humboldt Avenue in accordance with the plans submitted with the
applications for special use permit to allow the construction of a one-story
addition at the northwest portion of the church building and the construction
of a two-story connection between the church and the residence, which will
consolidate the two buildings into a single structure, all subject to the
conditions and limitations hereinafter set forth, in order to consolidate
worship and other functions of the Church in a single location.
   SECTION 3: That the special use permit hereby granted is conditioned upon
the commencement of the proposed construction within twelve (12) months after
the effective date of this ordinance.
   SECTION 4: That this Ordinance shall be in full force and effect from and
after its passage, approval, and posting.
   Passed and approved this 18th day of August, 1998.
   AYES: Trustees Lien, Meuer, Derning and President Holland
   NAYS: None
   ABSENT:   Trustees Duhl, Lanphier and Hilton
               Signed:
               ss/Louise A. Holland
               Village President
