ORDINANCE NO. M-538-98
AN ORDINANCE AUTHORIZING THE LEASE OF MUNICIPAL PROPERTY TO THE HARRIS BANK
WINNETKA
WHEREAS, the Harris Bank Winnetka, a national banking corporation located at
520 Green Bay Road, Winnetka, Illinois (hereinafter referred to as “Harris
Bank”) has requested that the Village of Winnetka (hereinafter the “Village”)
renew its lease of a certain parcel of real estate, being a portion of Lots 9
and 10 in Wilson and Dale’s Subdivision of the north one half of Block 26 in
Winnetka, as more fully described in the form of a lease attached to this
ordinance as Exhibit A and shown in the plat of leasehold attached thereto
(hereinafter the “Leasehold”); and
WHEREAS, the Leasehold is owned by the Village and has been leased to the
Harris Bank and its predecessor since 1968 for use by the Harris Bank as an
additional driveway area for expanded drive-in banking facilities; and
WHEREAS, it is in the interest of the public safety and welfare to renew the
lease of the Subject Property which assists traffic flow and allows a more
gradual turning radius for vehicles entering the drive-in banking facilities
from the immediately adjoining alley; and
WHEREAS, the Village is authorized by Sections 11-75-1 through 11-75-5 of the
Illinois Municipal Code, 65 ILCS 5/11-75-1 through 5/11-75-5, to lease
municipal property above and around municipally owned buildings for a term not
to exceed 99 years; and
WHEREAS, the Council of the Village of Winnetka have determined that $10,000.00
paid in ten equal annual installments is reasonable compensation for the
requested Leasehold.
NOW, THEREFORE, the Council of the Village of Winnetka do ordain as follows:
SECTION 1: the Village Council hereby adopts by reference the foregoing
recitals as its findings of fact, as if those recitals were fully set forth
herein.
   SECTION 2: The lease agreement by and between the Village of Winnetka and
the Harris Bank Winnetka is hereby approved, in substantially the form attached
hereto as Exhibit A.
   SECTION 3: The Village President and Village Clerk are hereby authorized and
directed to execute and seal, on behalf of the Village, the lease agreement
substantially in the form attached hereto as Exhibit A.
   SECTION 4: That the Village President and Village Clerk are hereby
authorized to take such other and further steps as may be necessary to
effectuate the lease agreement, including the recording of the lease with the
Cook County Recorder of Deeds in the manner provided by statute.
   SECTION 4: This Ordinance shall be in full force and effect from and after
its passage, approval and posting as required by law.
   ADOPTED this 6th day of October, 1998, pursuant to the following roll call
vote:
   AYES: Trustees Derning, Lanphier, Meuer, Hilton, Lien
   NAYS: None
   ABSENT: Trustee Duhl
   APPROVED this 6th day of October, 1998.
               Signed:
               ss/Louise A. Holland
               Village President
Countersigned:
ss/Douglas G. Williams
Village Clerk
Introduced: September 1, 1998
Posted: September 2, 1998
Passed and Approved: October 6, 1998
Posted: October 7, 1998
EXHIBIT A
LEASE
   THIS LEASE, executed in duplicate this _________ day of ________________,
1998, by and between the Village of Winnetka, Cook County, Illinois
(hereinafter sometimes referred to as “Lessor”) and The Harris Bank Winnetka, a
national banking corporation, of Winnetka, Illinois (hereinafter sometimes
referred to as “Lessee”);
WITNESSETH:
   1.   Lessor hereby leases to Lessee, and Lessee hereby leases from Lessor,
the following described real estate in the Village of Winnetka, County of Cook,
State of Illinois:
That portion of Lots 9 and 10 in WILSON AND DALE’S SUBDIVISION of the North ½
of Block 26 of “Winnetka”, in the Northeast ¼ of the Northeast ¼ of Section 20,
Township 42 North, Range 13 East of the Third Principal Meridian, described as
follows: Beginning at the Northwest corner of said Lot 9; thence East along the
North line of said Lot 9 a distance of 12.50 feet; thence South along a line
parallel to the West line of aforesaid Lots 9 and 10 a distance of 10.0 feet;
thence Southwesterly to a point on the aforesaid West line of said Lot 10,
being 40.0 feet South of the aforesaid Northwest corner of Lot 9; thence North
along said West line of Lots 9 and 10 a distance of 40.0 feet to the place of
beginning, in the Village of Winnetka, Cook County, Illinois,
said real estate being indicated by the shaded area on the Plat of Leasehold
attached hereto as Exhibit 1.
   2.   The term of this lease (the “Lease Term”) shall be for ten years,
commencing on the 1st day of August, 1998, and ending on the last day of July,
2008.
   3.   Lessee agrees to pay a rental of Ten Thousand Dollars ($10,000.00) for
the Lease Term, payable in annual installments of One Thousand Dollars
($1,000.00) in advance on the first day of each lease year.
   4.   Lessee shall have the right to remove existing curbs and pavement on
the leased premises as necessary and to construct new curbs and pavement as
appropriate, at Lessee’s expense, subject to prior approval of plans or
specifications therefor by the Director of Public Works of the Village. No
building shall be erected upon or extended upon the leased premises.
   5.   Use of the premises by Lessee shall be limited to the purpose of
providing driveway access to and from Lessee’s drive-in banking facilities.
Lessee shall not prohibit or restrict the passage of pedestrians over the
leased premises, except at the direction or request of the Lessor.
   6.   Lessee will erect or provide, at its expense, such pedestrian and
vehicular traffic signs, consistent with reasonable driveway use, as may from
time to time be requested by the Director of Public Works.
   7.   Lessee’s lease shall be subject to an easement for any underground
municipal or public utilities which the Lessor determines to be necessary or
desirable.
   8.   Lessee hereby agrees to indemnify and hold Lessor harmless, to the
fullest extent permitted by law, from any and all losses, claims, demands,
suits or actions by any persons, including the agents and servants of Lessee,
arising from or in connection with the conduct, condition, or management of the
leased premises, arising from any work or thing done in or about the leased
premises by Lessee or its agents or servants, or arising from any act or
negligence of Lessee or its agents, servants, patrons or customers, during the
term of this Lease. The obligation to indemnify the Lessor shall extend to
attorneys fees incurred by Lessor in defending against any of such losses,
claims, demands, suits or actions.
   9.   If Lessee defaults in the performance of any of its obligations under
this Lease, if Lessee otherwise breaches this Lease agreement, or if Lessee
abandons or vacates the leased premises during the term of this lease, and if
the default or breach continues for thirty (30) days after written notice from
Lessor to Lessee specifying the default or breach, then Lessor may, at its
option, terminate this lease and the term hereby created, in which case Lessor
may forthwith repossess the leased premises.
   10.   On expiration of this lease, or upon termination thereof pursuant to
the provisions of paragraph 9, Lessee shall, on demand by Lessor, restore the
leased premises to the condition thereof existing at the commencement of the
lease term.
   11.   Lessor, by the making of this lease, shall not forfeit and does retain
any right Lessor would otherwise have to condemn the Lessee’s interest in the
leased premises by proceeding under “An Act to provide for the exercise of the
right of eminent domain,” approved April 10, 1872, as heretofore and hereafter
amended.
   12.   Lessee shall not assign this Lease or sublet the leased premises or
any part thereof; provided that this Lease may be assigned to any parent,
subsidiary, corporate affiliate or corporate successor of the Lessee hereunder.
