ORDINANCE NO. M-539-98
AN ORDINANCE GRANTING A VARIATION IN THE APPLICATION OF THE ZONING ORDINANCE OF
THE VILLAGE OF WINNETKA COOK COUNTY, ILLINOIS (159 SHERIDAN ROAD)
   WHEREAS, there has been presented to the Council of the Village of Winnetka,
Cook County, Illinois, the request of the owners of the following described
real estate (the “Subject Property”):
All that part of Lot 4 lying northerly of a straight line drawn from a point in
the easterly line of Sheridan Road located 50 feet northwesterly (measured
along said easterly line) from the southwesterly corner of said Lot 4 to the
water’s edge of Lake Michigan and passing through a point equi-distant from and
in the same straight line with a point in the southerly line of said Lot 4
located 468.4 feet easterly from the easterly line of Sheridan Road (measured
along said southerly line) and a point in the northerly line of said Lot 4
located 456.8 feet easterly from the easterly line of said Sheridan Road
(measured along said northerly line) and all that part of Lot 5 lying southerly
of a straight line drawn from a point in the easterly line of Sheridan Road
located 50 feet northwesterly (measured along said easterly line) from the
southwesterly corner of said Lot 5 to the water’s edge of Lake Michigan and
passing through a point equi-distance from and in the same straight line with a
point in the southerly line of said Lot 5 located 456.8 feet easterly from the
easterly line of Sheridan Road (measured along said southerly line) and a point
in the northerly line of said Lot 5 located 445.3 feet easterly from the
easterly of said Sheridan Road (measured along said northerly line) said Lots 4
and 5 being R. Williamson’s Sheridan Road Subdivision of parts of Lots 2,3,4 of
Simons and others Subdivision of a part of the fractional southeast quarter of
Section 21 and part of the fractional southwest quarter of Section 22, Township
42 North, Range 13, East of the Third Principal Meridian, as shown by plat of
said R. Williamson’s Sheridan Road Subdivision recorded in Recorder’s Office
Cook County, Illinois April 8, 1920 as Document 6786370, together with all
riparian rights belonging or pertaining to the premises aforesaid in Cook
County, Illinois;
commonly known as 159 Sheridan Road, Winnetka, Illinois, and located in the "A-
3" (One-Half Acre) Single-Family District provided in the Winnetka Zoning
Ordinance, Chapter 22, Winnetka Village Code, for a variation from the 50-foot
front setback provisions of Section 22.07(h) of the Winnetka Zoning Ordinance,
as applied to the east front yard of the subject property abutting Lake
Michigan, to allow the construction of a boathouse with a front setback of 27
feet, resulting in a variation of 23 feet (46%), the construction of a deck
with a front setback of 14 feet, resulting in a variation of 36 feet (72%), and
the construction of a boat ramp to the water’s edge, resulting in no front
setback and a variation of 50 feet (100%); and
   WHEREAS, there are practical difficulties associated with carrying out the
strict application of the Zoning Ordinance with respect to the Subject Property
in that: a) the subject property is a riparian lot having its eastern boundary
on the shore of Lake Michigan; b) a boathouse, deck and ramp at the water’s
edge is a reasonable accessory use for the Subject Property; and c) observing
the full 50-foot front yard setback for the uses requested would place the
boathouse, deck and ramp at the top of the bluff, which would impede access to
the water, increase operational and safety difficulties, and impose the risk of
damage and loss of stability to the bluff; and
   WHEREAS, there are unique circumstances due to the slope and characteristics
of the lake bluff at the Subject Property, which impact on engineering and
design considerations in order to provide a structure that is reasonably
accessible to the water’s edge, while being relatively protected against wave
and storm damage, and while maintaining and protecting the structural integrity
of the bluff; and
   WHEREAS, the proposed variation will neither impair the essential character
of the locality nor impair an adequate supply of light and air, because the
proposed location is below the top of the bluff, making it less visible than if
it were located on the top of the bluff in a permitted location; and
   WHEREAS, the proposed construction of the boathouse, deck and boat ramp will
not increase the hazard from fire and other damage to the Subject Property,
because it will comply with all applicable building codes; and
   WHEREAS, the proposed variation will not increase congestion on the public
streets, as the proposed boathouse, deck and boat ramp are intended to provide
private access to the lake; and
   WHEREAS, there is no evidence that the proposed variation will otherwise
impair the public health, safety, comfort, morals, and welfare of the
inhabitants of the Village; and
   WHEREAS, the proposed construction of the boathouse, deck and boat ramp will
not diminish the taxable value of land and buildings throughout the Village
because they will be improvements to the Subject Property and are therefore
likely to increase the taxable value of the Subject Property without negatively
impacting on other properties in the immediate vicinity; and
   WHEREAS, on August 17, 1998, on due notice thereof, the Zoning Board of
Appeals conducted a public hearing on said requested variation and, on the
unanimous vote of the six members then present, has reported to the Council
recommending that the requested variations be granted.
   NOW, THEREFORE, the Council of the Village of Winnetka do ordain:
   SECTION 1: That the foregoing recitals are hereby incorporated as the
findings of the Council of the Village of Winnetka, as if fully set forth
herein.
   SECTION 2: That a variation is hereby granted with respect to the Subject
Property, which is commonly known as 159 Sheridan Road and is located in the
"A-3" (One-Half Acre) Single-Family Residential District provided in said
Zoning Ordinance, for variations from the 50-foot front setback provisions of
Section 22.07(h) of the Winnetka Zoning Ordinance, as applied to the east front
yard of the subject property abutting Lake Michigan, to allow the construction
of a boathouse with a front setback of 27 feet, resulting in a variation of 23
feet (46%), the construction of a deck with a front setback of 14 feet,
resulting in a variation of 36 feet (72%), and the construction of a boat ramp
to the water’s edge, resulting in no front setback and a variation of 50 feet
(100%), all in accordance with the application and plans submitted with the
application for said variations.
   SECTION 3: That the variation hereby granted is further conditioned upon the
the owners’ obtaining required permits from the U.S. Army Corps of Engineers,
the U.S. Fish and Wildlife Service, the Illinois Environmental Protection
Agency, the Illinois Department of Conservation’s Division of Water Resources,
and the Illinois Historic Preservation Agency and the commencement of the
proposed construction within 24 months after the effective date of this
Ordinance.
   SECTION 4: That this Ordinance shall be in full force and effect from and
after its passage, approval, and posting.
   ADOPTED this 6th day of October, 1998, pursuant to the following roll call
vote:
   AYES:      Trustees Derning, Lanphier, Meuer, Hilton, Lien
   NAYES:   None
   ABSENT:   Trustee Duhl
   APPROVED this 6th day of October, 1998.
   Signed
   ss/Louise A. Holland
   Village President
Countersigned:
ss/Douglas G. Williams
Village Clerk
Introduced:   September 15, 1998
Posted:   September 16, 1998
Passed and Approved: October 6, 1998
Posted:   October 7, 1998
ORDINANCE NO. M-540-98
AN ORDINANCE GRANTING A VARIATION IN THE APPLICATION OF THE ZONING ORDINANCE OF
THE VILLAGE OF WINNETKA COOK COUNTY, ILLINOIS (656 ARDSLEY ROAD)
   WHEREAS, there has been presented to the Council of the Village of Winnetka,
Cook County, Illinois, the request of the owners of the following described
real estate (the “Subject Property”):
Lot 1 in Gorham’s Subdivision of Lot 11 (except the north 7.50 feet thereof
west of easement) in Skokie View, a subdivision of that part of the southeast ¼
of the southwest ¼, lying west of and adjoining the center line of Rosewood
Avenue, and the east 15 acres of the southwest ¼ of the southwest ¼ of Section
17, Township 42 North, Range 13 East of the Third Principal Meridian, in Cook
County, Illinois;
commonly known as 656 Ardsley Road, Winnetka, Illinois, and located in the "A-
3" (One-Half Acre) Single-Family District provided in the Winnetka Zoning
Ordinance, Chapter 22, Winnetka Village Code, for a variation from the front
setback provisions of Section 22.07(h) of the Winnetka Zoning Ordinance, from
29.6 feet to 0 feet in the north front yard setback, resulting in a variation
of 29.6 feet (100%), and from 50 feet to 10 feet in the front yard (through-
lot) setback, resulting in a variation of 40 feet (80%), to permit structural
alterations to window openings in the legal nonconforming room addition that is
located in the required front yard setbacks; and
   WHEREAS, there are unique circumstances and practical difficulties
associated with carrying out the strict application of the Zoning Ordinance
with respect to these premises in that: a) the Subject Property is an
irregularly shaped, trapezoidal, corner lot, which has three street frontages
and requires 50-foot setbacks along the Ardsley Road frontage and 29.6 foot
setbacks along the Pelham Road frontages; b) the house on the Subject Property
was built in 1920; and c) the one-story addition that is the subject of the
requested variations was constructed in 1936, pursuant to a variation from the
front setback requirements; and
   WHEREAS, the proposed variation will neither impair the essential character
of the locality nor impair an adequate supply of light and air, because the
proposed variation which is for window alterations will add new windows on the
north and northwest sides of the existing addition, and will replace windows on
the south and southwest sides of the addition; and
   WHEREAS, the proposed alteration to the window openings will not increase
the hazard from fire and other damage to the Subject Property, because it will
comply with all applicable building and fire protection codes; and
   WHEREAS, the proposed variation will not increase congestion on the public
streets, as the size of the building will not be changed by the variations and
the building will continue to be used as a single family residence; and
   WHEREAS, the proposed variation will not otherwise impair the public health,
safety, comfort, morals, and welfare of the inhabitants of the Village; and
   WHEREAS, the proposed window alterations will not diminish the taxable value
of land and buildings throughout the Village because they will be improvements
to the Subject Property and are therefore likely to increase the taxable value
of the Subject Property without negatively impacting on other properties in the
immediate vicinity; and
   WHEREAS, on August 17, 1998, on due notice thereof, the Zoning Board of
Appeals conducted a public hearing on said requested variation and, on the
unanimous vote of the six members then present, has reported to the Council
recommending that the requested variations be granted.
   NOW, THEREFORE, the Council of the Village of Winnetka do ordain:
   SECTION 1: That the foregoing recitals are hereby incorporated as the
findings of the Council of the Village of Winnetka, as if fully set forth
herein.
   SECTION 2: That a variation is hereby granted with respect to the Subject
Property, which is commonly known as 656 Ardsley Road and is located in the "A-
3" (One-Half Acre) Single-Family Residential District provided in said Zoning
Ordinance, for a variation from the front setback provisions of Section 22.07
(h) of the Winnetka Zoning Ordinance, Chapter 22, Winnetka Village Code, from
29.6 feet to 0 feet in the north front yard setback, resulting in a variation
of 29.6 feet (100%), and from 50 feet to 10 feet in the front yard (through-
lot) setback, resulting in a variation of 40 feet (80%), to permit structural
alterations to window openings in the legal nonconforming room addition that is
located in the required front yard setbacks, all in accordance with the
application and plans submitted with the application for said variation.
   SECTION 3: That the variation hereby granted is further conditioned upon the
commencement of the proposed construction within 12 months after the effective
date of this Ordinance.
   SECTION 4: That this Ordinance shall be in full force and effect from and
after its passage, approval, and posting.
   ADOPTED this 6th day of October, 1998, pursuant to the following roll call
vote:
   AYES:      Trustees Derning, Lanphier, Meuer, Hilton and Lien
   NAYES:   None
   ABSENT:   Trustee Duhl
   APPROVED this 6th day of October, 1998.
   Signed
   ss/Louise A. Holland
   Village President
Countersigned:
Douglas G. Williams
Village Clerk
Introduced:   September 15, 1998
Posted:   September 16, 1998
Passed and Approved: October 6, 1998
