ORDINANCE NO. M-541-98
AN ORDINANCE PROVIDING FOR THE MAKING OF A LOCAL IMPROVEMENT IN AND FOR THE
VILLAGE OF WINNETKA, COOK COUNTY, ILLINOIS, FOR THE CONSTRUCTION OF A STORM
DRAIN AND THE REPAVING OF THE PUBLIC ALLEY BETWEEN ASH AND CHERRY STREETS FROM
LOCUST TO ROSEWOOD STREETS
   WHEREAS, the owners of more than 50% of the property located on the south
side of Ash Street and the north side of Cherry Street between Locust Street
and Rosewood Street in the Village of Winnetka have submitted a petition
requesting that the public alley bounded by said streets be paved and that
storm sewers be installed in said alley; and
   WHEREAS, on July 7, 1998, the Board of Local Improvements adopted Resolution
No. SA-1-98, describing the proposed improvements, setting out the engineer’s
certified estimate of costs, and setting a public hearing on the proposed
improvements for July 21, 1998; and
   WHEREAS,    on July 21, 1998, pursuant to notice as required by statute, the
Board of Local Improvements held a public hearing on the proposed improvements,
at which time no persons stepped forward to object to the proposed
improvements; and
   WHEREAS, upon concluding the hearing, the Board of Local Improvements
determined that the proposed improvements should proceed, as described in the
Contract Plans admitted into the record as Exhibit 4, and that there should be
no change in either the scope or the estimate cost of the proposed
improvements.
NOW, THEREFORE, the Council of the Village of Winnetka do ordain as follows:
   SECTION 1 : That the Council of the Village of Winnetka hereby adopts the
foregoing recitals as its findings of fact as if fully set forth herein.
   SECTION 2 : That a local improvement (the “Improvement”) shall be made in
the Village of Winnetka, Cook County, Illinois, the nature, character, locality
and description of which improvement is as follows:
The paving of the center 12 feet of the public alley right-of-way in Block 9 of
Groveland Addition to Winnetka in Section 20, Township 42, Range 13, East of
the Third Principal Meridian, in the Village of Winnetka, County of Cook,
Illinois, more commonly referred to as the public alley between Ash Street and
Cherry Street, said paving to be from the west curb line of the Locust Street
right-of-way to the east curb line of the Rosewood Street right-of-way, and to
consist of the excavation of the existing gravel alley, the installation of a
corrugated metal storm sewer, the regrading of the alley and the installation
of a new, 5-inch compacted stone sub-base and a 12-foot wide, 7-inch thick
Portland cement concrete alley pavement surface, plus site restoration.
   SECTION 3: That the recommendation of the Board of Local Improvements of the
Village of Winnetka, Cook County, Illinois, providing for the Improvement, the
estimate of the cost thereof and the plans therefor, all attached hereto and
incorporated herein by reference, be and the same are hereby approved.
   SECTION 4: That said improvement shall be made and the cost thereof which is
estimated to be $43,389.00, shall be paid for by special assessment in
accordance with Article 9, Division 2, of the Illinois Municipal Code (65 ILCS
5/9-2-1, et seq.), and an amount not exceeding $5,208.00 is hereby provided for
to apply towards the payment of all lawful costs and expenses incurred in
making, levying and collecting the assessment for said improvement and the cost
of providing funds for deficiency of interest
   SECTION 5 : That the aggregate amount herein ordered to be assessed and each
individual assessment shall be divided into annual installments which shall
bear interest at the rate of no more than seven percent (7%) per annum until
paid, all in the manner and in accordance with the provisions of the aforesaid
Article 9, Division 2, of the Illinois Municipal Code.
   SECTION 6 : That for the purpose of anticipating the collection of the
second and succeeding installments of said assessment for said improvement,
bonds are hereby authorized to be issued for a term of no more than six years,
the bonds to be payable out of said installments, bearing interest at the rate
of no more than seven percent (7%) per annum, payable annually, and signed by
the Village President and attested by the Village Clerk, under the corporate
seal of the Village. The bonds shall be issued in accordance with and shall in
all respects conform to the provisions of the aforesaid Article 9, Division 2,
of the Illinois Municipal Code.
   SECTION 7 : That Douglas G. Williams, Village Manager of the Village of
Winnetka, Illinois, is hereby designated as the person to file a petition in
the Circuit Court of Cook County, Illinois, as provided by law in the name of
the Village, praying that steps may be taken to ascertain what property will be
benefited by said improvements and the amount of such benefit, the just
compensation to be paid for the taking of such property, and also that steps be
taken to levy a special assessment for said improvement in accordance with the
provisions of this ordinance and in the manner prescribed by law.
   SECTION 8: This Ordinance shall take effect immediately upon passage,
approval and posting.
   ADOPTED this 17th day of November, 1998, pursuant to the following roll call
vote:
   AYES: Trustees Derning, Lanphier, Meuer, Hilton, Lien         
   NAYS: None                           
   ABSENT: Trustee Duhl                     
   APPROVED this 17th day of November, 1998.
               Signed:
               ss/Louise A. Holland
               Village President
Countersigned:
Douglas G. Williams
Village Clerk
Introduced: September 15, 1998            
Posted: September 16, 1998               
Passed and Approved: November 17, 1998         
Posted: November 18, 1998                
ORDINANCE NO. M-542-98
AN ORDINANCE GRANTING A VARIATION IN THE APPLICATION OF THE ZONING ORDINANCE OF
THE VILLAGE OF WINNETKA COOK COUNTY, ILLINOIS (512 ORCHARD)
   WHEREAS, there has been presented to the Council of the Village of Winnetka,
Cook County, Illinois, the request of the owners of the following described
real estate (the “Subject Property”):
   The east 47.00 feet of the west 93.00 feet of the northeast 1/4 of block 14
(except so much thereof as falls in the street on the north side thereof) in
Garlands Addition to Winnetka in the Southwest 1/4 Section, Township 42 North,
Range 13 East of the Third Principal Meridian, in Cook County, Illinois,
commonly known as 512 Orchard, Winnetka, Illinois, and located in the "A-1"
(One-Sixth Acre) Single-Family Residential District provided in the Winnetka
Zoning Ordinance, Chapter 22, Winnetka Village Code, for variations from
Sections 22.05(c), 22.05(f) and 22.05(g) of the Winnetka Zoning Ordinance, to
allow the replacement of an existing two-car garage with a new garage having
the footprint, which would result in: (a) a building height of 14.25 feet
rather than the 14.0 feet permitted by Section 22.05(c) of the Zoning
Ordinance, representing a variation of .25 feet (1.79%); (b) a total roofed lot
coverage of 2,082.07 square feet rather than the maximum of 1,942.63 square
feet permitted by Section 22.05(f) of the Zoning Ordinance, representing a
variation of 139.44 square feet (7.18%); (c) total impermeable surfaces of
4,300.93 square feet rather than the maximum of 3,885.26 square feet permitted
by Section 22.05(f) of the Zoning Ordinance, representing a variation of 415.67
square feet (10.7%); and (d) a maximum building size (gross floor area) of
3,451.87 square feet rather than the maximum of 3,108.20 square feet permitted
by Section 22.05(g) of the Zoning Ordinance, representing a variation of 343.67
square feet (11.06%); and
   WHEREAS, on August 17, 1998, on due notice thereof, the Zoning Board of
Appeals conducted a public hearing on the requested variations and has reported
to the Council recommending that the requested variations be granted, with four
of the six members then present voting in favor of the variations requested for
building height and building size and all six members then present voting in
favor of the variations requested for roofed lot coverage and total impermeable
surface; and
   WHEREAS, the owners have modified their plans to reduce the building height
so that it will conform with the limits of Section 22.05(c) of the Zoning
Ordinance, and so that the attic space in the garage does not contribute to
gross floor area; and
   WHEREAS, there are practical difficulties and unique hardships associated
with carrying out the strict application of the Zoning Ordinance with respect
to the Subject Property in that (a) the application is for the purpose of
allowing the replacement of a dilapidated garage with a new garage that will
also mirror the style of the residence on the Subject Property; (b) the
existing legally nonconforming roofed lot coverage and gross floor area on the
Subject Property will be increased by only 12.8 square feet; and (c) the
proposed new construction will improve the appearance of the Subject Property
and neighborhood while reducing the degree of nonconforming impermeable surface
by 237.20 square feet; and
WHEREAS, the Subject Property cannot yield a reasonable return if permitted to
be used only under the conditions allowed by the Zoning Ordinance, in that if
the variations are not granted, the owners will be required either to continue
to use a dilapidated garage or to remove the garage altogether; and
WHEREAS, the requested variation will not alter the essential character of the
neighborhood because the proposed garage will replace an existing garage in
poor condition with one that is designed to be more consistent with the design
of the residence on the Subject Property; and
   WHEREAS, the requested variations will not impair an adequate supply of
light and air because the increase in building area is minimal and building
height is within the limits established by the Zoning Ordinance; and
   WHEREAS, the requested variations will not increase the hazard from fire and
other dangers to the Subject Property, as it will comply with all applicable
building and fire protection codes; and
   WHEREAS, the requested variations will not diminish the taxable value of
land and buildings throughout the Village, and the taxable value of the Subject
Property may be increased because of the proposed improvements; and
   WHEREAS, the proposed new garage will not contribute to congestion on the
public streets, as the Subject Property will continue to be used for single
family occupancy and the proposed structure will not have a greater vehicular
capacity than the one it will replace; and
   WHEREAS, there is no evidence that the proposed construction of the detached
two-car garage will otherwise impair the public health, safety, comfort,
morals, and welfare of the inhabitants of the Village.
NOW, THEREFORE, the Council of the Village of Winnetka do ordain as follows:
SECTION 1 : That the foregoing recitals are hereby incorporated as the findings
of the Council of the Village of Winnetka, as if fully set forth herein.
   SECTION 2: That a variation is hereby granted with respect to the Subject
Property, commonly known as 512 Orchard, which is located in the "A-1" (One-
Sixth Acre) Single-Family Residential District provided in the Winnetka Zoning
Ordinance, Chapter 22, Winnetka Village Code, for the following variations: (a)
from the maximum building size (Gross Floor Area) limitations of Section 22.05
(g), to allow a gross floor area of 3,273.42 square feet, a variation of 165.22
square feet (5.32%) over the 3,108.20 square foot permitted maximum; (b) from
the intensity of use of lot limitations of Section 22.05(f), to allow a roofed
lot coverage of 2,082.07 square feet, a variation of 139.44 square feet (7.18%)
over the 1,942.63 square foot permitted maximum; and (c) to allow an
impermeable surface coverage of 4,050.93 square feet, a variation of 165.67
square feet (or 4.26%) over the 3,885.26 square foot permitted maximum, all for
the purpose of constructing a detached two-car garage on the Subject Property,
in accordance with the application for variation and plans submitted with the
application, as revised to reflect a conforming building height and no gross
floor area in the attic.
   SECTION 3: That the variation hereby granted is conditioned upon the
commencement of the proposed construction within 12 months after the effective
date of this Ordinance.
SECTION 4: This Ordinance shall take effect immediately upon passage, approval
and posting.
   ADOPTED this 5th day of November, 1998, pursuant to the following roll call
vote:
   AYES: Trustees Derning, Lanphier, Duhl, Meuer and Hilton
   NAYS: None
   ABSENT: Trustee Hilton
   APPROVED this 5th day of November, 1998.
               Signed:
               ss/Louise A. Holland
               Village President
Countersigned:
Douglas G. Williams
Village Clerk
Introduced: October 6, 1998
Posted: October 7, 1998
Passed and Approved: November 5, 1998
Posted: November 6, 1998
ORDINANCE NO. M-543-98
AN ORDINANCE GRANTING A VARIATION IN THE APPLICATION OF THE ZONING ORDINANCE OF
THE VILLAGE OF WINNETKA COOK COUNTY, ILLINOIS (1175 WHITEBRIDGE HILL ROAD)
   WHEREAS, there has been presented to the Council of the Village of Winnetka,
Cook County, Illinois, the request of the owners of the following described
real estate (the “Subject Property”):
   Lot 1 in Lakeside Subdivision of that part of the Southeast fractional
quarter of fractional Section B, Township 42 North, Range 13, East of the Third
Principal Meridian, lying Easterly and southerly of the following described
lines. Beginning at the stone of the Southwest corner of the Southeast quarter
of said Section 8, and running thence Northerly along the North-South quarter
Section line of said Section 8, 271.26 feet, thence North 77 degrees 52 minutes
East, 77.86 feet, thence North 16 degrees 02 minutes West, 14.98 feet, thence
North 60 degrees 23 minutes East 142.0 feet, thence Northerly along a curved
line (said line being concave to the East and having a radius of 105.0 feet)
45.92 feet, thence North 60 degrees 23 minutes East, 480.0 feet, more or less
to the Shore line of Lake Michigan, (except that part lying South and East of
the following described lines. Beginning at a point in the South line of said
Section, 369.14 feet East of the Southwest corner of said fractional quarter of
said Section 8, thence Northeasterly, 75.06 feet to a point which is 395.38
feet East of the West line and 70.32 feet North of the South line, measured at
right angles thereto of said fractional quarter of said Section 8, thence
Northeasterly 204.37 feet to a point which is 655.52 feet East of the West line
and 308.71 feet North of the South line, measured at right angles thereto, of
said fractional quarter of said Section 8, thence Northeasterly along a line
deflecting to the North from said last described line 1 degree 06 minutes, a
distance of 177.0 feet, more or less, to the Shore line of Lake Michigan).
   Also part of the Northeast fractional quarter of Section 17, Township 42
North, Range 13, East of the Third Principal Meridian, lying Northerly of the
Northerly and Easterly line of Sheridan Road, and Westerly of a line drawn from
a beginning point in the North line of said Section, which is 369.14 feet East
of the Northwest corner of said fractional quarter of said Section 17, to a
point in the Northeasterly line of Sheridan Road, which is 332.38 feet East of
the West line and 988.51 feet South of the North line, measured at right angles
thereto, of said fractional quarter of said Section 17, all in Cook County,
Illinois.
commonly known as 1175 Whitebridge Hill Road, Winnetka, Illinois, and located
in the A-3 (One-Half Acre) Single-Family Residential District provided in the
Winnetka Zoning Ordinance, Chapter 22, Winnetka Village Code, for a variation
from the front (corner) yard setback requirements of Section 22.07(h) of the
Zoning Ordinance, to allow a front (corner) yard setback of 34.73 feet from the
south property line, whereas a setback of 50.0 feet is required, resulting in a
variation of 15.27 feet (30.54%), in order to permit the removal and
reconstruction of the roof of an existing attached garage on the south side of
the house on the Subject Property; and
   WHEREAS, on September 14, 1998, on due notice thereof, the Zoning Board of
Appeals conducted a public hearing on the requested variation and by the
unanimous vote of the six members then present, has reported to the Council
recommending that the requested variation be granted; and
   WHEREAS, there are practical difficulties and unique hardships associated
with carrying out the strict application of the Zoning Ordinance with respect
to the Subject Property in that (a) the Subject Property has two street
frontages in addition to having Lake Michigan at its east property line; (b)
the garage is in a legally nonconforming location and was originally
constructed 50 to 60 years ago at the side of the house; (c) the garage is
located in the basement of the structure and includes a terrace on the roof
level which connects to a terrace at the rear of the house; and (d) the repairs
are necessary to correct water damages discovered in the course of repairing
the home following a fire in August 1997; and
   WHEREAS, the Subject Property cannot yield a reasonable return if permitted
to be used only under the conditions allowed by the Zoning Ordinance, in that
denying the variation would prohibit the owners from protecting their residence
and garage from water damage which has caused structural deterioration; and
   WHEREAS, the requested variation will not alter the essential character of
the neighborhood because the exterior of the garage will be unchanged, with the
original railings, stone coping, and terrace surface being returned to their
original locations; and
   WHEREAS, the requested variation will not impair an adequate supply of light
and air because the exterior dimensions of the existing structures will not
change; and
   WHEREAS, the requested variation will not increase the hazard from fire and
other dangers to the Subject Property as it will comply with all applicable
building and fire protection codes; and
   WHEREAS, the requested variation will not diminish the taxable value of land
and buildings throughout the Village, and the taxable value of the Subject
Property may be increased because of the proposed improvements; and
   WHEREAS, the removal and reconstruction of the existing garage roof will not
contribute to congestion on the public streets; and
WHEREAS, there is no evidence that the proposed construction will otherwise
impair the public health, safety, comfort, morals, and welfare of the
inhabitants of the Village.
NOW, THEREFORE, the Council of the Village of Winnetka do ordain as follows:
SECTION 1 : That the foregoing recitals are hereby incorporated as the findings
of the Council of the Village of Winnetka, as if fully set forth herein.
   SECTION 2: That a variation is hereby granted with respect to the Subject
Property, commonly known as 1175 Whitebridge Hill Road, which is located in the
“A-3” (One-Half Acre) Single Family Residential District provided in the
Winnetka Zoning Ordinance, Chapter 22, Winnetka Village Code, for a variation
from the front (corner) setback requirements of Section 22.07(h) of the Zoning
Ordinance, to allow a front (corner) setback of 34.73 feet from the south lot
line, whereas a setback of 50.00 feet is required, resulting in a variation of
15.27 feet (30.54%), in order to permit the removal and reconstruction of the
roof of an existing attached garage, in accordance with the application for
variation and plans submitted with the application.
   SECTION 3: That the variation hereby granted is conditioned upon the
commencement of the proposed constructing within 12 months after the effective
date of this Ordinance.
SECTION 4: This Ordinance shall take effect immediately upon passage, approval
and posting.
   ADOPTED this 20th day of October, 1998, pursuant to the following roll call
vote:
   AYES: Trustees Derning, Duhl, Hilton, Lanphier, Lien and Meuer
   NAYS: None
   ABSENT: None
   APPROVED this 20th day of October, 1998.
   Signed:
   ss/Louise A. Holland
   Village President
Countersigned:
ss/Douglas G. Williams
Village Clerk
