ORDINANCE NO. M-550-98
AN ORDINANCE GRANTING A VARIATION IN THE APPLICATION OF THE ZONING ORDINANCE OF
THE VILLAGE OF WINNETKA COOK COUNTY, ILLINOIS (575 SHERIDAN ROAD)
   WHEREAS, there has been presented to the Council of the Village of Winnetka,
Cook County, Illinois, the request of the owner of the following described real
estate (the “Subject Property”):
   Lot 4 in owners resubdivision of Block 8 in Winnetka, a subdivision of
Sections 20 and 21, Township 42 North, Range 13 East of the Third Principal
Meridian, excepting however that part of said Lot 4 described as follows:
Commencing at northwesterly corner of said lot, thence running along the
northwesterly line of said lot in a northeasterly direction to a point in said
northwesterly line which is 163.00 feet from place of beginning, thence
southeasterly 82.00 feet 4 inches more or less along a line which is at right
angles to the northwesterly line of said lot to a point in the southeasterly
line of said lot which is 163.00 feet from the southwesterly corner of said Lot
4; thence southwesterly a distance of 163.00 feet along the southeasterly line
of said lot to the southwesterly corner of said lot; thence northwesterly 82.00
feet 4 inches more or less along the westerly line of said lot to place of
beginning also described as being westerly 163.00 feet of said Lot 4, in Cook
County, Illinois,
commonly known as 575 Sheridan Road, Winnetka, Illinois, and located in the “A-
3” (One-Half Acre) Single-Family Residential Zoning District provided in the
Winnetka Zoning Ordinance, Chapter 22, Winnetka Village Code, for a variation
from the maximum building size (gross floor area) limitations of Section 27.07
(g) of the Zoning Ordinance to allow a maximum building size (gross floor area
) of 8,673.71 square feet, rather than the maximum of 6,614.84 square feet
allowed by Section 22.07(g) of the Zoning Ordinance, resulting in a variation
of 2,058.87 square feet (31.13%), for the purpose of removing a bay window and
constructing a 132 square foot single story addition to the kitchen on the east
side of the single-family home on the Subject Property; and
   WHEREAS, on October 12, 1998, on due notice thereof, the Zoning Board of
Appeals conducted a public hearing on the requested variation and by the
favorable vote of five of the six members then present, has reported to the
Council recommending that the requested variation be granted; and
   WHEREAS, there are practical difficulties and unique hardships associated
with carrying out the strict application of the Zoning Ordinance with respect
to the Subject Property in that; (a) the Subject Property is bordered on the
east by Lake Michigan and the maximum allowable building size varies due to the
fluctuations in the level of the lake; and (b) reconfiguring existing interior
spaces to achieve a complying alternative is not practical due to the location
of a chimney and fireplace in each of the two rooms adjoining the kitchen which
the proposed addition will expand; and
   WHEREAS, the Subject Property cannot yield a reasonable return if permitted
to be used only under the conditions allowed by the Zoning Ordinance, in that
the residence is over 100 years old and the proposed addition will allow the
upgrading of the condition of the kitchen to contemporary standards, which
cannot otherwise be accomplished without building an entirely new residence;
and
   WHEREAS, the requested variation will not alter the essential character of
the neighborhood because the proposed addition will add only 132 square feet to
the existing building, will replace a 64 square foot bay window, will be
consistent with the style of architecture of the existing building, and will
not be visible from Sheridan Road; and
   WHEREAS, the requested variation will not impair an adequate supply of light
and air because it will be located at the rear of the house, facing Lake
Michigan and its one-story height and area of 132 square feet will not be large
enough to cast shadows or block off light to the single-family residence on the
property to the south; and
   WHEREAS, the requested variation will not increase the hazard from fire and
other dangers to the Subject Property as it will comply with all applicable
building and fire protection codes; and
   WHEREAS, the requested variation will not diminish the taxable value of land
and buildings throughout the Village, and the taxable value of the Subject
Property may be increased because of the proposed improvements; and
   WHEREAS, the single story addition to the home will not contribute to
congestion on the public streets, as the Subject Property will continue to be
used as a single-family residence; and
WHEREAS, there is no evidence that the proposed addition will otherwise impair
the public health, safety, comfort, morals, and welfare of the inhabitants of
the Village.
NOW, THEREFORE, the Council of the Village of Winnetka do ordain as follows:
   SECTION 1: That the foregoing recitals are hereby incorporated as the
findings of the Council of the Village of Winnetka, as if fully set forth
herein.
   SECTION 2 : That a variation is hereby granted with respect to the Subject
Property, commonly known as 575 Sheridan Road, which is located in the “A-3”
(One-Half Acre) Single-Family Residential District provided in the Winnetka
Zoning Ordinance, Chapter 22, Winnetka Village Code, for a variation from the
maximum building size (gross floor area) limitations of Section 22.07(g) of the
Zoning Ordinance to allow a maximum building size (gross floor area) of
8,673.71 square feet, rather than the maximum of 6,614.84 square feet allowed
by Section 22.07(g) of the Zoning Ordinance, resulting in a variation of
2,058.87 square feet (31.13%), for the purpose of removing a bay window and
constructing a 132 square foot single story addition to the kitchen on the east
side of the single-family home on the Subject Property, in accordance with the
application for variation and plans submitted with the application.
   SECTION 3: That the variation hereby granted is conditioned upon the
commencement of the proposed construction within twelve months after the
effective date of this Ordinance.
   SECTION 4: This Ordinance shall take effect immediately upon passage,
approval and posting.
   ADOPTED this 17th day of November, 1998, pursuant to the following roll call
vote:
   AYES: Trustees Derning, Hilton, Lanphier, Lien and Meuer
   NAYS: None
   ABSENT: Trustee Duhl
   APPROVED this 17th day of November, 1998.
   Signed:
   ss/Louise A. Holland
   Village President
Countersigned:
ss/Douglas G. Williams
Village Clerk
Introduced: November 5, 1998
Posted: November 6, 1998
Passed and Approved: November 17, 1998
Posted: November 18, 1998
ORDINANCE NO. M-551-98
AN ORDINANCE GRANTING A VARIATION IN THE APPLICATION OF THE ZONING ORDINANCE OF
THE VILLAGE OF WINNETKA COOK COUNTY, ILLINOIS (687 CHERRY STREET)
   WHEREAS, there has been presented to the Council of the Village of Winnetka,
Cook County, Illinois, the request of the owner of the following described real
estate (the “Subject Property”):
   All that part of Block 37 in Winnetka, being a subdivision of the northeast
quarter (1/4) of Section 20 and the north fractional half (1/2) of Section 21,
Township 42 North, Range 13 East of the Third Principal Meridian, in Cook
County, Illinois, according to the plat thereof recorded March 1, 1858, in Book
143 of Maps, page 53 as document 98349 and re-recorded August 8, 1873, as
Document 119381, described as follows beginning at a point in the north line of
Cherry Street intersected by a line, 150.0 feet west of (as measured at right
angles) and parallel with the westerly line of Maple Street, thence west along
said north line of Cherry Street, 56.0 feet; thence north along a line parallel
with the westerly line of Maple Street, thence west along said north line of
Cherry Street, 56.0 feet; thence north along a line parallel with the westerly
line of Maple Street, 126.46 feet more or less to its intersection with a line
drawn at right angles to the easterly line of the right of way of the Chicago
North Shore and Milwaukee Railroad at a point 95.0 feet northerly (as measured
along said right of way line from the north line of Cherry Street); thence
northeasterly along said line drawn at right angles to the easterly line of
said right of way, a distance of 6.47 feet more or less to its intersection
with a line 200.0 feet west of the westerly line of Maple Street, 4.9 feet more
or less to its intersection with a line 240.0 feet (as measured at right
angles) south of and parallel with the south line of Oak Street; thence east
along said line 240.0 feet south of and parallel with the south line of Oak
Street, 50.12 feet to its intersection with a line 150.0 feet (measured at
right angles) west of and parallel with the westerly line of Maple Street;
thence south along said line, 150.0 feet west of and parallel with the westerly
line of Maple Street, a distance of 134.36 feet to the point of beginning, in
Cook County, Illinois.
commonly known as 687 Cherry Street, Winnetka, Illinois, and located in “A-5”
(One-Fourth Acre) Single-Family Residential Zoning District provided in the
Winnetka Zoning Ordinance, Chapter 22, Winnetka Village Code, for the following
variations: (a) a variation from the intensity of use of lot limitations of
Section 22.05A(f) of the Zoning Ordinance to allow total impermeable surfaces
of 4,715.48 square feet, whereas 3,707.64 square feet are permitted, resulting
in a variation of 1007.84 square feet (27.18%), and to allow a total roofed lot
coverage of 1,925.13 square feet, whereas 1853.82 square feet are permitted,
resulting in a variation of 71.31 square feet (3.85%); (b) from the maximum
building size (gross floor area) limitations of Section 22.05A(g) of the Zoning
Ordinance to allow a total gross floor area of 3958.01 square feet, whereas
2966.12 square feet are permitted, resulting in a variation of 991.89 square
feet (33.44%); and (c) a variation from the side yard requirements of Section
22.05A(i) of the Zoning Ordinance to allow a side yard of 5.59 feet, whereas
6.0 feet are required, resulting in a variation of .41 feet (6.83%), all for
the purpose of constructing a new masonry chimney and masonry veneer and to
permit structural alterations to existing nonconforming walls of the residence
on the Subject Property, in accordance with the application for variation and
plans accompanying the application; and
   WHEREAS, on October 12, 1998, on due notice thereof, the Zoning Board of
Appeals conducted a public hearing on the requested variation and by the
unanimous vote of the six members then present, has reported to the Council
recommending that the requested variations be granted; and
   WHEREAS, the requested variations are in harmony with the general purpose
and intent of the Winnetka Zoning Ordinance, because the proposed improvements
will decrease the extent of nonconformities on the Subject Property by
converting the building from a two-family dwelling to a permitted single-family
dwelling and by reducing the total gross floor area; and
   WHEREAS, there are practical difficulties and unique hardships associated
with carrying out the strict application of the Zoning Ordinance with respect
to the Subject Property in that the Subject Property abuts the B-1 Multi-Family
Residential Zoning District, is improved with a nonconforming two-family
dwelling, and has other existing nonconformities in lot width, roofed lot
coverage, gross floor area, impermeable surface and east side yard, and in
that, although the proposed variations will increase roofed lot coverage and
impermeable surface by 27.34 square feet, they will not increase the side yard
nonconformity, will reduce the gross floor area on the Subject Property by
60.35 square feet, and will eliminate the nonconforming use by converting the
structure into a conforming single-family dwelling; and
   WHEREAS, the Subject Property cannot yield a reasonable return if permitted
to be used only under the conditions allowed by the Zoning Ordinance, in that
bringing the Subject Property into full conformity with all zoning requirements
and limitations would require that the building be demolished and replaced with
a new structure; and
   WHEREAS, the requested variation will not alter the essential character of
the neighborhood because the building alterations and additions will allow the
Subject Property to be used as a single-family residence in conformity with the
zoning district in which it is located, and the 27.34 square foot increase in
roofed lot coverage and impermeable surface is the result of adding a new
masonry veneer to enclose converted interior living space, adding a new masonry
chimney and adding a new masonry parapet, all to match the existing building,
which was constructed in 1939 and has existed in its present form since the
construction of an addition in 1951; and
   WHEREAS, the requested variation will not impair an adequate supply of light
and air because they will allow the removal of the stairway from the second
story and reduce the bulk of the building; and
   WHEREAS, the requested variations will not increase the hazard from fire and
other dangers to the Subject Property as it will comply with all applicable
building and fire protection codes; and
   WHEREAS, the requested variations will not diminish the taxable value of
land and buildings throughout the Village, and the taxable value of the Subject
Property may be increased because of the proposed improvements; and
   WHEREAS, the proposed alterations and additions will not contribute to
congestion on the public streets, as they will reconfigure the structure from a
two-family dwelling to a single-family dwelling; and
WHEREAS, there is no evidence that the proposed alterations and additions will
otherwise impair the public health, safety, comfort, morals, and welfare of the
inhabitants of the Village.
NOW, THEREFORE, the Council of the Village of Winnetka do ordain as follows:
   SECTION 1 : That the foregoing recitals are hereby incorporated as the
findings of the Council of the Village of Winnetka, as if fully set forth
herein.
   SECTION 2:  That a variation is hereby granted with respect to the Subject
Property, commonly known as 687 Cherry Street, Winnetka, Illinois, which is
located in the “A-5” (One-Fourth Acre) Single-Family Residential District
provided in the Winnetka Zoning Ordinance, Chapter 22, Winnetka Village Code,
for the following variations: (a) a variation from the intensity of use of lot
limitations of Section 22.05A of the Zoning Ordinance to allow total
impermeable surfaces of 4,715.48 square feet, whereas 3,707.64 square feet are
permitted, resulting in a variation of 1,007.84 square feet (27.18%), and to
allow a total roofed lot coverage of 1,925.13 square feet, whereas 1,853.82
square feet are permitted, resulting in a variation of 71.31 square feet
(3.85%); (b) a variation from the maximum building size (gross floor area)
limitations of Section 22.05A(g) of the Zoning Ordinance to allow a total gross
floor area of 3,958.01 square feet, whereas 2,966.12 square feet are permitted,
resulting in a variation of 991.89 square feet (33.44%); and (c) a variation
from the side yard requirements of Section 22.05A(i) of the Zoning Ordinance to
allow a side yard of 5.59 feet, whereas 6.0 feet are required, resulting in a
variation of .41 feet (6.83%); all for the purpose of constructing a new
masonry chimney and masonry veneer, and to permit structural alterations to
existing nonconforming walls of the existing residence on the Subject Property,
all in accordance with the application for variation and plans accompanying the
application.
   SECTION 3: That the variations hereby granted are conditioned upon the
commencement of the proposed construction within twelve months after the
effective date of this Ordinance.
   SECTION 4: This Ordinance shall take effect immediately upon passage,
approval and posting.
   ADOPTED this 17th day of November, 1998, pursuant to the following roll call
vote:
   AYES: Trustees Derning, Hilton, Lanphier, Lien and Meuer
   NAYS: None
