ORDINANCE NO. M-552-98
AN ORDINANCE GRANTING A VARIATION IN THE APPLICATION OF THE ZONING ORDINANCE OF
THE VILLAGE OF WINNETKA COOK COUNTY, ILLINOIS (380 Poplar Street)
   WHEREAS, there has been presented to the Council of the Village of Winnetka,
Cook County, Illinois, the request of the owner of the following described real
estate (the “Subject Property”):
   The North 65.0 feet of Southeast Quarter of Block 66 (except the West 60.0
feet thereof in Winnetka, of Section 20 and 21 Township 42 North Range 13 East
of the Third Principal Meridian.
commonly known as 380 Poplar Street, Winnetka, Illinois, and located in the “A-
5” (One-Fourth Acre) Single-Family Residential Zoning District provided in the
Winnetka Zoning Ordinance, Chapter 22, Winnetka Village Code, for a variation
from the intensity of use of lot limitations of Section 22.05A(f) of the Zoning
Ordinance to allow a total roofed lot coverage of 2,311.19 square feet, whereas
2,063.75 square feet are permitted, resulting in a variation of 247.44 square
feet (11.99%), and a variation from the maximum building size (gross floor
area) limitations of Section 22.05A(g) to allow a total gross floor area of
4,116.49 square feet, whereas 3,302.00 square feet are permitted, resulting in
a variation of 814.49 square feet (24.67%), all for the purpose of constructing
four dormers, a 38.5 square foot room addition and a 32 square foot front porch
roof for the residence on the Subject Property; and
   WHEREAS, the extent of the variations requested was subsequently reduced
when the plat of survey of the Subject Property was corrected to indicate that
a shed which contributed 67.25 square feet to gross floor area and roofed lot
coverage had been removed; and
   WHEREAS, on October 5, 1998, on due notice thereof, the Zoning Board of
Appeals conducted a public hearing on the requested variation and by the
favorable vote of five of the six members then present, has reported to the
Council recommending that the requested variation be granted; and
   WHEREAS, there are practical difficulties and unique hardships associated
with carrying out the strict application of the Zoning Ordinance with respect
to the Subject Property in that the Subject Property currently exceeds the
roofed lot coverage and gross floor limitations and the requested variations,
which are for minimal increases over the existing lot coverage and gross floor
area, will improve safety, increase the amount of light and air in the
residence and increase the utility of the residence while improving its
appearance in the existing streetscape; and
   WHEREAS, the Subject Property cannot yield a reasonable return if permitted
to be used only under the conditions allowed by the Zoning Ordinance, in that
the proposed variations will increase the utility of the residence by
increasing the habitability and safety of the second floor, improving the
appearance of the building and bringing the kitchen up to contemporary
standards, which could not otherwise be accomplished within the limitations of
the Zoning Ordinance without replacing the residence in its entirety; and
   WHEREAS, the requested variation will not alter the essential character of
the neighborhood because the new dormers will match existing dormers on the
residence, the new front entry will be consistent with the architecture of the
building and is set back substantially from the front lot line, and the
breakfast addition is not visible from the street; and
   WHEREAS, the requested variation will not impair an adequate supply of light
and air because the 38.5 square foot one-story breakfast room addition is
located in the center of the rear of the house, the front entry roof is located
in a reverse corner of the house and the dormers are in line with the existing
building lines and roof slopes; and
   WHEREAS, the requested variation will not increase the hazard from fire and
other dangers to the Subject Property as it will comply with all applicable
building and fire protection codes; and
   WHEREAS, the requested variation will not diminish the taxable value of land
and buildings throughout the Village, and the taxable value of the Subject
Property may be increased because of the proposed improvements; and
   WHEREAS, the proposed breakfast room addition front door roof and dormers
will not contribute to congestion on the public streets, as the Subject
Property will continue to be used for single-family residential purposes; and
   WHEREAS, there is no evidence that the proposed building additions and
dormers will otherwise impair the public health, safety, comfort, morals, and
welfare of the inhabitants of the Village.
NOW, THEREFORE, the Council of the Village of Winnetka do ordain as follows:
   SECTION 1 : That the foregoing recitals are hereby incorporated as the
findings of the Council of the Village of Winnetka, as if fully set forth
herein.
   SECTION 2: That variations are hereby granted with respect to the Subject
Property, commonly known as 380 Poplar Street, which is located in the “A-5”
(One-Fourth Acre) Single-Family Residential Zoning District provided in the
Winnetka Zoning Ordinance, Chapter 22, Winnetka Village Code, for a variation
from the intensity of use of lot limitations of Section 22.05A(f) of the Zoning
Ordinance to allow a total roofed lot coverage of 2,243.94 square feet, whereas
2,063.75 square feet is allowed, resulting in a variation of 180.19 square feet
(8.73%), and a variation from the maximum building size (gross floor area)
limitations of Section 22.05A(g) of the Zoning Ordinance to allow a total gross
floor area of 4,049.24 square feet, whereas 3,302.00 square feet are permitted,
resulting in a variation of 747.24 square feet (22.63%), all for the purpose of
constructing four dormers, a 38.5 square foot room addition and a 32 square
foot front porch roof for the residence on the Subject Property, in accordance
with the application for variation and plans submitted with the application.
   SECTION 3: That the variations hereby granted are conditioned upon the
commencement of the proposed construction within twelve months after the
effective date of this Ordinance.
   SECTION 4: This Ordinance shall take effect immediately upon passage,
approval and posting.
   ADOPTED this 1st day of December, 1998, pursuant to the following roll call
vote:
   AYES: Trustees Derning, Lanphier and Meuer, President Holland
   NAYS: Trustees Lien, Duhl and Hilton
   ABSENT: None
   APPROVED this 1st day of December, 1998.
   Signed:
   ss/Louise A. Holland
   Village President
Countersigned:
ss/Douglas G. Williams
Village Clerk
Introduced: November 17, 1998
Posted: November 18, 1998
Passed and Approved: December 1, 1998
Posted: December 2, 1998
ORDINANCE NO. M-553-98
AN ORDINANCE GRANTING A VARIATION IN THE APPLICATION OF THE ZONING ORDINANCE OF
THE VILLAGE OF WINNETKA COOK COUNTY, ILLINOIS (1138 Scott Avenue)
   WHEREAS, there has been presented to the Council of the Village of Winnetka,
Cook County, Illinois, the request of the owner of the following described real
estate (the “Subject Property”):
   Lot 1 in Block 11 in Chicago North Shore Land Company’s Subdivision in
Sections 8, 17 and 18, Township 42 North, Range 13 East of the Third Principal
Meridian, in Cook County, Illinois.
commonly known as 1138 Scott Street, Winnetka, Illinois, and located in “A-1”
(One-Sixth Acre) Single-Family Residential Zoning District provided in the
Winnetka Zoning Ordinance, Chapter 22, Winnetka Village Code, for a variation
from Section 22.05(i) of the Zoning Ordinance to allow a side yard setback of
1.59 feet, whereas a minimum side yard of 6.0 feet is required, resulting in a
variation of 4.41 feet (73.5%), for the purpose of converting the existing
attached garage on the Subject Property into a sunroom and to remodel a portion
of the existing kitchen; and
   WHEREAS, on October 12, 1998, on due notice thereof, the Zoning Board of
Appeals conducted a public hearing on the requested variation and by the
unanimous vote of the five members then present, has reported to the Council
recommending that the requested variation be granted; and
   WHEREAS, there are practical difficulties and unique hardships associated
with carrying out the strict application of the Zoning Ordinance with respect
to the Subject Property in that: (a) the attached garage for which the
variation is sought is in a nonconforming location; (b) a variation was granted
in 1985 for the remodeling of the same garage; (c) the Subject Property is a
corner lot which must observe two front setbacks; (d) the existing house was
constructed prior to the enactment of the Zoning Ordinance in what is now a
nonconforming location; and (e) the proposed building modifications will not
alter the existing legal nonconformities in roofed lot coverage, gross floor
area and front (corner) yard setback; and
   WHEREAS, the Subject Property cannot yield a reasonable return if permitted
to be used only under the conditions allowed by the Zoning Ordinance, in that
the requested variation will allow an expansion of habitable space in the
existing residence without increasing the exterior dimensions, and the
increased living space and utility of the residence could not be otherwise
accomplished within the limits of the Zoning Ordinance without replacing the
building in its entirety; and
   WHEREAS, the requested variation will not alter the essential character of
the neighborhood because the only change to the exterior of the building will
be the addition of an open deck, which complies with all applicable zoning
regulations; and
   WHEREAS, the requested variation will not impair an adequate supply of light
and air because it does not alter either the building footprint or the building
size; and
   WHEREAS, the requested variation will not increase the hazard from fire and
other dangers to the Subject Property as it will comply with all applicable
building and fire protection codes; and
   WHEREAS, the requested variation will not diminish the taxable value of land
and buildings throughout the Village, and the taxable value of the Subject
Property may be increased because of the proposed improvements; and
   WHEREAS, the proposed remodeling of the existing attached garage to convert
it to habitable space will not contribute to congestion on the public streets,
as the Subject Property will continue to be used for single family residential
purposes, and a larger, detached garage exists on the Subject Property for off-
street parking; and
   WHEREAS, there is no evidence that the requested variation will otherwise
impair the public health, safety, comfort, morals, and welfare of the
inhabitants of the Village.
NOW, THEREFORE, the Council of the Village of Winnetka do ordain as follows:
   SECTION 1 : That the foregoing recitals are hereby incorporated as the
findings of the Council of the Village of Winnetka, as if fully set forth
herein.
   SECTION 2: That a variation is hereby granted with respect to the Subject
Property, commonly known as 1138 Scott Avenue, which is located in the “A-1”
(One-Sixth Acre) Single-Family Residential District provided in the Winnetka
Zoning Ordinance, Chapter 22, Winnetka Village Code, for a variation from
Section 22.05(i) of the Zoning Ordinance to allow a side yard setback of 1.59
feet, whereas a minimum side yard of 6.0 feet is required, resulting in a
variation of 4.41 feet (73.5%), for the purpose of converting the existing
attached garage on the Subject Property into a sunroom and to remodel a portion
of the existing kitchen, in accordance with the application for variation and
plans submitted with the application.
   SECTION 3: That the variations hereby granted are conditioned upon the
commencement of the proposed construction within twelve months after the
effective date of this Ordinance.
   SECTION 4: This Ordinance shall take effect immediately upon passage,
approval and posting.
   ADOPTED this 17th day of November, 1998, pursuant to the following roll call
vote:
AYES: Trustees Derning, Hilton, Lanphier, Lien and Meuer
   NAYS: None.
   ABSENT: Trustee Duhl.
   APPROVED this 17th day of November, 1998.
   Signed:
   ss/Louise A. Holland
    Village President
Countersigned:
ss/Douglas G. Williams
Village Clerk
