ORDINANCE NO. M-570-99
AN ORDINANCE OF THE VILLAGE OF WINNETKA, COOK COUNTY, ILLINOIS, TO APPROVE THE
ADMISSION OF THE VILLAGE OF ALBANY AS A NEW MEMBER OF THE ILLINOIS MUNICIPAL
ELECTRIC AGENCY AND TO AUTHORIZE EXECUTION OF A SUPPLEMENT TO THE AGENCY
AGREEMENT ESTABLISHING THE ILLINOIS MUNICIPAL ELECTRIC AGENCY
   WHEREAS, the Village of Winnetka, Cook County, Illinois, is a member of the
Illinois Municipal Electric Agency ("IMEA"); and
   WHEREAS, the Village of Albany, Whiteside County, Illinois (hereinafter
referred to as “Albany”), desires to become a member of the Illinois Municipal
Electric Agency; and
   WHEREAS, Albany shall comply with all conditions for membership of IMEA,
shall adopt the Agency Agreement and shall pay all applicable fees; and
   WHEREAS, the Board of Directors of the Illinois Municipal Electric Agency
shall by Ordinance approve the Supplement to its Agency Agreement which will
cause Albany to become a member of the Agency.
   NOW, THEREFORE, the Council of the Village of Winnetka do ordain:
   SECTION 1:   The findings and determinations set forth in the preamble to
this Ordinance are hereby made findings and determinations of the Council of
the Village of Winnetka and are hereby incorporated into the text of this
Ordinance by this reference.
   SECTION 2:   The Village of Albany, Whiteside County, Illinois, is hereby
approved as a new member of the Illinois Municipal Electric Agency.
   SECTION 3:   The Council of the Village of Winnetka hereby approve the terms
and conditions of the Illinois Municipal Electric Agency's Agreement and a
Supplement to the Agency Agreement, substantially in the same form attached
hereto as Exhibit No. 1.
   SECTION 4:   The Village President is hereby authorized and directed to
execute and the Village Clerk attest, respectively, the Supplement to the
Agency Agreement, substantially in the same form attached hereto as Exhibit No.
1, for the admission of the new member of the Illinois Municipal Electric
Agency.
   SECTION 5:   That this Ordinance shall be in full force and effect from and
after its passage, approval, and posting.
   Passed and approved this 2nd day of March, 1999.
   AYES: Trustees Derning, Duhl, Lanphier, Lien and Meuer
   NAYS: None.
   ABSENT: Trustee Hilton.
