ORDINANCE NO. M-572-99
AN ORDINANCE DESIGNATING DEPOSITORIES FOR VILLAGE FUNDS AND MONEY
   WHEREAS, Section 3.1-35-50(a) of the Illinois Municipal Code authorizes the
Village Council to require the Village Treasurer to keep all Village funds and
money in the Treasurer’s custody in places of deposit designated by ordinance;
and
   WHEREAS, Section 3.04(c) of the Winnetka Village Code provides for
designation of approved depositories by ordinance and sets out the procedures
and standards whereby the Village Council may designate and approve such
depositories when so requested by the Village Treasurer; and
   WHEREAS, pursuant to Section 3.1-35-50(a) of the Illinois Municipal Code and
Section 3.04(c) of the Winnetka Village Code, the Treasurer of the Village of
Winnetka has evaluated various financial institutions and has requested that
the Council designate Amalgamated Bank of Chicago, Bank One, the Federal
Reserve Bank of Chicago, the Illinois Funds, and Harris Trust and Savings Bank
as authorized depositories for Village funds, monies and securities.
   WHEREAS, the Council of the Village of Winnetka have determined that said
financial institutions shall be designated and approved as depositories for
Village funds, monies and securities, subject to compliance with the
requirements set forth in subparagraph 1 of Section 3.04(c) of the Winnetka
Village Code.
   NOW, THEREFORE, the Council of the Village of Winnetka do ordain as follows:
   SECTION 1 : That the foregoing recitals are hereby incorporated as the
findings of the Council of the Village of Winnetka, as if fully set forth
herein.
   SECTION 2: Subject to the conditions set forth herein, the following
entities are hereby designated and approved as depositories for all funds,
monies and securities of the Village of Winnetka in the custody of the Village
Treasurer:
   Amalgamated Bank of Chicago
   Bank One
   The Federal Reserve Bank of Chicago
   The Illinois Funds
   Harris Trust and Savings Bank
The designation and approval of each of the foregoing depositories shall be
subject to that depository’s having first complied with the requirements of
paragraph 1 of Section 3.04(c) of the Winnetka Village Code.
   SECTION 3 : Subject to the foregoing conditions, the Village Treasurer is
hereby authorized and directed to deposit all funds or monies in his custody
belonging to the Village of Winnetka, and all securities received by him by
virtue of his office or by any law of the State of Illinois or any ordinance of
the Village of Winnetka, in one or more of the depositories designated and
approved pursuant to this Ordinance.
   SECTION 4: This Ordinance shall take effect immediately upon passage,
approval and posting.
   ADOPTED this 4th day of May, 1999, pursuant to the following roll call vote:
   AYES: Trustees Aquilino, Derning, Duhl, Hilton, and Powell.
   NAYS: None.
   ABSENT: Trustee Lien.
   APPROVED this 4th day of May, 1999.
   Signed:
   ss/Louise A. Holland
    Village President
