ORDINANCE NO. M-574-99
AN ORDINANCE GRANTING A VARIATION IN THE APPLICATION OF THE ZONING ORDINANCE OF
THE VILLAGE OF WINNETKA COOK COUNTY, ILLINOIS (480 Oak Street)
   WHEREAS, there has been presented to the Council of the Village of Winnetka,
Cook County, Illinois, the request of the owner of the following described real
estate (the “Subject Property”):
   Lot 1 in Winnetka Beach Estates, being a Subdivision of that part of Block
42 in Charles E. Peck’s Subdivision of the Northeast ¼ of Section 20 and the
north ½ of (tract) Section 21, in Township 42 North, Range 13, East of the
Third Principal Meridian, lying North of the Northerly line of that party of
Non-vacated Cherry Street and South of the Northerly line of the Original South
10 feet of Oak Street (before Subdivision) and Easterly of the East line of
Sheridan Road, all in the Village of Winnetka, in Cook County, Illinois,
commonly known as 480 Oak Street, Winnetka, Illinois, and located in the R-
3 Single-Family Residential District (formerly the A-3 One-Half Acre Zoning
District) provided in the Winnetka Zoning Ordinance, Chapter 22, Winnetka
Village Code, for a variation from the maximum building size limitations of
Section 22.07(g) to allow a gross floor area of 6,894.11 square feet, whereas
6,869.56 square feet are permitted, resulting in a variation of 298.20 square
feet (4.52%) for the purpose of constructing a one-story addition to replace an
existing greenhouse and to update the existing kitchen on the Subject Property
in accordance with the plans submitted with the application; and
   WHEREAS, on April 12, 1999, on due notice thereof, the Zoning Board of
Appeals conducted a public hearing on the requested variation and by the
unanimous vote of the four members then present, has reported to the Council
recommending that the requested variation be granted; and
   WHEREAS, there are practical difficulties and unique hardships associated
with carrying out the strict application of the Zoning Ordinance in that the
Subject Property adjoins Lake Michigan, has a legally non-conforming gross
floor are of 6,869.56 square feet as a result of erosion from the lake which
decreased the size of the lot, and to rebuild the lakeshore would be too
costly; and
   WHEREAS, the Subject Property cannot yield a reasonable return if permitted
to be used only under the conditions allowed by the Zoning Ordinance, in that
the existing kitchen is inadequate; and
   WHEREAS, the requested variation will not alter the essential character of
the neighborhood because the proposed addition, which has an area of 141.98
square feet, is only 24.55 square feet larger than the existing greenhouse that
it will be replace; and
   WHEREAS, the requested variation will not impair an adequate supply of light
and air because the addition is of a similar size to the existing structure and
is one story; and
   WHEREAS, the requested variation will not increase the hazard from fire and
other dangers to the Subject Property as it will comply with all applicable
building and fire protection codes; and
   WHEREAS, the requested variation will not diminish the taxable value of land
and buildings throughout the Village, and the taxable value of the Subject
Property may be increased because of the proposed improvements; and
   WHEREAS, the proposed one-story addition will not contribute to congestion
on the public streets, as the residence will continue to be used as a single-
family home; and
   WHEREAS, there is no evidence that the proposed construction will otherwise
impair the public health, safety, comfort, morals, and welfare of the
inhabitants of the Village.
   NOW, THEREFORE, the Council of the Village of Winnetka do ordain as follows:
   SECTION 1 : That the foregoing recitals are hereby incorporated as the
findings of the Council of the Village of Winnetka, as if fully set forth
herein.
   SECTION 2: That a variation is hereby granted to the Subject Property,
commonly known as 480 Oak Street, Winnetka, Illinois, and located in the R-
3 Single-Family Residential District (formerly A-3 One-Half Acre Zoning
District) provided in the Winnetka Zoning Ordinance, Chapter 22, Winnetka
Village Code, from the maximum building size limitations of Section 22.07(g) to
allow a gross floor area of 6,894.11 square feet, whereas 6,869.56 square feet
are permitted, resulting in a variation of 298.20 square feet (4.52%), for the
purpose of constructing a one-story addition to replace an existing greenhouse
and to update the existing kitchen on the Subject Property in accordance with
the plans submitted with the application.
   SECTION 3: That the variation hereby granted is subject to the following
conditions: (1) the commencement of the proposed constructing within 12 months
after the effective date of this Ordinance; and (2) the removal of the fence
and any other obstructions to the Oak Street right-of-way prior to the issuance
of any permits for the proposed construction.
   SECTION 4: This Ordinance shall take effect immediately upon passage,
approval and posting.
   ADOPTED this 18th day of May, 1999, pursuant to the following roll call
vote:
   AYES: Trustees Aquilino, Derning, Duhl, Hilton, Lien, and Powell.
   NAYS: None.
   ABSENT: None.
   APPROVED this 18th day of May, 1999.
   Signed:
   ss/Louise A. Holland
    Village President
