ORDINANCE NO. M-575-99
AN ORDINANCE GRANTING A VARIATION IN THE APPLICATION OF THE ZONING ORDINANCE OF
THE VILLAGE OF WINNETKA COOK COUNTY, ILLINOIS (220 Poplar Street)
   WHEREAS, there has been presented to the Council of the Village of Winnetka,
Cook County, Illinois, the request of the owner of the following described real
estate (the “Subject Property”):
   Lot 2 (except the South 37 feet measured on the East line of said Lot 2) in
Block 22 in Subdivision of Blocks 18, 21, 22, and 23 in J.C. Garland’s Addition
to Winnetka, being a Subdivision of the North 120 acres of the Southwest
quarter of Section 21, Township 42 North, Range 13 East of the Third Principal
Meridian, according to the plat thereof recorded June 9, 1909, Document
4388795, In Cook County, Illinois,
commonly known as 220 Poplar Street, Winnetka, Illinois, and located in the R-
5 Single-Family Residential District (formerly the A-1, One Sixth Acre Zoning
District) provided in the Winnetka Zoning Ordinance, Chapter 22, Winnetka
Village Code, for the following variations: (a) a variation from the front set
back requirements of Section 22.05(f) to permit a 6-foot front setback along
Wilson Avenue, whereas 30 feet are required, resulting in a variation of 24
feet (80.0%); and (b) a variation from the roofed lot coverage limitations of
Section 22.05(h) to permit a total roofed lot coverage of 1,824.09 square feet,
whereas 1,718.72 square feet are permitted, resulting in a variation of 105.37
square feet (6.13%), said variations being requested to permit the construction
of a 400 square foot, two-car detached garage on the Subject Property in
accordance with the plans submitted with the application on March 2, 1999; and
   WHEREAS, in 1993, the applicants were granted variations from front setback
and side yard requirements in order to permit the construction of a two-car
detached garage, but did not construct the garage within the 12 month period
specified in the ordinance granting the variation; and
   WHEREAS, the current application was submitted subsequent to a hearing
conducted by the Zoning Board of Appeals on February 8, 1999, on the
applicant’s renewed request for the same variation from the front set back
along Wilson Avenue, a 183.56 square foot variation from the roofed lot
coverage limitations and a north side yard variation of 4 feet to allow a side
yard of 2 feet, rather than the 6 feet required, all to allow construction of a
22-foot by 22-foot two-car garage; and
   WHEREAS, the current application reduces the size of the garage, thereby
reducing the extent of the roofed lot coverage variation, and eliminates the
need for a variation in the north side yard requirements; and
   WHEREAS, on April 12, 1999, on due notice thereof, the Zoning Board of
Appeals conducted a public hearing on the requested variation and by the
unanimous vote of the four members then present, has reported to the Council
recommending that the requested variation be granted; and
   WHEREAS, there are practical difficulties and unique hardships associated
with carrying out the strict application of the Zoning Ordinance with respect
to the Subject Property in that the Subject Property is an irregularly shaped
through lot, requires two front yard setbacks, has a legally nonconforming lot
area of 6,874.74 square feet and is located in an area where parking on the
street is prohibited; and
   WHEREAS, the Subject Property cannot yield a reasonable return if permitted
to be used only under the conditions allowed by the Zoning Ordinance, in that
the front setbacks required prohibit a conforming location for a functional
garage; and
   WHEREAS, the requested variation will not alter the essential character of
the neighborhood because there are similarly located detached garages along the
street, and the garage will provide enclosed, off-street parking for the
Subject Property; and
   WHEREAS, the requested variation will not impair an adequate supply of light
and air in that the proposed garage will be adjacent to the rear yards and open
areas of the neighboring properties; and
   WHEREAS, the requested variation will not increase the hazard from fire and
other dangers to the Subject Property as it will comply with all applicable
building and fire protection codes; and
   WHEREAS, the requested variation will not diminish the taxable value of land
and buildings throughout the Village, and the taxable value of the Subject
Property may be increased because of the proposed improvements; and
   WHEREAS, the proposed detached garage will not contribute to congestion on
the public streets, as it will not increase the occupancy or change the use of
the property and will provide for off-street parking; and
   WHEREAS, there is no evidence that the detached garage will otherwise impair
the public health, safety, comfort, morals, and welfare of the inhabitants of
the Village.
   NOW, THEREFORE, the Council of the Village of Winnetka do ordain as follows:
   SECTION 1 : That the foregoing recitals are hereby incorporated as the
findings of the Council of the Village of Winnetka, as if fully set forth
herein.
   SECTION 2: That the following variations are hereby granted to the Subject
Property, commonly known as 220 Poplar Street, Winnetka, Illinois, and located
in the R-5 Single-Family Residential District (formerly the A-1, One Sixth Acre
Zoning District) provided in the Winnetka Zoning Ordinance, Chapter 22,
Winnetka Village Code: (a) a variation from the front set back requirements of
Section 22.05(f) to permit a 6-foot front setback along Wilson Avenue, whereas
30 feet are required, resulting in a variation of 24 feet (80.0%); and (b) a
variation from the roofed lot coverage limitations of Section 22.05(h) to
permit a total roofed lot coverage of 1,824.09 square feet, whereas 1,718.72
square feet are required, resulting in a variation of 105.37 square feet
(6.13%); said variations being granted to permit the construction of a 400
square foot, two-car detached garage on the Subject Property in accordance with
the plans submitted with the application on March 2, 1999.
   SECTION 3: That the variations hereby granted are conditioned upon the
commencement of the proposed construction within 12 months after the effective
date of this Ordinance.
   SECTION 4: This Ordinance shall take effect immediately upon passage,
approval and posting.
   ADOPTED this 18th day of May, 1999, pursuant to the following roll call
vote:
   AYES: Trustees Aquilino, Derning, Duhl, Hilton, Lien, and Powell.
   NAYS: None.
   ABSENT: None.
   APPROVED this 18th day of May, 1999.
   Signed:
   ss/Louise A. Holland
    Village President
Countersigned:
ss/Douglas G. Williams
Village Clerk
