ORDINANCE NO. M-584-99
AN ORDINANCE GRANTING A SPECIAL USE PERMIT FOR THE RENOVATION OF HUBBARD WOODS
PARK
   WHEREAS, the Winnetka Park District is the owner of a parcel of real estate
(the “Subject Property”) that is located at 939 Green Bay Road, is commonly
known as the Hubbard Woods Park, and is legally described as follows:   
Lots 1 through 8, inclusive, in Block 4 in Jared Gages Subdivision, together
with a strip of land 50 feet wide northeasterly of and adjoining Lots 1 through
8 inclusive in Block 4 in Jared Gages Subdivision, said Subdivision being a
subdivision of part of the East half of the Northwest quarter of fractional
Section 17, also part of the West half of the Northwest quarter fractional
Section 17, also part of the East half of the Southwest quarter of fractional
Section 8, all in Township 42 North, Range 13, East of the Third Principal
Meridian, in Cook County, Illinois.
   WHEREAS, the Subject Property is located in the C-2 (General Retail)
Commercial Zoning District of the Village of Winnetka, as provided in the
Winnetka Zoning Ordinance, Chapter 22, Winnetka Village Code; and
   WHEREAS, Hubbard Woods Park is a public park consisting of a playground,
shelter, gazebo, picnic area and open spaces and is therefore a public use,
which uses are permitted as special uses in all zoning districts, subject to
the conditions and requirements pertaining to special uses, as set forth in
Section 22.13 of the Winnetka Zoning Ordinance; and
   WHEREAS, the Winnetka Park District has submitted an application to the
Village of Winnetka seeking a special use permit pursuant to said Section
22.13, to permit the renovation of the existing playground located in the
northwest corner of Hubbard Woods Park with new playground equipment, play
surface, tables, benches, curbing and drainage; and
   WHEREAS, upon due notice on July 12, 1999, the Zoning Board of Appeals held
a public hearing on the proposed special use and, by the unanimous vote of the
six members then present, has reported to the Council recommending that the
requested special use be granted; and
   WHEREAS, upon due notice, the Design Review Board met on July 15, 1999, to
consider the redesign of the playground and by the unanimous vote of the five
members then present, has submitted a comment that a Certificate of
Appropriateness would issue for the design presented; and
   WHEREAS, upon due notice, the Plan Commission met on August 25, 1999, to
consider the application of the Park District, and by the unanimous vote of the
eight members then present, found that the proposed special use is consistent
with the Winnetka Park District policy listed in the 1979 Statement of
Community Objectives in the Winnetka Comprehensive Plan, with the Parks and
Open Space System policy and recommendations of Chapter XI of the Winnetka
Comprehensive Plan, and with the Hubbard Woods Business District policy and
recommendations of Chapter XXI of the Winnetka Comprehensive Plan, and
recommended that the special use be granted; and
   WHEREAS, the proposed replacement of the playground equipment at Hubbard
Woods Park will benefit the public health, safety, comfort, morals and general
welfare of the Village, by improving the safety, accessibility and appearance
of the playground through the installation of new playground equipment, benches
and a brick paver pathway, and by improving the storm drainage on the Subject
Property, all in accordance with applicable requirements of the Americans with
Disabilities Act, playground safety standards and the Village Code; and
   WHEREAS, the proposed special use will not be substantially injurious to the
use and enjoyment of other property in the immediate vicinity, nor will it
substantially diminish or impair property values in the immediate vicinity, as
the use is established in the neighborhood, the renovation will not increase
the intensity of the existing use, and the renovation will improve both the
functionality and appearance of the park; and
   WHEREAS, the proposed special use will not impede the normal and orderly
development or improvement of other property in the immediate vicinity for uses
permitted under applicable zoning regulations, as the playground is an
established use in an existing location on the Subject Property and the type of
use of the Subject Property will not be changed; and
   WHEREAS, adequate measures have been taken to provide ingress and egress in
a manner which minimizes pedestrian and vehicular traffic congestion, in that
the existing pedestrian circulation routes through the park, points of access
tot he Subject Property and parking will not be changed; and
   WHEREAS, adequate parking and access roads serve the Subject Property; and
   WHEREAS, adequate utilities, drainage and other facilities necessary to the
operation of the special use exists or will be provided in that there is
presently water service to the existing water fountains and a new storm drain
will connect directly to the Village’s storm sewer system and provide drainage
for the playground area; and
   WHEREAS, the special use in all other respects conforms to the applicable
regulations of this and other Village ordinances and codes;
   NOW, THEREFORE, the Council of the Village of Winnetka do ordain:
   SECTION 1:   That the Village Council hereby adopts the foregoing recitals
as their findings, as if fully set forth herein.
   SECTION 2: That pursuant to Section 22.13 of the Winnetka Zoning Ordinance,
Chapter 22 of the Winnetka Village Code, a special use permit is hereby granted
with respect to the Subject Property, which is located in the C-2 (General
Retail) Commercial District provided in said Zoning Ordinance and which is
commonly known as Hubbard Woods Park, to permit the renovation of the Subject
Property by installing new playground equipment, play surface, pathways,
benches, landscaping, curbing and drainage in the playground located on the
Subject Property, said work to be done in accordance with the application for
special use permit and the plans dated June 7, 1999, which accompanied the
application.
   SECTION 3: That the special use permit hereby granted is conditioned upon
the commencement of the proposed construction within 12 months after the
effective date of this Ordinance.
   SECTION 4: That, pursuant to Section 22.13(g) of the Zoning Ordinance, all
stipulations, conditions and restrictions set forth in this Ordinance as part
of the terms under which the special use is granted, may be modified or revised
from time to time by the Village Council following public notice and hearing,
using the same procedures set forth in the Zoning Ordinance for processing the
original special use application.
   SECTION 5:   That this Ordinance shall be in full force and effect from and
after its passage, approval, and posting.
   ADOPTED this 7th day of September, 1999, pursuant to the following roll call
vote:
   AYES: Trustees Aquilino, Derning, Duhl, Hilton, Lien and Powell
   NAYS: None
   ABSENT: None
   APPROVED this 7th day of September, 1999.
   Signed:
   /ss/Louise A. Holland
   Village President
