ORDINANCE NO. M-585-99
AN ORDINANCE GRANTING A VARIATION IN THE APPLICATION OF THE ZONING ORDINANCE OF
THE VILLAGE OF WINNETKA COOK COUNTY, ILLINOIS (545 Sheridan Road)
   WHEREAS, there has been presented to the Council of the Village of Winnetka,
Cook County, Illinois, the request of the owner of the following described real
estate (the “Subject Property”):
The Westerly 170 feet of Lot 1 only in Owner’s Re-subdivision of Block 18
(except Northerly 33) feet together with vacated Baldwin Place, lying within
said Block 18 and accretions thereto in Winnetka, a Subdivision of Northeast
Quarter of Section 20 and North Half of Fractional Section 21, Township 42
North, Range 13 East of the Third Principal Meridian, in Lake County, Illinois.
commonly known as 545 Sheridan Road, Winnetka, Illinois, located in the R-
2 Single-Family Residential Zoning District provided in the Winnetka Zoning
Ordinance, Chapter 22, Winnetka Village Code, for variations from several
provisions of Section 22.07 of the Winnetka Zoning Ordinance, all to permit
structural alterations to an existing attached garage, as more fully described
in the plans and specifications submitted with the June 10, 1999, said
variations being as follows: (a) a variation from the setback requirements of
Section 22.07(h), to allow a front setback of 45.45 feet, whereas 50.0 feet are
required, resulting in a variation of 4.55 feet (9.17%); (b) a variation from
the side yard requirements of Section 22.07(i), to allow a north side yard of
5.95 feet, whereas 12.0 feet are required, a variation of 6.05 feet (50.4%);
and (c) a variation from paragraph 1 of Section 22.07(p) to allow a front
facing garage door having a width of 16 feet, whereas a width of 9 feet is
permitted, resulting in a variation of 7 feet, on the Subject Property; and
   WHEREAS, on July 12, 1999, on due notice thereof, the Zoning Board of
Appeals conducted a public hearing on the requested variations and by the
unanimous vote of the six members then present, has reported to the Council
recommending that the requested variations be granted; and
   WHEREAS, there are practical difficulties and unique hardships associated
with carrying out the strict application of the Zoning Ordinance with respect
to the Subject Property in that the Subject Property is a corner lot which is
subject to setbacks along both street frontages, the existing attached garage
observes a nonconforming front setback and side yard, and the only way to
modify the garage to accommodate two cars without increasing the garage’s
footprint is to allow the single garage door that has been requested; and
   WHEREAS, the Subject Property cannot yield a reasonable return if permitted
to be used only under the conditions allowed by the Zoning Ordinance, in that:
the existing garage can only be used by a single vehicle, the existing garage
door is unsafe and in need of replacement; there are no conforming alternatives
that would allow the existing garage to accommodate two cars; removing the
garage and rebuilding it in a conforming location would be unreasonably costly
and would reduce the value of the property by altering the appearance of the
residence and placing the garage on the opposite side of the Subject Property,
away from the entrances to the residence, and away from the direct access to
the kitchen and mud room that now exists; and
   WHEREAS, the requested variations will not alter the essential character of
the neighborhood because the scope of the exterior modifications is minor and
the modifications are designed to be more consistent with the architectural
style of the residence; and
   WHEREAS, the requested variations will not impair an adequate supply of
light and air because the building height and building footprint will not be
changed; and
   WHEREAS, the requested variations will not increase the hazard from fire and
other dangers to the Subject Property as it will comply with all applicable
building, fire protection and life safety codes; and
   WHEREAS, the requested variations will not diminish the taxable value of
land and buildings throughout the Village, and the taxable value of the Subject
Property may be increased because of the proposed improvements; and
   WHEREAS, the proposed modifications to the garage will not contribute to
congestion on the public streets, as the Subject Property will continue to be
used for a single family residence and the capacity of the garage will be
increased; and
   WHEREAS, there is no evidence that the proposed modifications to the garage
will otherwise impair the public health, safety, comfort, morals, and welfare
of the inhabitants of the Village.
   NOW, THEREFORE, the Council of the Village of Winnetka do ordain as follows:
   SECTION 1 : That the foregoing recitals are hereby incorporated as the
findings of the Council of the Village of Winnetka, as if fully set forth
herein.
   SECTION 2: That the following variations are hereby granted to the Subject
Property, commonly known as 545 Sheridan Road, Winnetka, Illinois, located in
the R-2 Single-Family Residential Zoning District provided in the Winnetka
Zoning Ordinance, Chapter 22, Winnetka Village Code, to allow structural
alterations to an existing attached garage, as more fully described in the
plans and specifications submitted with the June 10, 1999, application for
variation: (a) a variation from the setback requirements of Section 22.07(h),
to allow a front setback of 45.45 feet, whereas 50.0 feet are required,
resulting in a variation of 4.55 feet (9.17%); (b) a variation from the side
yard requirements of Section 22.07(i), to allow a north side yard of 5.95 feet,
whereas 12.0 feet are required, a variation of 6.05 feet (50.4%); and (c) a
variation from paragraph 1 of Section 22.07(p) to allow a front facing garage
door having a width of 16 feet, whereas 9 feet is permitted, resulting in a
variation of 7 feet.
   SECTION 3: That the variation hereby granted is conditioned upon the
commencement of the proposed construction within 12 months after the effective
date of this Ordinance.
   SECTION 4: This Ordinance shall take effect immediately upon passage,
approval and posting.
   ADOPTED this 17th day of August, 1999, pursuant to the following roll call
vote:
   AYES: Trustees Derning, Aquilino, Hilton, Powell and Lien
   NAYS: None
   ABSENT: President Holland
   APPROVED this 17th day of August, 1999.
   Signed:
   /ss/Michael F. Duhl
   President Pro Tem
Countersigned:
/ss/Douglas G. Williams
Village Clerk
