ORDINANCE NO. M-589-99
AN ORDINANCE CHANGING THE NAME OF THE ALLEY EXTENDING FROM TOWER ROAD TO GAGE
STREET ALONG THE WEST SIDE OF THE RAILROAD CUT
   WHEREAS, there exists within the Village of Winnetka, an alley that adjoins
the west edge of the railroad right-of-way between Tower Road north to Gage
Street (the “Alley”); and
   WHEREAS, several buildings abut the west edge of the Alley and are the
locations of various service and retail businesses, all of which are accessible
only from the Alley; and
   WHEREAS, the Alley has never been given a name, and all of the buildings and
businesses fronting on the Alley bear Tower Road addresses, although the Alley
runs in a north-south direction, while Tower Road is an east-west roadway; and
   WHEREAS, the owners and operators of the businesses located along the Alley
have requested that the Alley be named “Tower Court;” and
   WHEREAS, the Council of the Village of Winnetka find that the use of a Tower
Road address for businesses that are neither located on nor visible from Tower
Road can be confusing to persons not familiar with the area and can hinder
access by consumers; and
   WHEREAS, paragraph six of Article III, Section 4, of the Village Charter
gives the Village Council exclusive power and control over the streets and
alleys within the Village; and
   WHEREAS, Section 11-80-19 of the Illinois Municipal Code, 65 ILCS 5/11-80-
19, establishes the procedure whereby corporate authorities may name or change
the names of any street, avenue, alley or other public place; and
   WHEREAS, the Fire Department, Police Department and Department of Public
Works have reviewed and approved the requested name change; and
   WHEREAS, the Council of the Village of Winnetka find that the public safety
and welfare will best be served by designating the Alley as Tower Court.
   NOW, THEREFORE, the Council of the Village of Winnetka do ordain as follows:
   SECTION 1: That the foregoing recitals are hereby incorporated as the
findings of the Council of the Village of Winnetka, as if fully set forth
herein.
   SECTION 2: That the alley adjoining the west edge of the railroad right-of-
way in the Village of Winnetka from Tower Road north to Gage Street is hereby
named “Tower Court,” said name change to be effective thirty days after the
date of the notices issued pursuant to the following Section 3 of this
Ordinance.
   SECTION 3 : The Village Clerk is hereby directed to send written notice of
the change in name to the Election Department of the Cook County Clerk and to
the Postmaster of the Winnetka Branch of the United States Postal Service. Said
notice shall be sent by certified or registered mail and shall include the date
of the passage and approval of this Ordinance, the effective date of the change
in name, and a certified copy of this Ordinance.
   SECTION 4 : Upon the effective date of the name change, the street addresses
of all businesses and other premises having their principal access by way of
the alley adjoining the west edge of the railroad right-of-way from Tower Road
north to Gage Street shall be changed from “Tower Road” to “Tower Court,”
without changing the street number of said addresses.
   SECTION 5: This Ordinance shall take effect immediately upon passage,
approval and posting.
   ADOPTED this 5th day of October, 1999, pursuant to the following roll call
vote:
   AYES: Trustees Derning, Duhl, Hilton, Lien, Powell, Aquilino
   NAYS: None
   ABSENT: None
   APPROVED this 5th day of October, 1999.
   Signed:
