ORDINANCE NO. M-7-2000 – 894 Cherry zoning variation - VOID
ORDINANCE NO. M-8-2000
AN ORDINANCE GRANTING A VARIATION IN THE APPLICATION OF THE ZONING ORDINANCE OF
THE VILLAGE OF WINNETKA COOK COUNTY, ILLINOIS (687 CHERRY STREET)
   WHEREAS, there has been presented to the Council of the Village of Winnetka,
Cook County, Illinois, the request of the owner of the following described real
estate (the “Subject Property”):
   All that part of Block 37 in Winnetka, being a subdivision of the northeast
quarter (1/4) of Section 20 and the north fractional half (1/2) of Section 21,
Township 42 North, Range 13 East of the Third Principal Meridian, in Cook
County, Illinois, according to the plat thereof recorded March 1, 1858, in Book
143 of Maps, page 53 as document 98349 and re-recorded August 8, 1873, as
Document 119381, described as follows beginning at a point in the north line of
Cherry Street intersected by a line, 150.0 feet west of (as measured at right
angles) and parallel with the westerly line of Maple Street, thence west along
said north line of Cherry Street, 56.0 feet; thence north along a line parallel
with the westerly line of Maple Street, thence west along said north line of
Cherry Street, 56.0 feet; thence north along a line parallel with the westerly
line of Maple Street, 126.46 feet more or less to its intersection with a line
drawn at right angles to the easterly line of the right of way of the Chicago
North Shore and Milwaukee Railroad at a point 95.0 feet northerly (as measured
along said right of way line from the north line of Cherry Street); thence
northeasterly along said line drawn at right angles to the easterly line of
said right of way, a distance of 6.47 feet more or less to its intersection
with a line 200.0 feet west of the westerly line of Maple Street, 4.9 feet more
or less to its intersection with a line 240.0 feet (as measured at right
angles) south of and parallel with the south line of Oak Street; thence east
along said line 240.0 feet south of and parallel with the south line of Oak
Street, 50.12 feet to its intersection with a line 150.0 feet (measured at
right angles) west of and parallel with the westerly line of Maple Street;
thence south along said line, 150.0 feet west of and parallel with the westerly
line of Maple Street, a distance of 134.36 feet to the point of beginning, in
Cook County, Illinois.
commonly known as 687 Cherry Street, Winnetka, Illinois, and located in R-
4 Single-Family Residential Zoning District provided in the Winnetka Zoning
Ordinance, Chapter 17, Winnetka Village Code, for the following variations: (a)
a variation from the intensity of use of lot limitations of Section 17.16.010.F
of the Zoning Ordinance to allow a total roofed lot coverage of 1,901.80 square
feet, whereas 1,867.25 square feet are permitted, resulting in a variation of
34.55 square feet (2.00%); and (b) a variation from the maximum building size
(gross floor area) limitations of Section 17.16.010.G of the Zoning Ordinance
to allow a total gross floor area of 3,944.89 square feet, whereas 2,987.00
square feet are permitted, resulting in a variation of 951.29 square feet (32%)
for the purpose of constructing a new 6-square foot masonry chimney, adding a
masonry veneer to the entire building, and making structural alterations,
including a 25.46-square foot addition to the second floor, in order to convert
the existing two-family residence into a single-family residence, in accordance
with the application for variation and plans accompanying the application; and
   WHEREAS, on March 13, 2000, on due notice thereof, the Zoning Board of
Appeals conducted a public hearing on the requested variation and by the
unanimous vote of the six members then present, has reported to the Council
recommending that the requested variations be granted; and
   WHEREAS, the requested variations are in harmony with the general purpose
and intent of the Winnetka Zoning Ordinance, because the proposed improvements
will decrease the extent of nonconformities on the Subject Property by
converting the building from a two-family dwelling to a permitted single-family
dwelling and by reducing the amount of impermeable surface by 1,329.8 square
feet; and
   WHEREAS, there are practical difficulties and unique hardships associated
with carrying out the strict application of the Zoning Ordinance with respect
to the Subject Property in that the Subject Property is adjacent to the B-
1 Multi-Family Residential Zoning District, is improved with a nonconforming
two-family dwelling, and has other existing nonconformities in lot width, lot
area, roofed lot coverage, gross floor area, impermeable surface and east side
yard, and in that, although the proposed variations will increase roofed lot
coverage by six square feet and the gross floor area by 25.46 square feet, the
proposed modifications will eliminate the nonconformity in impermeable surface,
and will eliminate the nonconforming use by converting the structure into a
conforming single-family dwelling; and
   WHEREAS, the Subject Property cannot yield a reasonable return if permitted
to be used only under the conditions allowed by the Zoning Ordinance, in that
bringing the Subject Property into full conformity with all zoning requirements
and limitations would require that the building be demolished and replaced with
a new structure; and
   WHEREAS, the requested variation will not alter the essential character of
the neighborhood because the building alterations and additions will allow the
Subject Property to be used as a single-family residence in conformity with the
zoning district in which it is located, and will result in a uniform masonry
veneer for the entire building, which was constructed in 1929 and has existed
in its present form since the construction of an addition in 1951; and
   WHEREAS, on November 17, 1998, the Village Council adopted ordinance M-551-
98, which granted a variation for similar work to convert the building to a
single-family residence; and
   WHEREAS, the building alterations that were approved by ordinance M-551-98
were never done, and the variations granted by that ordinance have expired; and
   WHEREAS, the alterations being proposed by the applicants add less area to
the roofed lot coverage and gross floor area than the alterations approved by
M-551-98, which were requested by the previous owners of the Subject Property;
and
   WHEREAS, the requested variations will not impair an adequate supply of
light and air because the size of the new chimney is minimal and the additional
floor area on the second floor results from replacing an existing stairway and
aligning the roof and exterior walls with the rest of the building; and
   WHEREAS, the requested variations will not increase the hazard from fire and
other dangers to the Subject Property as the proposed additions will comply
with all applicable building and fire protection codes; and
   WHEREAS, the requested variations will not diminish the taxable value of
land and buildings throughout the Village, and the taxable value of the Subject
Property may be increased because of the proposed improvements; and
   WHEREAS, the proposed alterations and additions will not contribute to
congestion on the public streets, as they will reconfigure the structure from a
two-family dwelling to a single-family dwelling; and
   WHEREAS, the requested variation is in harmony with the general purpose and
intent of the Winnetka Zoning Ordinance, in that it allows the renovation,
restoration and rehabilitation of a structurally sound existing building while
maintaining the existing scale and appearance of the community and protecting
established trees and landscaping.
   WHEREAS, there is no evidence that the proposed alterations and additions
will otherwise impair the public health, safety, comfort, morals, and welfare
of the inhabitants of the Village.
   NOW, THEREFORE, the Council of the Village of Winnetka do ordain as follows:
   SECTION 1: That the foregoing recitals are hereby incorporated as the
findings of the Council of the Village of Winnetka, as if fully set forth
herein.
   SECTION 2:  That variations are hereby granted with respect to the Subject
Property, commonly known as 687 Cherry Street, Winnetka, Illinois, which is
located in the R-4 Single-Family Residential District provided in the Winnetka
Zoning Ordinance, Chapter 17, Winnetka Village Code, for the following
variations: (a) a variation from the intensity of use of lot limitations of
Section 17.16.010.F of the Zoning Ordinance to allow a total roofed lot
coverage of 1,901.80 square feet, whereas 1,867.25 square feet are permitted,
resulting in a variation of 34.55 square feet (2.00%); and (b) a variation from
the maximum building size (gross floor area) limitations of Section 17.16.010.G
of the Zoning Ordinance to allow a total gross floor area of 3,944.89 square
feet, whereas 2,987.00 square feet are permitted, resulting in a variation of
951.29 square feet (32%) for the purpose of constructing a new 6-square foot
masonry chimney, adding a masonry veneer to the entire building, and making
structural alterations, including a 25.46-square foot addition to the second
floor, in order to convert the existing two-family residence into a single-
family residence, in accordance with the application for variation and plans
accompanying the application.
   SECTION 3: That the variations hereby granted are conditioned upon the
commencement of the proposed construction within twelve months after the
effective date of this Ordinance.
   SECTION 4: This Ordinance shall take effect immediately upon passage,
approval and posting.
   ADOPTED this 2nd day of May, 2000, pursuant to the following roll call vote:
   AYES: Trustees Aquilino, Brower, Lien, Powell, Presser and Woodbury
