ORDINANCE NO. M-14-2000
AN ORDINANCE GRANTING A VARIATION IN THE APPLICATION OF THE ZONING ORDINANCE OF
THE VILLAGE OF WINNETKA COOK COUNTY, ILLINOIS (381 Poplar Street)
   WHEREAS, there has been presented to the Council of the Village of Winnetka,
Cook County, Illinois, the request of the owner of the following described real
estate (the “Subject Property”):
That part lying North of a line drawn parallel to and 112.0 feet North of the
North line of Willow Road of the following described property: The west 65.0
feet measured from the east line of Poplar Street of the South ½ of Block 67 in
Winnetka, a Subdivision of the Northeast ¼ of Section 20 and the Northeast
fractional ½ of Section 21, all in Township 42 North, Range 13, East of the
Third Principal Meridian, in Cook County, Illinois.
commonly known as 381 Poplar Street, Winnetka, Illinois, and located in the R-
4 Single Family Zoning District provided in Chapter 17.16 of the Winnetka
Zoning Ordinance, Title 17 of the Winnetka Village Code, for the following
variations: (a) from the intensity of use of lot limitations of Section
17.16.010.F, to permit a roofed lot coverage of 1,298 square feet, although the
maximum allowable is 1,207.38 square feet, resulting in a variation of 90.99
square feet (7.54%); (b) from the setback requirements of Section 17.16.010.H,
to permit a front yard setback of 15.24 feet, although a 30.00-foot setback is
required, resulting in a variation of 14.76 feet (49.20%); and (c) from the
side yard requirements of Section 17.16.010.I, to permit a north side yard of
5.07 feet , although a minimum of 6.0 feet is required, resulting in a
variation of 0.93 feet (15.5%); all to allow the construction of an addition to
the first floor and the replacement of the second floor of the residence on the
Subject Property; and
   WHEREAS, as originally filed, the plaintiffs’ application also included a
request, which was withdrawn on April 10, 2000, at the end of the Zoning Board
of Appeals hearing, to construct a detached garage, which would have required
additional variations from the roofed lot coverage, gross floor area, south
side yard and rear yard requirements imposed by the Zoning Ordinance; and
   WHEREAS, on April 10, 2000, on due notice thereof, the Zoning Board of
Appeals conducted a public hearing on the requested variations and by the
unanimous vote of the 4 members then present, has reported to the Council
recommending that the requested variations be granted; and
   WHEREAS, there are practical difficulties and unique hardships associated
with carrying out the strict application of the Zoning Ordinance with respect
to the Subject Property in that: (a) the Subject Property is a shallow,
relatively square, legally nonconforming lot that was created by a metes and
bounds division prior to the Village’s adoption of its Subdivision Ordinance,
and has a total lot area of 4,825.50 square feet; (b) the single-family
residence on the Subject Property was constructed in the 1880’s, prior to the
adoption of the Village’s original Zoning Ordinance and prior to the time that
the Village first began issuing building permits; and (c) the existing
nonconformities in setback, side yard and intensity of use of lot cannot be
cured without removing a significant portion of the residence; and
   WHEREAS, the Subject Property cannot yield a reasonable return if permitted
to be used only under the conditions allowed by the Zoning Ordinance, in that
the proposed modifications are necessary to retrofit the existing home to
accommodate a more functional, modern layout, including an increase in headroom
in the second floor; and
   WHEREAS, the requested variation will not alter the essential character of
the neighborhood because the proposed changes are consistent with the original
style and historical character of the building and will maintain the existing
scale and presence of the residence within the neighborhood; and
   WHEREAS, the requested variations will not impair an adequate supply of
light and air because the proposed building addition raises the height of the
building within permitted limits and the existing building is located closest
to the north and east lot lines of the Subject Property, which abut the rear
yards of the adjoining parcels; and
   WHEREAS, the requested variations will not increase the hazard from fire and
other dangers to the Subject Property as the proposed work will comply with all
applicable building and fire protection codes; and
   WHEREAS, the requested variation will not diminish the taxable value of land
and buildings throughout the Village, and the taxable value of the Subject
Property may be increased because of the proposed improvements; and
   WHEREAS, the proposed building additions will not contribute to congestion
on the public streets, as the building and subject property will continue to be
used for single-family residential purposes; and
   WHEREAS, there is no evidence that the proposed building additions will
otherwise impair the public health, safety, comfort, morals, and welfare of the
inhabitants of the Village.
   WHEREAS, the requested variations are in harmony with the general purpose
and intent of the Winnetka Zoning Ordinance, in that they will allow the
renovation, restoration and rehabilitation of a structurally sound building
that has existed in the current location for more than 100 years, while
maintaining the existing scale and appearance of the community and protecting
established trees and landscaping.
   NOW, THEREFORE, the Council of the Village of Winnetka do ordain as follows:
   SECTION 1: That the foregoing recitals are hereby incorporated as the
findings of the Council of the Village of Winnetka, as if fully set forth
herein.
   SECTION 2:  That variations are hereby granted to the Subject Property,
commonly known as 381 Poplar Street, Winnetka, Illinois, and located in the R-
4 Single Family Zoning District provided in Chapter 17.16 of the Winnetka
Zoning Ordinance, Title 17 of the Winnetka Village Code, for the following
variations: (a) from the intensity of use of lot limitations of Section
17.16.010.F, to permit a roofed lot coverage of 1,298 square feet, although the
maximum allowable is 1,207.38 square feet, resulting in a variation of 90.99
square feet (7.54%); (b) from the setback requirements of Section 17.16.010.H,
to permit a front yard setback of 15.24 feet, although a 30.00-foot setback is
required, resulting in a variation of 14.76 feet (49.20%); and (c) from the
side yard requirements of Section 17.16.010.I, to permit a north side yard of
5.07 feet , although a minimum of 6.0 feet is required, resulting in a
variation of 0.93 feet (15.5%); all to allow the construction of an addition to
the first floor and the replacement of the second floor of the residence on the
Subject Property, in accordance with the plans and specifications submitted
with the application for variations as amended by the withdrawal of the request
for the construction of the detached garage.
   SECTION 3: That the variations hereby granted are conditioned upon the
commencement of the proposed construction within 12 months after the effective
date of this Ordinance.
   SECTION 4: This Ordinance shall take effect immediately upon passage,
approval and posting.
   ADOPTED this 6th day of June, 2000, pursuant to the following roll call
vote:
   AYES: Trustees Brower, Presser, Aquilino, Powell and Lien
   NAYS: None
   ABSENT: Trustee Woodbury
   APPROVED this 6th day of June, 2000.
   Signed:
   /ss/Louise A. Holland
   Village President
Countersigned:
/ss/Douglas G. Williams
Village Clerk
Introduced: May 16, 2000
Posted: May 17, 2000
Passed and Approved: June 6, 2000
