ORDINANCE NO. M-19-2000 (Not Adopted)
AN ORDINANCE GRANTING A SPECIAL USE PERMIT TO ALLOW SURFACE PARKING FOR A NEW
BUILDING TO BE CONSTRUCTED AT 576-582 LINCOLN AVENUE IN THE VILLAGE OF WINNETKA
   WHEREAS, there has been presented to the Council of the Village of Winnetka,
Cook County, Illinois, the request of the owner of the following described real
estate (the “Subject Property”):
Lot 1 in Donovan Bulger consolidation of the East 120.0 feet of Lot 5 and the
East 120 feet of the North 30 feet of Lot 6 in Louis D. Webster’s Re-
subdivision of Lots 6, 8, 9, and 10 (Except the North 75 feet) Block 11 in Park
Addition to Winnetka, East of the Third Principal Meridian, in Cook County,
Illinois.
commonly known as 576-582 Lincoln Avenue, Winnetka, Illinois, and located in
the C-2 General Retail Zoning District provided in Chapter 17.44 of the
Winnetka Zoning Ordinance, Title 17 of the Winnetka Village Code, for a special
use permit pursuant to Section 17.44.010.K.11 and Chapter 17.56 of the Zoning
Ordinance to allow 5 of the parking spaces required for the proposed
redevelopment of the Subject Property to be located at ground level; and
   WHEREAS, the Subject Property is located on the west side of Lincoln Avenue,
just to the north of the commercial overlay in the East Elm business district;
and
   WHEREAS, the properties adjoining the Subject Property to the north and are
both developed with small commercial buildings, and the property adjoining the
Subject Property to the west is the site of the Lincoln Avenue parking lot, a
public parking facility owned and operated by the Village of Winnetka; and
   WHEREAS, the applicant proposes to redevelop the Subject Property with a 2.5
story structure that will contain the North Shore Community Bank and other
offices; and
   WHEREAS, the applicant proposes to place most of its off-street parking
underground, as required by the Zoning Ordinance, but proposes to place 5 of
the required spaces adjacent to the south building line of the new structure;
and
   WHEREAS, the proposed grade level parking will be accessed directly from
Lincoln Avenue through a 10-foot wide private alley, which comprises the south
5 feet of the Subject Property and the north 5 feet of the adjacent property to
the south; and
   WHEREAS, the applicants propose to make the private alley one way,
westbound, with egress to be made by way of a proposed 18-foot wide service
drive that would be located entirely on the Village’s Lincoln Avenue Parking
Lot, adjoining the west lot line of the Subject Properly; and
   WHEREAS, the applicants also propose to provide ingress and egress to the
underground parking by way of a ramp that would also be located entirely on the
Village’s Lincoln Avenue Parking Lot; and
   WHEREAS, the applicants made a similar request for surface parking in 1999,
in conjunction with their application for a 2.5 story bank and office building
with a drive-through facility, but the application was withdrawn without final
consideration of the surface parking request after the Village Council denied
the request for the drive-through facility; and
   WHEREAS, on May 18, 2000, on due notice thereof, the Design Review Board
considered the applicant’s proposal and issued unanimous favorable comment on
the architectural features of the new building, while expressing concerns about
a directional sign for the parking access ramp, which the applicants propose to
place in the right-of-way, north of the building; and
   WHEREAS, on June 12, 2000, on due notice thereof, the Zoning Board of
Appeals held a public hearing on the requested special use and, by the
favorable vote of the five of the six members then present, has reported to the
Council recommending that the requested special use permit be granted; and
   WHEREAS, on June 28, 2000, on due notice thereof, the Plan Commission
considered the proposal and its request for a special use and has submitted
extensive findings to the Village Council, with the 11 members of the
Commission then in attendance unanimously finding that the proposal, is
consistent with the Winnetka Comprehensive Plan, Winnetka 2020, and
recommending that the special use permit be granted; and
   WHEREAS, the Village Engineer provided comment to the Village Council on the
proposed access plan for the Subject Property in a memorandum dated June 27,
2000, noting that the proposed underground ramp will eliminate some public
parking spaces and that it also has a restrictive impact on future use of the
Village’s parking lot for a parking deck
   WHEREAS, the proposed exterior parking at ground level will not be
detrimental to the public health, safety, comfort and welfare of the
inhabitants of the Village in that it enables the applicants to fully comply
with the Zoning Ordinance’s parking requirements; and
   WHEREAS, the proposed exterior parking at ground level will not be
substantially injurious to the use and enjoyment of other property in the
immediate vicinity and will not substantially diminish or impair property
values in the immediate vicinity because the surface parking spaces will be
private spaces that will accommodate the users of the proposed building and
will thereby reduce the building’s demand for public parking; and
   WHEREAS, there is no evidence that construction of the proposed ground level
parking subject to the terms and conditions of this ordinance will impede the
normal and orderly development or improvement of other property in the
immediate vicinity; and
   WHEREAS, adequate measures have been taken to provide ingress and egress in
a manner which minimizes pedestrian and vehicular traffic congestion in the
public ways, in that the one-way entrance off Lincoln Avenue improves
visibility and safety; and
   WHEREAS, adequate utilities, access roads, drainage and other facilities
necessary for the operation of the proposed special use on the Subject Property
will be provided when the proposed ground level parking is constructed in
compliance with applicable Village Code requirements; and
   WHEREAS, the proposed ground level parking, when constructed in accordance
with the terms and conditions of this ordinance, will conform to the applicable
regulations of the Zoning Ordinance and the Winnetka Village Code;
   NOW, THEREFORE, the Council of the Village of Winnetka do ordain as follows:
   SECTION 1 : That the foregoing recitals are hereby incorporated as the
findings of the Council of the Village of Winnetka, as if fully set forth
herein.
   SECTION 2: Pursuant to Section 17.40.010.K.11 of the Winnetka Zoning
Ordinance, a special use permit is hereby granted to the Subject Property,
which is commonly known as 518 Winnetka Avenue, Winnetka, Illinois, and is
located in the C-2 General Retail Commercial District provided in Chapter 17.40
of the Winnetka Zoning Ordinance, Title 17 of the Winnetka Village Code, to
permit 21 parking spaces to be located at the street level, subject to the
terms and conditions hereinafter set forth.
   SECTION 3: That the special use hereby granted is subject to the condition
that the Applicants enter into an access agreement to provide the use of a
portion of the Lincoln Avenue parking lot for ingress and egress to the
underground parking on the Subject Property, said agreement to be approved by
the Village Council.
   SECTION 4: That the special use hereby granted is further conditioned upon
the commencement of the proposed construction within 12 months after the
effective date of this Ordinance.
   SECTION 5: This Ordinance shall take effect immediately upon passage,
approval and posting.
   ADOPTED this ________ day of September, 2000, pursuant to the following roll
call vote:
   AYES:    
   NAYS:    
   ABSENT:    
   APPROVED this _____day of _______________, 2000.
   Signed:
   _________________________
   Village President
