ORDINANCE NO. M-23-2000
AN ORDINANCE GRANTING A VARIATION IN THE APPLICATION OF THE ZONING ORDINANCE OF
THE VILLAGE OF WINNETKA COOK COUNTY, ILLINOIS (567 Hill Terrace)
   WHEREAS, there has been presented to the Council of the Village of Winnetka,
Cook County, Illinois, the request of the owner of the following described real
estate (the “Subject Property”):
That part lying within Lots 1 and 2 in Whitman’s Subdivision of part of the S¼
of the SW¼ of fractional Section 21, Township 42 North, Range 13, East of the
Third Principal Meridian, according to the plat thereof recorded July 10, 1914,
as Document No. 5454153 in Book 130 of Plats, page 20 described as follows:
Beginning at a point in the North line of said Lot 2, 64.97 feet East from the
Northwest corner of said Lot 2 (as measured along the North line thereof);
thence Southeasterly in a straight line parallel with the West line of Lot 3 of
said Subdivision (which last mentioned West line is East line of Church Road)
to a point in the South line of said Lot 1 which point is 25 feet East from the
Southwest corner of said Lot 1 (as measured along the South line thereof);
thence East along the South line of said Lot 1, 50 feet to the Southeast corner
thereof; thence Northwesterly along a straight line parallel with the said West
line of said Lot 3 to a point in the North line of said Lot 1 which point is
39.97 feet East from the Northwest corner of said Lot 1 (as measured along the
North line thereof); thence 50 feet West along the North lines of said Lots 1
and 2 to the point of beginning together with half of private road known as
Hill Terrace South of and adjoining said premises, in Cook County, Illinois.
commonly known as 567 Hill Terrace, Winnetka, Illinois, and located in the R-
4 Single Family Residential District provided in Chapter 17.12 of the Winnetka
Zoning Ordinance, Title 17, Winnetka Village Code, for a variation from the
maximum building size (Gross Floor Area) limitations of Section 17.12.010(G) to
allow a gross floor area of 3,868.28 square feet, whereas 3,433.80 square feet
are permitted, resulting in a variation of 434.48 square feet (12.65%), and for
a variation from the building line articulation requirements of Section
17.12.010(Q) to allow the existing nonconforming west building line to be
extended vertically, said variations being requested for the purpose of
allowing the construction of a second story addition above the northern portion
of the existing first story at the rear of the residence on the Subject
Property; and
   WHEREAS, there are practical difficulties and particular hardships
associated with carrying out the strict application of the Zoning Ordinance
with respect to the Subject Property in that: (a) the Subject Property and the
other parcels on the same block face are located between Church Street and
Green Bay Road and, as a result, the Subject Property’s side lot lines are not
perpendicular to the front lot line; (b) the building line articulation
requirements were added to the Winnetka Zoning Ordinance in 1999; (c) when the
building line articulation requirements are applied to the residence on the
Subject Property, which was constructed in 1924, all but a small, triangular
portion near the center of the house is in a conforming location because the
sides of the house are not fully parallel to the side lot lines; (d) because of
the non-perpendicular side lot lines, the garage, which is parallel to the side
lot lines, is not parallel to the rear lot line, as a result of which only a
small, triangular portion of the garage is not located in the rear quarter of
the lot; and (e) the garage cannot reasonably be located farther back in the
lot because the angle of the side lot lines would cause the garage to be
shifted farther to the west, which would place it almost directly behind the
house, obstructing views, adding driveway surface in the middle of the yard,
and reducing the utility of the back yard; and
   WHEREAS, the Subject Property cannot yield a reasonable return if permitted
to be used only under the conditions allowed by the Zoning Ordinance, in that
the proposed variations are being requested to add a master bedroom suite and
the nonconforming building line cannot be corrected without either removing the
entire rear portion of the house or carving off a triangular portion, both of
which would substantially reduce the utility and value of the Subject Property;
and
   WHEREAS, the requested variations will not alter the essential character of
the neighborhood, in that the proposed addition will be consistent with the
style of the existing house and will be located at the rear of the house and
therefore it will not substantially impact the streetscape; and
   WHEREAS, the requested variations will not impair an adequate supply of
light and air because the addition conforms with building height and setback
requirements and the small, triangular nonconforming portion is of such a
minimal size that it has no visual impact; and
   WHEREAS, the requested variations will not increase the hazard from fire and
other dangers to the Subject Property as it will comply with all applicable
building and fire protection codes; and
   WHEREAS, the requested variations will not diminish the taxable value of
land and buildings throughout the Village, and the taxable value of the Subject
Property may be increased because of the proposed addition; and
   WHEREAS, the requested variations will not contribute to congestion on the
public streets, as the structure will continue to be used as a single family
residence; and
   WHEREAS, there is no evidence that the requested variations will otherwise
impair the public health, safety, comfort, morals, and welfare of the
inhabitants of the Village.
   WHEREAS, July 10, 2000, on due notice thereof, the Zoning Board of Appeals
conducted a public hearing on the requested variations and by the unanimous
vote of the six members then present, has reported to the Council recommending
that the variations be granted.
   NOW, THEREFORE, the Council of the Village of Winnetka do ordain:
   SECTION 1: That the foregoing recitals are incorporated as the findings of
the Council of the Village of Winnetka, as if fully set forth herein.
   SECTION 2: That the following variations are hereby granted with respect to
the Subject Property, commonly known as 567 Hill Terrace, which is located in
the R-4 Single Family Residential District provided in Chapter 17.12 of the
Winnetka Zoning Ordinance, Title 17, Winnetka Village Code: (a) a variation
from the maximum building size (Gross Floor Area) limitations of Section
17.12.010(G) to allow a gross floor area of 3,868.28 square feet, whereas
3,433.80 square feet are permitted, resulting in a variation of 434.48 square
feet (12.65%), and (b) a variation from the building line articulation
requirements of Section 17.12.010(Q) to allow the existing nonconforming west
building line to be extended vertically, said variations being requested for
the purpose of allowing the construction of a second story addition above the
northern portion of the existing first story at the rear of the residence on
the Subject Property.
   SECTION 3: That the variations hereby granted are conditioned upon the
commencement of the proposed construction within 12 months after the effective
date of this Ordinance.
   SECTION 4: That this Ordinance shall be in full force and effect from and
after its passage, approval, and posting.
   ADOPTED this 5th day of September, 2000, pursuant to the following roll call
vote:
   AYES: Trustees Aquilino, Brower, Lien, Powell and Woodbury
   NAYS: None
   ABSENT: Trustee Presser
   APPROVED this 5th day of September, 2000.
   Signed:
   /ss/Louise A. Holland
   Village President
Countersigned:
/ss/Douglas G. Williams
Village Clerk
Introduced: August 15, 2000
Posted: August 16, 2000
Passed and Approved: September 5, 2000
