ORDINANCE NO. M-31-2000
AN ORDINANCE GRANTING A SPECIAL USE PERMIT FOR THE INSTALLATION OF WIRELESS
TELECOMMUNICATIONS ANTENNAS AND EQUIPMENT AT 566 CHESTNUT, WINNETKA, ILLINOIS
   WHEREAS, the LaSalle Bank National Association is the trustee for Trust No.
R-1896, which owns the following described real estate (the “Subject Property”)
for the benefit of the Winnetka Laundry Partnership (the “Owners”):
   Lots 1,2 and 3 in Depot Place Subdivision of Block 13 in original Village of
Winnetka in the east half of the North East quarter of Section 20, Township 42
North, Range 13 East, of the Third Principal Meridian according to the plat
thereof recorded March 09, 1891 as document number 1430559, all in Cook County,
Illinois,
which is commonly known as 566 Chestnut Street, Winnetka, Illinois, located in
the C-2 General Retail Commercial Zoning District provided in the Winnetka
Zoning Ordinance, Title 17 of the Winnetka Village Code; and
   WHEREAS, Cook Inlet/VoiceStream Operating Company LLC (“VoiceStream”) has
entered into an agreement with the Owner of the Subject Property, whereby
VoiceStream will be allowed to place certain wireless telecommunications
service antennas and equipment on the chimney located on the roof of the
Laundry Mall building located on the Subject Property; and
   WHEREAS, the Owner and VoiceStream (the “Applicants”) have applied for a
special use permit in accordance with Chapters 17.52 and 17.56 of the Winnetka
Zoning Ordinance, Title 17 of the Winnetka Village Code, to permit the
installation of concealed wireless telecommunication service antennas and
equipment on the chimney located on the roof of the existing Laundry Mall
building on the Subject Property; and
   WHEREAS, on September 11, 2000, on due notice thereof, the Zoning Board of
Appeals conducted a public hearing on the requested special use and by the
unanimous vote of the seven members of the Board, has reported to the Council
recommending that the requested special use permit be granted; and
   WHEREAS, pursuant to a 5 to 2 vote taken at the hearing on September 11,
2000, the Zoning Board of Appeals has further recommended that the Council
limit the height of the shroud proposed to conceal the antennas, so that the
existing chimney height will be maintained, rather than increasing the height
of the chimney by eight feet, as proposed; and
   WHEREAS, on October 4, 2000, the engineer retained by the Village (the
“Independent Engineer”) to perform the independent technical review submitted a
report that supports the application of VoiceStream, finding the data submitted
by VoiceStream to be accurate and complete, and finding that the analysis
techniques, methodologies and conclusions pertaining to the proposed antenna
site are valid; and
   WHEREAS, on September 27, 2000, on due notice thereof, the Plan Commission
met to consider the application and, by the unanimous vote of the 10 members
then present, found that the requested special use is consistent with the
Village’s comprehensive plan; and
   WHEREAS, the data submitted by VoiceStream, and confirmed by the Independent
Engineer, establishes that the proposed site on the Laundry Mall building on
the Subject Property is a matter of absolute engineering necessity, the higher
priority sites established by Section 17.52.010 of the Zoning Ordinance either
being unavailable for a new site or being technically unsuitable for the
coverage sought under VoiceStream’s network design; and
   WHEREAS, the RF coverage projections made by the Applicants and confirmed by
the Independent Engineer establish that antennas on the Subject Property and at
the height proposed are a matter of engineering necessity, in order to provide
adequate height and spacing between sites, to reduce gaps in coverage, to
provide reliable in-building service in the vicinity of downtown Winnetka; and
   WHEREAS, VoiceStream has demonstrated that locating antenna arrays on the
western edge of the golf course, at the Winnetka landfill or Public Works yards
at 1390 Willow Road, or on the golf netting poles at the golf course driving
range, is not technically feasible for its system, in that those locations
would not provide in-building coverage in the residential areas and along the
lake shore, would decrease the reliability of outdoor coverage in the eastern
part of the Village and would be too close to other VoiceStream antenna sites;
and
   WHEREAS, no replacement site is available either on the smokestack of the
Water and Electric Plant or on the monopole of the Public Safety Building; and
   WHEREAS, the proposed antenna site is more than 250 feet away from the
nearest single-family residence; and
   WHEREAS, the Applicants have met the standards for granting special uses for
antenna arrays in the C-2 Zoning District, as set forth in Section 17.52.010
and Section 17.56.010(M) of the Zoning Ordinance; and
   WHEREAS, the requested special use is in harmony with the general purpose
and intent of the Winnetka Zoning Ordinance, in that it furthers the continuing
use of a structurally sound existing building while maintaining the existing
scale and appearance of the community and protecting established trees and
landscaping.
   NOW, THEREFORE, the Council of the Village of Winnetka do ordain as follows:
   SECTION 1 : That the foregoing recitals are hereby incorporated as the
findings of the Council of the Village of Winnetka, as if fully set forth
herein.
   SECTION 2: That a special use permit under Section 17.52.010(N) and Section
17.56.010(M) of the Winnetka Zoning Ordinance is hereby granted with respect to
the Subject Property, which is located in the C-2 General Retail Commercial
Zoning District and is commonly known as 566 Chestnut Street, to allow the
installation of wireless telecommunications antennas and related structures on
and in the building on the Subject Property, in accordance with the plans dated
June 13, 2000, and other materials submitted with and in support of the
application for special use permit, subject to the conditions and limitations
hereinafter set forth.
   SECTION 3: That the special use hereby granted is subject to the following
conditions: (a) that the shroud used to conceal the antennas be of a synthetic
material that matches, as nearly as possible, the existing brick of the chimney
of the Laundry Mall building; and (b) that the Applicants provide structural
engineering certifications, as required by Section 17.52.010(R) of the Zoning
Ordinance, for review and approval prior to the issuance of any building
permit.
   SECTION 4: That the special use hereby granted is further conditioned upon
the commencement of the proposed construction within 12 months after the
effective date of this Ordinance.
   SECTION 5: This Ordinance shall take effect immediately upon passage,
approval and posting.
   ADOPTED this 4th day of December, 2000, pursuant to the following roll call
vote:
   AYES:    Trustees Aquilino, Brower, Lien, Powell and Woodbury
   NAYS:    None
   ABSENT:    Trustee Presser
   APPROVED this 4th day of December, 2000.
   Signed:
   /s/ Louise A. Holland
   Village President
Countersigned:
/s/Douglas G. Williams
Village Clerk
Introduced: November 9, 2000
Posted: November 10, 2000
Passed and Approved: December 4, 2000
