ORDINANCE NO. M-32-2000
AN ORDINANCE GRANTING A VARIATION IN THE APPLICATION OF THE ZONING ORDINANCE OF
THE VILLAGE OF WINNETKA COOK COUNTY, ILLINOIS (191 Linden)
   WHEREAS, there has been presented to the Council of the Village of Winnetka,
Cook County, Illinois, the request of the owner of the following described real
estate (the “Subject Property”):
   Lots 3, 4, 5 and 6 in Block 1, Alles First Addition to Winnetka being a sub.
of that part of the SE ¼ of the SE ¼ of Section 20, T42N, R13 East of the 3rd
Principal Meridian, lying North of the center of Winnetka Avenue, in the
Village of Winnetka, Cook County, Illinois.
commonly known as 191 Linden, Winnetka, Illinois, and located in the R-
3 Single-Family Residential Zoning District provided in the Winnetka Zoning
Ordinance, Title 17, Winnetka Village Code, for a variation from the intensity
of use of lot provisions of Section 17.20.010(F) to add another 245 square feet
to the existing legally nonconforming impermeable lot coverage of 107,030
square feet, resulting in a total impermeable lot coverage of 107,275 square
feet, which exceeds the 86,767.50 square feet of permitted impermeable surface
by 20,507.50 square feet (23.64%) for the purpose of constructing a handicapped
accessible ramp on the Subject Property; and
   WHEREAS, on October 9, 2000, on due notice thereof, the Zoning Board of
Appeals conducted a public hearing on the requested variation and by the
favorable vote of the six members then present, including one abstention, has
reported to the Council recommending that the requested variation be granted;
and
   WHEREAS, the Subject Property is a 175,535.00 square foot parcel that is the
site of Sts. Faith, Hope and Charity Church and is improved with a church
building, school, rectory, playground, parking areas and other church-related
structures; and
   WHEREAS, the proposed wheel-chair accessible ramp will be located adjacent
to the rectory entrance and will be equipped with an anodized aluminum railing
that is designed to match existing metal details on the Subject Property; and
   WHEREAS, Sts. Faith, Hope and Charity Church (“the Church”) is subject to
the accessibility requirements of the Americans with Disability Act and the
Illinois Accessibility Act and the Church must provide the proposed ramp in
order to comply with those statutory requirements; and
   WHEREAS, there are practical difficulties and unique hardships associated
with carrying out the strict application of the Zoning Ordinance with respect
to the Subject Property in that the Subject Property currently exceeds the lot
coverage limitations applicable to the R-3 Zoning District, which were designed
for properties developed with single family residences rather than church
facilities and it is impossible for the Church to comply with both the
statutory accessibility mandates and the Zoning Ordinances impermeable surface
limitations; and
   WHEREAS, the plight of the Church is due to unique circumstances (a) because
of the applicability of statutory accessibility requirements, (b) because the
Church's use of the Subject Property is for the furtherance of its religious
ministry rather than the private comfort, convenience or monetary benefits that
typically attach to residential and commercial uses of property, and (c) if the
Church is prevented from complying with the statutory accessibility
requirements it will not be able to legally continue the current use of the
facility; and
   WHEREAS, the variations, if granted, will not alter the essential character
of the locality, in that: (1) the proposed ramp is of minimal size and has been
designed to be sensitive to its surroundings and compatible with the
architecture of the existing church, which is a recognized visual fixture in
the neighborhood; and (2) the addition of the ramp will not alter the
established use of the Subject Property; and
   WHEREAS, an adequate supply of light and air to adjacent property will not
be impaired, because the maximum height of the proposed ramp will be at the
first floor level of the rectory; and
   WHEREAS, the hazard from fire and other damages to the property will not be
increased, since the addition will be constructed in accordance with all
applicable building codes, making it no more hazardous than any other
construction built according to those codes; and
   WHEREAS, there is no evidence that the taxable value of land and buildings
throughout the Village will diminish as a result of the construction of the
proposed ramp; and
   WHEREAS, there is no evidence that congestion in the public streets will
increase, as the ramp will not increase the size of the church buildings or the
use of the Church’s facilities; and
   WHEREAS, there is no evidence that the public health, safety, comfort,
morals and welfare of the inhabitants of the Village will be impaired by the
proposed addition, if it is constructed subject to the conditions specified in
this ordinance; and
   WHEREAS, the requested variation is in harmony with the general purpose and
intent of the Winnetka Zoning Ordinance, in that it allows the existing church
facilities to be upgraded and brought into full statutory compliance while
maintaining the existing scale and appearance of the community and protecting
established trees and landscaping.
   NOW, THEREFORE, the Council of the Village of Winnetka do ordain as follows:
   SECTION 1 : That the foregoing recitals are hereby incorporated as the
findings of the Council of the Village of Winnetka, as if fully set forth
herein.
   SECTION 2: That a variation is hereby granted to the Subject Property,
commonly known as 191 Linden, Winnetka, Illinois, and located in the R-
3 Single-Family Residential Zoning District provided in the Winnetka Zoning
Ordinance, Title 17, Winnetka Village Code, for a variation from the intensity
of use of lot provisions of Section 17.20.010(F) to add another 245 square feet
to the existing legally nonconforming impermeable lot coverage of 107,030
square feet, resulting in a total impermeable lot coverage of 107,275 square
feet, which exceeds the 86,767.50 square feet of permitted impermeable surface
by 20,507.50 square feet (23.64%) for the purpose of constructing a handicapped
accessible ramp on the Subject Property, in accordance with the plans submitted
with application.
   SECTION 3: That the variation hereby granted is conditioned upon the
commencement of the proposed construction within 12 months after the effective
date of this Ordinance.
   SECTION 4: This Ordinance shall take effect immediately upon passage,
approval and posting.
   ADOPTED this 9th day of November, 2000, pursuant to the following roll call
vote:
   AYES:    Trustees Brower, Presser, Aquilino, Powell, Woodbury, and Lien
   NAYS:    None.
   ABSENT:    None
   APPROVED this 9th day of November, 2000.
   Signed:
   /s/Louise A. Holland
   Village President
Countersigned:
/s/Douglas G. Williams
Village Clerk
Introduced: Waived pursuant to Winnetka Village Code § 2.04.040(D)
Posted: Waived pursuant to Winnetka Village Code § 2.04.040(D)
Passed and Approved: November 9, 2000
