ORDINANCE NO. M-36-2000
ORDINANCE ABATING THE TAX HERETOFORE LEVIED FOR THE YEAR 2000 TO PAY THE
PRINCIPAL OF AND INTEREST ON $3,600,000 GENERAL OBLIGATION BONDS (SALES TAX
ALTERNATIVE REVENUE SOURCE), SERIES 1994, OF THE VILLAGE OF WINNETKA, COOK
COUNTY, ILLINOIS
   WHEREAS, the Council (the “Council”) of the Village of Winnetka, Cook
County, Illinois (the “Village”), by Ordinance Number M-415-94, adopted on the
13th day of December, 1994 (the “Ordinance”), did provide for the issue of
$3,600,000 General Obligation Bonds (Sales Tax Alternate Revenue Source),
Series 1994 (the “Bonds”), and the levy of a direct annual tax sufficient to
pay the principal of and interest on the Bonds; and
   WHEREAS, the Village will have the sufficient funds in the appropriate fund
pursuant to the Ordinance for the purpose of paying the principal of and
interest on the Bonds up to and including December 1, 2001; and
   WHEREAS, it is necessary and in the best interests of the Village that the
tax heretofore levied for the year 2000 to pay the principal of and interest on
the Bonds be abated.
   NOW, THEREFORE, the Council of the Village of Winnetka do ordain as follows:
   SECTION 1:   Abatement of Tax. The tax heretofore levied for the year 2000
of $382,366.26 in Ordinance Number M-35-2000 to pay the principal of and
interest on $3,600,000 General Obligation Bonds (Sales Tax Alternate Revenue
Source), Series 1994, of the Village of Winnetka, Cook County, Illinois, is
hereby abated in its entirety.
   SECTION 2: Filing of Ordinance. Forthwith upon the adoption of this
Ordinance, the Village Clerk shall file a certified copy hereof with the County
Clerk of the County of Cook, Illinois, and it shall be the duty of said County
Clerk to abate said tax levied for the year 2000 in accordance with the
provisions hereof.
   SECTION 3: Effective Date. That this Ordinance shall be in full force and
effect from and after its passage, approval, and posting.
   ADOPTED this 19th day of December, 2000, pursuant to the following roll call
vote:
   AYES: Trustees Aquilino, Brower, Lien, Powell and Presser
   NAYS: None
   ABSENT: Trustee Woodbury
   APPROVED this 19th day of December, 2000.
   Signed:
   /s/Louise A. Holland
   Village President
