ORDINANCE NO. M-8-2001
AN ORDINANCE AUTHORIZING THE SALE OR OTHER DISPOSITION OF PERSONAL PROPERTY OF
THE VILLAGE OF WINNETKA
   WHEREAS, from time to time, the Winnetka Police Department comes into
possession of items of personal property that have been lost, found or stolen,
which personal property includes the “Bicycles” described in Exhibit A and the
miscellaneous property shown on Exhibit B (hereinafter collectively referred to
as the “Personal Property”), attached to this ordinance; and
   WHEREAS, the Personal Property has been in the possession of the Winnetka
Police Department for more than 6 months, during which time the Chief of Police
of the Winnetka Police Department has made reasonable inquiry and efforts to
identify and notify the owners or other persons entitled to possession of the
Personal Property, but has been unsuccessful in those attempts; and
   WHEREAS, pursuant to Section 3 of the Law Enforcement Disposition of
Property Act, 765 ILCS 1030/3, the Chief of Police has transferred the custody
of the Personal Property to the Village of Winnetka; and
   WHEREAS, the Village of Winnetka owns computer equipment, some of which will
be retired as it is replaced during the fiscal year, April 1, 2001 through
March 31, 2002 (hereinafter referred to as “Retired Computer Equipment”), and
which the Finance Director has recommended be disposed of by methods that are
consistent with past disposal methods; and
   WHEREAS, the Council of the Village of Winnetka have determined that the
Personal Property and Retired Computer Equipment, described herein (hereinafter
referred to collectively as the “Surplus Property”) are no longer necessary or
useful to the Village of Winnetka, that the cost of storing said Surplus
Property exceeds its value to the Village of Winnetka, that it is not in the
best interests of the Village of Winnetka to retain said Surplus Property and
that the Surplus Property should be disposed of in the manner hereinafter
provided, pursuant to Section 11-76-4 of the Illinois Municipal Code (65 ILCS
5/11-76-4), so as to avoid incurring additional costs for storing said Surplus
Property.
   NOW, THEREFORE, the Council of the Village of Winnetka do ordain:
   SECTION 1 : Pursuant to Section 11-76-4 of the Illinois Municipal Code (65
ILCS 5/11-76-4), the Council of the Village of Winnetka find that the above-
described Surplus Property, consisting of the items of Personal Property shown
on the attached Exhibits A and B is not necessary or useful to the Village of
Winnetka and that the best interests of the Village of Winnetka will be served
by the sale or other disposition of such Surplus Property.
   SECTION 2 : The Council of the Village of Winnetka further find that, based
on prior experience in disposing of similar items of property, the cost of
conducting a public sale of the Surplus Property, including the costs of
advertising and publishing, and the costs of personnel needed to maintain
security and to conduct the public sale, exceeds the value of such items.
   SECTION 3: Pursuant to said Section 11-76-4, the Village Manager is hereby
authorized and directed to determine the value of and to dispose of the
Personal Property in any manner he deems reasonable under the circumstances.
   SECTION 4: Pursuant to said Section 11-76-4, the Director of Finance is
hereby authorized and directed to determine the value of and to dispose of
Retired Computer Equipment that is retired during the fiscal year April 1,
2001, through March 31, 2002, using disposal methods that are consistence with
past disposal practices.
   SECTION 5: This Ordinance shall be in full force and effect from and after
its passage, approval, and posting.
   ADOPTED this 17th day of April, 2001, pursuant to the following roll call
vote:
   AYES: Trustees Aquilino, Lien, Powell Woodbury, Brower and Presser
   NAYS: None
   ABSENT: None
   APPROVED this 17th day of April, 2001.
   Signed:
   /s/Louise A. Holland
   Village President
Countersigned:
/s/Douglas G. Williams
Village Clerk
