ORDINANCE NO. M-10-2001
AN ORDINANCE GRANTING A VARIATION IN THE APPLICATION OF THE ZONING ORDINANCE OF
THE VILLAGE OF WINNETKA COOK COUNTY, ILLINOIS (885 Hill Road)
   WHEREAS, there has been presented to the Council of the Village of Winnetka,
Cook County, Illinois, the request of the owner of the following described real
estate (the “Subject Property”):
All that part of that certain tract of land more particularly described as
follows: Beginning at a point (marked with a concrete monument) in the East
line of the Southwest quarter of the Southeast quarter of Section 20, Township
42 North, Range 13, East of the Third Principal Meridian, 353.40 feet North of
the Southeast corner of said Southwest quarter; thence North 50 degrees 24
minutes West, a distance of 10.90 feet to a point marked with an iron stake;
thence Southerly to a point in the South line of the Southwest quarter of the
Southeast quarter aforesaid, which point is 262.67 feet West of the Southeast
corner of said Southwest quarter of the Southeast quarter aforesaid, thence
East along said South line to the Southeast corner aforesaid; thence North
353.40 feet to the point of beginning; in Cook County, Illinois, except the
East 133.0 feet of the South 186.0 feet of the Southwest quarter of the
Southeast quarter of Section 20, Township 42 North, Range 13, East of the Third
Principal Meridian and running thence Northwesterly to a point in the Westerly
line of said tract, 279.6 feet Northerly from the Southwest corner of said
tract, subject to the rights of the public in the South 30 feet thereof, all in
Cook County, Illinois,
commonly known as 885 Hill Road, Winnetka, Illinois, and located in the R-
2 Single-Family Residential Zoning District provided in Chapter 17.24 of the
Winnetka Zoning Ordinance, Title 17 of the Winnetka Village Code, for a
variation from Section 17.24.010(P)2 of the Zoning Ordinance to permit
alteration of the existing, 23.25-foot wide attached garage to allow the garage
doors to face the front of the property, thereby exceeding the maximum width of
22 feet for front-facing garages, resulting in a variation of 1.25 feet
(5.68%); and
   WHEREAS, on March 12, 2001, on due notice thereof, the Zoning Board of
Appeals conducted a public hearing on the requested variation and by the
unanimous vote of the five members then present, has reported to the Council
recommending that the requested variation be granted; and
   WHEREAS, there are practical difficulties and unique hardships associated
with carrying out the strict application of the Zoning Ordinance with respect
to the Subject Property in that: (a) the Subject Property is an irregularly
shaped lot on the north side of Hill Road, having a north lot line that is
angled toward the center of the property and is nearly 100 feet longer than the
east lot line, thereby forming a narrowing, nearly triangular rear yard; (b)
the irregular shape of the lot, coupled with the large front setback, limits
the locations available for a garage; (c) the attached garage is part of the
existing residence, and the relocation of the doors from the rear of the
property to the front of the property is being proposed as part of a project
that includes a building addition in conforming locations at the rear of the
existing residence; (d) the dimensions of the existing garage and the east side
yard are not sufficient to allow access to the garage from the side; (e) the
difference between a 22-foot wide garage and 23.25-foot wide garage will not be
discernible from the street due to the large front setback, the presence of
trees near the front lot line and a new fence that will be constructed near the
front lot line; and
   WHEREAS, the Subject Property cannot yield a reasonable return if permitted
to be used only under the conditions allowed by the Zoning Ordinance, in that
requiring the owners to maintain rear facing garage doors would restrict their
ability to expand the usable space in the residency and construct an otherwise
conforming addition at the rear of the existing house, and would reduce the
utility of the rear yard by requiring the owners to maintain the existing paved
area at the rear of the house, which is necessary to turn vehicles when
entering and exiting the garage; and
   WHEREAS, the requested variation will not alter the essential character of
the neighborhood because the reoriented garage doors will form part of a
redesigned south building face, will be consistent with the other design
details of the building, and will maintain the existing building dimensions
along the front of the building; and
   WHEREAS, the requested variation will not impair an adequate supply of light
and air because the relocated garage doors will not change the existing
dimensions of the garage; and
   WHEREAS, the requested variation will not increase the hazard from fire and
other dangers to the Subject Property, the proposed construction will comply
with all applicable building and fire protection codes; and
   WHEREAS, the requested variation will not diminish the taxable value of land
and buildings throughout the Village, and the taxable value of the Subject
Property may be increased because of the proposed improvements; and
   WHEREAS, the requested variation will not contribute to congestion on the
public streets, as the existing garage will continue to provide off-street
parking and the use of the Subject Property will not change; and
   WHEREAS, there is no evidence that the requested variation will otherwise
impair the public health, safety, comfort, morals, and welfare of the
inhabitants of the Village.
   WHEREAS, the requested variation is in harmony with the general purpose and
intent of the Winnetka Zoning Ordinance, in that it allows the renovation,
restoration and rehabilitation of a structurally sound existing building while
maintaining the existing scale and appearance of the community and protecting
established trees and landscaping.
   NOW, THEREFORE, the Council of the Village of Winnetka do ordain as follows:
   SECTION 1 : That the foregoing recitals are hereby incorporated as the
findings of the Council of the Village of Winnetka, as if fully set forth
herein.
   SECTION 2:  There is hereby granted to the Subject Property, commonly known
as 885 Hill Road, Winnetka, Illinois, and located in the R-2 Single-Family
Residential Zoning District provided in Chapter 17.24 of the Winnetka Zoning
Ordinance, Title 17 of the Winnetka Village Code, a variation from Section
17.24.010(P)2 of the Zoning Ordinance to permit alteration of the existing,
23.25-foot wide attached garage to allow the garage doors to face the front of
the property, thereby exceeding the maximum width of 22 feet for front-facing
garages, resulting in a variation of 1.25 feet (5.68%), in accordance with the
plans and specifications submitted with the application for variations.
   SECTION 3: The variation hereby granted is conditioned upon the commencement
of the proposed construction within 12 months after the effective date of this
Ordinance.
   SECTION 4: This Ordinance shall take effect immediately upon passage,
approval and posting.
   ADOPTED this 1st day of May, 2001, pursuant to the following roll call vote:
   AYES:    Trustees Brower, Aquilino, Greenough, Powell, Presser and Woodbury
   NAYS:    None
   ABSENT:    None
   APPROVED this 1st day of May, 2001.
   Signed:
   /s/Michael F. Duhl
   Village President
Countersigned:
/s/ Douglas G. Williams
Village Clerk
Introduced: April 17, 2001
Posted: April 18, 2001
Passed and Approved: May 1, 2001
