ORDINANCE NO. M-11-2001
AN ORDINANCE GRANTING A VARIATION IN THE APPLICATION OF THE ZONING ORDINANCE OF
THE VILLAGE OF WINNETKA COOK COUNTY, ILLINOIS (757 Locust Avenue)
   WHEREAS, there has been presented to the Council of the Village of Winnetka,
Cook County, Illinois, the request of the owner of the following described real
estate (the “Subject Property”):
The South 100 feet of Lot 6 Block 19 in County Clerk’s Division of the
Southwest ¼ of Section 17, Township 42 North, Range 13, East of the Third
Principal Meridian, in Cook County, Illinois,
commonly known as 757 Locust Avenue, Winnetka, Illinois, and located in the R-
4 Single-Family Residential Zoning District provided in Chapter 17.16 of the
Winnetka Zoning Ordinance, Title 17, Winnetka Village Code, for variations from
the front setback requirements of Section 17.16.010(H) of the Zoning Ordinance
to allow a front setback of 25.83 feet along the west lot line (Locust Avenue)
and a corner setback of 23.78 feet along the south lot line (Westmoor Road),
whereas a setback of 30 feet is required from both the front and corner lot
lines of a corner lot, resulting in a variation of 4.17 feet (13.9%) along the
Locust Avenue frontage and a variation of 6.22 feet (20.73%), along the
Westmoor Road frontage, to allow the one-story front entrance to be enlarged by
9.38 square feet, to provide a front hall closet for the residence on the
Subject Property; and
   WHEREAS, on March 12, 2001, on due notice thereof, the Zoning Board of
Appeals conducted a public hearing on the requested variations and by the
unanimous vote of the five members then present, has reported to the Council
recommending that the requested variations be granted; and
   WHEREAS, there are practical difficulties and unique hardships associated
with carrying out the strict application of the Zoning Ordinance with respect
to the Subject Property in that (a) the Subject Property is a corner lot
located on the northeast corner of Locust Avenue and Westmoor Road, and is
therefore subject to 30-foot setbacks along both street frontages; (b) the home
on the Subject Property was built circa 1908, before the Winnetka Zoning
Ordinance was enacted in 1925, and the Subject Property has legally
nonconforming front and corner yard setbacks; (c) the variation would allow a
9.38 square foot addition extending to the north along the existing front
entrance, in order to provide a hall closet for a reconfigured front entry that
includes a small porch that is a permitted encroachment into the setbacks; and
   WHEREAS, the Subject Property cannot yield a reasonable return if permitted
to be used only under the conditions allowed by the Zoning Ordinance, in that:
(a) a hall closet is a standard amenity in residences in the area; (b) due to
the configuration of the existing residence and the location of the house
within the front and corner setbacks, there is no conforming location for a
hall closet in the vicinity of the front entrance; (c) the proposed addition is
approximately 2 feet wide and does not extend further into the front setback
than the front entrance itself; and
   WHEREAS, the requested variations will not alter the essential character of
the neighborhood because of the minimal size of the addition and because the
new front entrance is consistent with the style of the house and improves the
appearance of the house in the neighborhood, and because the proposed addition
will be located within the entryway, between the house and the new porch, that
is permitted to encroach into the setback; and
   WHEREAS, the requested variations will not impair an adequate supply of
light and air because the front entrance is modest in size, the additional
space for the closet is minimal, and the street frontages that define the front
and corner yards provide a permanent additional expanse of open space between
the proposed construction and buildings on the opposite sides of the streets;
and
   WHEREAS, the requested variations will not increase the hazard from fire and
other dangers to the Subject Property as the new construction will comply with
all applicable building and fire protection codes; and
   WHEREAS, the requested variations will not diminish the taxable value of
land and buildings throughout the Village, and the taxable value of the Subject
Property may be increased because of the proposed improvements; and
   WHEREAS, the proposed expansion to the front entrance to include a hall
closet will not contribute to congestion on the public streets, as it will not
alter the use of the house; and
   WHEREAS, there is no evidence that the proposed addition will otherwise
impair the public health, safety, comfort, morals, and welfare of the
inhabitants of the Village.
   WHEREAS, the requested variations are in harmony with the general purpose
and intent of the Winnetka Zoning Ordinance, in that it allows the renovation,
restoration and rehabilitation of a structurally sound existing building while
maintaining the existing scale and appearance of the community and protecting
established trees and landscaping.
   NOW, THEREFORE, the Council of the Village of Winnetka do ordain as follows:
   SECTION 1 : The foregoing recitals are hereby incorporated as the findings
of the Council of the Village of Winnetka, as if fully set forth herein.
   SECTION 2:  There are hereby granted to the Subject Property, commonly known
as 757 Locust Avenue, Winnetka, Illinois, and located in the R-4 Single-Family
Residential Zoning District provided in Chapter 17.16 of the Winnetka Zoning
Ordinance, Title 17, Winnetka Village Code, variations from the front setback
requirements of Section 17.16.010(H) to allow a front setback of 25.83 feet
along the west lot line (Locust Avenue) and a corner setback of 23.78 feet
along the south lot line (Westmoor Road), whereas a setback of 30 feet is
required from both the front and corner lot lines of the Subject Property,
resulting in a variation of 4.17 feet (13.9%) along the west lot line and a
variation of 6.22 feet (20.73%), along the south lot line, for the purpose of
enlarging the one-story front entrance by 9.38 square feet, to provide a front
hall closet for the existing residence on the Subject Property, in accordance
with the plans and specifications submitted with the application for
variations.
   SECTION 3: The variations hereby granted is conditioned upon the
commencement of the proposed construction within 12 months after the effective
date of this Ordinance.
   SECTION 4: This Ordinance shall take effect immediately upon passage,
approval and posting.
   ADOPTED this 1st day of May, 2001, pursuant to the following roll call vote:
   AYES:    Trustees Aquilino, Brower, Greenough, Powell, Presser and Woodbury
   NAYS:    None
   ABSENT:    None
   APPROVED this 1st day of May, 2001.
   Signed:
   /s/Michael F. Duhl
   Village President
