ORDINANCE NO. M-13-2001
AN ORDINANCE AUTHORIZING THE VACATION OF THE ALLEY RIGHT-OF-WAY AT THE REAR OF
329 FAIRVIEW AND ACCEPTING A PLAT OF CONSOLIDATION
   WHEREAS, pursuant to Section 11-91-1 of the Illinois Municipal Code (65 ILCS
5/11-91-1), the Council of the Village of Winnetka are authorized to vacate any
street or alley or part thereof within the corporate limits of the Village if
the corporate authorities determine that the public interest will be served by
the vacation; and
   WHEREAS, the property commonly known as 329 Fairview (the “Adjoining
Property”) is legally described as follows:
Lot 10 in Block 3 in Dale’s Addition to Winnetka, a Subdivision in the
Southeast ¼ of Section 21, Township 42 North, Range 13, East of the Third
Principal Meridian, in Cook County, Illinois.
   WHEREAS, the Village Council have considered whether it should vacate all or
portions of the 10-foot alley right-of-way adjoining the east lot line of the
property commonly known as 329 Fairview Avenue; and
   WHEREAS, the alley adjoining the east property line of the Adjoining
Property is a 20-foot wide dedicated alley, and the Village has previously
vacated 10-foot portions of the alley adjoining the properties directly to the
north and south of the Adjoining Property; and
   WHEREAS, the Council of the Village of Winnetka have determined that it is
in the best interests of the Village that the 10-foot alley right-of-way
adjoining the east lot line of the Adjoining Property be vacated and
consolidated with the Adjoining Property, in order to provide consistency of
lot lines and lot sizes and to relieve the Village of maintenance
responsibility for the alley; and
   WHEREAS, the Council of the Village of Winnetka have determined that the
fair market value of the part of the alley to be vacated is $27,000 and the
owner of the Adjoining Property has agreed to pay the Village that amount if
the alley is vacated and consolidated with the Adjoining Property; and
   WHEREAS, the vacation of the above-described right-of-way, as depicted in
the Plat of Vacation attached hereto as Exhibit A, will result in the
consolidation of the vacated alley to the Adjoining Property, resulting in the
reconfiguration of that lot, as depicted in the plat of consolidation entitled
“Humpal’s Consolidation,” which is attached hereto as Exhibit B; and
   WHEREAS, pursuant to Section 16.08.010.F of Title 16 of the Winnetka Village
Code, “Subdivisions,” the Acting Director of Community Development has reviewed
the plat of consolidation and has recommended that the consolidation be
approved, subject to the condition that an easement for water and electrical
utilities be reserved along the 10-foot wide vacated alley and that a 5-foot
easement for water and electrical utilities be reserved along the west (front)
lot line; and
   WHEREAS, the President and the Board of Trustees have determined that the
public interest will be served by vacating the above-described alley right-of-
way, which is legally described as follows:
The West Half of the 20.00 Foot Public Alley Lying South of the North Line
Extended East and North of the South Line Extended East of Lot 10 in Block 3 in
Dale’s Addition to Winnetka, a Subdivision in the Southeast Quarter of Section
21, Township 42 North, Range 13, East of the Third Principal Meridian, in Cook
County, Illinois,
as depicted on the Plat of Vacation attached hereto as Exhibit A; and
   WHEREAS, the Council of the Village of Winnetka have determined that it is
in the best interests of the public for the vacation of the alley right-of-way
to be subject to the reservation of the easement as recommended by the Acting
Director of Community Development.
   NOW, THEREFORE, the Council of the Village of Winnetka do ordain:
   SECTION 1 : The foregoing recitals are hereby adopted by the Council as its
findings and are incorporated by reference as if fully set forth herein.
   SECTION 2: The alley right-of-way adjoining the east property line of the
Adjoining Property, as depicted in the attached Plat of Vacation attached
hereto as Exhibit A and legally described as follows (the “Vacated Alley”):
The West Half of the 20.00 Foot Public Alley Lying South of the North Line
Extended East and North of the South Line Extended East of Lot 10 in Block 3 in
Dale’s Addition to Winnetka, a Subdivision in the Southeast Quarter of Section
21, Township 42 North, Range 13, East of the Third Principal Meridian, in Cook
County, Illinois,
is hereby vacated, subject to the conditions hereinafter set forth.
   SECTION 3 : The vacation of the Alley shall be subject to: (1) the
reservation of a 10-foot water and electric utility easement along the Vacated
Alley, and the reservation of a 5-foot water and electric utility easement
along the west (front) lot line of the parcel of land to be formed by the
consolidation of the Vacated Alley with the Adjoining Property; (2) the receipt
by the Village of the full payment of $27,000.00 from the Adjoining Owner; and
(3) the payment by the Adjoining Owner of all costs related to the vacation of
the alley and the preparation and recording of the plat.
   SECTION 4: Provided that the conditions set forth in Section 3 of this
ordinance are met, the Vacated Alley shall be consolidated with the Adjoining
Property into a single parcel of land, as depicted on the plat of consolidation
entitled “Humpal’s Consolidation,” which is attached hereto as Exhibit B, said
consolidated parcel thereafter to remain commonly known as 325 Fairview Avenue
and to be legally described as:
Lot 1 of Humpal’s Consolidation in the Southeast Quarter of Section 21,
Township 42 North, Range 13, East of the Third Principal Meridian, in Cook
County, Illinois; and
   SECTION 5 : The corporate authorities of the Village of Winnetka do hereby
authorize the Village President and Village Clerk to execute the Plat of
Vacation and the plat entitled "Humpal’s Consolidation," and to take all other
steps necessary to effectuate the vacation of the alley right-of-way and the
recording of the Humpal’s Consolidation plat, provided that all of the
conditions set forth in Section 2 of this ordinance have first been met.
   SECTION 6 : Upon the execution of the plats, and the Adjoining Owners’ full
performance of all of the conditions set forth in this ordinance, the Village
Clerk of the Village of Winnetka is hereby authorized and directed to cause a
certified copy of this Ordinance, the Plat of Vacation and the Humpal’s
Consolidation plat to be recorded in the Office of the Cook County Recorder of
Deeds.
   SECTION 7 : This ordinance shall be in full force and effect from and after
its passage, approval, and posting.
   ADOPTED this 15th day of May, 2001, pursuant to the following roll call
vote:
   AYES: Trustees Aquilino, Brower, Greenough, Powell and Woodbury
   NAYS: None
   ABSENT: Trustee Presser
   APPROVED this 15th day of May, 2001.
   Signed:
   /s/Michael F. Duhl
   Village President
Countersigned:
/s/Douglas G. Williams
Village Clerk
Introduced: May 1, 2001
Posted: May 2, 2001
Passed and Approved: May 15, 2001
