ORDINANCE NO. M-18-2001
AN ORDINANCE AMENDING AN EXISTING SPECIAL USE PERMIT TO ALLOW THE RENOVATION
AND EXPANSION OF FACILITIES FOR THE PUBLIC WORKS AND WATER & ELECTRIC
DEPARTMENTS AT THE VILLAGE OF WINNETKA PUBLIC WORKS YARDS (1390 Willow Road)
   WHEREAS, the Village of Winnetka is the owner of the following described
real estate (the “Subject Property”):
The Northeast ¼ of the Southeast ¼ (except the East 10.0 Acres thereof) of
Section 19, Township 42 North, Range 13 East of the Third Principal Meridian in
the Village of Winnetka, Cook County, Illinois,
commonly known as the Village of Winnetka Public Works Yards (“Village Yards”),
1390 Willow Road, Winnetka, Illinois, which is located in the R-2 Single-Family
Residential Zoning District provided in the Winnetka Zoning Ordinance, Title 17
of the Winnetka Village Code; and
   WHEREAS, the Subject Property is improved with a maintenance facility for
the Public Works and Water & Electric Departments, a parking area, a dome for
the storage of road salt, a firefighting training tower, municipal and
emergency communications facilities, and the Village of Winnetka’s composting
facility and yard waste transfer station, which operate pursuant to permits
issued by the Illinois Environmental Protection Agency in the area of the
Subject Property occupied by the Village’s landfill, which was closed in 1994;
and
   WHEREAS, the maintenance facility for the Water & Electric Department, the
firefighting training tower and the communications facilities on the Subject
Property are essential public uses, which are permitted uses in the R-2 Zoning
District pursuant to Section 17.24.010(B)(3) of the Winnetka Zoning Ordinance;
and
   WHEREAS, the maintenance facility for the Public Works Department, the
closed landfill, the composting facility, the landscape waste transfer station,
the salt storage dome and the parking areas on the Subject Property are non-
essential public uses and are lawful special uses, pursuant to Sections
17.56.010(B) and 17.56.010(K) of the Winnetka Zoning Ordinance, and pursuant to
Resolution R-1299-95 and prior resolutions pertaining to the use of the Subject
Property; and
   WHEREAS, the Village of Winnetka (the “Village”) has applied for a special
use permit under Section 17.56.010 and Section 17.24.010(B)(3) of the Winnetka
Zoning Ordinance to amend the existing special use permit by allowing the
renovation and expansion of the existing municipal maintenance facility and
related parking on the Subject Property; and
   WHEREAS, on July 9, 2001, pursuant to due notice thereof, the Zoning Board
of Appeals conducted a public hearing on the requested special use and, by the
unanimous vote of the seven members of the Board, has reported to the Council,
recommending that the requested special use be granted; and
   WHEREAS, on July 19, 2001, the Design Review Board considered the proposal
and, by the unanimous vote of the five members then in attendance, issued
generally favorable preliminary comment on the proposed design, but also made
the following recommendations: (a) that the scale of the end walls of the
garage bays be reduced by considering additional fenestration or the addition
of a one-story element, (b) that further consideration be given to brick color,
overhang and eave details, and an open archway in the clock tower, and (c) that
the landscape plan be refined before it is approved; and
   WHEREAS, on July 25, 2001, pursuant to due notice thereof, the Plan
Commission considered the special use application and, by the unanimous vote of
the full Commission, found that the proposed special use is consistent with the
Comprehensive Plan, Winnetka 2020, subject to the following conditions: (a)
that there be further review of the landscaping plan and building details as
recommended by the Design Review Board, and (b) that further consideration be
given to alternative locations for employee parking; and
   WHEREAS, in response to the comments received from the Zoning Board of
Appeals, Plan Commission and Design Review Board, the plans and elevations were
revised; and
   WHEREAS, the revised plans and elevations, dated August 7, 2001, were
considered by the Village Council at its regular meeting on August 7, 2001; and
   WHEREAS, the existing facilities no longer meet the needs of the Public
Works and Water and Electric Departments due to: (a) a lack of office, work and
locker space for employees, (b) inadequate work areas for the mechanics who
maintain the Village’s fleet of vehicles, (c) lack of space to properly store
equipment, vehicles and supplies, (d) lack of suitable facilities to meet the
needs of current and future female employees, (e) lack of compliance with
accessibility requirements of the Americans with Disabilities Act, and (f)
general deterioration of the aging building structures and systems; and
   WHEREAS, the proposed expansion and restoration of the maintenance
facilities and the related reconfiguration of parking at the Village Yards will
benefit the public health, safety, comfort, morals and general welfare because
it will enhance the Village’s ability to provide public works, water and
electric services for the entire Village by providing increased and more
efficient space for those operations and by providing adequate workspace that
meets current operational, safety and accessibility standards, all without
interfering with the operation of any of the other existing essential and non-
essential public services on the Subject Property; and
   WHEREAS, the proposed rehabilitation of the Village Yards will not be
substantially injurious to the use and enjoyment of other property in the
immediate vicinity, will not substantially diminish or impair property values
in the immediate vicinity, and will not impede the normal and orderly
development or improvement of other property in the immediate vicinity for uses
permitted under applicable zoning regulations because: (a) the Subject Property
is not adjacent to any single family residences, being opposite the Skokie
Playfields, part of the Winnetka Park District Golf Course and the Madsen Water
Reservoir, and immediately west of property owned by the Forest Preserve
District of Cook County, (b) the Village Yards is an established presence in
the neighborhood, (c) all of the current operations have been established on
the Subject Property for at least 30 years, (d) the proposed renovated and
expanded facilities will improve the appearance of the Subject Property because
they will be designed to be consistent with the Comprehensive Plan, Winnetka
2020, and with the Interim Design Guidelines adopted by the Design Review Board
on May 17, 2001, and (e) the landscaping that will be provided along Willow
Road will enhance the public view of the Subject Property; and
   WHEREAS, when constructed in accordance with the conditions imposed by this
ordinance, the existing parking, utilities, access roads, drainage and other
facilities necessary to the uses on the Subject Property will be enhanced; and
   WHEREAS, the proposed traffic circulation patterns proposed for the
reconfigured Village Yards takes adequate measures to provide ingress and
egress without interfering with pedestrian traffic and without causing
vehicular congestion in the public ways; and
WHEREAS, the proposed rehabilitation of the Village Yards, when constructed in
accordance with the terms and conditions of this ordinance, will conform to the
applicable regulations of the Zoning Ordinance and the Winnetka Village Code.
   NOW, THEREFORE, the Council of the Village of Winnetka do resolve:
   SECTION 1: That a special use permit is granted with respect to the Subject
Property, which is located in the R-2 Single-Family Residential Zoning District
provided in the Winnetka Zoning Ordinance, Title 17 of the Winnetka Village
Code and is commonly known as 1390 Willow Road, to allow all existing
operations to continue and to allow the existing maintenance facilities to be
expanded and renovated, in accordance with the application and plans submitted
with the original application, as modified by the revised plans dated August 7.
   SECTION 2: That the special use permit hereby granted is subject to the
following conditions:
      A.   The final building design and building materials shall be subject to
the final approval of the Village Council after review and comment by the
Design Review Board. To the extent that the Council shall deem it is reasonably
possible, the final building design and building materials shall be consistent
with the Interim Design Guidelines adopted by the Design Review Board on May
17, 2001.
      B.   The final landscaping plan shall be subject to the final approval of
the Village Council after review and comment by the Forestry Commission and the
Design Review Board. The final landscaping plan shall use materials approved by
the Village Forester and shall be designed to be consistent with the other
landscaping on the Subject Property, to enhance the appearance of the proposed
buildings and, to the extent the Council shall deem it is reasonably possible,
to provide a visual buffer between the parking areas and Willow Road.
      C.   The proposed construction shall commence within 12 months after the
effective date of this ordinance.
   SECTION 3: Pursuant to Section 17.56.010(G) of the Zoning Ordinance, the
stipulations, conditions and restrictions set forth in this ordinance as part
of the terms under which the special use is granted, may be modified or revised
from time to time by the Village Council following public notice and hearing,
using the same procedures set forth in the Zoning ordinance for processing the
original special use application.
   SECTION 4: This ordinance shall be in full force and effect from and after
its passage, approval, and posting.
   Passed and approved this 21st day of August, 2001.
   AYES:      Trustees Aquilino, Brower, Greenough, Powell, Presser and
Woodbury
   NAYS:   None
   ABSENT:   None
               Signed:
                  /s/Michael F. Duhl
Countersigned:            Village President
/s/Douglas G. Williams
Village Clerk
Introduced: August 7, 2001
Posted: August 8, 2001
