ORDINANCE NO. M-22-2001
AN ORDINANCE AUTHORIZING AN AGREEMENT FOR THE PURCHASE OF CERTAIN REAL ESTATE
(93 Green Bay Road)
   WHEREAS, the Council of the Village of Winnetka deem it advisable, necessary
and in the public interest of the Village of Winnetka to acquire the following
described real estate:
Lot 1 of the Woyner’s Subdivision in the North Half of Section 28, Township 42
North, Range 13, East of the Third Principal Meridian, in the Village of
Winnetka, in Cook County, Illinois
commonly known as 93 Green Bay; and
   WHEREAS, pursuant to the provisions of Section 11-61-3 of Article 11 of the
Illinois Municipal Code, the Village of Winnetka is authorized to purchase real
estate for public purposes pursuant to contracts that provide for the
consideration for such purchase to be paid in annual installments during a
period not exceeding 20 years and to provide for the levy and collection of a
direct annual tax sufficient to pay said installments; and
   WHEREAS, the owner of the Property, Robert V. Woyner (Seller), has agreed to
convey the Property to the Village for the purchase price hereinafter set
forth; and
   WHEREAS, the Council of the Village of Winnetka have determined that
sufficient funds are available to acquire the Property by direct purchase, with
the purchase price to be paid in a single lump sum at the time of closing,
without the need to levy any additional taxes; and
    NOW THEREFORE, the Council of the Village of Winnetka do ordain as follows:
   SECTION 1: The foregoing recitals are incorporated herein as findings of the
Council of the Village of Winnetka, as if fully set forth herein.
   SECTION 2: The Council of the Village of Winnetka hereby approve an
agreement for the purchase of the Property, which agreement shall provide for:
(a) a purchase price of $650,000, which shall include the Property and all
fixtures thereon; (b) conveyance of the Property to be by warranty deed; (c)
conveyance of fixtures and other personal property by bill of sale; (d) the
Seller to provide proof of title and proof of environmental compliance prior to
the closing date; and (e) the Seller to assume all standard seller’s costs, and
the Village to assume all standard purchaser’s costs. The agreement shall be
substantially in the form (the Agreement) attached hereto as Exhibit A.
   SECTION 3: From and after the effective date of this Ordinance the Village
President and Village Clerk are hereby authorized and directed to execute the
Agreement, and to do all things necessary and essential, including the
execution of any documents and certificates, to carry out the provisions of the
Agreement.
   SECTION 4: This Ordinance shall be in full force and effect from and after
its passage, approval, and posting in the manner provided by law.
   ADOPTED this 4th day of September, 2001, pursuant to the following roll call
vote:
   AYES: Trustees Aquilino, Brower, Greenough, Powell, Presser and Woodbury
   NAYS: None
   ABSENT: None
   APPROVED this 4th day of September, 2001.
   Signed:
   /s/Barbara Aquilino
   Village President Pro Tem
Countersigned:
/s/Douglas G. Williams
Village Clerk
Introduced: August 21, 2001
Posted: August 22, 2001
Passed and Approved: September 4, 2001
Posted: September 5, 2001
ORDINANCE NO.: M-23-2001
AN ORDINANCE AUTHORIZING THE DISPOSITION OF CERTAIN PERSONAL PROPERTY OWNED BY
THE VILLAGE OF WINNETKA
WHEREAS, the Village of Winnetka owns the following described items of personal
property (hereinafter the “Personal Property”) and has established a minimum
value for each such item of personal property as hereinafter described:
 
Vehicle ID        Inventory No Year Make  Model     Minimum Value
1G1AW81W4K6228435 592          1989 Chevy Celebrity $575.00
1G1BL5376NW146230 593          1992 Chevy Caprice   $500.00
1FACP5742PG257439 586          1993 Ford  Taurus    $500.00
None              504          1967 Tarco TTL-1     $300.00
None              505          1967 Tarco TTL-1     $300.00
None              508          1967 Tarco TTL-1     $300.00
 
   WHEREAS, the Council of the Village of Winnetka have determined that it is
no longer useful to, or in the best interests of, the Village of Winnetka to
retain said Personal Property and that said Personal Property should be sold in
the manner hereinafter provided, pursuant to Section 11-76-4 of the Illinois
Municipal Code (65 ILCS 5/11-76-4); and
   WHEREAS, the Village Manager of the Village of Winnetka has authorized the
Northwest Municipal Conference to advertise and obtain bids for the sale of the
items of Personal Property at an auction to be conducted by the Northwest
Municipal Conference at 11:00 a.m., Saturday, September 22, 2001, Vernon Hills
Public Works, 490 Greenleaf Drive, Illinois, with the acceptance of any bids
being subject to the approval of the corporate authorities pursuant to a duly
enacted ordinance.
   NOW, THEREFORE, the Council of the Village of Winnetka do ordain:
   SECTION 1: Pursuant to Section 11-76-4 of the Illinois Municipal Code 65
(ILCS 5/11-76-4), the Council the Village of Winnetka find that the above-
described Personal Property is no longer necessary or useful to the Village of
Winnetka and that the best interests of the Village of Winnetka will be served
by the sale of said Personal Property.
   SECTION 2: Pursuant to said Section 11-76-4, the Village Manager is hereby
authorized to direct the sale of the Personal Property at an auction to be
conducted by the Northwest Municipal Conference (the “NWMC”) at 11:00 a.m.,
Saturday, September 22, 2001, Vernon Hills Public Works, 490 Greenleaf Drive,
Illinois.
   SECTION 3: The Village Manager is further authorized to direct the NWMC to
advertise the sale of the Personal Property through area newspapers, direct
mailings, and other channels as the NWMC deems appropriate prior to the date of
the auction.
   SECTION 4: The Village Manager is further authorized to direct the NWMC to
enter into an agreement for the sale of the Personal Property, whereby the
Personal Property shall be sold at the auction to the highest bidder or
bidders, according to the terms set forth in the Specifications for the Sale of
Vehicles and Equipment at Northwest Municipal Conference Auctions, which
specifications are attached hereto and made a part of this ordinance.
   SECTION 5: No bid shall be accepted for the sale of any item of the Personal
Property which is less than the minimum value of said item of personal property
as set forth in the preamble to this ordinance, unless the Village Manager, or
his designee, so authorizes at the time of the auction, and unless the highest
bid received for such item is less than the minimum value set forth in this
ordinance.
   SECTION 6: Upon payment in full of the auctioned price by the highest bidder
or bidders for any item of the Personal Property, the Village Manager is
authorized to direct the NWMC to convey and transfer the title and ownership of
said item of Personal Property to the highest bidder or bidders.
   SECTION 7: That this ordinance shall be in full force and effect from and
after its passage, approval, and posting.
   PASSED this 4th day of September, 2001, pursuant to the following roll call
vote
   AYES: Trustees Aquilino, Brower, Greenough, Powell, Presser and Woodbury
   NAYS: None
   ABSENT: None
   APPROVED this 4th day of September, 2001.
