ORDINANCE NO. M-32-2001
AN ORDINANCE GRANTING A VARIATION IN THE APPLICATION OF THE ZONING ORDINANCE OF
THE VILLAGE OF WINNETKA COOK COUNTY, ILLINOIS (785 Lincoln Avenue)
   WHEREAS, there has been presented to the Council of the Village of Winnetka,
Cook County, Illinois, the request of the owner of the following described real
estate (the “Subject Property”):
Lot 1 in Garner’s Consolidation of Lots 16 and 17 (except the North 31 feet) in
Block 8 in Winnetka Park Bluffs, a subdivision of William H. Cairnduff of Part
of Sections 16, 17 and Section 20, Township 42 North, Range 13, East of the
Third Principal Meridian, in Cook County, Illinois,
commonly known as 785 Lincoln Avenue, Winnetka, Illinois, and located in the R-
4 Single-Family Residential Zoning District provided in Title 17 of the
Winnetka Village Code, for a variation from the maximum building size
limitations of Section 17.16.010(G) of the Winnetka Zoning Ordinance, to allow
a total gross floor area of 4,351.32 square feet, whereas the maximum building
size limitation for the Subject Property is 3,679.97 square feet, resulting in
a variation of 671.35 square feet (18.24%), for the purpose of changing the
fenestration in existing walls on the second floor and constructing a one-story
134.73 square foot expansion of the kitchen and service porch to the residence
on the Subject Property; and
   WHEREAS, on October 8, 2001, on due notice thereof, the Zoning Board of
Appeals conducted a public hearing on the requested variations and by the
unanimous vote of the four members then present, has reported to the Council
recommending that the requested variations be granted; and
   WHEREAS, there are practical difficulties and unique hardships associated
with carrying out the strict application of the Zoning Ordinance with respect
to the Subject Property in that: (a) the single family residence on the Subject
Property, which is a legally nonconforming structure built after May 7, 1989,
has an existing gross floor area of 4,216.59 square feet, which exceeds the
maximum allowable building size by 536.62 square feet; (b) because the
residence is a nonconforming building, the proposed changes in fenestration,
which involve structural changes that do not increase the size of the building,
cannot be made without a variation; (c) the proposed changes in fenestration
are de minimis and do not increase the size of the second floor; (d) the
existing, 106-sqare foot kitchen is small, inefficiently laid out and has no
eating area; (e) the existing 104.04-square foot breakfast nook does not adjoin
any wall of the kitchen; (f) the 134.73-square foot proposed kitchen and
service porch addition will allow for the kitchen to be expanded and
reconfigured, with the kitchen and breakfast nook being incorporated into a
larger, more open space that is more consistent with the size and configuration
of kitchens in homes of comparable size and age in the Village; and (g) the
proposed kitchen addition does not add significantly to the total gross floor
area of the residence and is located primarily within the footprint of an
existing rear porch; and
   WHEREAS, the Subject Property cannot yield a reasonable return if permitted
to be used only under the conditions allowed by the Zoning Ordinance, in that:
(a) prohibiting the changes in fenestration would prevent the owner from making
improvements that improve the appearance and utility of the residence without
increasing the nonconforming building size, (b) a kitchen large enough to
provide adequate work space, incorporate an eating area, and accommodate modern
appliances is a standard feature in homes in the Village, and (c) the existing
configuration of the residence precludes modifying the interior space to
provide an adequate kitchen; and
   WHEREAS, the requested variations will not alter the essential character of
the neighborhood or impair an adequate supply of light and air because: (a) the
change in the windows is consistent with the design of the remainder of the
residence and does not relocate any walls and the one-story kitchen is lower
than the rest of the house; and
   WHEREAS, the requested variations will not increase the hazard from fire and
other dangers to the Subject Property as the refenestration of the second floor
and the first floor kitchen and service porch addition will comply with all
applicable building and fire protection codes; and
   WHEREAS, the requested variations to allow the refenestration of existing
walls and the construction of a kitchen addition and service porch will not
diminish the taxable value of land and buildings throughout the Village, and
the taxable value of the Subject Property may be increased because of the
proposed improvements; and
   WHEREAS, the requested variations will not contribute to congestion on the
public streets, as they will not change the function or capacity of the single
family residence; and
   WHEREAS, there is no evidence that the proposed refenestration of existing
walls the construction of a kitchen and service porch addition will otherwise
impair the public health, safety, comfort, morals, and welfare of the
inhabitants of the Village.
   WHEREAS, the requested variations are in harmony with the general purpose
and intent of the Winnetka Zoning Ordinance, in that they allow the renovation,
restoration and rehabilitation of a structurally sound existing building while
maintaining the existing scale and appearance of the community and protecting
established trees and landscaping.
   NOW, THEREFORE, the Council of the Village of Winnetka do ordain as follows:
   SECTION 1 : That the foregoing recitals are hereby incorporated as the
findings of the Council of the Village of Winnetka, as if fully set forth
herein.
   SECTION 2: The Subject Property, commonly known as 785 Lincoln Avenue,
Winnetka, Illinois, and located in the R-4 Single-Family Residential Zoning
District provided in Title 17 of the Winnetka Village Code, is hereby granted a
variation from the maximum building size limitations of Section 17.16.010(G) of
the Winnetka Zoning Ordinance, to allow a total gross floor area of 4,216.59
square feet, whereas the maximum building size limitation for the Subject
Property is 3,679.97 square feet, resulting in a variation of 671.35 square
feet (18.24%), for the purpose of changing the fenestration in existing walls
on the second floor and constructing a one-story, 134.73-square foot expansion
of the kitchen and service porch to the residence on the Subject Property, all
in accordance with the drawings and plans filed with the application for
variations.
   SECTION 3: That the variations hereby granted is conditioned upon the
commencement of the proposed construction within 12 months after the effective
date of this Ordinance.
   SECTION 4: This Ordinance shall take effect immediately upon passage,
approval and posting.
   ADOPTED this 20th day of November, 2001, pursuant to the following roll call
vote:
   AYES:    Trustees Aquilino, Brower, Presser and Greenough
   NAYS:    Trustees Powell and Woodbury
   ABSENT:    None
   APPROVED this 20th day of November, 2001.
   Signed:
   /s/Michael F. Duhl
   Village President
Countersigned:
/s/Douglas G. Williams
Village Clerk
