ORDINANCE NO. M-33-2001
AN ORDINANCE AUTHORIZING A SHORT TERM LEASE OF VILLAGE PROPERTY TO LAND ROVER
WINNETKA (93 Green Bay Road)
   WHEREAS, on November 1, 2001, pursuant to Ordinance M-22-2001, the Village
of Winnetka purchased the property commonly known as 93 Green Bay Road (the
“Property”), which is legally described as follows:
Lot 1 of the Woyner’s Subdivision in the North Half of Section 28, Township 42
North, Range 13, East of the Third Principal Meridian, in the Village of
Winnetka, in Cook County, Illinois; and
   WHEREAS, the Property is located at the southeast corner of Winnetka Avenue
and Green Bay Road and has been identified in the Comprehensive Plan, Winnetka
2020, as a location for a future Village park; and
   WHEREAS, the Property is bordered on the east by the Union Pacific Railroad
right-of-way and is bordered on the south by the South Indian Hill Parking Lot,
which is owned by the Village; and
   WHEREAS, the Property is the former site of G & W Auto Repair and is
improved with a service garage, air compressor, underground lift and a 3-tank
waste boil heating system; and
   WHEREAS, G & W Auto Repair has relocated to a site outside of the Village
and the Village’s acquisition of the property prevents commercial redevelopment
of the Property and secures its availability for conversion to a park in
accordance with the Comprehensive Plan; and
   WHEREAS, M. E. Fields, Inc. is a Delaware corporation authorized to do
business in the State of Illinois, and does business as Land Rover Winnetka, a
retail automobile sales and services business, at 80 Green Bay Road, Winnetka,
Illinois, pursuant to a special use permit and license agreement authorized by
Ordinance M-456-96; and
   WHEREAS, Land Rover Winnetka has requested that the Village lease the
property to it for the storage and servicing of vehicles in conjunction with
its retail sales of new automobiles from its main showroom at 80 Green Bay
Road; and
   WHEREAS, the Village and Land Rover Winnetka have agreed to terms and
conditions for such lease, which is attached hereto as Exhibit A; and
   WHEREAS, leasing the Property to Land Rover Winnetka subject to the terms
and conditions set forth in Exhibit A, is in the public interest in that it
allows the Village to recover some of the costs of acquiring the property,
keeps the property on the tax rolls and assures that Land Rover Winnetka will
remain on Green Bay Road within the Village of Winnetka, thereby securing
continuing sales tax revenues and anchoring the Indian Hill commercial
district; and
   WHEREAS, pursuant to the provisions of Section 11-76-1 of Article 11 of the
Illinois Municipal Code, the Village of Winnetka is authorized to lease
property owned by the Village for a term of up to 99 years.
   NOW, THEREFORE, the Council of the Village of Winnetka do ordain as follows:
   SECTION 1: The foregoing recitals are hereby incorporated as the findings of
the Council of the Village of Winnetka, as if fully set forth herein.
   SECTION 2:  The Council of the Village of Winnetka hereby approve an
agreement for the lease of the Property to Land Rover Winnetka for a period of
five years, with an option for a five-year extension, said lease agreement
being substantially in the form attached hereto as Exhibit A and incorporated
herein by reference.
   SECTION 3: From and after the effective date of this Ordinance, the Village
President and Village Clerk are hereby authorized and directed to execute the
Lease and to do all things necessary and essential to carry out the provisions
of the Lease.
   SECTION 4: This Ordinance shall take effect immediately upon passage,
approval and posting.
   ADOPTED this 8th day of January, 2002, pursuant to the following roll call
vote:
   AYES:    Trustees Brower, Greenough, Powell, presser and Woodbury
   NAYS:    None
   ABSENT:    Trustee Aquilino
   APPROVED this 8th day of January, 2002.
   Signed:
   /s/Michael F. Duhl
   Village President
Countersigned:
/s/Douglas G. Williams
Village Clerk
Introduced: December 18, 2001
Posted: December 19, 2001
Passed and Approved: January 8, 2002
Posted: January 9, 2002
ORDINANCE NO. M-34-2001
AN ORDINANCE LEVYING TAXES FOR THE YEAR 2001
   WHEREAS, on March 6th, 2001, the Council of the Village of Winnetka adopted
Resolution No. R-7-2001, which budgeted $22,986,230 to meet the expenses and
liabilities of the Village for general corporate purposes, refuse collection
and disposal, debt service principal and interest, and retirement fund
contributions for the fiscal year beginning April 1, 2001, and ending March 31,
2002; and
   WHEREAS, on October 2, 2001, the Council of the Village of Winnetka
determined the amounts of money estimated to be necessary to be raised by
taxation of taxable property within the Village for general corporate purposes,
for refuse collection and disposal, for debt service principal and interest and
for retirement fund contributions for the fiscal year beginning April 1, 2001,
and ending March 31, 2002; and
   WHEREAS, pursuant to the Cook County Truth in Taxation Law, 35 ILCS 200/18-
101.1, et seq., the Council of the Village of Winnetka published notice of its
proposed tax levy in the November 22, 2001, edition of the Winnetka Talk, an
English language newspaper in general circulation within the Village; and
   WHEREAS, pursuant to said notice, and in accordance with the Cook County
Truth in Taxation Law, as amended by Public Act 92-475, the Council of the
Village of Winnetka conducted a public hearing on the proposed levy at the
first regularly scheduled Council meeting in the month of December, on Tuesday,
December 4, 2001; and
   WHEREAS, the Council of the Village of Winnetka have determined that the
total amount of money necessary to be raised by the levy and collection of
taxes for general corporate purposes, for refuse collection and disposal, for
debt service principal and interest and for retirement fund contributions, is
$10,054,710.
   NOW, THEREFORE, the Council of the Village of Winnetka do ordain:
   SECTION 1: That the foregoing recitals are hereby adopted as the findings of
the Council of the Village of Winnetka, as fully set forth herein.
   SECTION 2: That in order to meet the expenses and liabilities of the Village
of Winnetka for the fiscal year beginning April 1, 2001, and ending March 31,
2002, for general corporate purposes, for refuse collection and disposal, for
debt service principal and interest and for retirement fund contributions,
there is hereby levied on all property within the corporate limits of said
Village subject to taxation, as assessed and equalized for the year 2001, the
sum of Ten Million, Fifty Four Thousand, Seven Hundred Ten Dollars
($10,054,710), which is to be collected from the levy of the Village of
Winnetka for the year 2001 for all purposes heretofore budgeted, the total of
which has been ascertained and is as indicated in the following Summary of 2001
Property Tax Levy and set forth in detail in the Tax Levy Report, which is
attached as Exhibit A and is incorporated herein by reference.
