ORDINANCE NO. M-37-2001
AN ORDINANCE GRANTING A VARIATION IN THE APPLICATION OF THE ZONING ORDINANCE OF
THE VILLAGE OF WINNETKA COOK COUNTY, ILLINOIS (1173 Asbury)
   WHEREAS, there has been presented to the Council of the Village of Winnetka,
Cook County, Illinois, the request of the owner of the following described real
estate (the “Subject Property”):
Lot 11 in Block 11 in Chicago North Shore Land Company’s Subdivision, in
Section 17 and 18, Township 42 North, Range 13, east of the third principal
meridian, in Cook County, Illinois,
commonly known as 1173 Asbury Avenue, Winnetka, Illinois, and located in the R-
5 Single-Family Residential Zoning District provided in Chapter 17.12 of the
Winnetka Zoning Ordinance, Title 17 of the Winnetka Village Code, for the
following variations from the intensity of use of lot limitations of Section
17.12.010(F) of the Winnetka Zoning Ordinance: (a) a variation of 484.18 square
feet (24.24.%) from the maximum allowable roofed lot coverage of 1,997.25
square feet, to allow the existing, legally nonconforming roofed lot coverage
to be increased from 2,259.49 square feet to 2,481.43 square feet, and (b) a
variation of 450.41 square feet (11.28%) from the maximum allowable impermeable
surface of 3,994.50 square feet, to allow the existing, legally nonconforming
impermeable surface to be increased from 4,222.97 square feet to 4,444.91
square feet, all to allow the construction of a 221.94 square foot open porch
at the front of the residence; and
   WHEREAS, on November 12, 2001, on due notice thereof, the Zoning Board of
Appeals conducted a public hearing on the requested variations and by the
unanimous vote of the five members then present, has reported to the Council
recommending that the requested variations be granted; and
   WHEREAS, there are practical difficulties and unique hardships associated
with carrying out the strict application of the Zoning Ordinance with respect
to the Subject Property in that: (a) the Subject Property is a nonconforming
lot, with both the average lot width and the lot size being below the minimum
standards for the R-5 zoning district; (b) the residence on the Subject
Property was constructed in 1908, prior to the existence of zoning regulations;
(c) the proposed porch will replace a small front stoop and will reduce the
hazard of water and ice directly outside the front door; (d) the area of the
proposed porch is approximately 28 square feet less than the 250 square feet of
porch area that would be excluded from roofed lot coverage if the owners built
a porch that extended across the entire front of the residence; and (e) the
owners are unable to take advantage of the 250 square foot front porch
exclusion from roofed lot coverage because of the nonconforming east building
line and the proximity of a 150 year old, 30-inch diameter oak tree; and
   WHEREAS, the Subject Property cannot yield a reasonable return if permitted
to be used only under the conditions allowed by the Zoning Ordinance, in that
the proposed front porch is necessary to reduce the hazard of water and ice
directly outside the front door and will more closely approximate the original
appearance of the residence, which at one time had an enclosed front porch of
comparable dimensions; and
   WHEREAS, the requested variations will not alter the essential character of
the neighborhood because the proposed front porch is consistent with the style
of the house, complies with front setback requirements, and more closely
approximates the original appearance of the building, with the mature oak tree
remaining and the porch being of comparable dimensions to the enclosed porch
that was located at the front of the house at one time; and
   WHEREAS, the requested variations will not impair an adequate supply of
light and air because the proposed open porch complies with all applicable
setbacks and has a roof that is only one story high; and
   WHEREAS, the requested variations will not increase the hazard from fire and
other dangers to the Subject Property as the proposed front porch will comply
with all applicable building and fire protection codes; and
   WHEREAS, the requested variations will not diminish the taxable value of
land and buildings throughout the Village, and the taxable value of the Subject
Property may be increased because of the proposed improvements; and
   WHEREAS, the proposed front porch will not contribute to congestion on the
public streets, because neither the use nor the capacity of the residence will
be changed; and
   WHEREAS, there is no evidence that the proposed open front porch will
otherwise impair the public health, safety, comfort, morals, and welfare of the
inhabitants of the Village; and
   WHEREAS, the requested variations are in harmony with the general purpose
and intent of the Winnetka Zoning Ordinance, in that they will allow the
renovation, restoration and rehabilitation of a structurally sound existing
building while maintaining the existing scale and appearance of the community
and protecting established trees and landscaping.
   NOW, THEREFORE, the Council of the Village of Winnetka do ordain as follows:
   SECTION 1 : The foregoing recitals are hereby incorporated as the findings
of the Council of the Village of Winnetka, as if fully set forth herein.
   SECTION 2:  The following variations from the intensity of use of lot
provisions of Section 17.12.010(F) of the Winnetka Zoning Ordinance are hereby
granted to the Subject Property, commonly known as 1173 Asbury Avenue,
Winnetka, Illinois, and located in the R-5 Single-Family Residential Zoning
District provided in Chapter 17.12 of the Winnetka Zoning Ordinance, Title 17
of the Winnetka Village Code: (a) a variation of 484.18 square feet (24.24.%)
from the maximum allowable roofed lot coverage of 1,997.25 square feet, to
allow the existing, legally nonconforming roofed lot coverage to be increased
from 2,259.49 square feet to 2,481.43 square feet, and (b) a variation of
450.41 square feet (11.28%) from the maximum allowable impermeable surface of
3,994.50 square feet, to allow the existing, legally nonconforming impermeable
surface to be increased from 4,222.97 square feet to 4,444.91 square feet, all
to allow the construction of a 221.94 square foot open porch at the front of
the residence, in accordance with the plans and elevations submitted with the
application for variation.
   SECTION 3: That the variations hereby granted are conditioned upon the
commencement of the proposed construction within 12 months after the effective
date of this Ordinance.
   SECTION 4: This Ordinance shall take effect immediately upon passage,
approval and posting.
   ADOPTED this 18th day of December, 2001, pursuant to the following roll call
vote:
   AYES:    Trustees Aquilino, Brower, Greenough, Powell, Presser and Woodbury
   NAYS:    None
   ABSENT:    None
   APPROVED this 18th day of December, 2001.
   Signed:
   /s/Michael F. Duhl
   Village President
Countersigned:
/s/Douglas G. Williams
Village Clerk
