ORDINANCE NO. M-38-2001
AN ORDINANCE GRANTING A VARIATION IN THE APPLICATION OF THE ZONING ORDINANCE OF
THE VILLAGE OF WINNETKA COOK COUNTY, ILLINOIS (1179 Asbury Avenue)
   WHEREAS, there has been presented to the Council of the Village of Winnetka,
Cook County, Illinois, the request of the owner of the following described real
estate (the “Subject Property”):
The east ½ of Lot 8 in block 11 in Lloyd’s Subdivision of Blocks 1 to 5
inclusive in Taylor’s second addition to Taylorsport, being a part of the NE ¼
of Section 18 and part of the NW ¼ of Section 17, Township 42 North, Range 13,
east of the Third Principal Meridian in Cook County, Illinois.
commonly known as 1179 Asbury Avenue, Winnetka, Illinois, and located in the R-
5 Single-Family Residential Zoning District provided in Chapter 17.12 of the
Winnetka Zoning Ordinance, Title 17 of the Winnetka Village Code, for the
following variations: (a) a variation from the intensity of use of lot
limitations of Section 17.12.010(F) of the Winnetka Zoning Ordinance, to allow
a roofed lot coverage of 2,070.30 square feet, which exceeds the maximum
allowable roofed lot coverage of 1,997.25 square feet, resulting in a variation
of 73.05 square feet (3.66%); and (b) a variation from the side yard setback
requirements of Section 17.12.010(I), to allow an east side yard setback of
0.96 feet, rather than the required minimum of 6.00 feet, resulting in a
variation of 5.04 feet (84%); all to allow the reconstruction of the front
porch, the construction of a mudroom addition and the construction of a
detached garage; and
   WHEREAS, on November 12, 2001, on due notice thereof, the Zoning Board of
Appeals conducted a public hearing on the requested variations and, by the
unanimous vote of the five members then present, has reported to the Council
recommending that the requested variation be granted; and
   WHEREAS, there are practical difficulties and unique hardships associated
with carrying out the strict application of the Zoning Ordinance with respect
to the Subject Property in that: (a) the Subject Property is a nonconforming
lot, having both an average lot width and lot size that are under the minimum
required in the R-5 zoning district; (b) the residence on the Subject Property
was constructed in 1914, prior to the enactment of the Winnetka Zoning
Ordinance; (c) the nonconformities in the side yard setback cannot be cured
without either removing substantial portions of the building or replacing it in
its entirety; (d) the nonconforming location of the east wall of the existing
attached garage and second floor office precludes any modifications to the
nonconforming east wall without first obtaining a variation; (e) due to the
orientation of the existing driveway and residence, and the proposed conversion
of the existing attached garage into a porte cochere is the only available
means of modifying the Subject Property to allow for the construction a two-car
garage; and
   WHEREAS, the Subject Property cannot yield a reasonable return if permitted
to be used only under the conditions allowed by the Zoning Ordinance, in that:
(a) the requested variations are necessary in order to provide a mudroom and
two-car garage on the Subject Property, both of which are standard features in
the real estate market within the Village; and (b) without the requested
variations, the owners of the Subject Property would be unable to create
additional living space within the existing building footprint and develop the
Subject Property in a manner consistent with the development of other
properties in the immediate vicinity; and
   WHEREAS, the requested variations will not alter the essential character of
the neighborhood because the proposed detached garage at the rear of the
Subject Property is in a location that is favored by the Winnetka Zoning
Ordinance, the creation of the porte cochere is consistent with the existing
style of the residence, the proposed change in roof form is consistent with the
building’s architectural character, and the building’s location and size in
relation to the streetscape will not change; and
   WHEREAS, the requested variations will not impair an adequate supply of
light and air because: (a) the proposed detached garage will be in a conforming
location;, (b) the proposed mudroom addition is located at an interior corner
of the building and is lower than the adjacent parts of the building; and (c)
the creation of the porte cochere significantly decreases the volume of
enclosed space that extends beyond required setbacks, by opening the north,
east and south walls below the office, adding an additional 325 square feet of
open space within the existing footprint of the building; and
   WHEREAS, the requested variations will not increase the hazard from fire and
other dangers to the Subject Property as the new construction will comply with
all applicable building and fire protection codes; and
   WHEREAS, the requested variations will not diminish the taxable value of
land and buildings throughout the Village, and the taxable value of the Subject
Property may be increased because of the proposed improvements; and
   WHEREAS, the reconstructed front porch, mudroom addition and detached garage
will not contribute to congestion on the public streets, as they will neither
increase the capacity of the residence nor alter its use, and the increased
length of driveway and addition of a two-car garage will provide additional
off-street parking; and
   WHEREAS, there is no evidence that the proposed reconstructed front porch,
mudroom addition and new detached garage will otherwise impair the public
health, safety, comfort, morals, and welfare of the inhabitants of the Village;
and
   WHEREAS, the requested variations are in harmony with the general purpose
and intent of the Winnetka Zoning Ordinance, in that they will allow the
renovation, restoration and rehabilitation of a structurally sound existing
building while maintaining the existing scale and appearance of the community
and protecting established trees and landscaping.
   NOW, THEREFORE, the Council of the Village of Winnetka do ordain as follows:
   SECTION 1 : That the foregoing recitals are hereby incorporated as the
findings of the Council of the Village of Winnetka, as if fully set forth
herein.
   SECTION 2:  The following variations are hereby granted to the Subject
Property, commonly known as 1179 Asbury Avenue, Winnetka, Illinois, and located
in the R-5 Single-Family Residential Zoning District provided in Chapter 17.12
of the Winnetka Zoning Ordinance, Title 17 of the Winnetka Village Code: (a) a
variation from the intensity of use of lot limitations of Section 17.12.010(F)
of the Winnetka Zoning Ordinance, to allow a roofed lot coverage of 2,070.30
square feet, which exceeds the maximum allowable roofed lot coverage of
1,997.25 square feet, resulting in a variation of 73.05 square feet (3.66%);
and (b) a variation from the side yard setback requirements of Section
17.12.010(I), to allow an east side yard setback of 0.96 feet, rather than the
required minimum of 6.00 feet, resulting in a variation of 5.04 feet (84%); all
to allow the reconstruction of the front porch, the construction of a mudroom
addition and the construction of a detached garage, in accordance with the
plans and elevations submitted with the application for variations.
   SECTION 3: That the variations hereby granted are conditioned upon the
commencement of the proposed construction within 12 months after the effective
date of this Ordinance.
   SECTION 4: This Ordinance shall take effect immediately upon passage,
approval and posting.
   ADOPTED this 18th day of December, 2001, pursuant to the following roll call
vote:
   AYES:    Trustees Aquilino, Brower, Greenough, Powell, Presser and Woodbury
   NAYS:    None
   ABSENT:    None
   APPROVED this 18th day of December, 2001.
   Signed:
   /s/Michael F. Duhl
   Village President
Countersigned:
/s/Douglas G. Williams
Village Clerk
