ORDINANCE NO. M-40-2001
AN ORDINANCE GRANTING A VARIATION IN THE APPLICATION OF THE ZONING ORDINANCE OF
THE VILLAGE OF WINNETKA COOK COUNTY, ILLINOIS (1092 Spruce Street)
   WHEREAS, there has been presented to the Council of the Village of Winnetka,
Cook County, Illinois, the request of the owner of the following described real
estate (the “Subject Property”):
Lot 7 in Block 3 in Groveland Addition to Winnetka Addition, being a
subdivision of the East 70 acres of the Northwest quarter of Section 20,
Township 42 North, Range 13, East of the Third Principal Meridian, in Cook
County, Illinois,
commonly known as 1092 Spruce Street, Winnetka, Illinois, and located in the R-
5 Single-Family Residential Zoning District provided in Chapter 17.12 of the
Winnetka Zoning Ordinance, Title 17 of the Winnetka Village Code, for a
variation from the side yard setback requirements of Section 17.12.010(I) of
the Winnetka Zoning Ordinance, to allow a proposed second floor addition to
align with the legally nonconforming first floor walls, observing a 6.29-foot
setback from the east property line rather than the required 8.0 feet,
resulting in a variation of 1.71 feet (21.38%); and
   WHEREAS, on November 12, 2001, on due notice thereof, the Zoning Board of
Appeals conducted a public hearing on the requested variation and by the
unanimous vote of the five members then present, has reported to the Council
recommending that the requested variation be granted; and
   WHEREAS, there are practical difficulties and unique hardships associated
with carrying out the strict application of the Zoning Ordinance with respect
to the Subject Property in that: (a) the Subject Property is a legally
nonconforming lot that is approximately 50 feet wide rather than the 60 foot
minimum required in the R-5 zoning district; (b) the residence was originally
constructed in 1908, before the Village’s enactment of zoning regulations in
1925; (c) due to the location of the residence on the Subject Property, both
the east and west side yards are nonconforming, with the west side yard being
approximately 2 feet rather than the required 6-foot minimum and the east side
yard being 6.29 feet rather than the 8-foot minimum; (d) as proposed, the
second floor addition will be achieved by vertically extending the walls of the
one-story addition constructed at the rear of the residence in 1993, prior to
the enactment of the zoning ordinance amendments that require an 8-foot setback
on one of the two side yards; and (e) setting the second floor in from the
first floor walls to conform with the east side yard setback requirement is
structurally and aesthetically undesirable and would create ongoing maintenance
problems for the small, flat roof area that would be created by the second
floor setback; and
   WHEREAS, the Subject Property cannot yield a reasonable return if permitted
to be used only under the conditions allowed by the Zoning Ordinance, in that:
(a) the proposed variation will allow the creation of a master suite, which is
a standard feature of single-family residences within the Village and the
immediate vicinity of the Subject Property; (b) reducing the size of the
proposed second floor addition to conform with the 8-foot setback would (i)
reduce the size of the master bedroom, (ii) increase construction costs, (iii)
increase long-term maintenance costs for the first floor roof, (iv) result in
walls and windows on the second floor being out of alignment with the first
floor, (v) affect the appearance of the building from the street and (vi)
result in a second floor alignment that is inconsistent with the development in
the immediate vicinity and the Village, all of which would have a negative
impact on the value of the Subject Property; and (c) reducing the footprint of
the existing first floor family room to conform with the 8-foot setback
requirement and to align with a conforming second floor addition would (i)
increase construction costs, (ii) require relocation of the building
foundation, (iii) reduce the size and utility of the existing family room and
basement room below it, and (iv) reduce the size and utility of the proposed
master bedroom, all of which would reduce the value of the residence; and
   WHEREAS, the requested variation will not alter the essential character of
the neighborhood because: (a) the style of the proposed addition is consistent
with the architectural style of the rest of the building; (b) having a second
floor wall that aligns with a first floor wall is a common feature of side
building walls in the Village of Winnetka and the immediate vicinity of the
Subject Property; (c) the 6.29-foot east side yard is consistent with the
existing side yards in the immediate vicinity, most of which are nonconforming
because the buildings were built before 1999; and (d) the resulting building
will be well within maximum building size limitations; and
   WHEREAS, the requested variation will not impair an adequate supply of light
and air because the proposed building height is within existing height
limitations and the proposed 6.29-foot east side yard setback is consistent
with the setbacks on properties within the immediate vicinity; and
   WHEREAS, the requested variation will not increase the hazard from fire and
other dangers to the Subject Property because the proposed second floor
addition will comply with all applicable building and fire protection codes;
and
   WHEREAS, the requested variation will not diminish the taxable value of land
and buildings throughout the Village, and the taxable value of the Subject
Property may be increased because of the proposed improvements; and
   WHEREAS, the proposed second floor addition will not contribute to
congestion on the public streets, as the structure will remain a single-family
residence and the existing garage will remain; and
   WHEREAS, there is no evidence that the proposed second floor addition will
otherwise impair the public health, safety, comfort, morals, and welfare of the
inhabitants of the Village; and
   WHEREAS, the requested variation is in harmony with the general purpose and
intent of the Winnetka Zoning Ordinance, in that it allows the renovation,
restoration and rehabilitation of a structurally sound existing building while
maintaining the existing scale and appearance of the community and protecting
established trees and landscaping.
   NOW, THEREFORE, the Council of the Village of Winnetka do ordain as follows:
   SECTION 1 : The foregoing recitals are hereby incorporated as the findings
of the Council of the Village of Winnetka, as if fully set forth herein.
   SECTION 2:  There is hereby granted to the Subject Property, commonly known
as 1092 Spruce Street, Winnetka, Illinois, and located in the R-5 Single-Family
Residential Zoning District provided in Chapter 17.12 of the Winnetka Zoning
Ordinance, Title 17 of the Winnetka Village Code, a variation from the side
yard setback requirements of Section 17.12.010(I) of the Winnetka Zoning
Ordinance, to allow a proposed second floor addition to align with the legally
nonconforming first floor walls, observing a 6.29-foot setback from the east
property line rather than the required 8.0 feet, resulting in a variation of
1.71 feet (21.38%), all in accordance with the plans and elevations submitted
with the application for variation.
   SECTION 3: The variation hereby granted is conditioned upon the commencement
of the proposed construction within 12 months after the effective date of this
Ordinance.
   SECTION 4: This Ordinance shall take effect immediately upon passage,
approval and posting.
   ADOPTED this 18th day of December, 2001, pursuant to the following roll call
vote:
   AYES:    Trustees Aquilino, Brower, Greenough, Powell, Presser and Woodbury
   NAYS:    None
   ABSENT:    None
   APPROVED this 18th day of December, 2001.
   Signed:
   /s/Michael F. Duhl
   Village President
Countersigned:
/s/Douglas G. Williams
Village Clerk
