ORDINANCE NO. M-18-2002
AN ORDINANCE GRANTING A VARIATION IN THE APPLICATION OF THE ZONING ORDINANCE OF
THE VILLAGE OF WINNETKA COOK COUNTY, ILLINOIS (779 Bryant)
   WHEREAS, there has been presented to the Council of the Village of Winnetka,
Cook County, Illinois, the request of the owner of the following described real
estate (the “Subject Property”):
Parcel 1: The South 35 feet of Lot 4, except that part thereof described as
follows: Beginning at the Southeast corner of said Lot 5; thence southwesterly
along the Southerly line of Lot 5 (being also a division line between said Lot
5 and Lot 7 in Said Subdivision) 47.5 feet; Thence Northeasterly along a
straight line 51.29 feet to a point on the east line of said Lot 5, 12 feet
North of the Southeast corner of said Lot 5; thence south along the East line
of said Lot 5, 12 feet to the point of beginning and
Parcel 2: That part of Lot 7 described as follows: Beginning at a point in the
Southerly line of Lot 5 of said Subdivision of Blocks 26 & 41 (being also a
Division line between said Lots 5 & 7) 47.5 feet Westerly of the Southeast
corner of said Lot 5; thence Westerly along the Southerly line of said Lot 5,
47.5 feet to the Westerly line of said Lot 7; thence South along the Westerly
line of said Lot 7, 12 feet; thence Northeasterly along a straight line, 51.29
feet to the point of beginning, all in the Subdivision of Blocks 26 & 41 in
Lake View Subdivision (Lake View Subdivision being a Subdivision of the
Southeast Quarter of Section 17, and the Southwest Quarter of Section 16,
Township 42 North, Range 13, East of the Third Principal Meridian, according to
the Plat thereof recorded July 13, 1857, in Book 133, Page 76, as Document
88987) in Cook County, Illinois,
commonly known as 779 Bryant, Winnetka, Illinois, and located in the R-
3 Single-Family Residential Zoning District provided in Chapter 17.20 of the
Winnetka Zoning Ordinance, Title 17 of the Winnetka Village Code, for a
variation from the rear yard setback requirements of Section 17.20.010(J) to
allow a new, detached three-car garage to be located 1.5 feet from the east
property line, which is less than the required 6-foot rear yard setback,
resulting in a variation of 4.5 feet (75%); and
   WHEREAS, on May 13, 2002, on due notice thereof, the Zoning Board of Appeals
conducted a public hearing on the requested variation and by the unanimous vote
of the five members then present, has reported to the Council recommending that
the requested variation be granted; and
   WHEREAS, there are practical difficulties and unique hardships associated
with carrying out the strict application of the Zoning Ordinance with respect
to the Subject Property in that: (a) the Subject Property is an irregularly
shaped lot that is 135 feet wide at the front lot line and has a notched rear
lot line consisting of a 40-foot wide segment and a 35-foot segment; (b) the
existing home on the Subject Property was built in 1909 and is located at the
rear of the buildable area of the Subject Property; (c) the existing garage is
located in the rear yard at the southeast corner of the Subject Property, 1.5
feet from the east property line; and (d) the applicants propose to replace the
existing, deteriorating, two-car garage with a three-car garage that will
observe the same south and east setbacks as the existing garage; and
   WHEREAS, the Subject Property cannot yield a reasonable return if permitted
to be used only under the conditions allowed by the Zoning Ordinance, in that:
(a) the irregular shape of the Subject Property and the irregular rear lot
lines limit reasonable locations for a garage; (b) a garage has been located in
the same location of the Subject Property since 1921; (c) the strict
application of the Zoning Ordinance to the Subject Property would prohibit the
reconstruction of the garage in its established location; and (d) the proposed
new garage will replace a structurally unsound existing garage that observes an
identical setback; and
   WHEREAS, the requested variation will not alter the essential character of
the neighborhood because the new garage (a) will be in the same location of the
Subject Property as the garage it is proposed to replace, and (b) it is
designed to be compatible with the existing residence, which has been located
on the Subject Property since 1909; and
   WHEREAS, the requested variation will not impair an adequate supply of light
and air because the proposed garage is located in the same area as the garage
it will replace; and
   WHEREAS, the requested variation will not increase the hazard from fire and
other dangers to the Subject Property as it will comply with all applicable
building and fire protection codes; and
   WHEREAS, the requested variation will not diminish the taxable value of land
and buildings throughout the Village, and the taxable value of the Subject
Property may be increased because of the proposed improvements; and
   WHEREAS, the proposed new garage will not contribute to congestion on the
public streets, as the Subject Property will continue to be used as a single-
family residential property and the garage will provide one additional off-
street parking space; and
   WHEREAS, there is no evidence that the proposed garage will otherwise impair
the public health, safety, comfort, morals, and welfare of the inhabitants of
the Village.
   WHEREAS, the requested variation is in harmony with the general purpose and
intent of the Winnetka Zoning Ordinance, in that it allows the renovation,
restoration and rehabilitation of a structurally sound existing building while
maintaining the existing scale and appearance of the community and protecting
established trees and landscaping.
   NOW, THEREFORE, the Council of the Village of Winnetka do ordain as follows:
   SECTION 1 : That the foregoing recitals are hereby incorporated as the
findings of the Council of the Village of Winnetka, as if fully set forth
herein.
   SECTION 2: There is hereby granted to the Subject Property, commonly known
as 779 Bryant, Winnetka, Illinois, and located in the R-3 Single-Family
Residential Zoning District provided in Chapter 17.20 of the Winnetka Zoning
Ordinance, Title 17 of the Winnetka Village Code, a variation from the rear
yard setback requirements of Section 17.20.010(J) to allow a new, detached
three-car garage to be located 1.5 feet from the east property line, which is
less than the required 6-foot rear yard setback, resulting in a variation of
4.5 feet (75%), in accordance with the plans and elevations submitted with the
application for variation.
   SECTION 3: That the variation hereby granted is conditioned upon the
commencement of the proposed construction within 12 months after the effective
date of this Ordinance.
   SECTION 4: This Ordinance shall take effect immediately upon passage,
approval and posting.
   ADOPTED this 18th day of June, 2002, pursuant to the following roll call
vote:
   AYES:    Trustees Aquilino, Brower, Powell, Presser, and Woodbury
   NAYS:    None
   ABSENT:    Trustee Greenough
   Signed:
   s/s Michael F. Duhl
    Village President
Countersigned:
s/s Douglas G. Williams
Village Clerk
Introduced: June 4, 2002
Posted: June 5, 2002
Passed and Approved: June 18, 2002
Posted: June 19, 2002
ORDINANCE NO. M-19-2002
AN ORDINANCE GRANTING A VARIATION IN THE APPLICATION OF THE ZONING ORDINANCE OF
THE VILLAGE OF WINNETKA COOK COUNTY, ILLINOIS (882 Willow Road)
   WHEREAS, there has been presented to the Council of the Village of Winnetka,
Cook County, Illinois, the request of the owner of the following described real
estate (the “Subject Property”):
Lot 5 and the West half of Lot 6 in Oak Grove Addition to Winnetka, being a
subdivision in the Northwest quarter of the Southeast quarter of Section 20,
Township 42 North, Range 13, East of the Third Principal Meridian, in Cook
County, Illinois,
commonly known as 882 Willow Road, Winnetka, Illinois, and located in the R-
2 Single-Family Residential Zoning District provided in Chapter 17.24 of the
Winnetka Zoning Ordinance, Title 17 of the Winnetka Village Code, for a
variation from the side yard setback requirements of Section 17.24.010(I) to
allow a west side yard of 6.8 feet and an east side yard of 8.16 feet, which
are less than the 12-foot required side yards, resulting in a west side yard
variation of 5.20 feet (43.33%) and an east side yard variation of 3.84 feet
(32%), to allow a proposed two-story addition at the rear of the existing
single-family residence to align with the existing walls, and to allow a new,
detached one-car garage to be constructed in the southeast corner of the
Subject Property; and
   WHEREAS, on May 13, 2002, on due notice thereof, the Zoning Board of Appeals
conducted a public hearing on the requested variation and by the unanimous vote
of the five members then present, has reported to the Council recommending that
the requested variation be granted; and
   WHEREAS, there are practical difficulties and unique hardships associated
with carrying out the strict application of the Zoning Ordinance with respect
to the Subject Property in that: (a) the Subject Property is a legally
nonconforming zoning lot with a lot width of 37.63 feet, which is substantially
less than the minimum 100-foot lot width required in the R-2 zoning district;
and (b) applying the 12-foot side yard requirement to both side yards reduces
the width of the buildable area on the Subject Property to 13.63 feet; and
   WHEREAS, the Subject Property cannot yield a reasonable return if permitted
to be used only under the conditions allowed by the Zoning Ordinance, in that:
(a) the residence on the Subject Property was built in 1907, before the
enactment of the first Zoning Ordinance in 1925; (b) due to the minimal width
of the buildable area, the entire existing residence is in a nonconforming
location, with a 6.8-foot west side yard and an 8.16-foot east side yard; (c)
the minimal buildable area on the Subject Property prevents construction of any
residence of a useable size on the Subject Property; and (d) the applicants
have modified their plans so that the proposed additions and garage meet all
other yard and setback requirements and fall within the applicable limitations
for roofed lot coverage and gross floor area; and
   WHEREAS, the requested variations will not alter the essential character of
the neighborhood because (a) the proposed renovation will maintain the
appearance of the residence in the streetscape by setting the second floor
addition back from the front of the building and by aligning with the existing
sides of the building, and (b) the garage will be placed in a conforming
location in the rear of the lot, which is a typical location for detached
garages; and
   WHEREAS, the requested variation will not impair an adequate supply of light
and air because the proposed addition and garage will conform with all building
height limitations; and
   WHEREAS, the requested variations will not increase the hazard from fire and
other dangers to the Subject Property as the proposed addition and garage will
comply with all applicable building and fire protection codes; and
   WHEREAS, the requested variations will not diminish the taxable value of
land and buildings throughout the Village, and the taxable value of the Subject
Property may be increased because of the proposed improvements; and
   WHEREAS, the proposed addition and detached garage will not contribute to
congestion on the public streets, as the Subject Property will continue to be
used as a single-family residence and the detached garage will provide
additional off-street parking; and
   WHEREAS, there is no evidence that the proposed addition and detached garage
will otherwise impair the public health, safety, comfort, morals, and welfare
of the inhabitants of the Village.
   WHEREAS, the requested variations are in harmony with the general purpose
and intent of the Winnetka Zoning Ordinance, in that they allow the renovation,
restoration and rehabilitation of a structurally sound existing building while
maintaining the existing scale and appearance of the community and protecting
established trees and landscaping.
   NOW, THEREFORE, the Council of the Village of Winnetka do ordain as follows:
   SECTION 1 : That the foregoing recitals are hereby incorporated as the
findings of the Council of the Village of Winnetka, as if fully set forth
herein.
   SECTION 2:  The following variations are hereby granted to the Subject
Property, commonly known as f882 Willow Road, Winnetka, Illinois, and located
in the R-2 Single-Family Residential Zoning District provided in Chapter 17.24
of the Winnetka Zoning Ordinance, Title 17 of the Winnetka Village Code: (a) a
variation from the side yard setback requirements of Section 17.24.010(I) to
allow a west side yard of 6.8 feet, which is less than the required 12-foot
side yard, resulting in a variation of 5.20 feet (43.33%); and (b) a variation
from the side yard setback requirements of Section 17.24.010(I) to allow an
east side yard of 8.16 feet, which is less than the required 12-foot side yard,
resulting in a variation of 3.84 feet (32%); to allow a proposed two-story
addition at the rear of the existing single-family residence to align with the
existing building walls, and to allow a new, detached one-car garage to be
constructed in the southeast corner of the Subject Property, all in accordance
with the plans and elevations dated February 12, 2002, as revised on May 6,
2002.
   SECTION 3: That the variation hereby granted is conditioned upon the
commencement of the proposed construction within 12 months after the effective
date of this Ordinance.
   SECTION 4: This Ordinance shall take effect immediately upon passage,
approval and posting.
   ADOPTED this 18th day of June, 2002, pursuant to the following roll call
vote:
   AYES:    Trustees Aquilino, Brower, Powell, Presser, and Woodbury
   NAYS:    None
   ABSENT:    Trustee Greenough
   Signed:
   s/s Michael F. Duhl
    Village President
Countersigned:
s/s Douglas G. Williams
Village Clerk
Introduced: June 4, 2002
Posted: June 5, 2002
Passed and Approved: June 18, 2002
