ORDINANCE NO. M-24-2002
AN ORDINANCE GRANTING A VARIATION IN THE APPLICATION OF THE ZONING ORDINANCE OF
THE VILLAGE OF WINNETKA COOK COUNTY, ILLINOIS (530 Winnetka Avenue)
   WHEREAS, there has been presented to the Council of the Village of Winnetka,
Cook County, Illinois, the request of the owner of the following described real
estate (the “Subject Property”):
Lots 3, 4 and 5 (except the west 33 feet of said Lot 5) in Block 2 in Manus
Indian Hill Subdivision of part of the North half of Section 28, Township 42
North, Range 13 east of the Third Principal Meridian, in the Village of
Winnetka, in Cook County, Illinois,
commonly known as 530 Winnetka Avenue, Winnetka, Illinois, and located in the
B-1 Multiple-Family Residential Zoning District provided in Chapter 17.32 of
the Winnetka Zoning Ordinance, Title 17 of the Winnetka Village Code, for the
following variations: (a) a variation from the use restrictions of Section
17.32.010(B)1, which does not include office uses within the permitted uses or
permitted special uses in the B-1 Multi-Family Residential Zoning District, and
(b) a variation from Section 17.64.010(A)3, which prohibits structural
alterations and expansions to nonconforming buildings containing nonconforming
uses; and
   WHEREAS, the requested variations would allow the construction of (a) an
addition and interior alterations to an existing medical office building to
provide a handicap accessible entry with additional office, reception and file
storage space at the northwest portion of the building, and (b) and addition to
the entrance on the west side of the building by replacing a 2-door entry with
a single door entry, and providing clearance for a new doorway to the existing
basement stairs, all in accordance with the plans and elevations dated February
8, 2002, as amended and presented to the Design Review Board on June 20, 2002;
and
   WHEREAS, the owners’ application originally included a request for
variations from the front setback requirements and impermeable surface
limitations of subsections H and F of Section 17.32.010 of the Winnetka Zoning
Ordinance to allow the construction of a parking area adjacent to the front of
the building; and
   WHEREAS, on April 8, 2002, on due notice thereof, the Zoning Board of
Appeals conducted a public hearing on the requested variations and, by the
unanimous vote of the Board, recommended that the Council grant all of the
requested variations; and
   WHEREAS, on April 18, 2002, the Winnetka Design Review Board considered the
proposed building alterations and front yard parking for the Subject Property,
and (a) issued unfavorable comment on the proposed parking lot and related new
curb cut, (b) recommended the use of real stucco rather than proposed synthetic
stucco for the north addition and (c) recommended that the brick for the
proposed 9.91-square foot entrance addition on the west elevation match the
existing building; and
   WHEREAS, on May 7, 2002, the Village Council considered all four zoning
variations and directed the owners to address the concerns raised by the Design
Review Board; and
   WHEREAS, the petitioners subsequently modified their plans by eliminating
the proposed parking lot expansion and withdrawing their request for the
related variations; and
   WHEREAS, on June 20, 2002, the modified plans, which eliminated the parking
lot expansion, provided for the use of natural stucco on the north edition and
face brick to match the existing brick on the west elevation, was considered by
the Design Review Board, which then issued favorable comment to the Village
Council on the modified plans; and
   WHEREAS, there are practical difficulties and unique hardships associated
with carrying out the strict application of the Zoning Ordinance with respect
to the Subject Property in that: (a) the Subject Property is located in the B-
1 Multi-Family Residential Zoning District; (b) the Subject Property is
improved with a one-story office building that is used for medical offices; (c)
both the building and its current use are legal nonconformities, having been in
conformity with the Zoning Ordinance prior to the enactment of Ordinance MC-
202-98, which eliminated offices as permitted uses within the B-1 Zoning
District; (d) recent development activities on other properties on the south
side of Winnetka Avenue near Green Bay indicate that the location of the
Subject Property, coupled with its relatively small size of 117 feet wide by
150 feet deep, would complicate the redevelopment of the Subject Property in
full conformity with the applicable zoning regulations; (e) the proposed
building modifications are modest, with less than 10 square feet being added to
the west side and the 334-square foot addition at the northwest corner of the
building being located within an area that is now a roofed, concrete porch; and
(f) the addition and interior alterations improve handicap accessibility and
provide safer ingress and egress, in addition to providing a more efficient use
of interior space
   WHEREAS, the Subject Property cannot yield a reasonable return if permitted
to be used only under the conditions allowed by the Zoning Ordinance, in that:
(a) the existing building cannot be converted into a multi-family residential
building; and (b) bringing the Subject Property into full conformity with the
Zoning Ordinance would impose an unreasonable burden on the owner because it
would require the replacement of the existing building and the displacement of
an established medical office; and
   WHEREAS, the requested variations will not alter the essential character of
the neighborhood because: (a) the office building is a well established
presence in the neighborhood; (b) the use of the building will not change; (c)
the exterior changes to the building will improve its appearance from Winnetka
Avenue; and (d) with the sole exception of the 9.91-square foot addition at the
west entrance, the building changes will lie under the current roofed area; and
   WHEREAS, the requested variations will not impair an adequate supply of
light and air because the only expansion of the building’s footprint will be
the one-story 9.91-square foot entrance addition at the west of the building;
and
   WHEREAS, the requested variations will not increase the hazard from fire and
other dangers to the Subject Property, as the proposed work will comply with
all applicable building and fire protection codes; and
   WHEREAS, there is no evidence that the requested variations will diminish
the taxable value of land and buildings throughout the Village, and
   WHEREAS, the proposed construction will not contribute to congestion on the
public streets, as the use of the building will remain unchanged and off-street
parking will continue to be provided; and
   WHEREAS, there is no evidence that the proposed building additions will
otherwise impair the public health, safety, comfort, morals and welfare of the
inhabitants of the Village; and
   WHEREAS, the requested variations are in harmony with the general purpose
and intent of the Winnetka Zoning Ordinance, in that it allows the renovation,
restoration and rehabilitation of a structurally sound existing building while
maintaining the existing scale and appearance of the community and protecting
established trees and landscaping.
   NOW, THEREFORE, the Council of the Village of Winnetka do ordain as follows:
   SECTION 1 : That the foregoing recitals are hereby incorporated as the
findings of the Council of the Village of Winnetka, as if fully set forth
herein.
   SECTION 2:  That the following variations are hereby granted to the Subject
Property, commonly known as 530 Winnetka Avenue, Winnetka, Illinois, and
located in the B-1 Multiple-Family Residential Zoning District provided in
Chapter 17.32 of the Winnetka Zoning Ordinance, Title 17 of the Winnetka
Village Code: (a) a variation from the use restrictions of Section 17.32.010
(B)1, which does not include office uses within the permitted uses or permitted
special uses in the B-1 Multi-Family Residential Zoning District, and (b) a
variation from Section 17.64.010(A)3, which prohibits structural alterations
and expansions to nonconforming buildings containing nonconforming uses, both
of said variations being to allow the modification of an existing medical
office building by constructing a handicap accessible entry, and additional
office, reception and file storage space at the northwest portion of the
building, and by constructing a 9.91-square foot addition to the entrance on
the west side of the building, by replacing a 2-door entry with a single door
entry, and providing clearance for a new doorway to the existing basement
stairs, with all work to be as depicted in the plans and elevations dated
February 8, 2002, as amended and presented to the Design Review Board on June
20, 2002, and as further amended to eliminate a prior request for parking and
an additional driveway to the north of the building.
   SECTION 3: That the variations hereby granted are conditioned upon the
commencement of the proposed construction within 12 months after the effective
date of this Ordinance.
   SECTION 4: This Ordinance shall take effect immediately upon passage,
approval and posting.
   ADOPTED this 21st day of August, 2002, pursuant to the following roll call
vote:
   AYES:    Trustees Aquilino, Brower, Greenough, Powell, Presser, and Woodbury
   NAYS:    None
   ABSENT:    None
   Signed:
   s/s Michael F. Duhl
    Village President
Countersigned:
s/s Douglas G. Williams
Village Clerk
Introduced: August 6, 2002
Posted: August 7, 2002
Passed and Approved: August 21, 2002
Posted: August 22, 2002
ORDINANCE NO. M-25-2002
AN ORDINANCE GRANTING A VARIATION IN THE APPLICATION OF THE ZONING ORDINANCE OF
THE VILLAGE OF WINNETKA COOK COUNTY, ILLINOIS (165 Westview Road)
   WHEREAS, there has been presented to the Council of the Village of Winnetka,
Cook County, Illinois, the request of the owner of the following described real
estate (the “Subject Property”):
Lot 4 in Block “B” of Broadmeadow Properties, being a subdivision of the south
two thirds of the southwest quarter of the southwest quarter of Section 20,
Township 42 North, Range 13 East of the Third Principal Meridian, according to
the plat thereof recorded August 7, 1936, as document number 11862729, in Cook
County, Illinois,
commonly known as 165 Westview Road, Winnetka, Illinois, and located in the R-
2 Single-Family Residential Zoning District provided in Chapter 17.24 of the
Winnetka Zoning Ordinance, Title 17 of the Winnetka Village Code, for a
variation from the maximum building size limitations of Section 17.30.040 of
the Winnetka Zoning Ordinance to permit the single family residence on the
Subject Property to have a gross floor area of 7,573.40 square feet, which
exceeds the maximum allowable gross floor area of 6,996.21 square feet by
577.19 square feet (8.25%); and
   WHEREAS, on July 22, 2002, on due notice thereof, the Zoning Board of
Appeals conducted a public hearing on the requested variation and by the
unanimous vote of the six members then present, has reported to the Council
recommending that the requested variation be granted; and
   WHEREAS, there are practical difficulties and unique hardships associated
with carrying out the strict application of the Zoning Ordinance with respect
to the Subject Property in that: (a) the owners are the purchasers of the
residence, which is newly constructed; (b) the excess gross floor area was
discovered in the course of the Village’s final inspection of the newly
constructed residence a week before the owners were scheduled to close on the
purchase of the Subject Property; (c) the excess gross floor area resulted from
structural changes to interior ceiling heights that affected the calculation of
the gross floor area; (d) the owners did not have knowledge that the final
ceiling heights were not accurately depicted in the approved construction
drawings and required Village approval; (e) under the provisions of the
Winnetka Zoning Ordinance that applied to the construction on the Subject
Property, it is possible to alter the interior ceiling heights to bring the
gross floor area into conformity with the applicable gross floor area
limitations, without having any impact on the exterior bulk of the building;
(f) the Winnetka Zoning Ordinance has since been amended to eliminate the
provisions that allowed interior structural changes to alter the calculated
gross floor area, so as to prevent a similar situation from occurring in the
future; (g) the Village has separately resolved enforcement issues with the
builder; and (h) requiring the owners to alter the interior of the residence to
conform mathematically with the gross floor area limitations, without affecting
the exterior bulk of the residence, would place an undue burden on the owners
by requiring them to bear the primary burden resulting from the nonconformity;
and
   WHEREAS, the requested variation will not alter the essential character of
the neighborhood because the building is already fully constructed and was
constructed at the time the nonconformity was discovered; and
   WHEREAS, the requested variation will not impair an adequate supply of light
and air because the residence conforms with the applicable height limitations
and setback requirements; and
   WHEREAS, the requested variation will not increase the hazard from fire and
other dangers to the Subject Property because the construction complies with
all applicable building and fire protection codes; and
   WHEREAS, the requested variation will not diminish the taxable value of land
and buildings throughout the Village, and the taxable value of the Subject
Property may be increased because of the proposed improvements; and
   WHEREAS, allowing the excess gross floor area to remain will not contribute
to congestion on the public streets, as the building will remain a single-
family residence with off-street parking; and
   WHEREAS, there is no evidence that allowing the excess gross floor area to
remain will otherwise impair the public health, safety, comfort, morals, and
welfare of the inhabitants of the Village.
   NOW, THEREFORE, the Council of the Village of Winnetka do ordain as follows:
   SECTION 1 : The foregoing recitals are hereby incorporated as the findings
of the Council of the Village of Winnetka, as if fully set forth herein.
   SECTION 2:  The Subject Property, commonly known as 165 Westview Road,
Winnetka, Illinois, and located in the R-2 Zoning District provided in Chapter
17.24 of the Winnetka Zoning Ordinance, Title 17 of the Winnetka Village Code,
is hereby granted a variation from the maximum building size limitations of
Section 17.30.040 of the Winnetka Zoning Ordinance to permit the single family
residence on the Subject Property, construction of which is complete, to have a
gross floor area of 7,573.40 square feet, which exceeds the maximum allowable
gross floor area of 6,996.21 square feet, resulting in a variation of 577.19
square feet (8.25%).
   SECTION 3: The variation granted by this ordinance is subject to the
following conditions:
      A.   All construction related to the variation shall be completed within
12 months after the effective date of this Ordinance; and
      B.   Except for repair and maintenance, no structural modification shall
be made to the residence if the modification will increase the size or exterior
dimensions of the original building in any way.
   SECTION 4: This Ordinance shall take effect immediately upon passage,
approval and posting.
   ADOPTED this 3rd day of September, 2002, pursuant to the following roll call
vote:
   AYES:    Trustees Aquilino, Brower, Greenough, Powell, Presser, and Woodbury
   NAYS:    None
   ABSENT:    None
   Signed:
   s/s Michael F. Duhl
    Village President
Countersigned:
s/s Douglas G. Williams
Village Clerk
Introduced: August 20, 2002
Posted: August 21, 2002
Passed and Approved: September 3, 2002
Posted: September 4, 2002
ORDINANCE NO. M-26-2002
AN ORDINANCE GRANTING A VARIATION IN THE APPLICATION OF THE ZONING ORDINANCE OF
THE VILLAGE OF WINNETKA COOK COUNTY, ILLINOIS (180 Ridge Avenue)
   WHEREAS, there has been presented to the Council of the Village of Winnetka,
Cook County, Illinois, the request of the owner of the following described real
estate (the “Subject Property”):
Lots 3, 4, 5 and 6 in Block 1, Alles’ First Addition to Winnetka, being a
subdivision of that part of the southeast ¼ of the southeast ¼ of Section 20,
Township 42 North, Range 13, East of the Third Principle Meridian in the
Village of Winnetka, Cook County, Illinois,
commonly known as 180 Ridge Avenue, Winnetka, Illinois, and located in the R-
3 Zoning District provided in Chapter 17.20 of the Winnetka Zoning Ordinance,
Title 17 of the Winnetka Village Code, for a variation from the front setback
requirements of Section 17.30.050(A) of the Winnetka Zoning Ordinance, to allow
a south front yard setback of 6.25 feet rather than the 40-foot front setback
required by Section 17.30.050(A), resulting in a variation of 33.75 feet
(84.38%), in order to allow the replacement of existing play equipment; and
   WHEREAS, the Subject Property is the site of Saints Faith Hope and Charity
School, church, parking lot and related structures; and
   WHEREAS, the church, school, parking lot and related buildings and
structures are permitted special uses under Section 17.20.020(C) and Section
17.56.010(K) of the Winnetka Village Code, having been in operation on the
Subject Property prior to the Village’s enactment of the special use provisions
now set forth in Chapter 17.56 of the Winnetka Village Code; and
   WHEREAS, on July 22, 2002, on due notice thereof, the Zoning Board of
Appeals conducted a public hearing on the requested variation and by the
unanimous vote of the six members then present, has reported to the Council
recommending that the requested variation be granted; and
   WHEREAS, pursuant to due notice thereof, on June 20, 2002, the Design Review
Board issued favorable comment for the proposed replacement of the existing
playground equipment; and
   WHEREAS, the existing playground area is located in the southeast corner of
the Subject Property; and
   WHEREAS, the replacement of the existing playground equipment does not alter
the location of the existing playground and therefore does not constitute a
substantial change to the existing special use; and
   WHEREAS, the plight of the applicant is unique, in that the playground
equipment is a necessary accessory to the school, which is one of the principal
uses of the Subject Property, and is similar to playground equipment located on
public school properties within the Village; and
   WHEREAS, the strict application of the front setback requirements create
practical difficulties and particular hardships for the applicant in that: (a)
placing the equipment in a conforming location would require the equipment to
be placed in the middle of the existing paved parking area, which is a
necessary accessory to the established church and school on the Subject
Property; (b) placing the play area in the center of the parking area would
reduce available parking space and would create additional hazards for the
school children, because children would have to cross the parking lot, which is
used throughout the day to get to the play equipment; and (c) there is no other
conforming location on the property for the playground equipment; and
   WHEREAS, the requested variation will not alter the essential character of
the neighborhood because the church, school and playground area are established
uses in the neighborhood, and the proposed new play equipment will be located
in the same area of the Subject Property as the play equipment it will replace;
and
   WHEREAS, the requested variation will not impair an adequate supply of light
and air to the adjacent property, because the new equipment is well below the
height limitations of the district and is not tall enough to cast shadows on
single-family properties across the street; and
   WHEREAS, the requested variation will not increase the hazard from fire and
other dangers to the Subject Property, because it will comply with all
applicable building and safety codes; and
   WHEREAS, there is no evidence that the requested variation will diminish the
taxable value of land and buildings throughout the Village; and
   WHEREAS, the proposed replacement of the playground equipment will not
contribute to congestion on the public streets, as the use of the Subject
Property will not change and the existing parking lot will remain intact; and
   WHEREAS, the proposed new playground equipment will not be detrimental to or
endanger the public health, safety, comfort, morals and welfare of the
inhabitants of the Village, because the upgraded playground will be in full
compliance with current safety standards and guidelines and will meet
accessibility requirements of the Americans with Disabilities Act; and
   WHEREAS, the requested variation is in harmony with the general purpose and
intent of the Winnetka Zoning Ordinance, in that it maintains the existing
scale and appearance of the neighborhood and protects established trees and
landscaping.
   NOW, THEREFORE, the Council of the Village of Winnetka do ordain as follows:
   SECTION 1 : The foregoing recitals are hereby incorporated as the findings
of the Council of the Village of Winnetka, as if fully set forth herein.
   SECTION 2:  There is hereby granted to the Subject Property, commonly known
as 180 Ridge Road, Saints Hope Faith and Charity School, a variation from the
front yard setback requirements of Section 17.30.050(A) of the Winnetka Zoning
Ordinance, to allow a south front yard setback of 6.25 feet, rather than the
40-foot setback required by Section 17.30.050(A) resulting in a variation of
33.75 feet (84.38%), said variation being to allow the replacement of existing
play equipment on the Subject Property, all in accordance with the plans and
elevations submitted with the application for variation.
   SECTION 3: The variation hereby granted is conditioned upon the commencement
of the proposed construction within 12 months after the effective date of this
Ordinance.
   SECTION 4: This Ordinance shall take effect immediately upon passage,
approval and posting.
   ADOPTED this 3rd day of September, 2002, pursuant to the following roll call
vote:
