ORDINANCE NO. M-38-2002
AN ORDINANCE AUTHORIZING THE VACATION OF THE ALLEY RIGHT-OF-WAY AT 334 RIDGE
AND ACCEPTING A PLAT OF CONSOLIDATION
   WHEREAS, Brookhaven Development (the "Owner") is the owner of record of the
property commonly known as 334 Ridge Road (the “Subject Property”), which is
legally described as follows:
LOT 5 AND 6 (EXCEPT THE SOUTH 35 FEET OF SAID LOT 6) TOGETHER WITH ALL OF
PRIVATE ALLEY BETWEEN SAID LOTS IN BLOCK 1 IN DALES 2ND SUBDIVISION OF THE
NORTHEAST QUARTER OF SECTION 20, TOWNSHIP 42 NORTH, RANGE 13 EAST OF THE THIRD
PRINCIPAL MERIDIAN, IN COOK COUNTY, ILLINOIS,
   WHEREAS, the Subject Property comprises three separately platted sections,
consisting of the 45-foot wide Lot 5, a 10-foot wide, unimproved, private alley
and the north 10 feet of Lot 6, which constitute a single zoning lot as defined
in the Winnetka Zoning Ordinance, Title 17 of the Winnetka village Code; and
   WHEREAS, the Owner desires to construct a new principal building on the
Subject Property; and
   WHEREAS, Section 15.32.980.C of the Winnetka Village Code requires the
consolidation of the fractional parcels of property into a formal lot of record
prior to the construction of the new principal building; and
   WHEREAS, the Owner has filed a plat of vacation vacating the private alley
and has now applied to the Village for the consolidation of the three component
parts of the subject Property into a single lot of record; and
   WHEREAS, the Council of the Village of Winnetka have determined that the
proposed consolidation meets the requirements of Section 15.32.980.C of the
Winnetka Village Code; and
   WHEREAS, pursuant to Section 16.08.010.F of Title 16 of the Winnetka Village
Code, “Subdivisions,” the Director of Community Development has reviewed the
plat of consolidation and has recommended that the consolidation be approved,
subject to the condition that a 5-foot easement for water and electrical
utilities be reserved along the east (front) lot line; and
   WHEREAS, the President and the Board of Trustees have determined that the
public interest will be served by vacating the above-described alley right-of-
way, which is legally described as follows:
Brookhaven Consolidation 3 in the Northeast Quarter of the Northeast Quarter of
the Southeast Quarter of Section 20, Township 42 North, Range 13 East of the
Third Principal Meridian, in Cook County, Illinois,
as depicted on the Plat of Consolidation attached hereto as Exhibit A; and
   WHEREAS, the Council of the Village of Winnetka have determined that it is
in the best interests of the public for the consolidation to be subject to the
reservation of the easement as recommended by the Director of Community
Development.
   NOW, THEREFORE, the Council of the Village of Winnetka do ordain:
   SECTION 1 : The foregoing recitals are hereby adopted by the Council as its
findings and are incorporated by reference as if fully set forth herein.
   SECTION 2: Subject to the conditions set forth in Section 3 of this
ordinance, the Council hereby approves the Plat of Consolidation attached
hereto as Exhibit A, consolidating the Subject Property, commonly known as 334
Ridge Avenue, Winnetka, Illinois, into a single lot of record, which shall be
legally described as follows:
Brookhaven Consolidation 3 in the Northeast Quarter of the Northeast Quarter of
the Southeast Quarter of Section 20, Township 42 North, Range 13 East of the
Third Principal Meridian, in Cook County, Illinois.
   SECTION 3 : The consolidation shall be subject to (1) the reservation of a
5-foot water and electric utility easement along the east (front) lot line of
the Subject Property; (2) the payment by the Owner of all costs related to the
vacation of the private alley and the preparation and recording of all plats
necessary to effectuate the consolidation; and (3) no permits shall be issued
for the construction of a new principal building on the Subject Property unless
and until the fully executed Plat of Consolidation has been recorded by the
Owner in the office of the Cook County Recorder.
   SECTION 4 : The Village President and Village Clerk are hereby authorized to
execute the Plat of Consolidation, entitled "Brookhaven Consolidation 3," and
to take all other steps necessary to effectuate the recording of the Plat of
Consolidation, provided that all of the conditions set forth in Section 3 of
this ordinance have first been met.
   SECTION 5 : This ordinance shall be in full force and effect from and after
its passage, approval, and posting.
   ADOPTED this 19th day of November, 2002, pursuant to the following roll call
vote:
   AYES:    Trustees Brower, Greenough, Powell and Presser
   NAYS:    None
   ABSENT:    Trustees Aquilino and Woodbury
   Signed:
   s/s Michael F. Duhl
    Village President
Countersigned:
s/s Douglas G. Williams
Village Clerk
Introduced: November 5, 2002
Posted: November 6, 2002
Passed and Approved: November 19, 2002
