ORDINANCE NO.: M-39-2002
AN ORDINANCE AUTHORIZING THE DISPOSITION OF CERTAIN PERSONAL PROPERTY OWNED BY
THE VILLAGE OF WINNETKA
WHEREAS, the Village of Winnetka owns the following described items of personal
property (hereinafter the “Personal Property”) and has established a minimum
value for each such item of personal property as hereinafter described:
 
Inventory No. Condition                       Year Make Model Minimum Value
Old PW 34     Non-operational and stripped of 1983 Ford F800  $0.00
              useful parts.
Old PW 17     Non-operational and stripped of 1979 IH   1800  $0.00
              useful parts.
 
   WHEREAS, the Council of the Village of Winnetka have determined that the
Personal Property is no longer necessary or useful to the Village of Winnetka,
that the cost of storing said Personal Property exceeds its value to the
Village of Winnetka, that it is not in the best interests of the Village of
Winnetka to retain said Personal Property and that the Personal Property should
be disposed of in the manner hereinafter provided, pursuant to Section 11-76-
4 of the Illinois Municipal Code (65 ILCS 5/11-76-4), so as to avoid incurring
additional costs for storing said Personal Property; and
   NOW, THEREFORE, the Council of the Village of Winnetka do ordain:
   SECTION 1: Pursuant to Section 11-76-4 of the Illinois Municipal Code 65
(ILCS 5/11-76-4), the Council the Village of Winnetka find that the above-
described Personal Property is no longer necessary or useful to the Village of
Winnetka and that the best interests of the Village of Winnetka will be served
by the disposal of said Personal Property.
   SECTION 2 : The Council of the Village of Winnetka further find that, based
on prior experience in disposing of similar items of property, the cost of
conducting a public sale of the Personal Property, including the costs of
advertising and publishing, and the costs of personnel needed to maintain
security and to conduct the public sale, exceeds the value of such items.
   SECTION 3: That pursuant to said Section 11-76-4, the Village Manager is
hereby authorized and directed to determine the value of and to dispose of the
Personal Property in any manner he deems reasonable under the circumstances.
   SECTION 4: That this ordinance shall be in full force and effect from and
after its passage, approval, and posting.
   PASSED this 3rd day of December, 2002, pursuant to the following roll call
vote
   AYES:    Trustees Brower, Greenough, Powell, Presser and Woodbury
   NAYS:    None
   ABSENT:    Trustee Aquilino
