ORDINANCE NO. M-26-2003
AN ORDINANCE GRANTING A VARIATION IN THE APPLICATION OF THE ZONING ORDINANCE OF
THE VILLAGE OF WINNETKA COOK COUNTY, ILLINOIS (910 Greenwood Avenue)
   WHEREAS, there has been presented to the Council of the Village of Winnetka,
Cook County, Illinois, the request of the owner of the following described real
estate (the “Subject Property”):
The South 66 2/3 feet of Lots 1, 2 and 3 in Block 31 in Chicago North Shore
Land Company’s Subdivision in Sections 17 and 18, Township 42 North, Range 13,
East of the Third Principal Meridian, in Cook County, Illinois,
commonly known as 910 Greenwood Avenue, Winnetka, Illinois, and located in the
R-5 Single-Family Residential Zoning District provided in Chapter 17.12 of the
Winnetka Zoning Ordinance, Title 17 of the Winnetka Village Code, a request for
the following variations: (a) a variation from the intensity of use of lot
limitations of Section 17.30.030 of the Zoning Ordinance to allow a roofed lot
coverage of 2,478.36 square feet, which exceeds the maximum allowable roofed
lot coverage of 2,391.28 square feet by 87.08 square feet (3.64%); and (b) a
variation from the building line articulation requirements of Section 17.30.090
to allow the north building wall to be extended by 6.69 feet, resulting in an
unarticulated length of 44.92 feet, although an 18-inch articulation is
required for the addition if the building wall is at least 40 feet long, said
variations being for the purpose of allowing the construction of a 61.21-square
foot, one-story mud room and porch addition at the northwest corner of the
residence on the Subject Property; and
   WHEREAS, on June 9, 2003, on due notice thereof, the Zoning Board of Appeals
conducted a public hearing on the requested variation and by the unanimous vote
of the six members then present, has reported to the Council recommending that
the requested variation be granted; and
   WHEREAS, there are practical difficulties and particular hardships
associated with carrying out the strict application of the Zoning Ordinance
with respect to the Subject Property in that: (a) the proposed addition will
replace an existing open porch with a mud room and 3.5-foot deep covered porch
at the rear entrance of the house; (b) the house on the Subject Property was
constructed before April 20, 1999, when the building articulation requirement
was added to the Zoning Ordinance; (c) the proposed addition is adjacent to the
kitchen, which is the typical location of a mud room entrance; and (d) the area
adjacent to the existing kitchen that currently functions as a rear entry area
is too small to accommodate a closet and to function as a mud room; and
   WHEREAS, the Subject Property cannot yield a reasonable return if permitted
to be used only under the conditions allowed by the Zoning Ordinance, in that:
(a) a mud room adjacent to the kitchen is a typical feature of houses in the
immediate vicinity; (b) strict application of the roofed lot coverage
limitations would prevent the addition of the mud room with a small covered
porch; and (c) strict application of the 18-inch articulation requirement would
result in a narrow, nonfunctional mud room and rear porch, and would prevent
the modest addition from appearing to be a part of the original house, all of
which would have a negative impact on the value of the house by reducing both
its functionality and visual appeal; and
   WHEREAS, the requested variations will not alter the essential character of
the neighborhood because the proposed addition will be at the rear of the
house, alongside the driveway, and will be fully integrated into the existing
building by being aligned with the north and west building walls and by using
the same siding materials as are on the existing house; and
   WHEREAS, the requested variations will not impair an adequate supply of
light and air because the one-story addition is of a minimal size and complies
with applicable height limitations and setback requirements; and
   WHEREAS, the requested variations will not increase the hazard from fire and
other dangers to the Subject Property as the construction will comply with all
applicable building and fire protection codes; and
   WHEREAS, the requested variations will not diminish the taxable value of
land and buildings throughout the Village, and the taxable value of the Subject
Property may be increased because of the proposed improvements; and
   WHEREAS, the proposed mud room and porch addition will not contribute to
congestion on the public streets, as the use of the single family residence
will not be changed; and
   WHEREAS, there is no evidence that the proposed mud room and porch addition
will otherwise impair the public health, safety, comfort, morals, and welfare
of the inhabitants of the Village; and
   WHEREAS, the requested variations are in harmony with the general purpose
and intent of the Winnetka Zoning Ordinance, in that they will allow the
renovation, restoration and rehabilitation of a structurally sound existing
building while maintaining the existing scale and appearance of the community
and protecting established trees and landscaping.
   NOW, THEREFORE, the Council of the Village of Winnetka do ordain as follows:
   SECTION 1 : That the foregoing recitals are hereby incorporated as the
findings of the Council of the Village of Winnetka, as if fully set forth
herein.
   SECTION 2: That the following variations are hereby granted to the Subject
Property, commonly known as 910 Greenwood Avenue, Winnetka, Illinois, and
located in the R-5 Single-Family Residential Zoning District provided in
Chapter 17.12 of the Winnetka Zoning Ordinance, Title 17 of the Winnetka
Village Code: (a) a variation from the intensity of use of lot limitations of
Section 17.30.030 of the Zoning Ordinance to allow a roofed lot coverage of
2,478.36 square feet, which exceeds the maximum allowable roofed lot coverage
of 2,391.28 square feet by 87.08 square feet (3.64%); and (b) a variation from
the building line articulation requirements of Section 17.30.090 to allow the
north building wall to be extended by 6.69 feet, resulting in an unarticulated
length of 44.92 feet, although and 18-inch articulation is required for the
addition if the building wall is at least 40 feet long, said variations being
for the purpose of allowing the construction of a 61.21-square foot, one-story
mud room and porch addition at the northwest corner of the residence on the
Subject Property, in accordance with the plans and elevations submitted with
the application for variation.
   SECTION 3: That the variations hereby granted is conditioned upon the
commencement of the proposed construction within 12 months after the effective
date of this Ordinance.
   SECTION 4: This Ordinance shall take effect immediately upon passage,
approval and posting.
   ADOPTED this 15th day of July, 2003, pursuant to the following roll call
vote:
   AYES:    Trustees Abell, Brower, Greenough, Presser and Webster
   NAYS:    None
   ABSENT:    Trustee Woodbury
