ORDINANCE NO. M-27-2003
AN ORDINANCE GRANTING A VARIATION IN THE APPLICATION OF THE ZONING ORDINANCE OF
THE VILLAGE OF WINNETKA COOK COUNTY, ILLINOIS (1255 Westmoor Road)
   WHEREAS, there has been presented to the Council of the Village of Winnetka,
Cook County, Illinois, the request of the owner of the following described real
estate (the “Subject Property”):
Lots 1 and 2 in Durham’s Subdivision of the South ½ of the West ¼ of the North
West ¼ of the South West ¼ of Section 17, Township 42, Range 13, East of the
Third Principal Meridian, in Cook County, Illinois,
commonly known as 1255 Westmoor Road, Winnetka, Illinois, and located in the R-
2 Single-Family Residential Zoning District provided in Chapter 17.24 of the
Winnetka Zoning Ordinance, Title 17 of the Winnetka Village Code, for a
variation from the 34.38-foot corner yard setback required along Hibbard Road
pursuant to Section 17.30.050 of the Zoning Ordinance, to allow a new,
rectangular swimming pool to observe the same corner setback of 25 feet as an
existing, kidney-shaped swimming pool, resulting in a variation of 9.38 feet
(27.28%); and
   WHEREAS, on June 9, 2003, on due notice thereof, the Zoning Board of Appeals
conducted a public hearing on the requested variation and, by the unanimous
vote of the six members then present, has reported to the Council recommending
that the requested variation be granted; and
   WHEREAS, there are practical difficulties and particular hardships
associated with carrying out the strict application of the Zoning Ordinance
with respect to the Subject Property in that: (a) the Subject Property is a
corner lot located at the northeast corner of Westmoor Road and Hibbard Road;
(b) access to the Subject Property is by way of a private road along the east
side of the Subject Property; (c) the private road along the east side of the
Subject Property serves two other properties in addition to the Subject
Property and is therefore considered to be a private street under the Zoning
Ordinance, making the Subject Property subject to an additional corner setback
along its east property line; (d) the existing, kidney-shaped swimming pool
encroaches into the corner setback along the Hibbard Road frontage; (e) the
existing swimming pool was constructed in 1964 and has outlived its useful
life; (e) the new swimming pool will have a long, rectangular shape and will be
located in the same area of the Subject Property as the existing swimming pool;
(f) the new swimming pool will be oriented so that it is parallel to the
existing house, which is situated at a slight northwesterly angle on the
Subject Property; and (g) there is no conforming location for the new swimming
pool, because of the location of the house and because the Subject Property is
heavily wooded; and
   WHEREAS, the Subject Property cannot yield a reasonable return if permitted
to be used only under the conditions allowed by the Zoning Ordinance, because
(a) the swimming pool is an established element of the use and value of the
Subject Property; (b) the existing pool has outlived its useful life; and (c)
strict application of the corner setback requirement would result in
constructing a substantially smaller pool, or constructing a pool in an area of
the Subject Property that would be inconsistent with the orientation of the
existing residence, and would require the removal of mature trees, all of which
would reduce the value of the Subject Property; and
   WHEREAS, the requested variation will not alter the essential character of
the neighborhood because the new swimming pool will be built into the ground
and will not be visible from Hibbard Road because the west side of the Subject
Property is heavily wooded and the stockade fence along the Hibbard Road
frontage will remain; and
   WHEREAS, the requested variation will not impair an adequate supply of light
and air because the new swimming pool will be built in the ground; and
   WHEREAS, the requested variation will not increase the hazard from fire and
other dangers to the Subject Property as the newly constructed pool and
accompanying pool equipment will comply with all applicable building and fire
protection codes; and
   WHEREAS, the requested variation will not diminish the taxable value of land
and buildings throughout the Village, and the taxable value of the Subject
Property may be increased because of the proposed improvements; and
   WHEREAS, the requested variation will not contribute to congestion on the
public streets, as the use of the single family residence on the Subject
Property will not change; and
   WHEREAS, there is no evidence that the requested variation will otherwise
impair the public health, safety, comfort, morals, and welfare of the
inhabitants of the Village; and
   WHEREAS, the requested variation is in harmony with the general purpose and
intent of the Winnetka Zoning Ordinance, in that it allows the renovation,
restoration and rehabilitation of a structurally sound existing building while
maintaining the existing scale and appearance of the community and protecting
established trees and landscaping.
   NOW, THEREFORE, the Council of the Village of Winnetka do ordain as follows:
   SECTION 1 : That the foregoing recitals are hereby incorporated as the
findings of the Council of the Village of Winnetka, as if fully set forth
herein.
   SECTION 2: That a variation is hereby granted to the Subject Property,
commonly known as 1255 Westmoor Road, Winnetka, Illinois, and located in the R-
2 Single-Family Residential Zoning District provided in Chapter 17.24 of the
Winnetka Zoning Ordinance, Title 17 of the Winnetka Village Code, from the
34.38-foot corner yard setback required along Hibbard Road pursuant to Section
17.30.050 of the Zoning Ordinance, to allow a new, rectangular swimming pool to
observe the same corner setback of 25 feet as an existing, kidney-shaped
swimming pool, resulting in a variation of 9.38 feet (27.28%), said new
swimming pool to be located in accordance with the site plan and drawings that
accompanied the application for variation.
   SECTION 3: That the variation hereby granted is conditioned upon the
commencement of the proposed construction within 12 months after the effective
date of this Ordinance.
   SECTION 4: This Ordinance shall take effect immediately upon passage,
approval and posting.
   ADOPTED this 15th day of April, 2003, pursuant to the following roll call
vote:
   AYES:    Trustees Abell, Brower, Greenough, Presser and Webster
   NAYS:    None
   ABSENT:    Trustee Woodbury
   Signed:
   s/s Michael F. Duhl
    Village President
Countersigned:
s/s Douglas G. Williams
Village Clerk
