ORDINANCE NO. M-47-2003
AN ORDINANCE GRANTING A VARIATION IN THE APPLICATION OF THE ZONING ORDINANCE OF
THE VILLAGE OF WINNETKA COOK COUNTY, ILLINOIS (592 Cherry Street)
   WHEREAS, there has been presented to the Council of the Village of Winnetka,
Cook County, Illinois, the request of the owner of the following described real
estate (the “Subject Property”):
The North 120 feet (lying South of the South line of street North and
adjoining) of the East 93 ½ feet (lying West of the West Line of street East
and adjoining) of Block 47 of the Original Village of Winnetka, in Section 21,
Township 42 North, Range 13, East of the Third Principal Meridian, in Cook
County, Illinois,
commonly known as 592 Cherry Street, Winnetka, Illinois, and located in the R-
4 Single-Family Residential Zoning District provided in Chapter 17.16 of the
Winnetka Zoning Ordinance, Title 17 of the Winnetka Village Code, for the
following variations: (a) a variation from the intensity of use of lot
limitations of Section 17.30.030 to allow a maximum roofed lot coverage of
2,848.98 square feet, which exceeds the maximum allowable roofed lot coverage
of 2,805.00 feet, resulting in a variation of 43.98 feet (1.5%); (b) a
variation from the side yard setback requirements of Section 17.30.060, to
allow a west side yard of 1.0 foot, rather than the required 9.35 feet,
resulting in a variation of 8.55 feet (89.3%); and (c) a variation from the
rear yard setback requirements of Section 17.30.070, to allow a rear yard
setback of 1.0 foot, rather than the required 6.70 feet, resulting in a
variation of 5.7 feet (85.07%); all of said variations to allow the
construction of a new two-car detached garage in the southwest corner of the
Subject Property; and
   WHEREAS, on November 10, 2003, on due notice thereof, the Zoning Board of
Appeals conducted a public hearing on the requested variations and, by the
unanimous vote of the six members then present, has reported to the Council
recommending that the requested variations be granted; and
   WHEREAS, there are practical difficulties and unique hardships associated
with carrying out the strict application of the Zoning Ordinance with respect
to the Subject Property in that: (a) the Subject Property is located at the
southwest corner of Cherry Street and Walnut Street; (b) the home on the
Subject Property was constructed in 1896, prior to the initial enactment of the
Winnetka Zoning Ordinance; (c) the existing two-car garage appears to have been
built in 1926 in the far southwest corner of the Subject Property; (d) the
existing garage is dilapidated and is beyond repair; and (e) the garage cannot
be situated farther to the north because of its proximity to the house; and
   WHEREAS, the Subject Property cannot yield a reasonable return if permitted
to be used only under the conditions allowed by the Zoning Ordinance, in that:
(a) the proposed new garage would replace a dilapidated garage that was built
in 1926 and that can no longer function because the roots of a large tree
located on the property to the south have broken up the garage floor and
rendered the garage doors inoperable; (b) two-car garages are a typical feature
of single family residential property in the vicinity; (c) requiring full
compliance with the roofed lot coverage would result in the construction of a
garage that could not accommodate two vehicles; (d) requiring full compliance
with the south, rear yard requirements would either reduce the width of the
garage to 10 feet, or would interfere with the footprint of the existing house,
which was built in 1896; and (e) shifting the garage further to the east to
fully comply with the west, side yard requirements would make the rear stairs
and entrance to the home inaccessible from the rear of the Subject Property;
and
   WHEREAS, the requested variations will not alter the essential character of
the neighborhood because the proposed new garage will be in the same general
location in the far southwest corner of the Subject Property as the garage that
it will replace, and will be consistent with the design of the existing
residence, thus improving the appearance of the Subject Property while
maintaining the Subject Property as it has existed on the block face for nearly
80 years; and
   WHEREAS, the requested variations will not impair an adequate supply of
light and air because the proposed garage will conform with the applicable
building height limitations, and will maintain a sufficient distance from other
structures on the adjoining properties; and
   WHEREAS, the requested variations will not increase the hazard from fire and
other dangers to the Subject Property, as the proposed garage will comply with
all applicable building and fire protection codes; and
   WHEREAS, the requested variations will not diminish the taxable value of
land and buildings throughout the Village, and the taxable value of the Subject
Property may be increased because of the proposed improvements; and
   WHEREAS, the proposed construction will not contribute to congestion on the
public streets, as the property will continue to be used for single family
residential purposes and the new garage will provide enclosed, off-street
parking for two vehicles; and
   WHEREAS, there is no evidence that the proposed garage will otherwise impair
the public health, safety, comfort, morals, and welfare of the inhabitants of
the Village; and
   WHEREAS, the requested variations are in harmony with the general purpose
and intent of the Winnetka Zoning Ordinance, in that they allow the replacement
of a structurally inadequate garage with a new garage that maintains the
existing scale and appearance of the community and protecting established trees
and landscaping.
   NOW, THEREFORE, the Council of the Village of Winnetka do ordain as follows:
   SECTION 1 : That the foregoing recitals are hereby incorporated as the
findings of the Council of the Village of Winnetka, as if fully set forth
herein.
   SECTION 2: That the following variations are hereby granted to the Subject
Property, commonly known as 592 Cherry Street, Winnetka, Illinois, and located
in the R-4 Single-Family Residential Zoning District provided in Chapter 17.16
of the Winnetka Zoning Ordinance, Title 17 of the Winnetka Village Code, for
the following variations: (a) a variation from the intensity of use of lot
limitations of Section 17.30.030 to allow a maximum roofed lot coverage of
2,848.98 square feet, which exceeds the maximum allowable roofed lot coverage
of 2,805.00 feet, resulting in a variation of 43.98 feet (1.5%); (b) a
variation from the side yard setback requirements of Section 17.30.060, to
allow a west side yard of 1.0 foot, rather than the required 9.35 feet,
resulting in a variation of 8.55 feet (89.3%); and (c) a variation from the
rear yard setback requirements of Section 17.30.070, to allow a rear yard
setback of 1.0 foot, rather than the required 6.70 feet, resulting in a
variation of 5.7 feet (85.07%); all of said variations to allow the
construction of a new two-car detached garage in the southwest corner of the
Subject Property all in accordance with the plans and elevations submitted with
the application.
   SECTION 3: That the variations hereby granted are conditioned upon the
commencement of the proposed construction within 12 months after the effective
date of this Ordinance.
   SECTION 4: This Ordinance shall take effect immediately upon passage,
approval and posting.
   ADOPTED this 16th day of December, 2003, pursuant to the following roll call
vote:
   AYES:    Trustees Abell, Brower, Greenough, Presser, Webster and Woodbury
   NAYS:    None
   ABSENT:    None
   Signed:
   s/s Michael F. Duhl
    Village President
Countersigned:
s/s Douglas G. Williams
Village Clerk
Introduced: December 2, 2003
Posted: December 3, 2003
Passed and Approved: December 16, 2003
