ORDINANCE NO. M-48-2003
AN ORDINANCE GRANTING A VARIATION IN THE APPLICATION OF THE ZONING ORDINANCE OF
THE VILLAGE OF WINNETKA COOK COUNTY, ILLINOIS (904 Elm Street)
   WHEREAS, there has been presented to the Council of the Village of Winnetka,
Cook County, Illinois, the request of the owner of the following described real
estate (the “Subject Property”):
Lot 7 (except the East 17 feet thereof in Block 5 in Provident Mutual Land
Association Subdivision of Blocks 7 to 12 inclusive, 28-33 inclusive, and 54 to
59 inclusive, in the Village of Winnetka, a Subdivision of the West half of the
Northeast quarter of Section 20, Township 42 North, Range 13, East of the Third
Principal Meridian, in Cook County, Illinois;
commonly known as 904 Elm Street, Winnetka, Illinois, and located in the R-
5 Single-Family Residential Zoning District provided in Chapter 17.12 of the
Winnetka Zoning Ordinance, Title 17 of the Winnetka Village Code, for the
following variations: (a) a variation from the intensity of use of lot
limitations of Section 17.30.030 to allow a maximum roofed lot coverage of
1,758.87 square feet, which exceeds the maximum allowable roofed lot coverage
of 1,547.8 feet by 211.07 feet (13.64%); and (b) a variation from the intensity
of use of lot limitations of Section 17.30.030 to allow an impermeable surface
area of 3,526.01 square feet, which exceeds the maximum allowable impermeable
surface area of 3,095.6 feet by 430.41 square feet (16.08%); (c) a variation
from the side yard setback requirements of Section 17.30.060, to allow a west
side yard of 2.25 feet, rather than the required 6.0 feet, resulting in a
variation of 3.75 feet (62.5%); and (d) a variation from the building line
articulation requirements of Section 17.30.090 to allow the west wall of the
building to have an unarticulated length of 68.72 feet, which exceeds the
maximum permitted unarticulated length of 30 feet by 38.72 feet; all of said
variations to allow the construction of a one-story family room addition at the
rear of the existing one-story residence; and
   WHEREAS, on November 10, 2003, on due notice thereof, the Zoning Board of
Appeals conducted a public hearing on the requested variations and, by the
unanimous vote of the six members then present, has reported to the Council
recommending that the requested variation be granted; and
   WHEREAS, there are practical difficulties and unique hardships associated
with carrying out the strict application of the Zoning Ordinance with respect
to the Subject Property in that: (a) the Subject Property is a long, narrow
nonconforming lot, having a width of approximately 32.96 feet, rather than the
60-foot average lot width required in the R-5 zoning district; (b) the Subject
Property is the west lot of three lots of approximately equal width that were
carved by metes and bounds from two 50-foot wide platted lots in the early
1900’s; (c) the home on the Subject Property is a Sears catalog bungalow style
that was built in 1916, prior to the initial enactment of the Winnetka Zoning
Ordinance; (d) the proposed family room addition measures 12 feet by 12 feet
and will replace an existing concrete deck at the rear of the house; (e) the
proposed one-story addition will adjoin the south wall of the kitchen located
at the south end of the house, and will have walls that align with the existing
kitchen’s walls; and (f) due to the narrow width of both the lot and the house,
and further due to the interior configuration of the house, there is no
conforming location for a family room addition; and
   WHEREAS, the Subject Property cannot yield a reasonable return if permitted
to be used only under the conditions allowed by the Zoning Ordinance, in that:
(a) the existing house is relatively small, with a gross floor area of 1,268.34
square feet, which is approximately 51% of the gross floor area that is allowed
on the Subject Property; (b) the existing house lacks a family room, which is a
standard feature of contemporary homes in the Village; (c) the existing roofed
lot coverage exceeds the maximum allowable roofed lot coverage, which would
preclude the construction of any addition unless a variation is granted; and
(d) the addition proposed is similar to an addition built on the adjoining lot
to the east pursuant to a variation granted by ordinance M-13-2003; and
   WHEREAS, the requested variations will not alter the essential character of
the neighborhood because the one-story family room addition is at the rear of
the house, is consistent with the architectural style of the existing house and
maintains the view of the building from the street, thus preserving the
appearance of the Subject Property in relation to the houses on the two
adjoining parcels, to the east, which were also built around the time the three
parcels were created; and
   WHEREAS, the requested variations will not impair an adequate supply of
light and air because of the one-story height and modest size of the family
room addition; and
   WHEREAS, the requested variations will not increase the hazard from fire and
other dangers to the Subject Property as they will comply with all applicable
building and fire protection codes; and
   WHEREAS, the requested variations will not diminish the taxable value of
land and buildings throughout the Village, and the taxable value of the Subject
Property may be increased because of the proposed improvements; and
   WHEREAS, the proposed family room addition will not contribute to congestion
on the public streets, as the use of the Subject Property will not change; and
   WHEREAS, there is no evidence that the proposed family room addition will
otherwise impair the public health, safety, comfort, morals, and welfare of the
inhabitants of the Village.
   WHEREAS, the requested variations are in harmony with the general purpose
and intent of the Winnetka Zoning Ordinance, in that they will allow the
renovation, restoration and rehabilitation of a structurally sound existing
building while maintaining the existing scale and appearance of the community
and protecting established trees and landscaping.
   NOW, THEREFORE, the Council of the Village of Winnetka do ordain as follows:
   SECTION 1 : That the foregoing recitals are hereby incorporated as the
findings of the Council of the Village of Winnetka, as if fully set forth
herein.
   SECTION 2: That the following variations are hereby granted to the Subject
Property, commonly known as 904 Elm Street, Winnetka, Illinois, and located in
the R-5 Single-Family Residential Zoning District provided in Chapter 17.12 of
the Winnetka Zoning Ordinance, Title 17 of the Winnetka Village Code, for the
following variations: (a) a variation from the intensity of use of lot
limitations of Section 17.30.030 to allow a maximum roofed lot coverage of
1,758.87 square feet, which exceeds the maximum allowable roofed lot coverage
of 1,547.8 feet by 211.07 feet (13.64%); and (b) a variation from the intensity
of use of lot limitations of Section 17.30.030 to allow an impermeable surface
area of 3,526.01 square feet, which exceeds the maximum allowable impermeable
surface area of 3,095.6 feet by 430.41 square feet (16.08%); (c) a variation
from the side yard setback requirements of Section 17.30.060, to allow a west
side yard of 2.25 feet, rather than the required 6.0 feet, resulting in a
variation of 3.75 feet (62.5%); and (d) a variation from the building line
articulation requirements of Section 17.30.090 to allow the west wall of the
building to have an unarticulated length of 68.72 feet, which exceeds the
maximum permitted unarticulated length of 30 feet by 38.72 feet; all of said
variations to allow the construction of a one-story family room addition at the
rear of the existing one-story residence, all in accordance with the plans and
elevations submitted with the application.
   SECTION 3: That the variations hereby granted are conditioned upon the
commencement of the proposed construction within 12 months after the effective
date of this Ordinance.
   SECTION 4: This Ordinance shall take effect immediately upon passage,
approval and posting.
   ADOPTED this 16th day of December, 2003, pursuant to the following roll call
vote:
   AYES:    Trustees Abell, Brower, Greenough, Presser, Webster and Woodbury
   NAYS:    None
   ABSENT:    None
   Signed:
   s/s Michael F. Duhl
    Village President
Countersigned:
s/s Douglas G. Williams
Village Clerk
