ORDINANCE NO. M-8-2004
AN ORDINANCE AUTHORIZING THE DISPOSITION OF CERTAIN PERSONAL PROPERTY OWNED BY
THE VILLAGE OF WINNETKA
   WHEREAS, the Village of Winnetka owns the following described vehicle
(“Vehicle”) and has established a minimum value for each such item of personal
property as hereinafter described:
 
Vehicle ID        Inventory No. Year Make Model          Minimum Value
2FAFP71W6WX156920 Squad 530     1998 Ford Crown Victoria Scrap, parts
 
   WHEREAS, the Director of Public Works has recommended that the Vehicle be
disposed of by selling it for the scrap value and/or the value of its parts
through methods that the Village Manager determines are consistent with past
disposal methods; and
   WHEREAS, the Village of Winnetka also owns computer equipment, some of which
will be retired as it is replaced during the remainder of the fiscal year
ending March 31, 2004, and during the following fiscal year, April 1, 2004
through March 31, 2005 (hereinafter referred to as “Retired Computer
Equipment”);
   WHEREAS, the Finance Director has recommended that the Computer Equipment be
disposed of by methods that are consistent with past disposal methods; and
   WHEREAS, the Council of the Village of Winnetka have determined that the
cost of storing the Vehicle and the Computer Equipment (collectively, the
“Personal Property”) exceeds their value to the Village of Winnetka and that it
is no longer useful to, or in the best interests of, the Village of Winnetka to
retain the Personal Property; and
   WHEREAS, the Council of the Village of Winnetka have determined that it is
in the best interests of the Village for the Personal Property to be sold in
the manner provided in this ordinance, pursuant to Section 11-76-4 of the
Illinois Municipal Code (65 ILCS 5/11-76-4).
   NOW, THEREFORE, the Council of the Village of Winnetka do ordain:
   SECTION 1 : Pursuant to Section 11-76-4 of the Illinois Municipal Code (65
ILCS 5/11-76-4), the Council of the Village of Winnetka find that the above-
described Surplus Property, consisting of the items of Personal Property shown
on the attached Exhibits A and the Retired Computer Equipment described in the
foregoing recitals, are not necessary or useful to the Village of Winnetka and
that the best interests of the Village of Winnetka will be served by the sale
or other disposition of such Surplus Property.
   SECTION 2 : The Council of the Village of Winnetka further find that, based
on prior experience in disposing of similar items of property, the cost of
conducting a public sale of the Surplus Property, including the costs of
advertising and publishing, and the costs of personnel needed to maintain
security and to conduct the public sale, exceeds the value of such items.
   SECTION 3: Pursuant to said Section 11-76-4, the Village Manager is hereby
authorized and directed to determine the value of and to dispose of the Vehicle
in any manner he deems reasonable under the circumstances, with or without
public notice and to convey title to the Vehicle upon receipt of payment in
full.
   SECTION 4: Pursuant to said Section 11-76-4, the Director of Finance is
hereby authorized and directed to determine the value of and to dispose of
Retired Computer Equipment that is retired during the remainder of the fiscal
year ending March 31, 2004, and during the following fiscal year, ending March
31, 2005, using disposal methods that are consistent with past disposal
practices.
   SECTION 6: This Ordinance shall take effect immediately upon passage,
approval and posting.
   ADOPTED this 17th day of February, 2004, pursuant to the following roll call
vote:
   AYES:    Trustees Abell, Brower, Greenough, Presser, Webster and Woodbury
   NAYS:    None
   ABSENT:    None
   APPROVED this 17th day of February, 2004.
   Signed:
   //s//Michael F. Duhl
   Village President
Countersigned:
//s//Douglas G. Williams
Village Clerk
Introduced: February 3, 2004
Posted: February 4, 2004
Passed and Approved: February 17, 2004
Posted: February 18, 2004
ORDINANCE NO. M-9-2004
AN ORDINANCE OF THE VILLAGE OF WINNETKA AUTHORIZING THE EXECUTION AND DELIVERY
OF A SECOND ADDENDUM TO THE POWER SALES CONTRACT WITH THE ILLINOIS MUNICIPAL
ELECTRIC AGENCY
   WHEREAS, the Village of Winnetka is a municipality owning and operating an
electric utility which furnishes retail electric service to the public; and
   WHEREAS, the Village of Winnetka is a member of the Illinois Municipal
Electric Agency (“Agency”); and
   WHEREAS, the Village of Winnetka is concerned about the availability of
long-term electric power and energy supply at economical and reliable sources
of electric energy for its ratepayers in the Village of Winnetka, Illinois; and
   WHEREAS, the Agency was created as a means to achieve economy, adequacy and
reliability in the supply of electric energy by planning, financing, owning and
operating facilities for the generation and transmission of electric power and
energy and related facilities or other facilities necessary or convenient for
the planning and operation of a system for the production and transmission of
electric power and energy thus making it possible for the Village and other
members to achieve economies and efficiencies not possible for municipalities
acting alone; and
   WHEREAS, the Agency and the Village have heretofore entered into a Power
Sales Contract, dated June 1, 1990 and effective October 1, 1990, as amended by
the Addendum to Power Sales Contract, dated December 7, 1990 (“Winnetka PSC”),
which sets forth the terms and conditions for sales of electric power and
energy by the Agency to the Village during the term of the Winnetka PSC; and
   WHEREAS, the Winnetka PSC provides that the Agency will sell and deliver to
the Village and requires the Village to purchase and receive from the Agency
all of the electric power and energy required by the Village for the operation
of the Village’s municipal electric system for a term of fifteen (15) years
from October 1, 1990, and thereafter from year to year until terminated by five
(5) years prior written notice, provided however that in no event shall the
Winnetka PSC extend beyond September 30, 2040; and
   WHEREAS, the revenues derived by the Agency under the Winnetka PSC have been
pledged, together with revenues derived by the Agency from other Power Sales
Contracts, to secure the payment of electric utility revenue bonds issued by
the Agency; and
   WHEREAS, under the Winnetka PSC, the Agency has full responsibility for
planning and obtaining an adequate supply of power and energy for the Village
and other Agency members; and
   WHEREAS, in planning to meet the long term, power and energy needs of the
Village and other members of the Agency, the Agency has determined that the
acquisition of an ownership interest in a second base load, coal-fired
generating unit, namely the proposed Trimble County Unit No. 2, which is
proposed to be constructed adjacent to the Trimble County Unit No. 1 with a
projected unit nameplate rating of 750 MW, approximately 91 MW of which would
be dedicated to IMEA (the “TC-2 Project”), will be the best long term resource
for meeting the power and energy needs of its Participating Members in the
future; and
   WHEREAS, the TC-2 Project will require the issuance of additional bonds by
the Agency; and
   WHEREAS, the Village Board of Trustees has determined that a twenty (20)
year extension of the term of the Contract to September 30, 2025 will allow for
a sufficient amortization of the additional bonds to be issued by the Agency
for the TC-2 Project; and
   WHEREAS, the Village of Winnetka and the Agency have agreed to amend the
Winnetka PSC to provide for a twenty (20) year extension thereof and as set
forth in the Second Addendum to Power Sales Contract (“Second Addendum”), a
copy of which, marked as Exhibit “A”, is attached hereto and incorporated
herein by reference; and
   WHEREAS, based upon the foregoing facts, the Village by this Ordinance
hereby finds and determines to approve the Second Addendum.
   NOW, THEREFORE, the Council of the Village of Winnetka do ordain:
   SECTION 1:   The findings and determinations set forth in the preambles to
this Ordinance are hereby made findings and determinations of the Board of
Trustees of the Village of Winnetka.
   SECTION 2:   The Village of Winnetka is authorized pursuant to this
Ordinance (a) to enter into the Second Addendum to Power Sales Contract in the
form attached hereto as Exhibit “A”, and (b) to be bound by the terms and
conditions of the Winnetka PSC, as amended by said Second Addendum and as
supplemented or modified from time to time.
   SECTION 3:   The Village’s electric utility shall purchase electric power
and energy from the Agency under and pursuant to the terms of the Winnetka PSC,
as amended by the Second Addendum, through September 30, 2025.
   SECTION 4:   By this Ordinance, the President of the Village of Winnetka is
hereby authorized and directed to execute and deliver and the Village Clerk is
hereby authorized to attest and seal the Second Addendum to Power Sales
Contract.
   SECTION 5:   All Ordinances and parts of Ordinances in conflict herewith are
hereby repealed.
   SECTION 6: This Ordinance shall take effect immediately upon passage,
approval and posting.
   ADOPTED this 17th day of February, 2004, pursuant to the following roll call
vote:
   AYES:    Trustees Abell, Brower, Greenough, Presser, Webster and Woodbury
   NAYS:    None
   ABSENT:    None
   APPROVED this 17th day of February, 2004.
   Signed:
   //s//Michael F. Duhl
   Village President
Countersigned:
//s//Douglas G. Williams
Village Clerk
Introduced: February 3, 2004
Posted: February 4, 2004
Passed and Approved: February 17, 2004
Posted: February 18, 2004
SECOND ADDENDUM TO POWER SALES CONTRACT BETWEEN THE ILLINOIS MUNICIPAL ELECTRIC
AGENCY AND THE VILLAGE OF WINNETKA
   This Second Addendum to the Power Sales Contract Between the Illinois
Municipal Electric Agency and the Village of Winnetka, dated June 1, 1990, is
made this ___ day of __________, 2004, by and between the ILLINOIS MUNICIPAL
ELECTRIC AGENCY, a municipal corporation and unit of local government of the
State of Illinois, and the VILLAGE OF WINNETKA, an Illinois municipal
corporation.
   WHEREAS, the Illinois Municipal Electric Agency ("IMEA" or "Agency") and the
Village of Winnetka ("Participating Member") have heretofore entered into a
Power Sales Contract(“Initial Power Sales Contract”), dated June 1, 1990 and
effective October 1, 1990, as amended by the Addendum to the PSC December 7,
1990 (“Winnetka PSC”), pursuant to which Participating Member has agreed to
purchase and the IMEA has agreed to provide and sell, subject to certain
limitations, all of the electric power and energy required for the operation of
Participating Member’s municipal electric utility for a term of fifteen (15)
years; and
   WHEREAS, in furtherance of its obligations under the Power Sales Contracts
with its Participating Members, the Agency issued bonds and purchased an
undivided 12.12 percent ownership interest in a coal-fired generating unit,
known as Trimble County Unit No. 1, in Trimble County, Kentucky, and all
Participating Members pay rates for power and energy from the Agency that are
designed to cover the debt service on the bonds issued by the Agency in
connection with the purchase of said unit, as well as all other Agency
expenses; and
   WHEREAS, in planning to meet the long-term power and energy needs of the
Participating Members, as well as other member municipalities that may be
interested in entering into long term, full requirements, power supply
agreements with IMEA, the Agency has caused both an Integrated Resource Plan
and a Feasibility Study regarding participation in a new base load, coal-fired
generating unit to be conducted; and
   WHEREAS, the results of the Integrated Resource Plan and the preliminary
recommendations from the Feasibility Study show that participation by IMEA in a
new base load, coal-fired generating unit to be constructed and operational in
the 2009/2010 timeframe is the best long-term resource for meeting the power
and energy needs of the Participating Members and other member municipalities
wishing to enter into long-term, full requirements, power supply agreements
with IMEA in the future; and
   WHEREAS, IMEA has exercised its right of first refusal to participate in the
development and acquisition of a 12.12% ownership in the Trimble County Unit
No. 2, which is proposed to be constructed adjacent to the Trimble County Unit
No. 1 with a projected unit nameplate rating of 750 MW, approximately 91 MW of
which would be dedicated to IMEA (the “TC-2 Project”); and
   WHEREAS, it is anticipated that the Agency’s costs associated with the TC-
2 Project, including financing costs, will not exceed $150,000,000; and
   WHEREAS, participation by IMEA in the proposed Trimble County Unit No. 2
will require the issuance of additional bonds by IMEA, which will in turn
necessitate extension of the terms of the existing Participating Members’ Power
Sales Contracts and the establishment of sufficient terms for any new
Participating Members’ long-term, full requirements, power supply contract; and
   WHEREAS, IMEA and Participating Member have reached an agreement as to terms
for Participating Member’s participation in the TC-2 Project and have
accordingly agreed to amend the Winnetka PSC as set forth herein.
   NOW, THEREFORE, the Illinois Municipal Electric Agency and the Village of
Winnetka hereby agree as follows:
      1.   IMEA shall take all commercially reasonable steps necessary to
participate with Louisville Gas and Electric Company, Kentucky Utilities
Company and the Indiana Municipal Power Agency in the development and ownership
of a 12.12% interest in the TC2 Project pursuant to the terms of the
Participation Agreement among IMEA and said entities regarding the TC2 Project.
      2.   The Agency’s Board of Directors shall set rates from time to time
pursuant to the provisions of Section 3 of the Power Sales Contracts so as to
amortize the proportionate share of debt service and associated costs for all
Participating Members electing to participate in the TC-2 Project. In setting
such rates, the Agency’s Board of Directors shall make appropriate adjustments
to account for payments by any Participating Member, including the Village of
Winnetka, that elected to pay its proportionate share of the debt service
associated with the bonds issued by IMEA in connection with the acquisition of
Trimble County Unit No. 1 over a shorter period of time. Provided the Village
of Winnetka shall have made all payments required under the schedule provided
pursuant to Section 4(c) of Schedule B to the Winnetka PSC, its rate for
service under the Winnetka PSC for periods after February 28, 2006 shall not
include any charges under the schedule provided pursuant to Section 4(c) of
Schedule B for Trimble County Unit No. 1. 
      3.   Participating Member hereby elects to participate in the Project and
to have its rates set pursuant to the Winnetka PSC so as to amortize its
proportionate share of debt service and other costs associated with the TC-
2 Project over a fifteen (15) year period from the in-service date of the TC-
2 Project.
      4.   Subject to paragraph 7 of this Second Addendum, IMEA and
Participating Member hereby extend the initial term of the Winnetka PSC for an
additional twenty (20) years in order to accomplish the fifteen (15) year
amortization described in the foregoing paragraph from the projected in-service
date of 2010. The initial term of the Power Sales Contract between IMEA and
Participating Member is hereby extended to September 30, 2025.
      5.   Subject to paragraph 7 of this Second Addendum, Section 1 of the
Power Sales Contract is amended by deleting the entire text of subsection (a)
and replacing it with the following:
This Contract shall take effect on October 1, 1990 and shall remain in effect
for an initial term of thirty-five (35) years through September 30, 2025, and
thereafter from year to year until terminated by five (5) years prior written
notice. In no event shall this Contract extend beyond September 30, 2040.
      6.   Subject to paragraph 7 of this Second Addendum, Section 1(c) of the
Power Sales Contract is hereby eliminated, and it shall have no further legal
effect.
      7.   Notwithstanding any other provision herein, this Second Addendum and
the contract term extension contained herein shall not become effective unless
the Agency’s Board of Directors determines that the mix of Participating
Members executing contract extensions or new Power Sales Contracts results in
sufficient benefits to the Participating Members to justify proceeding with the
issuance of bonds to fund the TC-2 Project. The Agency shall provide the
Participating Member with written notice within sixty days of any final
decision by the Agency that the Addendum is to become effective. In addition,
this Second Addendum shall become null and void unless the Agency shall have
issued bonds in connection with the TC-2 Project by a date not later than
December 31, 2007.
      8.   It is agreed between the parties that in the event there is a
conflict between the provisions of this Second Addendum and provisions of the
Winnetka PSC that the provisions of this Second Addendum shall prevail and
control.
   IN WITNESS THEREOF the parties have authorized the execution of this Second
Addendum and have caused their duly authorized representatives to sign as of
the day and year first written above.
                  ILLINOIS MUNICIPAL ELECTRIC AGENCY
                  ________________________________________
