ORDINANCE NO. M-26-2004
AN ORDINANCE AUTHORIZING THE DISPOSITION OF CERTAIN PERSONAL PROPERTY OWNED BY
THE VILLAGE OF WINNETKA
   WHEREAS, Article VII, Section 10 of the Constitution of the State of
Illinois, and the Intergovernmental Cooperation Act, 220 ILCS 220/1, et seq.,
authorize and encourage intergovernmental cooperation; and
   WHEREAS, the Northwest Municipal Conference, is a corporate organization
that represents municipalities and townships chartered within the State of
Illinois and Counties of Cook, DuPage, Kane, Lake, and McHenry, and organizes
joint municipal auctions for the sale of surplus vehicles and equipment; and
   WHEREAS, the Village of Winnetka owns the following described items of
personal property (hereinafter the “Personal Property”) and has established a
minimum value for each such item of personal property as hereinafter described:
Vehicle ID Number  Inventory No.   Year Make   Model     Minimum Value
1G1BJK34M8BJ157693 Old PW 005      1981 Chevy  K30       $ 500.00
1GBKC34F7TJ112703  Old PW 012      1996 Chevy  3500HD    $ 7,000.00
2FDLF47G6MCB01060  Old WE 069      1991 Ford   F450      $ 2,000.00
2FDLF47GXMCB01059  Old WE 059      1991 Ford   F450      $ 2,400.00
2FAFP71W8WX156918  Old PW 93       1998 Ford   Crown Vic $ 2,000.00
2FAFP71W6YX162817  Old PD 447      2000 Ford   Crown Vic $ 4,000.00
2FAFP71W8YX162818  Old PD 445      2000 Ford   Crown Vic $ 2,500.00
2FAFP71W4YX162816  Old PD 446      2000 Ford   Crown Vic $ 2,500.00
2W9MPK632RP044674  Old PW 024      1995 Go-4   P-35      $ 50.00
2W9MPK634TP044     Old PW 023      1996 Go-4   P-35      $ 50.00
1J4FJ68SXRL169657  Old PD 429      1994 Jeep   Cherokee  $ 2,700.00
S57004742          Old WE 151      1975 Davis  40+4      $ 1,500.00
BCJ764             Old WE 163      1990 Green  Trailer   $ 0.00
No Tag             Old PW 206      1987 McCull 700       $ 50.00
11-085546          Old PW 208      1993 McCull 700       $ 50.00
11-075162          Old PW 203      1993 McCull 700       $ 50.00
B1064              Old Shop Equip. 1985 Benwil SP-45     $ 300.00
514-8716           Old PW 106      1988 Ford   710       $ 500.00
TTL-I-60A          Old PW 107      1987 Tarco            $500.00
 
   WHEREAS, the Council of the Village of Winnetka have determined that it is
no longer useful to, or in the best interests of, the Village of Winnetka to
retain said Personal Property and that said Personal Property should be sold in
the manner hereinafter provided, pursuant to Section 11-76-4 of the Illinois
Municipal Code (65 ILCS 5/11-76-4); and
   WHEREAS, the Village Manager of the Village of Winnetka has authorized the
Northwest Municipal Conference to advertise and obtain bids for the sale of the
items of Personal Property at an auction to be conducted by the Northwest
Municipal Conference at 10:00 a.m., Saturday, October 16, 2004 at the Village
of Winnetka Public Works Facility, 1390 Willow Road, Winnetka, Illinois, with
the acceptance of any bids being subject to the approval of the corporate
authorities pursuant to a duly enacted ordinance; and
   WHEREAS, the Village of Elk Grove Village has expressed an interest in
purchasing the item of personal property described in the table above as a 1988
Ford Model 710, with a Vehicle ID Number of 514-8716, and an Inventory Number
of “Old PW 106” (hereinafter “Surplus Leaf Catcher”); and
   WHEREAS, the Council of the Village of Winnetka have determined that,
provided that the Village of Winnetka and the Village of Elk Grove Village can
agree to a purchase price by Friday, October 15, 2004, the interests of
intergovernmental cooperation will be fostered by selling the Surplus Leaf
Catcher to the Village of Elk Grove Village.
   NOW, THEREFORE, the Council of the Village of Winnetka do ordain:
   SECTION 1:   Pursuant to Section 11-76-4 of the Illinois Municipal Code 65
(ILCS 5/11-76-4), the Council the Village of Winnetka find that the above-
described Personal Property is no longer necessary or useful to the Village of
Winnetka and that the best interests of the Village of Winnetka will be served
by the sale of said Personal Property.
   SECTION 2:   Pursuant to said Section 11-76-4, and subject to the condition
set forth in Section 7 of this Ordinance, the Village Manager is hereby
authorized to direct the sale of the Personal Property at an auction to be
conducted by the Northwest Municipal Conference (the “NWMC”) at 10:00 a.m.,
Saturday, October 16, 2004 at the Village of Winnetka Public Works Facility,
1390 Willow Road, Winnetka, Illinois.
   SECTION 3: The Village Manager is further authorized to direct the NWMC to
advertise the sale of the Personal Property through area newspapers, direct
mailings, and other channels as the NWMC deems appropriate prior to the date of
the auction.
   SECTION 4:   The Village Manager is further authorized to direct the NWMC to
enter into an agreement for the sale of the Personal Property, whereby the
Personal Property shall be sold at the auction to the highest bidder or
bidders, according to the terms set forth in the Specifications for the Sale of
Vehicles and Equipment at Northwest Municipal Conference Auctions, which
specifications are attached hereto and made a part of this ordinance.
   SECTION 5:   No bid shall be accepted for the sale of any item of the
Personal Property which is less than the minimum value of said item of personal
property as set forth in the preamble to this ordinance, unless the Village
Manager, or his designee, so authorizes at the time of the auction, and unless
the highest bid received for such item is less than the minimum value set forth
in this ordinance.
   SECTION 6:   Upon payment in full of the auctioned price by the highest
bidder or bidders for any item of the Personal Property, the Village Manager is
authorized to direct the NWMC to convey and transfer the title and ownership of
said item of Personal Property to the highest bidder or bidders.
   SECTION 7:   Notwithstanding the foregoing, the Village Manager shall be
authorized to sell the item of personal property described in the table set
forth in the preamble to this Ordinance as a 1988 Ford Model 710, with a
Vehicle ID Number of 514-8716, and an Inventory Number of “Old PW 106” (the
“Surplus Leaf Catcher”), provided that the Village of Winnetka and the Village
of Elk Grove Village can agree to a purchase price by the close of business on
Friday, October 15, 2004, and provided further that the negotiated purchase
price is no less than the Minimum Value established for the Surplus Leaf
Catcher in the aforementioned table. In the event of a negotiated sale to the
Village of Elk Grove Village, the Village Manager of the Village of Winnetka
shall have the authority to convey title and ownership of the Surplus Leaf
Catcher to the Village of Elk Grove Village upon receipt of payment in full of
the negotiated price.
   SECTION 8:   This Ordinance shall take effect immediately upon passage,
approval and posting.
   ADOPTED this 5th day of October, 2004, pursuant to the following roll call
vote:
   AYES:    Trustees Eilers, Greenough, Ritchell and Tucker
