ORDINANCE NO. M-28-2004
AN ORDINANCE LEVYING TAXES FOR THE YEAR 2004
   WHEREAS, on March 2, 2004, the Council of the Village of Winnetka adopted
Resolution No. R-2-2004, which budgeted $23,866,040 to meet the expenses and
liabilities of the Village for general corporate purposes, refuse collection
and disposal, debt service principal and interest, and retirement fund
contributions for the fiscal year beginning April 1, 2004, and ending March 31,
2005; and
   WHEREAS, on October 19, 2004, the Council of the Village of Winnetka
determined the amounts of money estimated to be necessary to be raised by
taxation of taxable property within the Village for general corporate purposes,
for refuse collection and disposal, for debt service principal and interest and
for retirement fund contributions for the fiscal year beginning April 1, 2004,
and ending March 31, 2005; and
   WHEREAS, the State Legislature has enacted Public Act 93-689 (the
“amendatory Act”), which amends certain provisions of the Illinois Pension Code
and the Illinois Property Tax Code, effective July 1, 2004, including Article 4
of the Illinois Pension Code, which applies to firefighter pension funds in
municipalities with a population of less than 500,000; and
   WHEREAS, the amendatory Act increases pension benefits for Village of
Winnetka firefighters and their survivors, and amends Section 18-185 of the
Property Tax Code, 30 ILCS 200/18-185, to exclude from the limitations imposed
by the Property Tax Extension Limitation Law, 30 ILCS 200/18-185 et seq., the
additional amounts required to be levied to meet the additional pension funding
requirements imposed by the amendatory Act; and
   WHEREAS, in accordance with Section 4-134 of the Illinois Pension Code, 40
ILCS 5/4-134, as amended by Public Act 93-689, the Winnetka Firefighters
Pension Board has obtained a report from the Village’s actuary, which report is
attached hereto as Exhibit A, and, pursuant to said report, has reported to the
Village Council, certifying that the increase in employer contributions to the
Winnetka Firefighters Pension Fund resulting from the implementation of the
amendatory Act is $63,161, which amount is included in the Fire Pension Levy
amount of $626,600 and shall be excluded from the “aggregate extension,” as
defined in Section 18-185 of the Property Tax Extension Limitation Law, 35 ILCS
200/18-185, et seq., as amended by said amendatory Act; and
   WHEREAS, pursuant to the Truth in Taxation Law, 35 ILCS 200/18-55, et seq.,
the Council of the Village of Winnetka published notice of its proposed tax
levy in the November 25, 2004, edition of the Winnetka Talk, an English
language newspaper in general circulation within the Village; and
   WHEREAS, on Tuesday, December 7, 2004, pursuant to said notice, and in
accordance with the Truth in Taxation Law, the Council of the Village of
Winnetka conducted a public hearing on the proposed levy; and
   WHEREAS, upon closing the aforesaid hearing, the Council of the Village of
Winnetka determined that no further amendment to the proposed tax levy was
required; and
   WHEREAS, the Council of the Village of Winnetka have determined that the
total amount of money necessary to be raised by the levy and collection of
taxes for general corporate purposes, for refuse collection and disposal, for
debt service principal and interest and for retirement fund contributions, is
$10,886,312.
   NOW, THEREFORE, the Council of the Village of Winnetka do ordain:
   SECTION 1:   That the foregoing recitals are hereby adopted as the findings
of the Council of the Village of Winnetka, as fully set forth herein.
   SECTION 2:   That in order to meet the expenses and liabilities of the
Village of Winnetka for the fiscal year beginning April 1, 2004, and ending
March 31, 2005, for general corporate purposes, for refuse collection and
disposal, for debt service principal and interest and for retirement fund
contributions, there is hereby levied upon all of the taxable property within
the corporate limits of the Village of Winnetka subject to taxation for the
current year, as assessed and equalized for the year 2004, the sum of Ten
Million Eight Hundred Eighty Six Thousand Three Hundred Twelve Dollars
($10,886,312), which is to be collected from the levy of the Village of
Winnetka for the year 2004 for all purposes heretofore budgeted, the total of
which has been ascertained and is as indicated in the following Summary of 2004
Property Tax Levy under the column labeled “Amount to Be Raised by Tax Levy,”
and as set forth in detail in the Tax Levy Report, which is attached as Exhibit
B and is incorporated herein by reference.
