ORDINANCE NO. M-30-2004
AN ORDINANCE AUTHORIZING THE DISPOSITION OF SURPLUS PERSONAL PROPERTY OF THE
VILLAGE OF WINNETKA
   WHEREAS, from time to time, the Winnetka Police Department comes into
possession of items of personal property that have been lost, found or stolen,
which personal property includes the “Bicycles” described in Exhibit A,
attached to this ordinance; and
   WHEREAS, said Bicycles have been in the possession of the Winnetka Police
Department for more than 6 months, during which time the Chief of Police of the
Winnetka Police Department has made reasonable inquiry and efforts to identify
and notify the owners or other persons entitled to possession of the Bicycles,
but has been unsuccessful in those attempts; and
   WHEREAS, pursuant to Section 3 of the Law Enforcement Disposition of
Property Act, 765 ILCS 1030/3, the Chief of Police has transferred the custody
of the Personal Property to the Village of Winnetka; and
   WHEREAS, the Council of the Village of Winnetka have determined that said
Bicycles (hereinafter referred to as the “Surplus Property”) are no longer
necessary or useful to the Village of Winnetka, that the cost of storing said
Surplus Property exceeds its value to the Village of Winnetka, that it is not
in the best interests of the Village of Winnetka to retain said Surplus
Property and that the Surplus Property should be disposed of in the manner
hereinafter provided, pursuant to Section 11-76-4 of the Illinois Municipal
Code (65 ILCS 5/11-76-4), so as to avoid incurring additional costs for storing
said Surplus Property.
   NOW, THEREFORE, the Council of the Village of Winnetka do ordain:
   SECTION 1:   Pursuant to Section 11-76-4 of the Illinois Municipal Code (65
ILCS 5/11-76-4), the Council of the Village of Winnetka find that the above-
described Surplus Property, consisting of the items of Bicycles described in
the attached Exhibits A, is not necessary or useful to the Village of Winnetka
and that the best interests of the Village of Winnetka will be served by the
sale or other disposition of such Surplus Property.
   SECTION 2:   The Council of the Village of Winnetka further find that, based
on prior experience in disposing of similar items of property, the cost of
conducting a public sale of the Surplus Property, including the costs of
advertising and publishing, and the costs of personnel needed to maintain
security and to conduct the public sale, exceeds the value of such items.
   SECTION 3:   Pursuant to said Section 11-76-4, the Village Manager is hereby
authorized and directed to determine the value of and to dispose of the Surplus
Property in any manner he deems reasonable under the circumstances, with or
without public notice.
   SECTION 4:   This Ordinance shall be in full force and effect from and after
its passage, approval, and posting.
Passed and approved this 21st day of December, 2004.
AYES:   Trustees Abell, Greenough, Ritchell and Tucker
NAYS:   None
