ORDINANCE NO. M-3-2005
AN ORDINANCE GRANTING A VARIATION IN THE APPLICATION OF THE ZONING ORDINANCE OF
THE VILLAGE OF WINNETKA COOK COUNTY, ILLINOIS (211 Birch)
   WHEREAS, there has been presented to the Council of the Village of Winnetka,
Cook County, Illinois, the request of the owner of the following described real
estate (the “Subject Property”):
The North 175.00 feet of Lot “A” (except the East 237.00 feet thereof) in
Greeley’s Resubdivision of Lots 1, 2, 3, 4, 9, 10, 11 and 12 in Block 5 in
Alles First Addition to Winnetka, in the Southeast ¼ of Section 20, Township 42
North, Range 13, East of the Third Principal Meridian, in Cook County, Illinois
commonly known as 211 Birch Street, Winnetka, Illinois, and located in the R-
3 Single-Family Residential Zoning District provided in Chapter 17.20 of the
Winnetka Zoning Ordinance, Title 17 of the Winnetka Village Code, for the
following variations from requirements of the Lot, Space, Bulk and Yard
Regulations for Single Family Residential Districts established by Section
17.30 of the Zoning Ordinance: (a) a variation from the 40-foot front setback
requirements of Section 17.30.050 to allow a nonconforming garage to be
replaced with a smaller, one-story room addition with a 29.75 foot setback, to
allow a one-story garage addition at the east side of the residence to encroach
5 inches into the required north front setback, and to allow the masonry
chimney for a proposed family room fireplace to be located 22.07 feet from the
Sunset Road right of way, resulting in a variation of 17.93 feet (44.82%); and
(b) a variation from the 40-foot corner setback requirement of Section
17.30.050 to allow a one-story roofed, open porch to be located 18.42 feet from
the Birch Street right of way, resulting in a variation of 21.58 feet (53.95%);
and
   WHEREAS, on February 10, 2005, on due notice thereof, the Zoning Board of
Appeals conducted a public hearing on the requested variations and, by the
unanimous vote of the 5 members then present, has reported to the Council
recommending that the requested variations be granted; and
   WHEREAS, there are practical difficulties and particular hardships
associated with carrying out the strict application of the Zoning Ordinance
with respect to the Subject Property in that: (a) the residence was built in
1914, prior to the enactment of the Winnetka Zoning Ordinance; (b) the Subject
Property is located at the southeast corner of the Sunset Road and Birch Street
rights-of-way and, as a corner lot, is subject to 40-foot setbacks along both
street frontages; (c) the southern portion of the Subject Property is located
in the floodplain, which precludes southward expansion of the existing
residence; (d) the existing north and west setbacks are legal nonconformities,
which cannot be corrected without removing substantial portions of the existing
residence; (e) due to the nonconforming north and west setbacks, any proposed
modifications to the north and west elevations require a variation; (f) due to
the existing configuration of the residence, there is no conforming location
for the proposed west front porch, which will replace the deteriorated existing
porch entry; (g) the one-story addition proposed for the north side of the
residence will have a setback that is more than 6 feet larger than the
nonconforming garage that it will replace; (h) the proposed nonconforming
location of the north building line of the one-story garage addition at the
east end of the residence is necessitated by the existing configuration of the
residence, and will encroach only 5 inches into the required front setback; (i)
the fireplace chimney proposed for the new family room is a minimal
encroachment that will increase the degree of nonconformity in the north front
setback by less than 18 inches for a distance of 5 feet; and (j) the proposed
additions along the north lot line will reduce the nonconforming area by
approximately 232.84 feet; and
   WHEREAS, the Subject Property cannot yield a reasonable return if permitted
to be used only under the conditions allowed by the Zoning Ordinance, in that:
(a) although the Subject Property has a lot area of 23,883.24 square feet,
which exceeds the R-3 Zoning District's minimum lot size of 16,800 square feet,
the existing roofed lot coverage, gross floor area and impervious surface on
the Subject Property are all substantially less than what would be permitted on
a lot of minimum size in the R-3 Zoning District; (b) the existing front porch,
which is falling apart and is no longer safe, cannot be replaced without
obtaining a variation; (c) the planned chimney construction on the north
elevation of the residence is placed so as not to disrupt the room plans and
elevations on the second floor of the home; (d) the requested variations are
part of proposed renovations and additions to the existing residence that will
relocate the garage, provide a more functional kitchen and dining room, provide
a family room adjacent to the kitchen and add a master bedroom suite to the
second floor, all of which are typical amenities for homes in the vicinity of
the Subject Property; and (e) upon completion of all of the work proposed for
the Subject Property, the improved residence's size and features will be
consistent with the size and type of development that is allowed and that
exists within the R-3 Zoning District; and
   WHEREAS, the requested variations will not alter the essential character of
the neighborhood because the proposed additions are in keeping with the
architectural style of the existing structure and with the scale of buildings
in the vicinity; and
   WHEREAS, the requested variations will not impair an adequate supply of
light and air because: (a) the setback reductions resulting from the proposed
nonconforming improvements are of minimal size; (b) there is a net reduction of
encroaching area; and (c) the requested variations are part of renovations and
additions to the existing residence that are well within the maximum roofed lot
coverage and gross floor area allowed in the R-3 Zoning District; and
   WHEREAS, the requested variations will not increase the hazard from fire and
other dangers to the Subject Property, as the proposed construction will comply
with all applicable building and fire protection codes; and
   WHEREAS, the requested variations will not diminish the taxable value of
land and buildings throughout the Village, and the taxable value of the Subject
Property may be increased because of the proposed improvements; and
   WHEREAS, the proposed construction will not contribute to congestion on the
public streets, as the property will continue to be used for single family
residential purposes; and
   WHEREAS, there is no evidence that the requested variations will otherwise
impair the public health, safety, comfort, morals, and welfare of the
inhabitants of the Village; and
   WHEREAS, the requested variations are in harmony with the general purpose
and intent of the Winnetka Zoning Ordinance, in that they allow the renovation,
restoration and rehabilitation of a structurally sound existing building while
maintaining the existing scale and appearance of the community and protecting
established trees and landscaping.
   NOW, THEREFORE, the Council of the Village of Winnetka do ordain as follows:
   SECTION 1:   The foregoing recitals are hereby incorporated as the findings
of the Council of the Village of Winnetka, as if fully set forth herein.
   SECTION 2:   The following variations from the Lot, Space, Bulk and Yard
Regulations for Single Family Residential Districts established by Section
17.30 of the Winnetka Zoning Ordinance are hereby granted to the Subject
Property, commonly known as 211 Birch Street, and located in the R-3 Single-
Family Residential District provided in Chapter 17.20 of the Winnetka Village
Code, Title 17 of the Winnetka Village Code: (a) a variation from the 40-foot
front setback requirements of Section 17.30.050 to allow a nonconforming garage
to be replaced with a smaller, one-story room addition with a 29.75 foot
setback, to allow a one-story garage addition at the east side of the residence
to encroach 5 inches into the required north front setback, and to allow the
masonry chimney for a proposed family room fireplace to be located 22.07 feet
from the Sunset Road right of way, resulting in a variation of 17.93 feet
(44.82%); and (b) a variation from the 40-foot corner setback requirement of
Section 17.30.050 to allow a one-story roofed, open porch to be located 18.42
feet from the Birch Street right of way, resulting in a variation of 21.58 feet
(53.95%); all to allow the construction of several one and two story additions
to the existing residence in accordance with the plans and elevations submitted
with the application for variations.
   SECTION 3:   The variations hereby granted are conditioned upon the
commencement of the proposed construction within 12 months after the effective
date of this Ordinance.
   SECTION 4:   This Ordinance shall take effect immediately upon passage,
approval and posting.
ADOPTED this 5th day of April, 2005, pursuant to the following roll call vote:
AYES:    Trustees Abell, Eilers, Greenough, Tucker
NAYS:    None
ABSENT:    Trustees Ritchell and Woodbury
APPROVED this 5th day of April, 2005.
   Signed:
   //s//Michael F. Duhl
   Village President
Countersigned:
//s//Douglas G. Williams
Village Clerk
Introduced: March 15, 2005
Posted: March 17, 2005
Passed and Approved: April 5, 2005
