ORDINANCE NO. M-13-2005
AN ORDINANCE GRANTING A VARIATION IN THE APPLICATION OF THE ZONING ORDINANCE OF
THE VILLAGE OF WINNETKA COOK COUNTY, ILLINOIS (408 Winnetka)
   WHEREAS, there has been presented to the Council of the Village of Winnetka,
Cook County, Illinois, the request of the owner of the following described real
estate (the “Subject Property”):
Lot 2 in Block 2 in Temple’s Resubdivision of that part of the West ½ of the
Northeast ¼ of Section 28, Township 42 North, Range 13, East of the Third
Principal Meridian, lying East of the railroad and North of the village limits
of Kenilworth in Cook County, Illinois,
commonly known as 408 Winnetka Avenue, Winnetka, Illinois, and located in the
R-5 Single-Family Residential Zoning District provided in Chapter 17.12 of the
Winnetka Zoning Ordinance, Title 17 of the Winnetka Village Code, for the
following variations from requirements of the Lot, Space, Bulk and Yard
Regulations for Single-Family Residential Districts established by Chapter
17.30 of the Zoning Ordinance: (a) a variation from the front setback
requirements of Section 17.30.050 to permit a front setback of 23.29 feet,
whereas a minimum of 30 feet is required, a variation of 6.71 feet (22.37%);
and (b) a variation from the intensity of use of lot conditions of Section
17.30.030 to allow a front yard lot coverage of 677.03 square feet, whereas a
maximum of 450 square feet is permitted, a variation of 227.03 square feet
(50.45%), all to permit the existing, nonconforming front porch to be replaced
by a larger front porch; and
   WHEREAS, on May 9, 2005, on due notice thereof, the Zoning Board of Appeals
conducted a public hearing on the requested variations; and
   WHEREAS, the requested variations did not receive a favorable recommendation
from the Zoning Board of Appeals, with only three members of the Zoning Board
of Appeals voting in favor of a motion to recommend approval, and the remaining
four members voting against the motion; and
   WHEREAS, pursuant to revised plans dated "19 July 2005," the applicants have
amended their request, by reducing the depth of the front porch by 1.5 feet,
with the resulting front setback variation being 5.21 feet (17.37%) and the
resulting front yard impermeable surface being 643.66 square feet, a variation
of 193.66 square feet (43.03%); and
   WHEREAS, there are practical difficulties associated with carrying out the
strict application of the Zoning Ordinance with respect to the Subject Property
in that: (a) the Subject Property is improved with a single family home, built
in 1908, prior to the enactment of the Winnetka Zoning Ordinance; (b) the
existing home is situated at a slight angle toward the northwest corner of the
Subject Property, and the existing front porch is in a legal, nonconforming
location; (c) the properties immediately to the east and west of the Subject
Property also have legal, nonconforming front yards and the block face is
characterized by relatively shallow front yards; (d) the northeast corner of
the existing porch and landing is located approximately 26.39 feet from the
front lot line, with the last three stairs extending further into the front
yard setback; (e) the existing front porch extends across approximately the
west half of the front of the building, with stairs and a landing extending
from the front of the house on the east side of the porch; (f) the proposed
porch, as modified in the drawings dated 19 July 2005, will extend from the
west edge of the house to the east edge of the bay in the front of the house;
(g) the proposed porch, as modified in the drawings dated 19 July 2005, and not
including the stairs, will extend approximately 7.9 feet from the front bay
toward the front lot line; (h) a front porch is necessary to provide access to
the front door and front living areas of the house; (i) the nonconforming
intensity of use of lot in the front yard results from the porch addition and
new stairs; (j) due to the location of the house on the Subject Property, it is
not possible to construct a functional front porch in a conforming location;
and (k) due to the location of the house on the Subject Property, it is not
possible to construct a new front porch in any configuration that would comply
with the front yard lot coverage limitations; and
   WHEREAS, the Subject Property cannot yield a reasonable return if permitted
to be used only under the conditions allowed by the Zoning Ordinance, in that:
(a) the existing porch is in a state of disrepair; (b) the basement of the
existing home experiences flooding during heavy rains due in part to front
foundation problems and to water penetrating through the existing porch,
neither of which can be corrected without removing the existing front porch;
(c) the proposed porch, as modified by the revised drawings dated 19 July 2005,
is necessary to provide functional access to the front entrance and front
living areas of the existing house; (d) due to the location of the house on the
Subject Property, it is not possible to construct a new front porch that
conforms with the front yard lot coverage limitations; and (e) requiring the
new porch to observe the minimum required front setback would result in an
unusable porch with a depth of less than two feet; and
   WHEREAS, the requested variations will not alter the essential character of
the neighborhood because (a) the proposed replacement porch will be consistent
with the relatively shallow front setbacks on the block face; (b) the open
front porch design and proposed details are consistent with the architectural
style of the existing home; (c) the resulting building height, side and rear
yard setbacks, building size, roofed lot coverage, and impermeable surface on
the Subject Property as a whole will remain in compliance with the applicable
provisions of Chapter 17.30 of the Zoning Ordinance; and
   WHEREAS, the requested variations will not impair an adequate supply of
light and air because (a) the proposed new porch is not enclosed; (b) the
proposed new porch does not extend toward any of the adjoining properties; and
(c) the proposed porch will comply with the applicable side yard setback
requirements and building height limitations; and
   WHEREAS, the requested variations will not increase the hazard from fire and
other dangers to the Subject Property, because (a) the proposed construction
will comply with all applicable building and fire protection codes; and (b) the
proposed new porch will maintain the existing separations from the adjoining
properties by fully complying with side yard setback requirements; and
   WHEREAS, there is no evidence that the requested variations will diminish
the taxable value of land and buildings throughout the Village, and the taxable
value of the Subject Property may be increased because of the proposed
improvement; and
   WHEREAS, the proposed porch replacement will not contribute to congestion on
the public streets, because: (a) the Subject Property will continue to be used
for single family residential purposes; and (b) the existing driveway
configuration will continue to extend to the garage at the rear of the 200-foot
deep Subject Property; and
   WHEREAS, there is no evidence that the requested variations will otherwise
impair the public health, safety, comfort, morals, and welfare of the
inhabitants of the Village; and
   WHEREAS, the requested variations are in harmony with the general purpose
and intent of the Winnetka Zoning Ordinance, in that: (a) the variation from
the limitations on front yard impermeable surface result from the existing
location of the house and from the proposed reconstruction of the front porch,
stairs and walkway, while the front yard impermeable surface limitations were
added to the Zoning Ordinance to restrict parking pads and driveway turnarounds
in the front yards of narrow lots; and (b) the proposed new front porch allows
the renovation, restoration and rehabilitation of a structurally sound existing
building while maintaining the existing scale and appearance of the community
and protecting established trees and landscaping.
   NOW, THEREFORE, the Council of the Village of Winnetka do ordain as follows:
   SECTION 1:   The foregoing recitals are hereby incorporated as the findings
of the Council of the Village of Winnetka, as if fully set forth herein.
   SECTION 2:   The following variations from the Lot, Space, Bulk and Yard
Regulations for Single-Family Residential Districts established by Section
17.30 of the Winnetka Zoning Ordinance, Title 17 of the Winnetka Village Code,
are hereby granted to the Subject Property, commonly known as 408 Winnetka
Avenue, and located in the R-5 Single-Family Residential District provided in
Chapter 17.12 of the Winnetka Zoning Ordinance: (a) a variation from the front
setback requirements of Section 17.30.050 to permit a front setback of
approximately 24.79 feet, whereas a minimum of 30 feet is required, a variation
of 5.21 feet (17.37%); and (b) a variation from the intensity of use of lot
conditions of Section 17.30.030 to allow a front yard lot coverage of 6643.66
square feet, whereas a maximum of 450 square feet is permitted, a variation of
193.66 square feet (43.03%), all to permit the existing, nonconforming front
porch to be replaced by a larger front porch, in accordance with the plans and
elevations submitted with the application for variations, as modified by the
revised plans dated 19 July 2005.
   SECTION 3:   The variations hereby granted are conditioned upon the
commencement of the proposed construction within 12 months after the effective
date of this Ordinance.
   SECTION 4:   This Ordinance is adopted by the Council of the Village of
Winnetka in the exercise of its home rule powers pursuant to Section 6 of
Article VII of the Illinois Constitution of 1970.
   SECTION 5:   This Ordinance shall take effect immediately upon its passage,
approval and posting as provided by law.
PASSED this 2nd day of August, 2005, pursuant to the following roll call vote:
AYES:    Trustees Behles, Berger, Eilers, Ritchell, Tucker
NAYS:    None
ABSENT:    Trustee Abell
APPROVED this 2nd day of August, 2005.
   Signed:
   //s//Edmund C. Woodbury
