ORDINANCE NO. M-14-2005
AN ORDINANCE PROVIDING FOR THE ADDITION OF TOWER ROAD, FROM THE WESTERN VILLAGE
CORPORATE LIMITS TO THE EAST EDGE OF THE PAVEMENT OF VERNON AVENUE, TO THE
MUNICIPAL STREET SYSTEM OF THE VILLAGE OF WINNETKA, COOK COUNTY, ILLINOIS
   WHEREAS, on October 17, 2000, the Council of the Village of Winnetka
(“Village Council”) authorized staff to sign a letter of intent ("Initial
Letter of Intent") for the transfer of jurisdiction, from the State of Illinois
to the Village of Winnetka, of that portion of Tower Road extending from the
western corporate limits of the Village to the east edge of the pavement of
Vernon Avenue; and
   WHEREAS, as part of the Initial Letter of Intent, the State of Illinois,
acting through the Illinois Department of Transportation ("IDOT"), agreed to
assume a portion of the costs of rehabilitating that portion of Tower Road
prior to the transfer of jurisdiction; and
   WHEREAS, the Village of Winnetka and the State of Illinois, under date of
September 3, 2002, entered into an agreement for the transfer of jurisdiction
of a part of Tower Road, from the western corporate limits of the Village to
the east edge of the pavement of Vernon Avenue, to the Municipal Street System
of the Village of Winnetka ("Initial Agreement"); and
   WHEREAS, on September 17, 2002, the Village Council passed Ordinance M-27-
2002, providing for the addition to the Village of Winnetka's street system,
Tower Road from the western corporate limits to the east edge of Vernon Avenue;
and
   WHEREAS, although the rehabilitation of Tower Road was substantially
completed at the time the Village passed Ordinance M-27-2002, State funding
covering the improvements contemplated under the Initial Letter of Intent and
Initial Agreement was not available until 2005; and
   WHEREAS, funding for the State's portion of the Tower Road rehabilitation
became available in 2005, and the Village of Winnetka and the State of
Illinois, pursuant to a renewed agreement for the transfer of jurisdiction of
Tower Road to the Municipal Street System ("Agreement") approved by the Village
Council on June 7, 2005; and
   WHEREAS, because of the change in Village administration since 2002, IDOT
has requested that the Village Council pass a new ordinance providing for the
jurisdictional transfer of Tower Road to the Village.
   NOW, THEREFORE, the Council of the Village of Winnetka do ordain as follows:
   SECTION 1 :   That the foregoing recitals are hereby incorporated as the
findings of the Council of the Village of Winnetka, as if fully set forth
herein.
   SECTION 2:   That Tower Road, from the western corporate limits of the
Village (approximately 1100' west of Forestway Drive) to the east edge of the
pavement of Vernon Avenue, be added to the Municipal Street System of the
Village of Winnetka.
   SECTION 3:   That all prior actions taken by the Village of Winnetka in
rehabilitating Tower and entering into the Initial Agreement and the 2005
Agreement are hereby approved and ratified.
   SECTION 3:   That the Village Clerk is directed to forward a certified copy
of this Ordinance to the State of Illinois, through its Deputy Director of
Highways, Region One Engineer’s office at 201 West Center Court, Schaumburg,
Illinois 60196-1096.
   SECTION 3:   That this Ordinance is adopted by the Council of the Village of
Winnetka in the exercise of its home rule powers pursuant to Section 6 of
Article VII of the Illinois Constitution of 1970.
   SECTION 4:   That this Ordinance shall take effect immediately upon its
passage, approval and posting as provided by law.
PASSED this 19th day of July, 2005, pursuant to the following roll call vote:
AYES:    Trustees Behles, Berger, Eielrs, Ritchell and Tucker
NAYS:    None
ABSENT: None
