ORDINANCE NO. M-13-2006
AN ORDINANCE GRANTING A VARIATION IN THE APPLICATION OF THE ZONING ORDINANCE OF
THE VILLAGE OF WINNETKA COOK COUNTY, ILLINOIS (445 Sheridan)
   WHEREAS, the Village of Winnetka is a home rule municipality in accordance
with Article VII, Section 6 of the Constitution of the State of Illinois of
1970; and
   WHEREAS, pursuant to Article VII, Section 6 of the Constitution of the State
of Illinois of 1970, the Village of Winnetka has the authority, except as
limited by said Section 6 of Article VII, to exercise any power and perform any
function pertaining to the government and affairs of the Village, including,
but not limited to, the powers (i) to regulate for the protection of the public
health, safety, morals and welfare, (ii) to license, (iii) to tax, and (iv) to
incur debt; and
   WHEREAS, the Village Council find that establishing standards for the use
and development of lands and buildings within the Village and establishing and
applying criteria for variations from those standards are matters pertaining to
the affairs of the Village; and
   WHEREAS, there has been presented to the Council of the Village of Winnetka,
Cook County, Illinois, the request of the owner of the following described real
estate (the “Subject Property”):
Parcel 1: That part of Block 43 in Peck’s Subdivision known as the Village of
Winnetka, extending from the center line of Sheridan Road (formerly Lake
Avenue) to Lake Michigan and lying Northwesterly from the Southeasterly line
extended of what was formerly Lots 1 and 8 in Grave’s Subdivision of Said Block
43; in Cook County , Illinois;
Parcel 2: That portion of Block 42 in said Peck’s Subdivision, lying within a
strip of land, 2 feet wide, north of and adjoining the center line of that part
of Cherry Street (now in part vacated) which lies North and adjoining Block 43,
in the Village of Winnetka, said Peck’s Subdivision being a subdivision of the
Northeast ¼ of Section 20 and the North Fractional Half of Section 21, Township
42 North, Range 13, East of the Third Principal Meridian, (excepting that part
of Cherry Street as excepted in vacation ordinance by Village of Winnetka on
April 8, 1882 also excepting Sheridan Road) in the Village of Winnetka, in Cook
County, Illinois,
commonly known as 445 Sheridan Road Winnetka, Illinois, and located in the R-
2 Single-Family Residential Zoning District provided in Chapter 17.24 of the
Winnetka Zoning Ordinance, Title 17 of the Winnetka Village Code, for the
following variations from requirements of the Lot, Space, Bulk and Yard
Regulations for Single Family Residential Districts established by Section
17.30 of the Zoning Ordinance: (a) a variation from the limitations on
permitted uses in Section 17.24.020, to permit the renovation and expansion of
the existing coach house on the Subject Property, which will result in two
principal buildings on a single zoning lot; (b) a variation from the
limitations in Section 17.64.040 on changes to nonconforming structures, to
allow the addition of dormers to the existing upper story of the coach house
and the construction of a porch on the south end of the coach house; and (c) a
variation from the 15-foot limitation on the height of accessory buildings in
Section 17.30.080, to permit the proposed dormers to be constructed at a height
of 21.06 feet, a variation of 6.06 feet (40.4%); and
   WHEREAS, on June 12, 2006, on due notice thereof, the Zoning Board of
Appeals conducted a public hearing on the requested variations and, by the
unanimous vote of the 6 members then present, has reported to the Council
recommending that the requested variations be granted; and
   WHEREAS, the Subject Property is commonly recognized in the Village as the
estate of the late W. Clement Stone and is improved with a substantial single
family residence and coach house, which were constructed in the 1920’s; and
   WHEREAS, the Owners propose to modify the coach house by removing the
mechanical room on the north side of the coach house and converting the center
and east portions of the first-floor garage into a pool house with a full
kitchen, sitting area, laundry and elevator to the second floor, and adding a
screened porch on the south side of the building, between the sitting area and
a swimming pool that is planned for construction; and
   WHEREAS, the Owners also propose to modify the second floor living quarters
by reducing the number of bedrooms, reconfiguring the living space and adding
two new dormers on the south side of the building, to provide two existing
windows to be converted into glass-paneled doors that will open onto a stone
patio deck atop the screened porch; and
   WHEREAS, there are practical difficulties and unique circumstances
associated with carrying out the strict application of the Zoning Ordinance
with respect to the Subject Property in that: (a) the Subject Property has a
lot area of 83,062 square feet, which is more than three times larger than the
minimum requirement for the R-2 Single Family Residential District; (b) the
existing coach house has a legally nonconforming height of 32.18 feet; (c) the
existing coach house has a legally nonconforming north side yard; (d) the coach
house has been continuously used as an accessory to the principal residence and
the proposed changes will continue the accessory nature of the uses of that
building; (e) the size and use of the coach house, both as it currently exists
and as proposed, are consistent with the large estate nature of the Subject
Property; (f) the changes to the second floor, which are the primary cause for
the requested variations, are modest in relation to the first floor changes and
have less visual impact on the appearance of the Subject Property; and (g) the
proposed changes enhance the Subject Property and help to assure its long-term
viability as a single, established estate; and
   WHEREAS, the Subject Property cannot yield a reasonable return if permitted
to be used only under the conditions allowed by the Zoning Ordinance, in that
(a) the requested variations are not substantial when considered in the context
of the size of the Subject Property and the estate nature of its established
development and use; and (b) zoning variations are necessary to make any
improvements to the coach house, which is in a state of disrepair; and (c) the
requested variations will allow the continued use and enjoyment of amenities
that are reasonably consistent with the large estate nature of the Subject
Property; and
   WHEREAS, the requested variations will not alter the essential character of
the neighborhood because the proposed additions will be in keeping with the
existing architecture of the coach house and the Principal residence; and
   WHEREAS, the requested variations will not impair an adequate supply of
light and air because (a) the Subject Property has an extremely large lot size;
(b) the improvements will not encroach into setbacks; and (c) the removal of
the mechanical room on the north side of the coach house will reduce the
nonconformity along the north lot line by increasing the north setback 14.06
feet; and
   WHEREAS, the requested variations will not increase the hazard from fire and
other dangers to the Subject Property, as the proposed construction will comply
with all applicable building and fire protection codes; and
   WHEREAS, the requested variations will not diminish the taxable value of
land and buildings throughout the Village, and the taxable value of the Subject
Property may be increased because of the proposed improvements; and
   WHEREAS, the proposed construction will not contribute to congestion on the
public streets, as the property will continue to be used for single family
residential purposes; and
   WHEREAS, there is no evidence that the requested variations will otherwise
impair the public health, safety, comfort, morals, and welfare of the
inhabitants of the Village; and
   WHEREAS, the requested variations are in harmony with the general purpose
and intent of the Winnetka Zoning Ordinance, in that they allow the renovation,
restoration and rehabilitation of a structurally sound existing building while
maintaining the existing scale and appearance of the community and protecting
established trees and landscaping.
   NOW, THEREFORE, the Council of the Village of Winnetka do ordain as follows:
   SECTION 1:   The foregoing recitals are hereby incorporated as the findings
of the Council of the Village of Winnetka, as if fully set forth herein.
   SECTION 2:   The following variations from the Lot, Space, Bulk and Yard
Regulations for Single Family Residential Districts established by Section
17.30 of the Winnetka Zoning Ordinance are hereby granted to the Subject
Property, commonly known as 445 Sheridan Road and located in the R-2 Single-
Family Residential District provided in Chapter 17.24 of the Zoning Ordinance,
Title 17 of the Winnetka Village Code: (a) a variation from the limitations on
permitted uses in Section 17.24.020, to permit the renovation and expansion of
the existing coach house on the Subject Property, which will result in two
principal buildings on a single zoning lot; (b) a variation from the
limitations in Section 17.64.040 on changes to nonconforming structures, to
allow the addition of dormers to the existing upper story of the coach house
and the construction of a porch on the south end of the coach house; and (c) a
variation from the 15-foot limitation on the height of accessory buildings in
Section 17.30.080, to permit the proposed dormers to be constructed at a height
of 21.06 feet, a variation of 6.06 feet (40.4%) all in accordance with the
plans and elevations submitted with the application for variations.
   SECTION 3:   The variations hereby granted are conditioned upon the
commencement of the proposed construction within 12 months after the effective
date of this Ordinance.
   SECTION 4:   This Ordinance is passed by the Council of the Village of
Winnetka in the exercise of its home rule powers pursuant to Section 6 of
Article VII of the Illinois Constitution of 1970.
   SECTION 5:   This Ordinance shall take effect immediately upon its passage,
approval and posting as provided by law.
PASSED this 18th day of July, 2006, pursuant to the following roll call vote:
AYES:    Trustees Abel,l Behles, Ritchell and President Woodbury
NAYS:    None
ABSENT:    Trustees Berger, Eilers and Tucker
APPROVED this 18th day of July, 2006.
   Signed:
   //s//Edmund C. Woodbury
   Village President
Countersigned:
//s//Douglas G. Williams
Village Clerk
Introduced:    July 6, 2006   
Posted:    July 7, 2006   
Passed and Approved:    July 18, 2006   
