ORDINANCE NO. M-14-2006
AN ORDINANCE GRANTING A VARIATION IN THE APPLICATION OF THE ZONING ORDINANCE OF
THE VILLAGE OF WINNETKA COOK COUNTY, ILLINOIS (902 Spruce)
   WHEREAS, the Village of Winnetka is a home rule municipality in accordance
with Article VII, Section 6 of the Constitution of the State of Illinois of
1970; and
   WHEREAS, pursuant to Article VII, Section 6 of the Constitution of the State
of Illinois of 1970, the Village of Winnetka has the authority, except as
limited by said Section 6 of Article VII, to exercise any power and perform any
function pertaining to the government and affairs of the Village, including,
but not limited to, the powers (i) to regulate for the protection of the public
health, safety, morals and welfare, (ii) to license, (iii) to tax, and (iv) to
incur debt; and
   WHEREAS, the Village Council find that establishing standards for the use
and development of lands and buildings within the Village and establishing and
applying criteria for variations from those standards are matters pertaining to
the affairs of the Village; and
   WHEREAS, there has been presented to the Council of the Village of Winnetka,
Cook County, Illinois, the request of the owner of the following described real
estate (the “Subject Property”):
The East 70 feet of Lot 7, in Block 4 of Provident Mutual Land Association a
Subdivision of Blocks 7 to 12 inclusive and Blocks 28 to 33 inclusive and
Blocks 54 to 59 inclusive in the Village of Winnetka in the West ½ of the
Northeast ¼ of Section 20, Township 42 North, Range 13 East of the Third
Principal Meridian, in Cook County, Illinois,
commonly known as 902 Spruce Street Winnetka, Illinois, and located in the R-
5 Single-Family Residential Zoning District provided in Chapter 17.12 of the
Winnetka Zoning Ordinance, Title 17 of the Winnetka Village Code, for the
following variations from Section 17.30.030 of the Lot, Space, Bulk and Yard
Regulations for Single Family Residential Districts established by Chapter
17.30 of the Zoning Ordinance: (a) a variation of 196.77 square feet (11.24%)
from the intensity of use of lot limitations of Section 17.30.030 to permit
impermeable lot coverage of 1,946.77 square feet, whereas a maximum of 1,750.00
square feet is allowed; and (b) a variation of 490.23 square feet (77.81%) from
the front yard lot coverage limitations of Section 17.30.030 to permit a front
yard lot coverage of 1,120.23 square feet, whereas a maximum of 630 square feet
is allowed; said variations being requested to allow the Owners to lay new
brick paver sidewalks in the front and west side yards, and to replace a
legally nonconforming 92.25 square-foot deck on the east side of the home with
a new 171.25 square-foot deck; and
   WHEREAS, the Owners are also requesting the following variations from
Section 17.30.050 of the Lot, Space, Bulk and Yard Regulations for Single
Family Residential Districts established by Chapter 17.30 of the Zoning
Ordinance: (a) a variation of 15.01 feet (50.03%) from the front setback
requirements of Section 17.30.050 to allow the proposed new front entry porch
and deck to observe a front setback of 14.99 feet, whereas a minimum of 30 feet
is required; and (b) a variation of 10.95 feet (36.5%) from the front setback
requirements of Section 17.30.050 to allow the expanded deck at the east side
of the house to observe a front setback of 19.05 feet, whereas a minimum of 30
feet is required; said variations being requested to allow the Owners to
reconstruct and expand the front entry and the side deck; and
   WHEREAS, on June 12, 2006, on due notice thereof, the Zoning Board of
Appeals conducted a public hearing on the requested variations and, by the
unanimous vote of the 6 members then present, has reported to the Council
recommending that the requested variations be granted; and
   WHEREAS, there are practical difficulties and particular hardships
associated with carrying out the strict application of the Zoning Ordinance
with respect to the Subject Property in that: (a) the Subject Property is a
substandard lot with a legally nonconforming lot size of 3,500 square feet,
which is 4,900 square feet smaller than the 8,400 square-foot requirement in
the R-5 Zoning District; (b) the Subject Property was created before the
enactment of the Zoning Ordinance by a metes and bounds conveyance of the rear
70 feet of the platted lot at the southeast corner of Spruce and Provident; (c)
the Subject Property has a lot width of 70 feet and a lot depth of 50 feet; (d)
the Subject Property is improved with a brick and stucco single family
residence that was constructed in 1917, prior to the enactment of the Winnetka
Zoning Ordinance; (e) because of the extremely shallow lot depth, the Subject
Property has a legally nonconforming rear yard of 2.6 feet and a legally
nonconforming front setback of 17.5 feet; (f) the rear yard is barely large
enough to provide egress, and provides no space for typical outdoor activities;
(g) because of the absence of a usable rear yard, outdoor activities
necessarily occur on the deck located on the east side of the house, in the
adjacent east side yard and in the front yard; and (h) due to the small lot
size of the Subject Property and the location of the home on the lot, few
improvements can be made to the existing residence without requesting a
variation; and
   WHEREAS, the Subject Property cannot yield a reasonable return if permitted
to be used only under the conditions allowed by the Zoning Ordinance, in that:
(a) the existing deck on the east side of the house is small and provides no
egress to the side or front lawns, which provide the only usable outdoor
activity space; (b) absent the use of the east side yard and front yard for
outdoor recreational space, the Subject Property lacks outdoor recreational
space, which is a standard amenity for single family residential properties
throughout the Village; (c) the existing front entry is in a deteriorating
condition, with rotting stairs and a low overhang with a severe pitch, which
makes entry into the residence awkward and unsafe; (d) the proposed new front
entry reflects a modest increase in area from 29.4 square feet to 35.85 square
feet; and (e) the increase in size of the new deck from 92.25 square feet to
171.25 square feet will allow the deck to provide more functional space,
including a seating area and stairs to the open yard; and
   WHEREAS, the requested variations will not alter the essential character of
the neighborhood because the proposed additions will be consistent with the
architectural style of the existing home and will maintain the configuration of
the Subject Property and its orientation to the street as it has existed since
1917; and
   WHEREAS, the requested variations will not impair an adequate supply of
light and air because the proposed roof for the new front porch is only
slightly higher than the roof it will replace and the proposed open decks will
meet side yard setback requirements and not be high enough to cast shadows on
the adjoining properties; and
   WHEREAS, the requested variations will not increase the hazard from fire and
other dangers to the Subject Property, as the proposed construction will comply
with all applicable building and fire protection codes; and
   WHEREAS, the requested variations will not diminish the taxable value of
land and buildings throughout the Village, and the taxable value of the Subject
Property may be increased because of the proposed improvements; and
   WHEREAS, the proposed construction will not contribute to congestion on the
public streets, as the property will continue to be used for single family
residential purposes; and
   WHEREAS, there is no evidence that the requested variations will otherwise
impair the public health, safety, comfort, morals, and welfare of the
inhabitants of the Village; and
   WHEREAS, the requested variations are in harmony with the general purpose
and intent of the Winnetka Zoning Ordinance, in that they allow the renovation,
restoration and rehabilitation of a structurally sound existing building while
maintaining the existing scale and appearance of the community and protecting
established trees and landscaping.
   NOW, THEREFORE, the Council of the Village of Winnetka do ordain as follows:
   SECTION 1:   The foregoing recitals are hereby incorporated as the findings
of the Council of the Village of Winnetka, as if fully set forth herein.
   SECTION 2:   The following variations from the Lot, Space, Bulk and Yard
Regulations for Single Family Residential Districts established by Chapter
17.30 of the Winnetka Zoning Ordinance are hereby granted to the Subject
Property, commonly known as 902 Spruce Street and located in the R-5 Single-
Family Residential District provided in Chapter 17.12 of the Zoning Ordinance,
Title 17 of the Winnetka Village Code: (a) a variation of 196.77 square feet
(11.24%) from the intensity of use of lot limitations of Section 17.30.030 to
permit impermeable lot coverage of 1,946.77 square feet, whereas a maximum of
1,750.00 square feet is allowed; (b) a variation of 490.23 square feet (77.81%)
from the front yard lot coverage limitations of Section 17.30.030 to permit a
front yard lot coverage of 1,120.23 square feet, whereas a maximum of 630
square feet is allowed; (c) a variation of 15.01 feet (50.03%) from the front
setback requirements of Section 17.30.050 to allow the proposed new front entry
porch and deck to observe a front setback of 14.99 feet, whereas a minimum of
30 feet is required; and (d) a variation of 10.95 feet (36.5%) from the front
setback requirements of Section 17.30.050 to allow the expanded deck at the
east side of the house to observe a front setback of 19.05 feet, whereas a
minimum of 30 feet is required; all of said variations being requested to allow
the Owners to reconstruct and expand the front entry and the side deck and to
lay new brick paver sidewalks in the front and west side yards, all in
accordance with the plans and elevations submitted with the application for
variations.
   SECTION 3:   The variations hereby granted are conditioned upon the
commencement of the proposed construction within 12 months after the effective
date of this Ordinance.
   SECTION 4:   Nothing in this Ordinance shall be construed as granting
permission to alter the drainage of the Subject Property, and any such proposed
changes shall remain subject to compliance with applicable provisions of the
Village Code.
   SECTION 5:   This Ordinance is passed by the Council of the Village of
Winnetka in the exercise of its home rule powers pursuant to Section 6 of
Article VII of the Illinois Constitution of 1970.
   SECTION 6:   This Ordinance shall take effect immediately upon its passage,
approval and posting as provided by law.
PASSED this 1t8h day of July, 2006, pursuant to the following roll call vote:
AYES:    Trustees Abell, Behles, Ritchell and President Woodbury
NAYS:    None
ABSENT:    Trustees Berger, Eilers and Tucker
APPROVED this 18th day of July, 2006.
   Signed:
   //s//Edmund C. Woodbury
   Village President
Countersigned:
//s//Douglas G. Williams
Village Clerk
Introduced:    July 6, 2006   
Posted:    July 7, 2006   
