ORDINANCE NO. M-15-2006
AN ORDINANCE GRANTING A SPECIAL USE PERMIT AND HEIGHT VARIATION FOR THE
INSTALLATION OF WIRELESS TELECOMMUNICATIONS ANTENNAS AND EQUIPMENT AT 874 GREEN
BAY ROAD, WINNETKA, ILLINOIS
   WHEREAS, Winnetka IV, LLC, (the “Owner”) is the owner of the following
described real estate (the “Subject Property”):
That part of Lot 1 lying southerly and westerly of Green Bay Road (formerly
known as Center Street) in Block 1 in County Clerk’s Division of the Southwest
Quarter of Section 17, Township 42 North, Range 13 East, of the Third Principal
Meridian, in Cook County, Illinois.
which is commonly known as 874 Green Bay Road, Winnetka, Illinois, located in
the C-2 General Retail Commercial Zoning District provided in Chapter 17.44 of
the Winnetka Zoning Ordinance, Title 17 of the Winnetka Village Code; and
   WHEREAS, T-Mobile USA, Inc., (“T-Mobile”) has entered into an agreement with
the Owner of the Subject Property, whereby T-Mobile will be allowed to place
certain wireless telecommunications service antennas and equipment on the walls
and roof of the penthouse and main building located on the Subject Property;
and
   WHEREAS, the Owner and T-Mobile (the “Applicants”) have applied for a
special use permit in accordance with Chapters 17.52 and 17.56 of the Winnetka
Zoning Ordinance, Title 17 of the Winnetka Village Code, to permit the
installation of concealed wireless telecommunication service antennas and
equipment on the penthouse and building walls and on the roof of the existing
building on the Subject Property; and
   WHEREAS, the Applicants have also applied for the following variations: (a)
a variation from the height limitations of Section 17.44.010 (C) of the Zoning
Ordinance, to allow antennas to have a height of 49.5 feet, which exceeds the
permitted height of 35 feet, resulting in a variation of 14.5 feet (41.4%); and
(b) a variation from the rear yard setback requirements of Section 17.44.010
(H) of the Zoning Ordinance, to allow a rear yard of 0.00 feet, rather than the
10-foot minimum, resulting in a variation of 10 feet (100%); and
   WHEREAS, on June 12, 2006, on due notice thereof, the Zoning Board of
Appeals conducted a public hearing on the requested special use and by the
unanimous vote of the six members of the Board then present, has reported to
the Council recommending that the requested special use permit and rear yard
setback variation be granted; and
   WHEREAS, on May 18, 2005, the engineer retained by the Village to perform
the independent technical review (the “Independent Engineer”) submitted a
report that supports the application of T-Mobile, finding the data submitted by
T-Mobile to be accurate and complete, that the simulation and measurement
techniques used by Applicants’ engineer reflect current industry practices; and
   WHEREAS, the Village’s Independent Engineer further found that the
conclusions of Applicants’ engineer pertaining to the proposed antenna site are
valid and establish that the antennas will be adequate to fill in T-Mobile’s
current coverage gap along Green Bay Road, but also noted that the height of
the proposed antennas may not be adequate to reliably extend T-Mobile’s
coverage eastward to residences in the Sheridan Road lakeshore area during the
summer months due to foliage attenuation when trees are fully leafed; and
   WHEREAS, on May 24, 2006, on due notice thereof, the Plan Commission met to
consider the application and, by the unanimous vote of the nine members then
present, found that the requested special use is consistent with the Village’s
comprehensive plan; and
   WHEREAS, the data submitted by T-Mobile, and confirmed by the Independent
Engineer, establishes that the proposed rooftop and penthouse site on the
building on the Subject Property is a matter of engineering necessity, as the
higher priority sites established by Section 17.52.010 of the Zoning Ordinance
are either unavailable for a new site or are technically unsuitable for the
coverage sought under T-Mobile’s network design; and
   WHEREAS, the RF coverage projections made by the Applicants and confirmed by
the Independent Engineer establish that antennas on the Subject Property and at
the height proposed are a matter of engineering necessity, in order to provide
adequate height and spacing between sites, to reduce gaps in coverage and to
provide reliable in-building service along and around Green Bay Road in the
Hubbard Woods area; and
   WHEREAS, locating antenna arrays on the western edge of the golf course, at
the Winnetka landfill or Public Works yards at 1390 Willow Road, or on the golf
netting poles at the golf course driving range, is not technically feasible for
T-Mobile’s system, in that antennas at those locations would have to be
substantially higher than the antennas being proposed for their signals to
extend far enough to fill the existing coverage gap along and east of Green Bay
Road in Hubbard Woods, and the signals from such antennas would still be
subject to foliage attenuation due to the Village’s mature tree canopy; and
   WHEREAS, T-Mobile will be the second wireless telecommunications carrier to
locate WTSF on the Subject Property, the Council having previously granted a
special use permit for that purpose to AT&T, now Cingular, pursuant to
Ordinance M-546-98; and
   WHEREAS, the height of the proposed antennas will be less than the height of
Cingular’s antennas on the building; and
   WHEREAS, there are no other suitable replacement sites available either on
the smokestack of the Water and Electric Plant or on the monopole of the Public
Safety Building; and
   WHEREAS, the proposed antenna site is more than 250 feet away from the
nearest single-family residence; and
   WHEREAS, the proposed special use is consistent with the objective stated in
Chapter II of the Winnetka Comprehensive Plan, Winnetka 2020, to encourage on-
going study and cooperation to bring the latest telecommunication technologies
to the Village, while preserving the Village’s appearance; and
   WHEREAS, the proposed special use is consistent with the recommendation
stated in Chapter IV of the Winnetka Comprehensive Plan, Winnetka 2020, to
minimize the visual impact of communication antennas and other visual pollution
when building infrastructure for new technology; and
   WHEREAS, the Applicants have met the standards for granting special uses for
antenna arrays in the C-2 Zoning District, as set forth in Section 17.52.010
and Section 17.56.010(M) of the Zoning Ordinance; and
   WHEREAS, the requested special use is in harmony with the general purpose
and intent of the Winnetka Zoning Ordinance, in that it furthers the continuing
use of a structurally sound existing building while maintaining the existing
scale and appearance of the community and protecting established trees and
landscaping; and
   WHEREAS, there are practical difficulties and unique circumstances
associated with carrying out the strict application of the Zoning Ordinance
with respect to the Subject Property in that: (a) the Subject Property is
within the area specifically designated as a location for wireless
telecommunications service facilities (“WTSF”) pursuant to Chapter 17.52 of the
Zoning Ordinance; (b) there are limited suitable locations for WTSF in the
vicinity of the Subject Property, and T-Mobile has demonstrated the necessity
of being allowed to install the proposed antennas and related equipment in the
vicinity of the Subject Property in order to provide continuous service
coverage within the context of the design of its network; (c) the number and
locations of the proposed antennas are based on T-Mobile’s demonstrated
engineering needs, and the antennas must necessarily be placed on the exterior
of the building; and (d) the height and location of the building is fixed on
the Subject Property and strict application of the Zoning Ordinance’s height
and setback requirements would preclude the location of any antennas on the
building; and
   WHEREAS, the requested variations are in harmony with the general purpose
and intent of the Winnetka Zoning Ordinance, and in particular with the stated
purpose of Chapter 17.52, in that granting the requested variations will
promote telecommunications service coverage within the Village while
maintaining the integrity and character of the underlying zoning district; and
   WHEREAS, when installed according to the conditions imposed by this
Ordinance, the WTSF will not alter the essential character of the neighborhood
because the antennas and equipment will be placed in locations that are least
visible from the street and will be painted to match the colors of the
backgrounds against which they will be viewed; and
   WHEREAS, the requested variations will not impair an adequate supply of
light and air to adjacent property in that the proposed antennas are not of
sufficient height or mass to cast shadows on sidewalks and area streets; and
   WHEREAS, the requested variations will not increase the hazard from fire and
other dangers to the Subject Property as the proposed installation will comply
with all applicable building and fire protection codes; and
   WHEREAS, there is no evidence that the requested variations will diminish
the taxable value of land and buildings throughout the Village; and
   WHEREAS, the placement of antennas on the roof of the Subject Property will
not change the principal use of the building and will not contribute in any way
to congestion on the public streets; and
   WHEREAS, there is no evidence that the requested variations will otherwise
impair the public health, safety, comfort, morals, and welfare of the
inhabitants of the Village.
   WHEREAS, the Village of Winnetka is a home rule municipality in accordance
with Article VII, Section 6 of the Constitution of the State of Illinois of
1970; and
   WHEREAS, pursuant to Article VII, Section 6 of the Constitution of the State
of Illinois of 1970, the Village of Winnetka has the authority, except as
limited by said Section 6 of Article VII, to exercise any power and perform any
function pertaining to the government and affairs of the Village, including,
but not limited to, the powers (i) to regulate for the protection of the public
health, safety, morals and welfare, (ii) to license, (iii) to tax, and (iv) to
incur debt; and
   WHEREAS, the Village Council find that establishing standards for the use
and development of lands and buildings within the Village and establishing and
applying criteria for variations from those standards are matters pertaining to
the affairs of the Village.
   NOW, THEREFORE, the Council of the Village of Winnetka do ordain as follows:
   SECTION 1 : That the foregoing recitals are hereby incorporated as the
findings of the Council of the Village of Winnetka, as if fully set forth
herein.
   SECTION 2:   That, pursuant to Section 17.52.010 (N) and Section 17.56.010
(M) of the Winnetka Zoning Ordinance, Title 17 of Winnetka Village Code, and
subject to the terms and conditions hereinafter set forth, a special use permit
is hereby granted with respect to the Subject Property, which is located in the
C-2 General Retail Commercial Zoning District and is commonly known as 5874
Green Bay Road, to permit the installation of 12 new wireless telecommunication
service antennas and related equipment on the exterior walls of the existing
building and its penthouse, as well as on the roof of the existing building on
the Subject Property, in accordance with the plans dated March 31, 2006, and
other materials submitted with and in support of the application for special
use permit dated April 15, 2006.
   SECTION 3:   That the following variations from the requirements of the
Winnetka Zoning Ordinance, Title 17 of the Winnetka Village Code, are hereby
granted with respect to the special use granted for the Subject Property,
commonly known as 874 Green Bay Road, which is located in the “C-2” (General
Retail) Commercial Zoning District: (a) a variation from the height limitations
of Section 17.44.010 (C) of the Zoning Ordinance, to allow the tops of the
proposed antennas to reach a height of up to 49.5 feet, which exceeds the
permitted height of 35 feet, resulting in a variation of 14.5 feet (41.4%); and
(b) a variation from the rear yard setback requirements of Section 17.44.010
(H) of the Zoning Ordinance, to allow antennas to be attached to the west side
of the building, which has a rear yard of 0.00 feet, rather than the 10-foot
minimum, resulting in a variation of 10 feet (100%), both of said variations
being granted to permit the installation of 12 new wireless telecommunication
service antennas and related equipment on the exterior walls of the existing
building and its penthouse, as well as on the roof of the existing building on
the Subject Property, in accordance with the plans dated March 31, 2006, and
other materials submitted with and in support of the application for special
use permit dated April 15, 2006.
   SECTION 4:   That the special use and zoning variation granted by this
Ordinance are subject to the following conditions:
      A.   The antenna installation shall be grouped into three separate
sectors, with four individual antennas in each sector. One of the antenna
sectors shall be mounted on the west side of the penthouse wall at a height of
49.5 feet above grade, and a second antenna sector shall be mounted at the same
height on the north side of the penthouse. The third antenna sector shall be
mounted on the south side of the building just above the building’s lower
parapet wall, at a height of 38.75 feet.
      B.   All wall mounted equipment, including antennas, mounting hardware,
cable and conduit shall be painted to match the color of the portion of the
building to which it is attached.
      C.   All antennas and equipment that extend above the building wall shall
be painted to match the color described by the Applicants as “
   SECTION 5:   That the special use and zoning variation granted by this
Ordinance are further conditioned upon the commencement of the proposed
construction within 12 months after the effective date of this Ordinance.
   SECTION 6:   This Ordinance is passed by the Council of the Village of
Winnetka in the exercise of its home rule powers pursuant to Section 6 of
Article VII of the Illinois Constitution of 1970.
   SECTION 7:   This Ordinance shall take effect immediately upon its passage,
approval and posting as provided by law.
PASSED this 18th day of July, 2006, pursuant to the following roll call vote:
AYES:    Trustees Abell, Behles, Ritchell and President Woodbury
NAYS:    None
ABSENT:    Trustees Berger, Eilers and Tucker
