ORDINANCE NO. M-16-2006
AN ORDINANCE GRANTING A VARIATION IN THE APPLICATION OF THE ZONING ORDINANCE OF
THE VILLAGE OF WINNETKA COOK COUNTY, ILLINOIS (73 Locust Road)
   WHEREAS, the Village of Winnetka is a home rule municipality in accordance
with Article VII, Section 6 of the Constitution of the State of Illinois of
1970; and
   WHEREAS, pursuant to Article VII, Section 6 of the Constitution of the State
of Illinois of 1970, the Village of Winnetka has the authority, except as
limited by said Section 6 of Article VII, to exercise any power and perform any
function pertaining to the government and affairs of the Village, including,
but not limited to, the powers (i) to regulate for the protection of the public
health, safety, morals and welfare, (ii) to license, (iii) to tax, and (iv) to
incur debt; and
   WHEREAS, the Village Council find that establishing standards for the use
and development of lands and buildings within the Village and establishing and
applying criteria for variations from those standards are matters pertaining to
the affairs of the Village; and
   WHEREAS, there has been presented to the Council of the Village of Winnetka,
Cook County, Illinois, the request of the owner of the following described real
estate (the “Subject Property”):
All that part of the West ½ of the West ½ of the Northwest ¼ of the Northeast ¼
of Section 29, Township 42 North, Range 13, East of the Third Principal
Meridian, described as follows: Beginning at a point in the east line of Locust
Road (being 30 feet east of the west line of the Northwest ¼ of the Northeast ¼
of said Section 29) 335.19 feet north of the south line of the North ½ of the
Northeast ¼ of said Section 29; thence east in a straight line, 134.09 feet to
a point in the east line of the West ½ of the West ½ of the West ½ of the
Northwest ¼ of the Northeast ¼ of said Section 29, 335.31 feet north of the
south line of the North ½ of the Northeast ¼ of Section 29, thence south along
said east line of said West ½ of the West ½ of the West ½ of the Northwest ¼ of
the Northeast ¼ of said Section 29, 124.75 feet; thence west in a straight
line, 134.12 feet to a point in the east line of Locust Road, 124.70 feet south
of the place of beginning; thence north along said east line of Locust Road,
124.70 feet to the place of beginning Cook County, Illinois (in the West ½ of
the Southeast ¼ of Section 21),
commonly known as 73 Locust Road, Winnetka, Illinois, and located in the R-
1 Single-Family Residential Zoning District provided in Chapter 17.28 of the
Winnetka Zoning Ordinance, Title 17 of the Winnetka Village Code, for the
following variations from requirements of the Lot, Space, Bulk and Yard
Regulations for Single Family Residential Districts established by Section
17.30 of the Zoning Ordinance: (a) a variation of 3 feet (6%) from the front
yard setback requirements of Section 17.30.050 to allow a front yard setback of
47 feet, whereas a minimum of 50 feet is required, and (b) a variation of 3.58
feet (7.16%) from the rear yard setback requirements of Section 17.30.070 to
allow a rear yard setback of 46.42 feet, whereas a minimum of 50 feet is
required, to allow the owners to replace their existing house, which has a
crumbling foundation and is not a viable candidate for rehabilitation, with a
new, single family home and attached garage, with nonconforming front and rear
yard setbacks and a building footprint of approximately 73 feet wide by 40.7
feet deep; and
   WHEREAS, on July 10, 2006, on due notice thereof, the Zoning Board of
Appeals conducted a public hearing on the requested variations and, by the
favorable vote of 5 of the 6 members then present, has reported to the Council
recommending that the requested variations be granted; and
   WHEREAS, there are practical difficulties associated with carrying out the
strict application of the Zoning Ordinance with respect to the Subject Property
in that: (a) the Subject Property is one of the parcels annexed to the Village
as part of the Indian Hill Subdivision, in which all of the lots were zoned R-
1, regardless of their size; (b) the minimum lot size in the R-1 Zoning
District is 48,000 square feet; (c) the minimum lot width in the R-1 Zoning
District is 150 feet; (d) the minimum lot depth in the R-1 Zoning District is
300 feet; (d) the Subject Property is a legally non-conforming lot, having a
lot size of 16,726.25 square feet, a lot width of 124.71 feet, and a lot depth
of 134.09 feet; and (e) strict application of the R-1 Zoning District’s 50-foot
setback requirements would prohibit any new home on the Subject Property from
being more than 34 feet deep, which would result in rooms that are too narrow
to be compatible with standard room sizes found in homes throughout the
Village; and
   WHEREAS, the Subject Property cannot yield a reasonable return if permitted
to be used only under the conditions allowed by the Zoning Ordinance, because
the restrictions of the zoning regulations would result in the construction of
home than is narrower than the homes permitted on 50-foot wide lots in the R-
5 Zoning Ordinance; and
   WHEREAS, the requested variations will not alter the essential character of
the neighborhood because the proposed new home will comply with side yard
setbacks and will have a front yard setback comparable to the front yard
setback of the home it will be replacing, thereby maintaining a consistent
appearance of the block face; and
   WHEREAS, the requested variations will not impair an adequate supply of
light and air because the conforming side yard setbacks of the proposed new
home will be greater than the side yard setbacks observed by the home it will
be replacing, and the proposed new home will comply with applicable height
limitations and all other applicable bulk regulations; and
   WHEREAS, the requested variations will not increase the hazard from fire and
other dangers to the Subject Property, as the proposed construction will comply
with all applicable building and fire protection codes; and
   WHEREAS, the requested variations will not diminish the taxable value of
land and buildings throughout the Village, and the taxable value of the Subject
Property may be increased because the proposed new home will replace an
deteriorating home that has exceeded its useful life; and
   WHEREAS, the proposed construction will not contribute to congestion on the
public streets, as the property will continue to be used for single family
residential purposes; and
   WHEREAS, there is no evidence that the requested variations will otherwise
impair the public health, safety, comfort, morals, and welfare of the
inhabitants of the Village; and
   WHEREAS, the requested variations are in harmony with the general purpose
and intent of the Winnetka Zoning Ordinance, in that they allow the
redevelopment of the Subject Property with a new home that will maintain the
existing scale and appearance of the community and protect established trees
and landscaping.
   NOW, THEREFORE, the Council of the Village of Winnetka do ordain as follows:
   SECTION 1:   The foregoing recitals are hereby incorporated as the findings
of the Council of the Village of Winnetka, as if fully set forth herein.
   SECTION 2:   The following variations from the Lot, Space, Bulk and Yard
Regulations for Single Family Residential Districts established by Section
17.30 of the Winnetka Zoning Ordinance are hereby granted to the Subject
Property, commonly known as 73 Locust Road and located in the R-1 Single-Family
Residential District provided in Chapter 17.28 of the Zoning Ordinance, Title
17 of the Winnetka Village Code: (a) a variation of 3 feet (6%) from the front
yard setback requirements of Section 17.30.050 to allow a front yard setback of
47 feet, whereas a minimum of 50 feet is required, and (b) a variation of 3.58
feet (7.16%) from the rear yard setback requirements of Section 17.30.070 to
allow a rear yard setback of 46.42 feet, whereas a minimum of 50 feet is
required, to allow the owners to replace their existing house, which has a
crumbling foundation and is not a viable candidate for rehabilitation, with a
new, single family home and attached garage, with nonconforming front and rear
yard setbacks and a building footprint of approximately 73 feet wide by 40.7
feet deep, all in accordance with the plans and elevations submitted with the
application for variations.
   SECTION 3:   The variations hereby granted are conditioned upon the
commencement of the proposed construction within 12 months after the effective
date of this Ordinance.
   SECTION 4:   This Ordinance is passed by the Council of the Village of
Winnetka in the exercise of its home rule powers pursuant to Section 6 of
Article VII of the Illinois Constitution of 1970.
   SECTION 5:   This Ordinance shall take effect immediately upon its passage,
approval and posting as provided by law.
PASSED this 15th day of August, 2006, pursuant to the following roll call vote:
AYES:    Trustees Abell, Eilers, Ritchell and Tucker
NAYS:    None
ABSENT:    Trustees Behles and Berger
APPROVED this 15th day of August, 2006.
   Signed:
   //s//Edmund C. Woodbury
   Village President
Countersigned:
//s//Douglas G. Williams
Village Clerk
