ORDINANCE NO. M-19-2006
AN ORDINANCE AUTHORIZING THE DISPOSITION OF CERTAIN PERSONAL PROPERTY OWNED BY
THE VILLAGE OF WINNETKA
   WHEREAS, Article VII, Section 10 of the Constitution of the State of
Illinois, and the Intergovernmental Cooperation Act, 220 ILCS 220/1, et seq.,
authorize and encourage intergovernmental cooperation; and
   WHEREAS, the Northwest Municipal Conference, is a corporate organization
that represents municipalities and townships chartered within the State of
Illinois and Counties of Cook, DuPage, Kane, Lake, and McHenry, and organizes
joint municipal auctions for the sale of surplus vehicles and equipment; and
   WHEREAS, the Northwest Municipal Conference has scheduled a joint municipal
auction for the sale of surplus vehicles and equipment at 10:00 a.m., Saturday,
September 16, 2006, at the Village of Winnetka Public Works Facility, 1390
Willow Road, Winnetka, Illinois,
   WHEREAS, the Village of Winnetka owns the following described items of
personal property (the “Personal Property”) and has established a minimum value
for each such item of personal property as hereinafter described:
Vehicle Serial    Village ID Type    Year Make      Model       Minimum Price
Number
2FALP71W1VX214787 PW-92      Sedan   1997 Ford      Crown Vic   $750
2FAFP71W1XX180785 WE-67      Sedan   1999 Ford      Crown Vic   $1,000
2FAFP71W6YX162817 PW-6       Sedan   2000 Ford      Crown Vic   $2,600
2FAFP71W71X169202 PD-440     Sedan   2001 Ford      Crown Vic   $3,000
1FMRU1669YLB56816 PW-02      SUV     2000 Ford      Expedition  $3,500
1G2HX52K7T4246054 PD-429     Sedan   1996 Pontiac   Bonneville  $1,500
JKAVF8A1918525889 PD-432     ATV     2001 Kawasaki  Prairie 300 $500
5037M25240        WE-158     Tractor 1987 Bobcat    843         $7,500
1C9261923H1203322 WE-159     Trailer 1987 Cronkhite Tandem      *
   *   Sold as unit with WE-158
   WHEREAS, the Council of the Village of Winnetka have determined that it is
no longer useful to, or in the best interests of, the Village of Winnetka to
retain said Personal Property and that said Personal Property should be sold in
the manner hereinafter provided; and
   WHEREAS, the Village Manager of the Village of Winnetka has authorized the
Northwest Municipal Conference to advertise and obtain bids for the sale of the
items of Personal Property at the joint municipal auction to be conducted by
the Northwest Municipal Conference at 10:00 a.m., Saturday, September 16, 2006,
at the Village of Winnetka Public Works Facility, 1390 Willow Road, Winnetka,
Illinois, with the acceptance of any bids being subject to the approval of the
corporate authorities pursuant to a duly enacted ordinance; and
   WHEREAS, the Village of Winnetka is a home rule municipality in accordance
with Article VII, Section 6 of the Constitution of the State of Illinois of
1970; and
   WHEREAS, pursuant to Article VII, Section 6 of the Constitution of the State
of Illinois of 1970, the Village of Winnetka has the authority, except as
limited by said Section 6 of Article VII, to exercise any power and perform any
function pertaining to the government and affairs of the Village, including,
but not limited to, the powers to regulate for the protection of the public
health, safety, morals and welfare; and
   WHEREAS, the Village Council find that the disposal of surplus personal
property owned by the Village, such as the surplus Personal Property described
in this ordinance is a matter pertaining to the affairs of the Village and that
the manner of disposal of such property pertains to the public health, safety
and general welfare of the Village and its citizens; and
   WHEREAS, the Council of the Village of Winnetka, in the exercise of its home
rule powers pursuant to Section 6 of Article VII of the Illinois Constitution
of 1970, have determined that it is in the best interests of the Village and
its citizens to dispose of the said Personal Property in a manner consistent
with the provisions of Section 11-76-4 of the Illinois Municipal Code (65 ILCS
5/11-76-4), as more fully set forth in this Ordinance.
   NOW, THEREFORE, the Council of the Village of Winnetka do ordain:
   SECTION 1:   Pursuant to the Village's home rule authority, and consistent
with Section 11-76-4 of the Illinois Municipal Code 65 (ILCS 5/11-76-4), the
Council the Village of Winnetka find that the above-described Personal Property
is no longer necessary or useful to the Village of Winnetka and that the best
interests of the Village of Winnetka will be served by the sale of said
Personal Property.
   SECTION 2:   Pursuant to the Village's home rule authority and consistent
with said Section 11-76-4, the Village Manager is hereby authorized to direct
the sale of the Personal Property at an auction to be conducted by the
Northwest Municipal Conference (the “NWMC”) at 10:00 a.m., Saturday, September
16, 2006 at the Village of Winnetka Public Works Facility, 1390 Willow Road,
Winnetka, Illinois.
   SECTION 3:   The Village Manager is further authorized to direct the NWMC to
advertise the sale of the Personal Property through area newspapers, direct
mailings, and other channels as the NWMC deems appropriate prior to the date of
the auction.
   SECTION 4:   The Village Manager is further authorized to direct the NWMC to
enter into an agreement for the sale of the Personal Property, whereby the
Personal Property shall be sold at the auction to the highest bidder or
bidders, according to the terms set forth in the Specifications for the Sale of
Vehicles and Equipment at Northwest Municipal Conference Auctions, which
specifications are attached hereto and made a part of this ordinance.
   SECTION 5:   No bid shall be accepted for the sale of any item of the
Personal Property which is less than the minimum value of said item of personal
property as set forth in the preamble to this ordinance, unless the Village
Manager, or his designee, so authorizes at the time of the auction, and unless
the highest bid received for such item is less than the minimum value set forth
in this ordinance.
   SECTION 6:   Upon payment in full of the auctioned price by the highest
bidder or bidders for any item of the Personal Property, the Village Manager is
authorized to direct the NWMC to convey and transfer the title and ownership of
said item of Personal Property to the highest bidder or bidders.
   SECTION 7:   This Ordinance is adopted by the Council of the Village of
Winnetka in the exercise of its home rule powers pursuant to Section 6 of
Article VII of the Illinois Constitution of 1970.
   SECTION 8:   This Ordinance shall take effect immediately upon passage,
approval and posting.
