ORDINANCE NO. M-21-2006
AN ORDINANCE OF THE VILLAGE OF WINNETKA, COOK COUNTY, ILLINOIS, APPROVING THE
WITHDRAWAL OF THE VILLAGES OF ALBANY, ALLENDALE AND RIVERTON, AND THE CITIES OF
BATAVIA, GENESEO, GENEVA, McLEANSBORO, ROCHELLE AND SPRINGFIELD, FROM
MEMBERSHIP IN THE ILLINOIS MUNICIPAL ELECTRIC AGENCY
   WHEREAS, the Village of Winnetka is a home rule municipality in accordance
with Article VII, Section 6 of the Constitution of the State of Illinois of
1970; and
   WHEREAS, the Village of Winnetka owns and operates a municipal electric
utility system, which furnishes retail electric service to the public; and
   WHEREAS, the Illinois Municipal electric Agency is a body corporate and
politic, municipal corporation and unit of local government of the State of
Illinois created and existing by virtue of the Illinois Joint Municipal
Electric Power Act, contained in Division 119.1 of Article 11 of the Illinois
Municipal Code, as amended (the “Act”), and the Agency Agreement Forming the
Illinois Municipal Electric Agency, dated May 16, 1984, as amended (“Agency
Agreement”); and
   WHEREAS, the Village of Albany, Whiteside County, Illinois (“Albany”), the
Village of Allendale, Wabash County, Illinois (“Allendale”), the City of
Batavia, Kane County, Illinois (“Batavia”), the City of Geneseo, Henry County,
Illinois (“Geneseo”), the City of Geneva, Kane County, Illinois (“Geneva”), the
City of McLeansboro, Hamilton County, Illinois “McLeansboro”), the Village of
Riverton, Sangamon County, Illinois (“Riverton”), the City of Rochelle, Ogle
County, Illinois (“Rochelle”), and the City of Springfield, located in Sangamon
County, Illinois (“Springfield”), are signatories to said Agency Agreement and
are Members of the Illinois Municipal Electric Agency; and
   WHEREAS, the primary purpose of the Illinois Municipal Electric Agency is to
plan for and provide wholesale electric power and energy to member
municipalities in the State of Illinois, however Albany, Allendale, Batavia,
Geneseo, Geneva, McLeansboro, Rochelle, Riverton and Springfield do not
purchase electric power and energy from the Agency; and
   WHEREAS, the Act, the Agency Agreement and the Bylaws of the Illinois
Municipal Electric Agency provide that any Member of the Agency may withdraw
from membership in the Agency upon the approval by ordinance adopted by the
governing body of the majority of the municipalities which are then members of
the Agency, provided that any member permitted to withdraw shall remain
obligated to make payments under any outstanding contract or agreement with the
Agency or any assessment budget of the Agency; and
   WHEREAS, Albany, Allendale, Batavia, Geneseo, Geneva, McLeansboro, Rochelle,
Riverton and Springfield have enacted Ordinances to withdraw from membership in
the Illinois Municipal Electric Agency and have executed Supplements to the
Agency Agreement to accomplish said withdrawal effective December 31, 2006; and
   WHEREAS, the Illinois Municipal Electric Agency has confirmed that each of
these withdrawing municipalities has complied with all conditions for
withdrawal from membership in the Agency and that none of them have any
outstanding obligations under any contract or agreement with the Agency or any
assessment budget of the Agency; and
   WHEREAS, the Village of Winnetka, Cook County, Illinois, hereby finds and
determines that it is reasonable and appropriate to approve the withdrawal of
Albany, Allendale, Batavia, Geneseo, Geneva, McLeansboro, Rochelle, Riverton
and Springfield from membership in the Illinois Municipal Electric Agency.
   NOW, THEREFORE, the Council of the Village of Winnetka do ordain:
   SECTION 1:   The findings and determinations set forth in the preamble to
this Ordinance are hereby made findings and determinations of the Village of
Winnetka and are incorporated into the text of this Ordinance by this
reference.
   SECTION 2:   The Board of Trustees of the Village of Winnetka, Cook County,
Illinois, hereby approves the withdrawal of the Village of Albany, the Village
of Allendale, the City of Batavia, the City of Geneseo, the City of Geneva, the
City of McLeansboro, the City of Rochelle, the Village of Riverton and the City
of Springfield from membership in the Illinois Municipal Electric Agency
effective December 31, 2006, pursuant to the Act, the Agency Agreement and the
Agency’s Bylaws.
   SECTION 3:   The Village President is hereby authorized and directed to
execute, and the Village Clerk shall attest, pursuant to this Ordinance,
Supplement Number 14 to the Agency Agreement, substantially in the form
attached hereto, to cause and effect the removal of Albany, Allendale, Batavia,
Geneseo, Geneva, McLeansboro, Rochelle, Riverton and Springfield from the list
of Members of the Illinois Municipal Electric Agency. The execution of
Supplement Number 14 shall serve as a republication and readoption of all of
the terms and conditions of the Agency Agreement as they relate to the Village
of Winnetka and the remaining Members of the Agency.
   SECTION 4:   This Ordinance is passed by the Council of the Village of
Winnetka in the exercise of its home rule powers pursuant to Section 6 of
Article VII of the Illinois Constitution of 1970.
   SECTION 6:   This Ordinance shall take effect immediately upon its passage,
approval and posting as provided by law. This Ordinance shall be published in
pamphlet form and deposited with the Village Clerk of the Village of Winnetka,
Cook County, Illinois.
PASSED this 19th day of December, 2006, pursuant to the following roll call
vote:
AYES:    Trustees Abell, Behles, Berger, Ritchell and Tucker
NAYS:    None
ABSENT: Trustee Eilers
