2007
ORDINANCE NO. M-1-2007
AN ORDINANCE ANNEXING CERTAIN TERRITORY (“Split Lots”) TO THE VILLAGE OF
WINNETKA, COOK COUNTY, ILLINOIS PURSUANT TO SECTION 7-1-24 OF THE ILLINOIS
MUNICIPAL CODE
WHEREAS, certain parcels of property lying along the north side of Scott Avenue
in the Village of Winnetka between Gordon Terrace and Grove Street are located
partially in the Village of Winnetka and partially in the Village of Glencoe,
and are commonly referred to as “Split Lots;” and
WHEREAS, all of the Split Lots are located in incorporated territory, with the
southern, “front” portion of each of the Split Lots abutting Scott Avenue being
located in the Village of Winnetka ("Winnetka Portion") and the northern,
“rear” portion of each of the Split Lots being located in the Village of
Glencoe ("Glencoe Portion"); and
WHEREAS, the Glencoe Portions of the Split Lots are contiguous to the Winnetka
Portions of the Split Lots; and
WHEREAS, Section 7-1-24 of the Illinois Municipal Code, 65 ILCS 5/7-1-24,
establishes a procedure whereby certain properties located in an incorporated
municipality that is adjacent to another incorporated municipality can be
disconnected from one of the municipalities and annexed to the adjoining
municipality pursuant to (a) a valid petition signed by 50% of the owners and
50% of the voters in the subject territory, and (b) the agreement of the two
municipalities; and
WHEREAS, at the request of the owners of certain of the Split Lots, the Village
of Glencoe and the Village of Winnetka entered into a certain agreement,
entitled "Intergovernmental Agreement Pertaining to Certain Parcels of Land
Located Partially in the Village of Glencoe and Partially in the Village of
Winnetka" and dated September 7, 2006 (the "Intergovernmental Agreement"),
whereby the Village of Glencoe agrees to consent to the disconnection of the
Subject Territory from the Village of Glencoe and the annexation of the Subject
Territory to the Village of Winnetka, and the Village of Winnetka agrees to
reimburse the Village of Glencoe for a portion of the real estate tax revenues
that the Village of Glencoe will lose from the disconnection of the Subject
Territory, subject to the terms and conditions set forth in the
Intergovernmental Agreement; and
WHEREAS, a written petition (the "Petition") has been filed with the Village
Clerk of the Village of Glencoe, Cook County, Illinois, pursuant to Section 7-
1-24 of the Illinois Municipal Code, 65 ILCS 5/7-1-24, requesting that certain
territory (the “Subject Territory”), be disconnected from the Village of
Glencoe and annexed to the Village of Winnetka; and
WHEREAS, on December 19, 2006, at a regularly scheduled meeting, the corporate
authorities of the Village of Glencoe unanimously passed Ordinance 2006-35-
3177, authorizing the disconnection of the Subject Territory from the Village
of Glencoe, subject to the annexation of said Subject Territory by the Village
of Winnetka, pursuant to Section 7-1-24 of the Illinois Municipal Code and the
Intergovernmental Agreement; and
WHEREAS, the Subject Territory consists of the Glencoe Portions of certain of
the Split Lots, and is more fully described in the Plat of Annexation attached
to this Ordinance as Exhibit A, which is hereby incorporated into this
Ordinance by reference and made a part hereof; and
WHEREAS, the Subject Territory is further identified in the Table of Annexation
Territory containing the common street address and Permanent Index Number (PIN)
of each parcel included in the Subject Territory, attached to this Ordinance as
Exhibit B, which is hereby incorporated into this Ordinance by reference and
made a part hereof; and
WHEREAS, the Petition was signed by at least 50% of the owners of record of the
Subject Territory; and
WHEREAS, at least one owner of each parcel included within the Petitioners'
Properties has executed the Petition; and
WHEREAS, the Petition has also been signed by at least 50% of the persons
registered to vote from the Subject Territory; and
WHEREAS, the Subject Territory has an area of less than 160 acres; and
WHEREAS, all of the properties in the Subject Territory have Winnetka mailing
addresses; and
WHEREAS, all of the properties in the Subject Territory are connected to the
Village of Winnetka's electric distribution system and receive electrical
service from the Village of Winnetka's municipal electric utility; and
WHEREAS, all of the properties in the Subject Territory are connected to the
Village of Winnetka's water, storm sewer and sanitary sewer systems and receive
all such services from the Village of Winnetka's municipal water utility and
municipal storm and sanitary sewer systems; and
WHEREAS, all of the properties in the Subject Territory abut Scott Avenue,
which is a dedicated public right-of-way in the Village of Winnetka, and the
Village of Winnetka paves, cleans, plows and otherwise maintains the street and
sidewalks within the Scott Avenue right-of-way; and
WHEREAS, all of the street lights in the Scott Avenue right-of-way are owned by
the Village of Winnetka and are powered by electricity from the Village of
Winnetka's municipal electric utility; and
WHEREAS, all of the properties in the Subject Territory also receive refuse
removal, recycling, and landscape waste disposal services from the Village of
Winnetka or its contractors; and
WHEREAS, all "911" emergency calls from the Subject Territory for fire,
ambulance, rescue and other emergency services are received by the Village of
Winnetka's emergency dispatch center; and
WHEREAS, the Village of Winnetka's Police and Fire Departments are the first
responders for all "911" emergency calls for fire, ambulance, rescue and other
emergency services for all of the parcels in the Subject Territory; and
WHEREAS, all of the land-line telephones within the Subject Territory have
phone numbers beginning with prefixes 441, 446, 501 or 784, all of which are
identified with the Village of Winnetka and are connected to and served through
the AT&T telephone switching station in the Village of Winnetka; and
WHEREAS, the Village of Glencoe levies property taxes against the Glencoe
Portions of the Petitioners’ Properties and annually receives approximately
$82,449.44 in general real estate taxes from the Subject Territory; and
WHEREAS, until the Consolidated Municipal Election of April 5, 2005, persons
registered to vote from the properties within the Subject Territory voted in
the Village of Winnetka's municipal elections, at either New Trier Precinct 49
or New Trier Precinct 8, which are polling places located within the Village of
Winnetka; and
WHEREAS, until the Consolidated Municipal Election held on April 5, 2005,
persons registered to vote from the properties within the Subject Territory
voted in Village of Winnetka municipal elections and cast their votes on
ballots that also included Winnetka School District No. 36, the Winnetka Park
District and the Winnetka-Northfield Library District; and
WHEREAS, at the Consolidated Municipal Election of 2005, without prior notice
and after absentee balloting had begun, the Cook County Clerk's Office dropped
the names of voters with Scott Avenue addresses from the list of registered
voters in New Trier Precinct 49 and transferred the registrations of those
voters to New Trier Precinct 6, which has its polling place in the Village of
Glencoe and uses ballots containing only candidates and issues related to the
Village of Glencoe and the other public bodies located within the Village of
Glencoe; and 
WHEREAS, at the Consolidated Municipal Election held on April 5, 2005, many of
the registered voters from the Split Lots located between Lake Street and Grove
Street, including Split Lots within the Subject Territory, were prohibited from
voting in Winnetka in New Trier Precinct 49, were prohibited from casting
provisional ballots at the Winnetka polling place for New Trier Precinct 49,
were prohibited from voting on Winnetka ballots and were required either to
forego voting altogether or to vote at the polling place in the Village of
Glencoe precinct that had been assigned without prior notice by the Cook County
Clerk, on ballots that contained only issues and candidates for the Village of
Glencoe and other Glencoe public bodies, but no issues or candidates for the
Village of Winnetka and other Winnetka public bodies; and
WHEREAS, the registered voters residing in the Subject Territory desire to
restore their participation in future elections as electors of the Village of
Winnetka, which will be facilitated by the requested disconnection of the
Subject Territory from Glencoe and the annexation of the Subject Territory to
the Village of Winnetka; and
WHEREAS, the Village of Winnetka finds and determines that the community of
interest of the Petitioners and the Subject Territory lies with the Village of
Winnetka, because the Village of Winnetka provides all municipal services to
the Subject Territory and because the residents of the properties within the
Subject Territory had continuously been registered to vote, and did vote, in
the Village of Winnetka since the Split Lots were first developed in the early
part of the 20th century; and
WHEREAS, the Village of Glencoe has acknowledged that the Petitioners believe
that they have more contacts with the Village of Winnetka, and has expressed a
desire to cooperate with the Petitioners, who wish to disconnect their
properties from the Village of Glencoe and annex them to the Village of
Winnetka; and
WHEREAS, the Village of Glencoe and the Village of Winnetka agree that the
disconnection of the Subject Territory from the Village of Glencoe, and the
annexation of the Subject Territory to the Village of Winnetka, will not result
in the isolation of any part of the Village of Glencoe from the remainder of
the Village of Glencoe, will not leave any unincorporated territory between the
Village of Glencoe and the Village of Winnetka, and will not disrupt any of the
Village of Glencoe's existing municipal facilities or any municipal services
provided by the Village of Glencoe; and
WHEREAS, the Village of Winnetka acknowledges that the Village of Glencoe will
lose the real estate tax revenues that have been received from the Subject
Territory if it is disconnected from the Village of Glencoe and annexed to the
Village of Winnetka; and
WHEREAS, the Village of Winnetka has continuously provided all services to both
the Glencoe Portions and Winnetka Portions of all of the Split Lots, including
the Split Lots in the Subject Territory, as if those Split Lots were located
entirely in the Village of Winnetka, without reimbursement from the Village of
Glencoe; and
WHEREAS, the Village of Winnetka finds that all petitions, documents, and other
necessary legal requirements are in full compliance with the applicable
statutes of the State of Illinois, specifically Section 7-1-24 of the Illinois
Municipal Code; and,
WHEREAS, the Village of Winnetka finds that annexing the Subject Territory as
provided in the Intergovernmental Agreement between the Village of Glencoe and
the Village of Winnetka will aid the governmental objectives of both
municipalities and is for the benefit of their respective communities; and
WHEREAS, the Village of Winnetka finds that it is in the best interests of the
Village of Winnetka and its citizens that the Subject Territory be annexed to
the Village of Winnetka.
NOW, THEREFORE, the Council of the Village of Winnetka do ordain:
SECTION 1:   That the foregoing recitals, findings and determinations set forth
in the preamble to this Ordinance are hereby adopted as the legislative
findings and determinations of the Village of Winnetka and are incorporated
into the text of this Ordinance by this reference as if stated fully herein.
SECTION 2:   That the following described territory:
That part of Lots 13, Lot 14 (except the East 20.0 ft.) and Lots 16 to 24 in
Block 28, also Lots 13, 15 to 22, the West Half of Lot 23 in Block 23, also
Lots 13 to 24 in Block 7, also the East 2 feet of Lot 10, the East Half of Lot
8, Lot 7, the East Half of Lot 5 and Lot 4 in Block 10 in Chicago North Shore
Land Company’s Subdivision in Sections 17 and 18, Township 42 North, Range 13,
East of the Third Principal Meridian, along with Lot 7, the West 50 feet of Lot
8 and Lots 9 To 12 in Block 8, also Lot 6 (except the Northerly 87 feet), the
West Half of Lot 5, and Lots 3 and 4 in Block 9, also Lot 6 in Block 10, in
Lloyd’s Subdivision of Blocks 1, 2, 3, 4, 5 in Taylor’s Second Addition to
Taylorsport, being a Subdivision of part of the Northeast Quarter of Section 18
and part of the Northwest Quarter of Section 17, and the East 24 Acres of the
North 48 Acres of the Northeast Quarter of Section 18, Township 42 North, Range
13, East of the Third Principal Meridian, also all of Grove Street lying West
of and adjacent to Block 28, all of Greenwood Avenue lying between said Blocks
23 and 28, all of Randolph Street lying between said Blocks 7 and 8, all of
Lake Street lying East of said Block 8 and all of Euclid Avenue lying West of
said Block 10, lying North of the South line of the Northwest Quarter of said
Section 18 and lying South of the North line of the aforementioned Lots said
North line extended across said Streets and Avenues, all in Cook County
Illinois, being depicted on the Plat of Annexation appended to this Ordinance
as Exhibit A and made a part hereof, is hereby annexed to the Village of
Winnetka, Cook County, Illinois.
SECTION 3:   That the Village President is hereby authorized and directed to
sign, and the Village Clerk to attest, the Plat of Annexation that is appended
to this Ordinance.
SECTION 4:   That the Village Clerk is hereby directed to record with the Cook
County Recorder, and to file with the Cook County Clerk, a certified copy of
this Ordinance, together with the accurate map of the Subject Territory, as
depicted on the Plat of Annexation appended to this Ordinance as Exhibit A, and
the Table of Annexation Territory appended to this Ordinance as Exhibit B.
SECTION 5:   That the Village President and Village Clerk are hereby authorized
and directed to take such other steps as may be necessary to effectuate the
annexation of the Subject Territory in accordance with the terms of this
Ordinance and the Intergovernmental Agreement.
SECTION 6:   That this Ordinance is passed by the Council of the Village of
Winnetka in the exercise of its home rule powers pursuant to Section 6 of
Article VII of the Illinois Constitution of 1970.
SECTION 7:   That this Ordinance shall take effect immediately upon its
passage, approval and posting as provided by law.
PASSED this 16th day of January, 2007, pursuant to the following roll call
vote:
AYES:    Trustees Abell, Behles, Berger, Eilers, Ritchell and Tucker
NAYS:    None
ABSENT:    None
APPROVED this 16th day of January, 2007.
