ORDINANCE NO. M-2-2007
AN ORDINANCE GRANTING A VARIATION IN THE APPLICATION OF THE ZONING ORDINANCE OF
THE VILLAGE OF WINNETKA COOK COUNTY, ILLINOIS (508 Birch)
WHEREAS, the property commonly known as 508 Birch Street, Winnetka, Illinois,
(the “Subject Property”) is legally described as follows:
The North half of Lot 32 in Block 5 in Provident Mutual Land Association
Subdivision of Blocks 7 to 12, 28 to 33 and 54 to 59 all inclusive, in
Winnetka, in Section 20, Township 42 North, Range 13 East of the Third
Principal Meridian, in Cook County, Illinois; and
WHEREAS, the Subject Property is located in the R-5 Single Family Zoning
District provided in Chapter 17.12 of the Winnetka Zoning Ordinance, Title 17
of the Winnetka Village Code; and
WHEREAS, on October 11, 2006, the owner of the Subject Property filed an
application for the following variations from requirements of the Lot, Space,
Bulk and Yard Regulations for Single Family Residential Districts established
by Section 17.30 of the Zoning Ordinance: (a) variation from the intensity of
use of lot limitations of Section 17.30.030 to allow a roofed lot coverage of
1,452.16 square feet, whereas a maximum of 1,176.75 square feet is permitted, a
variation of 275.41 square feet (23.4%); (b) a front yard variation of 11.83
feet (39.43%) from the 30-foot minimum required in Section 17.30.050, resulting
in a front yard setback of 18.17 feet; (c) a variation from the side yard
setback provisions of Section 17.30.060, to allow a south side yard setback of
5.4 feet, a variation of 4.01 (42.61%) feet from the 9.41-foot required
minimum; and (d) a north side yard variation of 3.56 feet (59.33%) from the
six-foot minimum required in Section 17.30.110, all in order to reconstruct a
one story enclosed porch and to rebuild a detached one-car garage; and
WHEREAS, on December 11, 2006, on due notice thereof, the Zoning Board of
Appeals held a public hearing on the requested variations and, by the unanimous
vote of the 5 members then present, has reported to the Council recommending
that the requested variations be granted; and
WHEREAS, there are practical difficulties and particular hardships associated
with carrying out the strict application of the Zoning Ordinance with respect
to the Subject Property in that: (a) the Subject Property was created by the
subdivision of a corner lot before the enactment of the Zoning Ordinance; (b)
the Subject Property is significantly shorter and wider than the typical zoning
lot, with a lot depth of 50 feet and a lot width of 94 feet; (c) the Subject
Property’s legally nonconforming lot area of 4,707 square feet is almost 3700
square feet less than the minimum lot size for the R-5 Single Family Zoning
District; (d) the Subject Property is improved with a residence that was built
in 1916, before the enactment of the Winnetka Zoning Ordinance; (e) the Subject
Property has a legally nonconforming roofed lot coverage, and legally
nonconforming front yard and south and north side yard setbacks; (f) the
enclosed porch on the south elevation of the residence is in a state of
disrepair and needs to be rehabilitated; (g) the nonconforming size and
location of the house cannot be cured without removing portions of the house;
(h) because of the extremely shallow lot depth, the garage cannot be
constructed in the rear 25% of the Subject Property, although it is set back
only 2.55 feet from the rear lot line; (i) the garage is dilapidated and needs
replacing; (j) rebuilding the garage in a conforming location would require the
removal of a 40 year old maple tree; and (k) the nonconforming side yards of
the Subject Property adjoin the rear yards of the properties to the north,
south and west; and
WHEREAS, the Subject Property cannot yield a reasonable return if permitted to
be used only under the conditions allowed by the Zoning Ordinance because: (a)
the existing house is in need of rehabilitation and the dilapidated garage
needs to be replaced; (b) building the garage in a conforming location would
require the removal of a mature maple tree, which is an asset to the Subject
Property; (c) limiting the reconstruction of the south porch area to a
conforming size and location would require reducing the size and configuration
of interior rooms and would negatively impact the livability of the space; and
(d) limiting the reconstruction of the south porch area to a conforming size
and location would have a negative impact on the appearance of the Subject
Property as viewed from the street; and
WHEREAS, the requested variations will not alter the essential character of the
neighborhood because the proposed improvements to the house will maintain the
existing building footprints and the location of the garage will be unchanged,
thus maintaining the appearance of the Subject Property as it has existed for
approximately 90 years; and
WHEREAS, the requested variations will not impair an adequate supply of light
and air because: (a) the proposed improvements will comply with applicable
height limitations and will not further reduce any of the existing setbacks,
and (b) all of the nonconforming setbacks are adjacent to the rear yards of the
adjoining properties; and
WHEREAS, the requested variations will not increase the hazard from fire and
other dangers to the Subject Property, as the proposed construction will comply
with all applicable building and fire protection codes; and
WHEREAS, the requested variations will not diminish the taxable value of land
and buildings throughout the Village, and the taxable value of the Subject
Property may be increased because of the proposed improvements; and
WHEREAS, the proposed construction will not contribute to congestion on the
public streets, as the property will continue to be used for single family
residential purposes; and
WHEREAS, there is no evidence that the requested variations will otherwise
impair the public health, safety, comfort, morals, and welfare of the
inhabitants of the Village; and
WHEREAS, the Village of Winnetka is a home rule municipality in accordance with
Article VII, Section 6 of the Constitution of the State of Illinois of 1970,
with the authority, except as limited by said Section 6 of Article VII, to
exercise any power and perform any function pertaining to the government and
affairs of the Village, including, but not limited to, the powers to regulate
for the protection of the public health, safety, morals and welfare; and
WHEREAS, the Village Council find that establishing standards for the use and
development of lands and buildings within the Village and establishing and
applying criteria for variations from those standards are matters pertaining to
the affairs of the Village; and
WHEREAS, the requested variations are in harmony with the general purpose and
intent of the Winnetka Zoning Ordinance, in that they allow the renovation,
restoration and rehabilitation of a structurally sound existing building while
maintaining the existing scale and appearance of the community and protecting
established trees and landscaping.
NOW, THEREFORE, the Council of the Village of Winnetka do ordain as follows:
SECTION 1:   The foregoing recitals are hereby incorporated as the findings of
the Council of the Village of Winnetka, as if fully set forth herein.
SECTION 2:   The following variations from the Lot, Space, Bulk and Yard
Regulations for Single Family Residential Districts established by Section
17.30 of the Winnetka Zoning Ordinance are hereby granted to the Subject
Property, commonly known as 508 Birch and located in the R-5 Single-Family
Residential District provided in Chapter 17.16 of the Winnetka Village Code,
Title 17 of the Winnetka Village Code: (a) variation from the intensity of use
of lot limitations of Section 17.30.030 to allow a roofed lot coverage of
1,452.16 square feet, whereas a maximum of 1,176.75 square feet is permitted, a
variation of 275.41 square feet (23.4%); (b) a front yard variation of 11.83
feet (39.43%) from the 30-foot minimum required in Section 17.30.050, resulting
in a front yard setback of 18.17 feet; (c) a variation from the side yard
setback provisions of Section 17.30.060, to allow a south side yard setback of
5.4 feet, a variation of 4.01 (42.61%) feet from the 9.41-foot required
minimum; and (d) a north side yard variation of 3.56 feet (59.33%) from the
six-foot minimum required in Section 17.30.110, all in order to reconstruct a
one story enclosed porch and to rebuild a detached one-car garage, in
accordance with the plans and elevations submitted with the application for
variations.
SECTION 3:   The variations hereby granted are conditioned upon the
commencement of the proposed construction within 12 months after the effective
date of this Ordinance.
SECTION 4:   This Ordinance shall take effect immediately upon passage,
approval and posting.
PASSED this 6th day of February 2007, pursuant to the following roll call vote:
AYES:    Trustees Abell, Behles, Berger, Eilers, Ritchell, Tucker
NAYS:    None
ABSENT:    None
APPROVED this 6th day of February, 2007.
   Signed:
   //s//Edmund C. Woodbury
   Village President
Countersigned:
//s//Douglas G. Williams
Village Clerk
Introduced:    January 16, 2007   
Posted:    January 17, 2007   
