ORDINANCE NO. M-3-2007
AN ORDINANCE GRANTING A VARIATION IN THE APPLICATION OF THE ZONING ORDINANCE OF
THE VILLAGE OF WINNETKA COOK COUNTY, ILLINOIS (1074 Laurel Avenue)
WHEREAS, the Village of Winnetka is a home rule municipality in accordance with
Article VII, Section 6 of the Constitution of the State of Illinois of 1970;
and
WHEREAS, pursuant to Article VII, Section 6 of the Constitution of the State of
Illinois of 1970, the Village of Winnetka has the authority, except as limited
by said Section 6 of Article VII, to exercise any power and perform any
function pertaining to the government and affairs of the Village, including,
but not limited to, the powers (i) to regulate for the protection of the public
health, safety, morals and welfare, (ii) to license, (iii) to tax, and (iv) to
incur debt; and
WHEREAS, the property commonly known as 1074 Laurel Avenue, Winnetka, Illinois
(the “Subject Property”), is legally described as follows:
Lot 1 (except the South 155 feet thereof) in Block 10 in County Clerk’s
Division of the Southwest ¼ of Section 17, Township 42 North, Range 13 East of
the Third Principal Meridian, in Cook County, Illinois; and
WHEREAS, the Subject Property is located in the R-2 Zoning District provided in
Chapter 17.24 of the Winnetka Zoning Ordinance, Title 17 of the Winnetka
Village Code; and
WHEREAS, on November 26, 2006, the owner of the Subject Property filed an
application for the following variations from requirements of the Lot, Space,
Bulk and Yard Regulations for Single Family Residential Districts established
by Section 17.30 of the Zoning Ordinance: (a) a variation from the intensity of
use of lot limitations of Section 17.30.030 to allow a gross floor area of
3,435.88 square feet, whereas a maximum of 2,907.2 square feet is permitted,
resulting in a variation of 528.68 square feet (18.18%); (b) a variation from
the maximum building size provisions of Section 17.30.040 to permit a roofed
lot coverage of 2,393.35 square feet, resulting in a variation of 576.35 square
feet (31.72%) from the allowed maximum of 1,817 square feet; and (c) a corner
yard setback variation of 1.41 feet (10.54%) from the 13.38-foot minimum
required in Section 17.30.050, to allow for a north corner yard setback of
11.97 feet; and
WHEREAS, all of said variations are being requested in order to (a) remove the
two-story west portion of the home, which currently consists of a two-car
garage on the first floor and a family room on the second floor, and to build
in its place a new two-story addition containing a first-floor family room and
second-floor bedroom; (b) expand the existing enclosed front porch into an open
porch that spans the front of the residence; and (c) construct a new, detached
two-car garage; and
WHEREAS, on January 8, 2007, on due notice thereof, the Zoning Board of Appeals
conducted a public hearing on the requested variations and, by the unanimous
vote of the 7 members then present, has reported to the Council recommending
that the requested variations be granted; and
WHEREAS, there are practical difficulties associated with carrying out the
strict application of the Zoning Ordinance with respect to the Subject Property
in that: (a) the Subject Property is a legally nonconforming, under-sized lot
with a lot area of 7,268 square feet, which is 17,932 square feet less than the
25,200 square-foot requirement for the R-2 Single Family Zoning District; (b)
the Subject Property’s lot is irregularly shaped, with a curving north property
line that reduces the size of the northeast corner of the lot; (c) as a corner
lot, the Subject Property is subject to front yard setbacks along both of its
street frontages; (d) the effect of the irregular shape of the Subject Property
is compounded by the orientation of the existing house, which was constructed
in 1915, before the enactment of the Winnetka Zoning Ordinance, and which is
oriented to the corner lot line rather than to the front lot line, so that it’s
effective width ranges from approximately 113.95 feet to 150.00 feet, and it’s
effective maximum lot depth is only 48.45 feet; (e) the Subject Property has
legally nonconforming roofed lot coverage and gross floor area, as well as
legally nonconforming front and side yards; and (f) the existing attached
garage is in poor condition and needs to be replaced; and
WHEREAS, the Subject Property cannot yield a reasonable return if permitted to
be used only under the conditions allowed by the Zoning Ordinance, in that (a)
the nonconformities in the generally sound existing house cannot be cured
without removing substantial portions of the house; (b) a new house of
comparable size could not be built on the Subject Property; and (c) there is no
conforming alternative for the location of the proposed front porch; and
WHEREAS, the requested variations will not alter the essential character of the
neighborhood because the proposed construction will be consistent with the
neighborhood and the open front porch will enhance the appearance of the
existing house within the neighborhood; and
WHEREAS, the requested variations will not impair an adequate supply of light
and air because the proposed construction (a) will replace the existing
attached garage with a slightly smaller addition; (b) the new construction will
comply with applicable height limitations; (c) the new detached garage will
conform with applicable setbacks; and (d) the lot coverage and setbacks related
to the front porch are facing the street and are located opposite an open,
triangular green space at the intersections of Laurel, Rosewood and Burr
Avenues; and
WHEREAS, the requested variations will not increase the hazard from fire and
other dangers to the Subject Property, as the proposed construction will comply
with all applicable building and fire protection codes; and
WHEREAS, the requested variations will not diminish the taxable value of land
and buildings throughout the Village, and the taxable value of the Subject
Property may be increased because of the proposed improvements; and
WHEREAS, the proposed construction will not contribute to congestion on the
public streets, as the property will continue to be used for single family
residential purposes and the new detached garage will increase available off-
street parking; and
WHEREAS, there is no evidence that the requested variations will otherwise
impair the public health, safety, comfort, morals, and welfare of the
inhabitants of the Village; and
WHEREAS, the requested variations are in harmony with the general purpose and
intent of the Winnetka Zoning Ordinance, in that they allow the renovation,
restoration and rehabilitation of a structurally sound existing building while
maintaining the existing scale and appearance of the community and protecting
established trees and landscaping.
NOW, THEREFORE, the Council of the Village of Winnetka do ordain as follows:
SECTION 1:   The foregoing recitals are hereby incorporated as the findings of
the Council of the Village of Winnetka, as if fully set forth herein.
SECTION 2:   The following variations from the Lot, Space, Bulk and Yard
Regulations for Single Family Residential Districts established by Section
17.30 of the Winnetka Zoning Ordinance are hereby granted to the Subject
Property, commonly known as 1074 Laurel Avenue, and located in the R-2 Single-
Family Residential District provided in Chapter 17.24 of the Winnetka Zoning
Ordinance, Title 17 of the Winnetka Village Code: (a) a variation from the
intensity of use of lot limitations of Section 17.30.030 to allow a gross floor
area of 3,435.88 square feet, whereas a maximum of 2,907.2 square feet is
permitted, resulting in a variation of 528.68 square feet (18.18%); (b) a
variation from the maximum building size provisions of Section 17.30.040 to
permit a roofed lot coverage of 2,393.35 square feet, resulting in a variation
of 576.35 square feet (31.72%) from the allowed maximum of 1,817 square feet;
and (c) a corner yard setback variation of 1.41 feet (10.54%) from the 13.38-
foot minimum required in Section 17.30.050, to allow for a north corner yard
setback of 11.97 feet; all of said variations being to allow the replacement of
the existing two-story attached garage/second floor west portion of the home
with a slightly smaller two-story addition, the construction of a detached
garage, and the replacement of the existing enclosed front porch with a larger,
open, roofed porch, all in accordance with the plans and elevations submitted
with the application for variations.
SECTION 3:   The variations hereby granted are conditioned upon the
commencement of the proposed construction within 12 months after the effective
date of this Ordinance.
SECTION 4:   This Ordinance shall take effect immediately upon passage,
approval and posting.
ADOPTED this 20th day of February, 2007, pursuant to the following roll call
vote:
AYES:    Trustees Behles, Berger, Eilers, Ritchell and Tucker
NAYS:    None
ABSENT:    Trustee Abell
APPROVED this 20th day of February, 2007.
         Signed:
   //s//Edmund C. Woodbury
   Village President
Countersigned:
//s//Douglas G. Williams
Village Clerk
Introduced:    February 6, 2007   
Posted:    February 7, 2007   
Passed and Approved:    February 20,2007   
Posted:    February 21, 2007   
ORDINANCE NO. M-4-2007
AN ORDINANCE OF THE VILLAGE OF WINNETKA, COOK COUNTY, ILLINOIS, AUTHORIZING
PROJECT FINANCING PARTICIPATION PURSUANT TO POWER SALES CONTRACT WITH THE
ILLINOIS MUNICIPAL ELECTRIC AGENCY
WHEREAS, the Village of Winnetka, Cook County, Illinois (the “Municipality”) is
a home rule municipality in accordance with Article VII, Section 6 of the
Constitution of the State of Illinois of 1970; and
WHEREAS, the Municipality owns and operates an electric utility which furnishes
retail electric service to the public; and
WHEREAS, the Municipality is a Participating Member of the Illinois Municipal
Electric Agency (“Agency”) pursuant to a Power Sales Contract, as amended, and
various addendums (the “Contract”); and
WHEREAS, the Agency has presented to the Municipality a Notice (the “Notice”)
to elect to receive service from and participate in the financing of a mine
mouth power generating project, commonly known as the "Prairie State Project”
(the “Project”) which election must be made by Municipality within 30 days, and
which Notice together with attached Agency Resolution No. 07-02-654 describing
the Project is now before the President and Board of Trustees (the “Corporate
Authorities”); and
WHEREAS, the Corporate Authorities have considered the merits and have decided
to elect to receive service from the Project and to participate in the
financing thereof;
NOW THEREFORE, be it ordained by the President and Board of Trustees of the
Village of Winnetka, Cook County, Illinois, as follows:
SECTION 1:   The findings and determinations set forth in the preambles to this
Ordinance are hereby made findings and determinations of the Corporate
Authorities of the Municipality and are incorporated into the body of this
Ordinance by reference.
SECTION 2:   Any and all prior action taken by the Corporate Authorities and
officers of the Municipality in connection with the Contract is hereby
ratified, confirmed and approved.
SECTION 3:   The Municipality elects (the “Election”) to receive service from
the Prairie State Project and to participate in the financing thereof.
SECTION 4:   The Municipality elects to have its electric rates set so as to
amortize its proportionate share of debt service as follows:
*  over the standard period of amortization as determined by IMEA’s Board of
Directors for other Participating Members, and the term of the Contract is
hereby extended through September 30, 2035.
*  over 15 years, and the term of the Contract is hereby extended through
September 30, 2028 or such later date as is necessary for IMEA to recover the
Municipality's proportionate share of debt service related to the Project.
SECTION 5:   The President and Village Clerk are authorized to execute and
deliver the Election as provided in this ordinance to IMEA; they may use the
form of Election provided by IMEA. All officers of the Municipality and its
employees are authorized to take such steps and do such acts as are necessary
or appropriate in furtherance of the determinations of this ordinance.
SECTION 6:   All ordinances, resolutions, motions or orders in conflict with
the provisions hereof are hereby superseded to the extent of such conflict.
SECTION 7:   This Ordinance is passed by the Council of the Village of Winnetka
in the exercise of its home rule powers pursuant to Section 6 of Article VII of
the Illinois Constitution of 1970.
SECTION 8:   This Ordinance shall take effect immediately upon its passage,
approval and posting as provided by law.
PASSED this 13th day of March, 2007, pursuant to the following roll call vote:
AYES:    Trustees Abell, Behles, Berger, Eilers, Ritchell and Tucker
NAYS:    None
ABSENT:    None
APPROVED this 13th day of March, 2007.
   Signed:
   //s//Edmund C. Woodbury
   Village President
Countersigned:
//s//Douglas G. Williams
Village Clerk
Introduced: March 6, 2007
Posted: March 7, 2007
Passed and Approved: March 13, 2007
