THIRD ADDENDUM TO POWER SALES CONTRACT
   This Third Addendum to the Power Sales Contract Between the Illinois
Municipal Electric Agency and the Village of Winnetka, dated June 1, 1990, is
made this ___ day of __________, 2007, by and between the ILLINOIS MUNICIPAL
ELECTRIC AGENCY, a municipal corporation and unit of local government of the
State of Illinois, and the VILLAGE OF WINNETKA, an Illinois municipal
corporation.
   WHEREAS, the Illinois Municipal Electric Agency ("IMEA" or "Agency") and the
Village of Winnetka ("Winnetka") have heretofore entered into a Power Sales
Contract (“PSC”), dated June 1, 1990 and effective October 1, 1990, as amended
by the Addendum to the PSC dated December 7, 1990, and the Second Amendment to
the PSC dated March 9, 2004, pursuant to which Winnetka has agreed to purchase
and the IMEA has agreed to provide and sell, subject to certain limitations,
all of the electric power and energy required for the operation of Winnetka’s
municipal electric utility for a term of thirty-five (35) years through
September 30, 2025; and
WHEREAS, in furtherance of its obligations under the PSCs, the Agency issued
bonds and purchased an undivided 12.12 percent ownership interest in a coal-
fired generating unit, known as Trimble County Unit No. 1 (“TC1”), in Trimble
County, Kentucky; and
WHEREAS, the Agency has also issued bonds and is participating in the
construction of a second coal-fired generating unit to be known as Trimble
County Unit No. 2 (“TC2”), which has a projected unit nameplate rating of 750
MW, approximately 91 MW or 12.12 percent of which will be dedicated to IMEA;
and
WHEREAS, all Participating Members of the Agency have paid or are paying rates
and charges for power and energy that are designed to cover the debt service on
the bonds issued by the Agency in connection with the purchase of TC1 and will
pay rates and charges for power and energy designed to cover the debt service
on the bonds issued by the Agency in connection with its participation in the
development and construction of TC2, as well as all other Agency expenses; and
WHEREAS, Winnetka elected to have its rates set pursuant to the PSC so as to
amortize its proportionate share of debt service associated with the bonds
issued to fund the purchase of TC1 over a fifteen (15) year period, and its
proportionate share of such bonds has been fully paid; and
WHEREAS, Winnetka initially elected to have its rates set pursuant to the PSC
so as to amortize its proportionate share of debt service associated with the
bonds issued to fund the construction of TC2 over a fifteen (15) year period;
however Winnetka now seeks to have and its rates set so as to amortize its
proportionate share of such debt service over the same period as all other
Participating Members through February 1, 2035; and
WHEREAS, on January 1, 2007, the Agency began charging rates sufficient to
recover debt service costs related to the Power Supply System Revenue Bonds,
Series 2006 under which Winnetka has been paying a charge under Rate Schedule B
based on a 15 year amortization of such costs (“Series 2006 Revenue Bonds Debt
Service Payment”) while other Participating Members have paid a rate under Rate
Schedule B based on an amortization to February 1, 2035 (“Series 2006 Bonds
Debt Service Demand Charge”); and
WHEREAS, upon execution of this Third Addendum to the Power Sales Contract,
Winnetka shall be billed according to the Series 2006 Revenue Bonds Debt
Service Demand Charge as may be amended from time-to-time by the Board of
Directors under Rate Schedule B and IMEA agrees to refund to Winnetka on the
next invoice for power supply delivered under the PSC, the difference between
the amounts previously paid by Winnetka related to the Series 2006 Revenue
Bonds Debt Service Payment and the amount that would have been paid under the
Series 2006 Bonds Debt Service Demand Charge for all months previously billed
by IMEA since January 1, 2007; and    
WHEREAS, the IMEA Board of Directors has approved and executed a long-term,
full requirements Power Sales Contract with the City of Naperville, and has
authorized participation in the development, construction, ownership and
operation of a new coal-fired, mine mouth power generating project known as the
“Prairie State Project,” being developed in Washington and St. Clair Counties,
Illinois by Prairie State Generating Company, LLC, an affiliate of Peabody
Energy Corporation, and other public power project participants (IMEA’s
ownership interest being between 240 MW and 300 MW out of a total projected
plant capability of 1,582 MW), as a source of additional baseload capacity and
energy to add to its existing mix of resources in order to be able to serve the
City of Naperville and the other Participating Members; and
   WHEREAS, participation in the Prairie State Project will require one or more
bond financings, and Winnetka has exercised its rights under Section 1(d)(iii)
to elect to receive service from the Prairie State Project and to participate
in the financing thereof with the further election to have its rates set so as
to amortize its proportionate share of debt service for bonds used to fund the
Prairie State Project over the standard period of amortization to be determined
by the IMEA Board of Directors for all other Participating Members; and
   WHEREAS, IMEA and Participating Member have agreed to amend the Power Sales
Contract as set forth herein.
   NOW, THEREFORE, the Illinois Municipal Electric Agency and the Village of
Winnetka hereby agree as follows:
   1.    The initial term of the Power Sales Contract between IMEA and Winnetka
is hereby extended an additional ten (10) years to September 30, 2035.
   2.   Section 1 of the Power Sales Contract is amended by deleting the entire
text of subsection (a) and replacing it with the following:
This Contract shall take effect on October 1, 1990 and shall remain in effect
for an initial term of forty-five (45) years through September 30, 2035, and
thereafter from year to year until terminated by five (5) years prior written
notice. In no event shall this Contract extend beyond September 30, 2040.
   3.   IMEA hereby accepts and approves the change to Winnetka’s election with
respect to the amortization period for its proportionate share of the debt
service costs related to the Power Supply System Revenue Bonds, Series 2006
(“Series 2006 Bonds”). IMEA agrees that Winnetka’s rate under Section 4(b)(2)
of Rate Schedule B shall be set pursuant to the Series 2006 Bonds Debt Service
Demand Charge as may be amended from time-to-time by the IMEA Board of
Directors so as to amortize its proportionate share of debt service associated
with the Series 2006 Bonds over a period to February 1, 2035. For any
subsequent bonds, Winnetka’s rates for debt service shall be set so as to
amortize its proportionate share over a standard period as determined by the
Board of Directors for all other Participating Members. To the extent that
Winnetka has paid rates and charges with respect to its proportionate share of
the debt service associated with the Series 2006 Bonds under the Series 2006
Bonds Debt Service Payment since January 1, 2007, IMEA shall refund on the next
invoice for power supply delivered under the PSC the difference between such
payments and the payments that would have been made by Winnetka under the
Series 2006 Bonds Debt Service Demand Charge for such periods.
    
   4.   It is agreed between the parties that in the event there is a conflict
between the provisions of this Third Addendum and provisions of either the
Power Sales Contract, the Addendum to Power Sales Contract or the Second
Addendum to Power Sales Contract the provisions of this Third Addendum shall
prevail and control.
   IN WITNESS THEREOF the parties have authorized the execution of this Third
Addendum and have caused their duly authorized representatives to sign as of
the day and year first written above.
