ORDINANCE NO. M-18-2007
AN ORDINANCE GRANTING A VARIATION IN THE APPLICATION OF THE ZONING ORDINANCE OF
THE VILLAGE OF WINNETKA, COOK COUNTY, ILLINOIS (1091 Sheridan)
WHEREAS, the Village of Winnetka is a home rule municipality in accordance with
Article VII, Section 6 of the Constitution of the State of Illinois of 1970,
pursuant to which it has the authority, except as limited by said Section 6 of
Article VII, to exercise any power and perform any function pertaining to the
government and affairs of the Village; and
WHEREAS, the Council of the Village of Winnetka (“Village Council”) find that
establishing standards for the use and development of lands and buildings
within the Village and establishing and applying criteria for variations from
those standards are matters pertaining to the affairs of the Village; and
WHEREAS, the property commonly known as 1091 Sheridan Road, Winnetka, Illinois
(the “Subject Property”), is legally described as follows:
Lot 3 in Porter’s Subdivision of Lot 1 in Campbell’s Resubdivision of Block 1
of Hubbard’s Estate Subdivision in the Northeast fractional quarter of Section
17, Township 42 North, Range 13, East of the Third Principal Meridian,
according to the plat thereof recorded July 25, 1944, as Document No. 13326297,
in Cook County, Illinois; and
WHEREAS, the Subject Property is located in the R-2 Single Family Residential
District provided in Chapter 17.24 of the Winnetka Zoning Ordinance, Title 17
of the Winnetka Village Code; and
WHEREAS, on August 8, 2007, the owner of the Subject Property filed an
application for the following variations from requirements of the Lot, Space,
Bulk and Yard Regulations for Single Family Residential Districts established
by Chapter 17.30 of the Zoning Ordinance: (a) a variation from the front yard
setback requirements of Section 17.30.050 to allow a front yard setback of 40
feet, whereas a minimum of 50 feet is required, resulting in a variation of 10
feet (20%); (b) a variation from the side yard setback provisions of Section
17.30.060 to permit a side yard setback of 4.25 feet, whereas the minimum
required is 12 feet, resulting in a variation of 7.75 feet (64.58%); (c) a
variation from the rear yard setback requirements of Section 17.30.070 to allow
a rear yard setback of 12.9 feet, whereas the required minimum is 24.71 feet,
resulting in a variation of 11.81 feet (47.79%); and (d) a variation from the
conforming uses restrictions of Section 17.64.060 to add two new windows in the
nonconforming north side wall, which has a nonconforming side yard setback of
4.25 feet, whereas a minimum of 12 feet is required, all being requested in
order to construct two one-story additions to the home for the purpose of
adding a guest suite and enlarging the one-car garage; and
WHEREAS, on August 8, 2007, on due notice thereof, the Zoning Board of Appeals
conducted a public hearing on the requested variations and, by the unanimous
vote of the seven members then present, has reported to the Council
recommending that the requested variations be granted; and
WHEREAS, there are practical difficulties and particular hardships associated
with carrying out the strict application of the Zoning Ordinance with respect
to the Subject Property in that: (a) the Subject Property has a legally
nonconforming lot size of 21,159 square feet, which is 2,841 square feet less
than the required minimum lot size in the R-2 Single Family Residential
District; (b) the Subject Property is an irregularly shaped lot located in the
ravines; (c) due to its irregular shape and topography, the Subject Property’s
buildable area is only 1,350 square feet; (d) the single family residence on
the Subject Property is a converted coach house that was constructed in 1896,
before the enactment of the Winnetka Zoning Ordinance; (e) the Subject Property
was created by a subdivision of a larger parcel that occurred before the
current subdivision standards were set and that resulted in situating the
residence in the extreme northeast corner of the Subject Property; (f) the
Subject Property is accessed from a private access driveway that extends from
the bottom of the ravine to the top of the bluff, and that cuts through the
middle of the Subject Property from north to south; (g) due to the number of
properties served by the access road, it is treated as a private street for
zoning purposes, as a result of which the Subject Property’s front yard setback
is measured from the edge of the private access driveway; (h) the Subject
Property has a legally nonconforming front yard setback of 31.25 feet, whereas
a 50-foot setback is required; (i) the Subject Property has a legally
nonconforming north side yard setback of 4.25 feet, whereas a 12-foot setback
is required; and (j) the rear yard of the Subject Property has a legally
nonconforming setback of 19.9 feet, whereas the requirement is 24.71 feet; and
WHEREAS, the Subject Property cannot yield a reasonable return if permitted to
be used only under the conditions allowed by the Zoning Ordinance, in that: (a)
the variations are being requested to allow the construction of two additions
along the north side of the existing residence, one that would extend the plane
of the existing north and west building lines and one at the northeast corner
of the building, to allow the construction of a new attached garage at the
northwest corner and to allow the existing garage area to be expanded and
converted into a mudroom and laundry area at the center of the north side of
the building, and a first floor guest bedroom, bath and den at the northeast
corner; (b) the proposed additions are for typical elements in single family
residences in the vicinity of the Subject Property; (c) the expanded residence
will be more than 2,000 square feet under the maximum allowable building size;
and (d) there are no conforming locations for improvements to the existing
residence; and
WHEREAS, the requested variations will not alter the essential character of the
neighborhood because the proposed additions: (a) do not encroach further toward
the adjoining property than the existing building line; (b) add a net of 354.48
square feet of roofed lot coverage, resulting in a building footprint that is
less than the maximum allowable; (c) are located at the top of the bluff and
are not visible from Sheridan Road; and (d) are consistent with the style of
the existing residence and with the scale of the adjacent neighborhood; and
WHEREAS, the requested variations will not impair an adequate supply of light
and air because the proposed additions are only one story high and are screened
from view from the adjoining property by existing, mature, dense landscaping;
and
WHEREAS, the requested variations will not increase the hazard from fire and
other dangers to the Subject Property, as the proposed construction will comply
with all applicable building and fire protection codes; and
WHEREAS, the requested variations will not diminish the taxable value of land
and buildings throughout the Village, and the taxable value of the Subject
Property may be increased because of the proposed improvements; and
WHEREAS, the proposed construction will not contribute to congestion on the
public streets, as the property will continue to be used for single family
residential purposes; and
WHEREAS, there is no evidence that the requested variations will otherwise
impair the public health, safety, comfort, morals, and welfare of the
inhabitants of the Village; and
WHEREAS, the requested variations are in harmony with the general purpose and
intent of the Winnetka Zoning Ordinance, in that they allow the renovation,
restoration and rehabilitation of a structurally sound existing building while
maintaining the existing scale and appearance of the community and protecting
established trees and landscaping.
NOW, THEREFORE, the Council of the Village of Winnetka do ordain as follows:
SECTION 1:   The foregoing recitals are hereby incorporated as the findings of
the Council of the Village of Winnetka, as if fully set forth herein.
SECTION 2:   The following variations from the Lot, Space, Bulk and Yard
Regulations for Single Family Residential Districts established by Chapter
17.30 of the Winnetka Zoning Ordinance are hereby granted to the Subject
Property, commonly known as 1091 Sheridan Road and located in the R-2 Single-
Family Residential District provided in Chapter 17.24 of the Winnetka Village
Code, Title 17 of the Winnetka Village Code: (a) a variation from the front
yard setback requirements of Section 17.30.050 to allow a front yard setback of
40 feet, whereas a minimum of 50 feet is required, resulting in a variation of
10 feet (20%); (b) a variation from the side yard setback provisions of Section
17.30.060 to permit a side yard setback of 4.25 feet, whereas the minimum
required is 12 feet, resulting in a variation of 7.75 feet (64.58%); (c) a
variation from the rear yard setback requirements of Section 17.30.070 to allow
a rear yard setback of 12.9 feet, whereas the required minimum is 24.71 feet,
resulting in a variation of 11.81 feet (47.79%); and (d) a variation from the
conforming uses restrictions of Section 17.64.060 to add two new windows in the
nonconforming north side wall, which has a nonconforming side yard setback of
4.25 feet, whereas a minimum of 12 feet is required, all being requested in
order to construct two one-story additions to the home for purposes of adding a
guest suite and enlarging the one-car garage, in accordance with the plans and
elevations submitted with the application for variations.
SECTION 3:   This Ordinance is passed by the Council of the Village of Winnetka
in the exercise of its home rule powers pursuant to Section 6 of Article VII of
the Illinois Constitution of 1970.
SECTION 4:   This Ordinance shall take effect immediately upon its passage,
approval and posting as provided by law.
PASSED this 6th day of November, 2007, pursuant to the following roll call
vote:
AYES:    Trustees Behles, Berger, Eilers, Poor, Tucker
NAYS:    None
ABSENT:    Trustee Ritchell
APPROVED this 6th day of November, 2007.
   Signed:
   s/Edmund C. Woodbury
   Village President
Countersigned:
s/Douglas G. Williams
Village Clerk
