ORDINANCE NO. M-20-2007
AN ORDINANCE GRANTING A VARIATION IN THE APPLICATION OF THE ZONING ORDINANCE OF
THE VILLAGE OF WINNETKA, COOK COUNTY, ILLINOIS (510 Walnut)
WHEREAS, the Village of Winnetka is a home rule municipality in accordance with
Article VII, Section 6 of the Constitution of the State of Illinois of 1970,
pursuant to which it has the authority, except as limited by said Section 6 of
Article VII, to exercise any power and perform any function pertaining to the
government and affairs of the Village; and
WHEREAS, the Council of the Village of Winnetka (“Village Council”) find that
establishing standards for the use and development of lands and buildings
within the Village and establishing and applying criteria for variations from
those standards are matters pertaining to the affairs of the Village; and
WHEREAS, the property commonly known as 510 Walnut, Winnetka, Illinois (the
“Subject Property”), is legally described as follows:
The North 60 feet of the South 200 feet of the East 120 feet of that part of
Block 22 lying North of the North line of Oak Street and West of the West line
of Walnut Street in Winnetka in fractional Section 21, Township 42 North, Range
13, East of the Third Principal Meridian, in Cook County, Illinois; and
WHEREAS, the Subject Property is located in the R-4 Single-Family Zoning
District provided in Chapter 17.16 of the Winnetka Zoning Ordinance, Title 17
of the Winnetka Village Code; and
WHEREAS, on September 11, 2007, the owner of the Subject Property filed an
application for the following variations from requirements of the Lot, Space,
Bulk and Yard Regulations for Single Family Residential Districts established
by Chapter 17.30 of the Zoning Ordinance: (a) a variation from the intensity of
use of lot provisions of Section 17.30.030 to permit a roofed lot coverage of
2,574.81 square feet, whereas the maximum allowed is 1,800 square feet,
resulting in a variation of 774.81 square feet (43.04%); (b) a variation from
the intensity of use of lot provisions of Section 17.30.030 to allow an
impermeable lot coverage of 3,691.86 square feet, whereas a maximum of 3,600
square feet is permitted, resulting in a variation of 91.86 square feet
(2.55%); (c) a variation from the rear yard setback requirements of Section
17.30.110 to allow a rear yard setback of 0.0 feet, whereas a minimum of 6 feet
is required, resulting in a variation of 6 feet (100%); and (d) a variation
from the side yard setback provisions of Section 17.30.110 to permit a north
side yard setback of 0.33 feet, whereas a minimum of 2 feet is required,
resulting in a variation of 1.67 feet (83.5%), all of said variations being
requested to rebuild a garage that was demolished in a storm on August 23,
2007; and
WHEREAS, on October 8, 2007, on due notice thereof, the Zoning Board of Appeals
conducted a public hearing on the requested variations and, by the unanimous
vote of the five members then present, has reported to the Council recommending
that the requested variations be granted; and
WHEREAS, there are practical difficulties and particular hardships associated
with carrying out the strict application of the Zoning Ordinance with respect
to the Subject Property in that: (a) the Subject Property is 60-feet wide and
120 feet deep and has a legally nonconforming lot area of 7,200 square feet,
which is 5,400 square feet less than the requirement in the R-4 Zoning
District; (b) the Subject Property is improved with a single-family residence,
which was constructed in 1921, prior to the enactment of the Winnetka Zoning
Ordinance; (c) the improvements on the Subject Property also include a legally
nonconforming one-car garage that was constructed in 1929 and encroaches into a
neighbor’s side yard by 2.15 feet; (d) during the brief, intense storm of
August 23, 2007, a large tree on a neighboring parcel was blown over onto the
garage, damaging it beyond repair; and (e) because of the location of the
existing residence, there is no suitable conforming location on the Subject
Property to rebuild the garage; and
WHEREAS, the Subject Property cannot yield a reasonable return if permitted to
be used only under the conditions allowed by the Zoning Ordinance, in that: (a)
a garage is a standard amenity for homes throughout the Village; (b) it is not
possible to rebuild the garage without a variation because, as long as the
house remains, there is no conforming location for a new garage; (c) if the
garage cannot be replaced, the value of the Subject Property will be reduced,
as the Subject Property will lose an improvement that has existed been part of
the improved property since 1929; and
WHEREAS, the requested variations will not alter the essential character of the
neighborhood because the new garage is replacing a similar sized structure in
approximately the same location; and
WHEREAS, the requested variations will not impair an adequate supply of light
and air because the proposed new garage will be in approximately the same
location and will be the same size as the demolished garage; and
WHEREAS, the requested variations will not increase the hazard from fire and
other dangers to the Subject Property, as the proposed construction will comply
with all applicable building and fire protection codes; and
WHEREAS, the requested variations will not diminish the taxable value of land
and buildings throughout the Village, and the taxable value of the Subject
Property may be increased because of the proposed improvements; and
WHEREAS, the proposed construction will not contribute to congestion on the
public streets, as the property will continue to be used for single family
residential purposes; and
WHEREAS, there is no evidence that the requested variations will otherwise
impair the public health, safety, comfort, morals, and welfare of the
inhabitants of the Village; and
WHEREAS, the requested variations are in harmony with the general purpose and
intent of the Winnetka Zoning Ordinance, in that they allow the renovation,
restoration and rehabilitation of a structurally sound existing building while
maintaining the existing scale and appearance of the community and protecting
established trees and landscaping.
NOW, THEREFORE, the Council of the Village of Winnetka do ordain as follows:
SECTION 1:   The foregoing recitals are hereby incorporated as the findings of
the Council of the Village of Winnetka, as if fully set forth herein.
SECTION 2:   The following variations from the Lot, Space, Bulk and Yard
Regulations for Single Family Residential Districts established by Section
17.30 of the Winnetka Zoning Ordinance are hereby granted to the Subject
Property, commonly known as 510 Walnut and located in the R-4 Single-Family
Residential District provided in Chapter 17.16 of the Winnetka Village Code,
Title 17 of the Winnetka Village Code: (a) a variation from the intensity of
use of lot provisions of Section 17.30.030 to permit a roofed lot coverage of
2,574.81 square feet, whereas the maximum allowed is 1,800 square feet,
resulting in a variation of 774.81 square feet (43.04%); (b) a variation from
the intensity of use of lot provisions of Section 17.30.030 to allow an
impermeable lot coverage of 3,691.86 square feet, whereas a maximum of 3,600
square feet is permitted, resulting in a variation of 91.86 square feet
(2.55%); (c) a variation from the rear yard setback requirements of Section
17.30.110 to allow a rear yard setback of 0.0 feet, whereas a minimum of 6 feet
is required, resulting in a variation of 6 feet (100%); and (d) a variation
from the side yard setback provisions of Section 17.30.110 to permit a north
side yard setback of 0.33 feet, whereas a minimum of 2 feet is required,
resulting in a variation of 1.67 feet (83.5%), all of said variations being
requested to rebuild a garage that was demolished in a storm on August 23,
2007, in accordance with the plans and elevations submitted with the
application for variations.
SECTION 3:   This Ordinance is passed by the Council of the Village of Winnetka
in the exercise of its home rule powers pursuant to Section 6 of Article VII of
the Illinois Constitution of 1970.
SECTION 4:   This Ordinance shall take effect immediately upon its passage,
approval and posting as provided by law.
PASSED this 20th day of November, 2007, pursuant to the following roll call
vote:
AYES:    Trustees Behles, Berger, Eilers, Poor, Ritchell and Tucker
NAYS:    None
ABSENT:    None
APPROVED this 20th day of November, 2007.
   Signed:
   s/Edmund C. Woodbury
   Village President
Countersigned:
s/Douglas G. Williams
Village Clerk
