ORDINANCE NO. M-26-2007
AN ORDINANCE AUTHORIZING THE SALE OR OTHER DISPOSITION OF SURPLUS ELECTRICAL
EQUIPMENT
WHEREAS, the Village of Winnetka (“Village”) owns and operates an electric
utility that uses various types of equipment in its operations; and
WHEREAS, the Water and Electric Department has reported to the Council of the
Village of Winnetka (“Village Council”) that the electrical equipment listed in
the attached Exhibit A (the “Surplus Personal Property”) has been replaced, is
no longer operable, or has otherwise become of no use to the Village’s electric
distribution system; and
WHEREAS, the Water and Electric Department has requested that the Village
Council determine that said Surplus Personal Property is no longer necessary or
useful to the Village and that the Village Council authorize its disposal; and
WHEREAS, the Village is a home rule municipality in accordance with Article
VII, Section 6 of the Constitution of the State of Illinois of 1970 and, except
as limited pursuant to said Section 6 of Article VII, the Village has the
authority to exercise any power and perform any function pertaining to the
government and affairs of the Village; and
WHEREAS, the Village Council find that the disposal of surplus property owned
by the Village, such as the Surplus Personal Property described in Exhibit A to
this Ordinance is a matter pertaining to the affairs of the Village; and
WHEREAS, the Village Council have determined that disposal of the Surplus
Personal Property as provided in this ordinance is necessary and proper so as
to avoid incurring unnecessary additional costs and unnecessary exposure to
liability related to storing or disposing of the Surplus Personal Property; and
WHEREAS, the Council of the Village of Winnetka, in the exercise of its home
rule powers pursuant to Section 6 of Article VII of the Illinois Constitution
of 1970, have determined that it is in the best interests of the Village and
its citizens to dispose of the Surplus Personal Property in a manner consistent
with the provisions of Section 11-76-4 of the Illinois Municipal Code (65 ILCS
5/11-76-4), as more fully set forth in this Ordinance.
NOW THEREFORE, the Council of the Village of Winnetka do ordain as follows:
SECTION 1:   The foregoing recitals are hereby incorporated as the findings of
the Council of the Village of Winnetka, as if fully set forth herein.
SECTION 2:   The Council of the Village of Winnetka (“Village Council’) find:
(a) that the electric equipment listed in the attached Exhibit A (“Surplus
Personal Property”) is no longer necessary or useful to the Village of
Winnetka; and (b) that the best interests of the Village of Winnetka will be
served by the sale or other disposition of the Surplus Personal Property as
hereinafter provided.
SECTION 3:   The Village Council further find that, based on prior experience
in disposing of similar items of surplus property, the cost of conducting a
public sale of such items, including the costs of advertising, publication and
providing personnel to maintain security and to conduct the public sale,
exceeds the value of such items.
SECTION 4:   The Village Manager is hereby authorized and directed to determine
the value and dispose of the Personal Property in the manner provided in
Sections 5 and 6 of this Ordinance.
SECTION 5:   The Village Manager, in the exercise of his discretion, may
dispose of any Surplus Personal Property that does not contain PCBs in any or
all of the following ways:
A.   by sale to the highest bidder, with or without advertising; and
B.   in furtherance of the goals of intergovernmental cooperation set forth in
Article VII, Section 10 of the Illinois Constitution of 1970, and the
Intergovernmental Cooperation Act, 5 ILCS 220/1, et seq., by transferring title
to any Illinois municipal electric utility, with or without competitive
bidding; provided, that (1) competitive bids may be obtained with or without
advertising, and (2) the terms and conditions of any transfer of title without
competitive bidding shall be established by the Village Manager on a case by
case basis, after considering such factors as the technical needs and financial
capabilities of such municipal electric utility and the estimated value of the
transformers.
SECTION 6:   All Surplus Personal Property that contains PCBs or that is PCB
contaminated (the “Contaminated Surplus Personal Property”) shall be disposed
of at the lowest cost to the Village, said cost being determined with or
without advertising; provided, that any person or entity that disposes of or
destroys any part of such Contaminated Surplus Personal Property shall provide
a sworn statement to the Village certifying that such disposal or destruction
complies with all applicable environmental laws and regulations.
SECTION 7:   This Ordinance is passed by the Council of the Village of Winnetka
in the exercise of its home rule powers pursuant to Section 6 of Article VII of
the Illinois Constitution of 1970.
SECTION 8:   This Ordinance shall take effect immediately upon its passage,
approval and posting as provided by law.
PASSED this 15th day of January, 2008, pursuant to the following roll call
vote:
AYES:    Trustees Behles, Berger, Eilers, Poor, Ritchell and Tucker
NAYS:    None
ABSENT: None
