ORDINANCE NO. M-3-2008
AN ORDINANCE GRANTING A VARIATION IN THE APPLICATION OF THE ZONING ORDINANCE OF
THE VILLAGE OF WINNETKA, COOK COUNTY, ILLINOIS (681 Garland)
WHEREAS, the Village of Winnetka is a home rule municipality in accordance with
Article VII, Section 6 of the Constitution of the State of Illinois of 1970,
pursuant to which it has the authority, except as limited by said Section 6 of
Article VII, to exercise any power and perform any function pertaining to the
government and affairs of the Village; and
WHEREAS, the Council of the Village of Winnetka (“Village Council”) find that
establishing standards for the use and development of lands and buildings
within the Village and establishing and applying criteria for variations from
those standards are matters pertaining to the affairs of the Village; and
WHEREAS, the property commonly known as 681 Garland Avenue, Winnetka, Illinois
(the “Subject Property”), is legally described as follows:
The East 75.0 feet of Lot 2 and the West 75.0 feet of the East 77.0 feet of the
South 17.56 feet of Lot 1 in Lydia D. Sutter’s Subdivision of that part of
Block 4 lying West of a line 436.55 feet East of and parallel with the center
line of Forest Street, in John C. Garland’s Addition to Winnetka, being a
subdivision of the North 120 acres of the Southwest ¼ of Section 21, Township
42 North, Range 13, East of the Third Principal Meridian, in Cook County,
Illinois; and
WHEREAS, the Subject Property is located in the R-5 Zoning District provided in
Chapter 17.12 of the Winnetka Zoning Ordinance, Title 17 of the Winnetka
Village Code; and
WHEREAS, on November 2, 2007, the owner of the Subject Property filed an
application for the following variations from requirements of the Lot, Space,
Bulk and Yard Regulations for Single Family Residential Districts established
by Chapter 17.30 of the Zoning Ordinance: (a) a variation from the intensity of
use of lot restrictions of Section 17.30.030(A) to allow a roofed lot coverage
of 2,702.59 square feet, whereas a maximum of 2,481.25 square feet is
permitted, resulting in a variation of 221.34 square feet (8.92%); (b) a
variation from the intensity of use of lot limitations of Section 17.30.030(B)
to permit an impermeable lot coverage of 5,167.93 square feet, whereas the
maximum allowed is 4,962.5 square feet, resulting in a variation of 205.43
square feet (4.14%); (c) a variation from the maximum building size limits of
Section 17.30.0340 to authorize a gross floor area of 4,069.63 square feet,
whereas the maximum allowed is 3,800 square feet, resulting in a variation of
269.63 square feet (7.09%); (d) a variation from the side yard setback
provisions of Section 17.30.060(A) to allow an exterior basement stairway in
the east side yard to have a setback of 2.12 feet, whereas a minimum of 7.49
feet is required, resulting in a variation of 5.37 feet (71.69%); and (e) a
variation from the setback requirements of Section 17.30.060(B) to permit a
total side yard setback of 11.12 feet, whereas a minimum of 18.73 feet is
required, resulting in a variation of 7.61 feet (40.63%), all of said
variations being requested to build a 48.47-square foot, one-story kitchen
addition, a new exterior basement stairway and a fireplace chimney for the
family room; and
WHEREAS, on January 14, 2008, on due notice thereof, the Zoning Board of
Appeals conducted a public hearing on the requested variations and, by the
unanimous vote of the seven members then present, has reported to the Council
recommending that the requested variations be granted; and
WHEREAS, the requested variation was considered by the Village Council at its
meeting on February 19, 2008, at which time the Council deferred action to
allow the applicant to consider conforming alternatives for the outside
stairway; and
WHEREAS, the applicant has since submitted revised plans that relocate the
exterior basement stairs to a conforming location north of the proposed
breakfast room, in approximately the same location as the existing exterior
stairs; and
WHEREAS, as a result of the relocation of the exterior basement stairs, the
stairs have a conforming side yard setback of 8.7 feet, which exceeds the
required side yard setback of 7.49 feet; and
WHEREAS, as a result of the stair relocation and other minor plan changes,
including the replacement of the proposed fireplace chimney with a bay window,
the requested gross floor area was reduced by 2.49 square feet, the requested
roofed lot coverage was reduced by 0.04 square feet, and the requested amount
of impermeable surface was reduced by 106.06 square feet; and
WHEREAS, there are practical difficulties associated with carrying out the
strict application of the Zoning Ordinance with respect to the Subject Property
in that: (a) the Subject Property is improved with a single family residence
that was constructed in 1928 and has legally nonconforming roofed lot coverage,
gross floor area, impermeable surface area and side yard setbacks; (b) the only
access to the basement is through a nonconforming interior stairway that has a
vertical clearance of 5.42 feet and a width of from 2.25 to 2.5 feet, making
them difficult and dangerous to use; (b) there is no exterior access to the
basement due to the existence of a deck at the rear of the house; (c) the
residence has a small kitchen with no room for an eating area; (d) due to the
interior configuration of the house, the interior basement stairs cannot be
brought into compliance and the only available area for a eating area is
adjacent to the northeast corner of the kitchen, which encroaches into the east
side yard; and (e) the proposed bay window will measure 7 feet by 1.66 feet and
will be located in a conforming location on the west wall of the family room;
and
WHEREAS, the Subject Property cannot yield a reasonable return if permitted to
be used only under the conditions allowed by the Zoning Ordinance, in that: (a)
an eating area in or adjacent to the kitchen is a typical amenity found in
homes throughout the Village; (b) it is not possible to enlarge the kitchen or
to correct the basement stairs within the existing building walls without
reconfiguring the interior and relocating structural elements of the house; and
(c) due to the nonconforming building size and lot coverage, it is not possible
to make any additions to the house without a variance; and
WHEREAS, the requested variations will not alter the essential character of the
neighborhood because the proposed additions are improvements typically
associated with a single family home and will be located along the side or rear
portions of the house where they are less visible from the street; and
WHEREAS, the requested variations will not impair an adequate supply of light
and air because (a) the proposed bay window addition will extend only 1.66 feet
from the west wall of the family room, the one-story kitchen addition will be
tucked into an interior corner along the east wall of the family room and north
wall of the kitchen; and (b) the existing, nonconforming east building line of
the home will be extended only 6.09 feet for the breakfast nook addition; and
WHEREAS, the requested variations will not increase the hazard from fire and
other dangers to the Subject Property, as the proposed construction will comply
with all applicable building and fire protection codes; and
WHEREAS, the requested variations will not diminish the taxable value of land
and buildings throughout the Village, and the taxable value of the Subject
Property may be increased because of the proposed improvements; and
WHEREAS, the proposed construction will not contribute to congestion on the
public streets, as the property will continue to be used for single family
residential purposes; and
WHEREAS, there is no evidence that the requested variations will otherwise
impair the public health, safety, comfort, morals, and welfare of the
inhabitants of the Village; and
WHEREAS, the requested variations are in harmony with the general purpose and
intent of the Winnetka Zoning Ordinance, in that they allow the renovation,
restoration and rehabilitation of a structurally sound existing building while
maintaining the existing scale and appearance of the community and protecting
established trees and landscaping.
NOW, THEREFORE, the Council of the Village of Winnetka do ordain as follows:
SECTION 1:   The foregoing recitals are hereby incorporated as the findings of
the Council of the Village of Winnetka, as if fully set forth herein.
SECTION 2:   The following variations from the Lot, Space, Bulk and Yard
Regulations for Single Family Residential Districts established by Section
17.30 of the Winnetka Zoning Ordinance are hereby granted to the Subject
Property, commonly known as 681 Garland Avenue, and located in the R-5 Single-
Family Residential District provided in Chapter 17.12 of the Winnetka Zoning
Ordinance, Title 17 of the Winnetka Village Code: (a) a variation from the
intensity of use of lot restrictions of Section 17.30.030(A) to allow a roofed
lot coverage of 2,702.55 square feet, whereas a maximum of 2,481.25 square feet
is permitted, resulting in a variation of 221.3 square feet (8.92%); (b) a
variation from the intensity of use of lot limitations of Section 17.30.030(B)
to permit an impermeable lot coverage of 5,061.87 square feet, whereas the
maximum allowed is 4,962.5 square feet, resulting in a variation of 99.37
square feet (2%); (c) a variation from the maximum building size limits of
Section 17.30.0340 to authorize a gross floor area of 4,067.14 square feet,
whereas the maximum allowed is 3,800 square feet, resulting in a variation of
267.14 square feet (7.03%); (d) a variation from the side yard setback
provisions of Section 17.30.060(A) to allow the breakfast room addition in the
east side yard to have a setback of 5.18 feet, whereas a minimum of 7.49 feet
is required, resulting in a variation of 1.68 feet (22.43%); and (e) a
variation from the setback requirements of Section 17.30.060(B) to permit a
total side yard setback of 14.81 feet, whereas a minimum of 18.73 feet is
required, resulting in a variation of 3.92 feet (20.93%), all of said
variations being requested to build a 45.98-square foot, one-story kitchen
addition, a new exterior basement stairway and a bay window for the family room
in accordance with the plans and elevations submitted with the application for
variations, as subsequently amended by the revised plans, as presented to the
Council in its March 18, 2008 agenda materials.
SECTION 3:   This Ordinance is passed by the Council of the Village of Winnetka
in the exercise of its home rule powers pursuant to Section 6 of Article VII of
the Illinois Constitution of 1970.
SECTION 4:   This Ordinance shall take effect immediately upon its passage,
approval and posting as provided by law.
PASSED this 18th day of March, 2008, pursuant to the following roll call vote: 
AYES:    Trustees Behles, Berger, Eilers, Poor, Ritchell, Tucker
NAYS:    None
ABSENT:    None
APPROVED this 18th day of March, 2008.
   Signed:
   /s/Edmund C. Woodbury
   Village President
Countersigned:
/s/Douglas G. Williams
Village Clerk
Introduced:   Waived March 18, 2008
Posted:   Waived March 18, 2008
Passed and Approved:   March 18, 2008
