Posted:   May 21, 2008
Passed and Approved:   June 3, 2008
Posted:   June 4, 2008
ORDINANCE NO. M-9-2008
AN ORDINANCE AMENDING THE LEASE OF MUNICIPAL PROPERTY TO THE HARRIS BANK
WINNETKA
WHEREAS, the Village of Winnetka ("Village") is a home rule municipality in
accordance with the Constitution of the State of Illinois of 1970 and, except
as limited by Section 6 of Article VII of the Constitution of the State of
Illinois of 1970, is authorized to exercise any power and perform any function
pertaining to its government and affairs, including, but not limited to, the
power to regulate for the protection of the public health, safety, morals and
welfare; and
WHEREAS, the Village is the owner of a certain parcel of real estate located
adjacent to the northwest corner of the Village Hall site, being a portion of
Lots 9 and 10 in Wilson and Dale’s Subdivision of the north one half of Block
26 in Winnetka (the "Village Property"); and
WHEREAS, since 1968, the Village has leased a portion of said Village Property
to the Harris Bank Winnetka, a national banking corporation located at 520
Green Bay Road, Winnetka, Illinois, (“Harris Bank”) and its predecessor, as an
additional driveway area for expanded drive-in banking facilities; and
WHEREAS, on October 6, 1998, the Council of the Village of Winnetka adopted
Ordinance M-538-98, renewing the lease agreement ("Lease") with the Harris Bank
pursuant to which Harris Bank leases approximately 312.5 square feet of the
aforesaid Village Property, as described more fully in the Lease and shown in
the plat of leasehold attached thereto (the “Leased Premises”); and
WHEREAS, the current Lease expires on July 31, 2008, and Harris Bank has
requested that the Village extend the Lease for 10 years, from August 1, 2008,
through July 31, 2018; and
WHEREAS, the Village's Finance Director has recommended, and Harris Bank has
agreed, that the rent for the 10-year extension ("Extension Term") should be
increased from the current annual rent of $1,000 to an annual rent of $1,600
for each of the first 5 years of the Extension Term, and to an annual rent of
$2,000 per year for each of the remaining 5 years of the Extension Term; and
WHEREAS, the Village Council find that extending the Lease as recommended by
the Finance Director will benefit the public health, safety and welfare of the
Village by allowing vehicles to continue to enter the Harris Bank’s drive-in
banking facilities from the immediately adjoining alley, providing a more
gradual turning radius and reducing interference with traffic on Green Bay
Road.
NOW, THEREFORE, the Council of the Village of Winnetka do ordain as follows:
SECTION 1: The foregoing recitals are hereby adopted as the findings of the
Council of the Village of Winnetka, and are incorporated by reference as if
fully set forth herein.
SECTION 2: The Amended Lease Agreement by and between the Village of Winnetka
and the Harris Bank Winnetka is hereby approved, in substantially the form
attached hereto as Exhibit A.
SECTION 3: The Village President and Village Clerk are hereby authorized and
directed to execute and seal, on behalf of the Village, the Amended Lease
Agreement substantially in the form attached hereto as Exhibit A, and to take
such other and further steps as may be necessary to effectuate the Amended
Lease Agreement, including recording the lease with the Cook County Recorder of
Deeds in the manner provided by statute.
SECTION 4: This Ordinance is passed by the Council of the Village of Winnetka
in the exercise of its home rule powers pursuant to Section 6 of Article VII of
the Illinois Constitution of 1970.
SECTION 5  This Ordinance shall take effect immediately upon its passage,
approval and posting as provided by law.
PASSED this 17th day of June, 2008, pursuant to the following roll call vote:
AYES:    Trustees Behles, Berger, Greable, Johnson, Poor, Rintz
NAYS:    None
ABSENT:    None
APPROVED this 17th day of June, 2008.
   Signed:
   Edmund C. Woodbury
   Village President
Countersigned:
Douglas G. Williams
Village Clerk
Introduced: June 3, 2008
Posted: June 4, 2008
Passed and Approved: June 17, 2008
Posted June 18, 2008
EXHIBIT A
AMENDED LEASE
   THIS AMENDED LEASE, executed in duplicate this _____ day of
________________, 2008, by and between the Village of Winnetka, Cook County,
Illinois (hereinafter sometimes referred to as “Lessor”) and The Harris Bank
Winnetka, a national banking corporation, of Winnetka, Illinois (hereinafter
sometimes referred to as “Lessee”);
WITNESSETH:
   1.   Lessor hereby leases to Lessee, and Lessee hereby leases from Lessor,
the following described real estate in the Village of Winnetka, County of Cook,
State of Illinois:
That portion of Lots 9 and 10 in WILSON AND DALE’S SUBDIVISION of the North ½
of Block 26 of “Winnetka”, in the Northeast ¼ of the Northeast ¼ of Section 20,
Township 42 North, Range 13 East of the Third Principal Meridian, described as
follows: Beginning at the Northwest corner of said Lot 9; thence East along the
North line of said Lot 9 a distance of 12.50 feet; thence South along a line
parallel to the West line of aforesaid Lots 9 and 10 a distance of 10.0 feet;
thence Southwesterly to a point on the aforesaid West line of said Lot 10,
being 40.0 feet South of the aforesaid Northwest corner of Lot 9; thence North
along said West line of Lots 9 and 10 a distance of 40.0 feet to the place of
beginning, in the Village of Winnetka, Cook County, Illinois, said real estate
(hereinafter referred to as the "Leased Premises") being indicated by the
shaded area on the Plat of Leasehold attached hereto as Exhibit 1.
   2.   The initial term of this lease (the “Initial Term”) shall be for ten
years, commencing on the 1st day of August, 1998, and ending on the last day of
July, 2008. The Initial Term shall be followed by a 10-year extension (the
"Extended Term"), that shall commence on the 1st day of August, 2008, and end
on the last day of July, 2018.
   3.   Lessee agrees to pay a rental fee of Ten Thousand Dollars ($10,000.00)
for the Lease Term, payable in annual installments of One Thousand Dollars
($1,000.00) in advance on the first day of each lease year. The rental fee for
the Extended Term shall be as follows:
 
Payable Prior To: Amount Due Payable Prior To Amount Due
8/1/2008          $1,600     8/1/2013         $2,000
8/1/2009          $1,600     8/1/2014         $2,000
8/1/2010          $1,600     8/1/2015         $2,000
8/1/2011          $1,600     8/1/2016         $2,000
8/1/2012          $1,600     8/1/2017         $2,000
   4.   Lessee shall have the right to remove existing curbs and pavement on
the leased premises as necessary and to construct new curbs and pavement as
appropriate, at Lessee’s expense, subject to prior approval of plans or
specifications therefor by the Director of Public Works of the Village. No
building shall be erected upon or extended upon the leased premises.
   5.   Use of the premises by Lessee shall be limited to the sole purpose of
providing driveway access to and from Lessee’s drive-in banking facilities.
Lessee shall not prohibit or restrict the passage of pedestrians over the
leased premises, except at the direction or request of the Lessor.
   6.   Lessee will erect or provide, at its expense, such pedestrian and
vehicular traffic signs, consistent with reasonable driveway use, as may from
time to time be requested by the Director of Public Works.
   7.   Lessee’s rights under this Amended Lease shall at all times be subject
to an easement for any underground municipal or public utilities which the
Lessor determines to be necessary or desirable.
   8.   Lessee hereby agrees to indemnify and hold Lessor harmless, to the
fullest extent permitted by law, from any and all losses, claims, demands,
suits or actions by any persons, including the agents and servants of Lessee,
arising from or in connection with the conduct, condition, or management of the
Leased Premises, arising from any work or thing done in or about the Leased
Premises by Lessee or its agents or servants, or arising from any act or
negligence of Lessee or its agents, servants, patrons or customers, at any time
during the Lease Term and the Extended Term. The obligation to indemnify the
Lessor shall extend to attorneys fees incurred by Lessor in defending against
any of such losses, claims, demands, suits or actions.
   9.   If Lessee defaults in the performance of any of its obligations under
this Amended Lease, if Lessee otherwise breaches this Amended Lease agreement,
or if Lessee abandons or vacates the Leased Premises at any time during the
Lease Term or the Extended Term, and if the default, breach, abandonment or
vacation continues for thirty (30) days after written notice from Lessor to
Lessee specifying the default, breach, abandonment or vacation, then Lessor
may, at its option, terminate this Amended Lease and the Lease Term and
Extended Term hereby created, in which case Lessor may forthwith repossess the
Leased Premises.
   10.   On expiration of this Amended Lease, or upon its termination as
provided in paragraph 9, Lessee shall, on demand by Lessor, restore the Leased
Premises to the condition thereof existing at the commencement of the Lease
Term.
   11.    Neither the making of this Amended Lease, nor Lessor's performance
under its provisions, shall be construed as a waiver or forfeiture of any right
Lessor may have to condemn the Lessee’s interest in the Leased Premises, and
Lessor hereby specifically reserves its right to exercise any condemnation or
eminent domain powers it now has or may hereafter obtain under applicable
Illinois law.
   12.   Lessee shall not assign this Amended Lease or sublet the Leased
Premises or any part thereof; provided that this Amended Lease may be assigned
to any parent, subsidiary, corporate affiliate or corporate successor of the
Lessee.
   IN WITNESS WHEREOF, the Village of Winnetka and the Harris Bank Winnetka
have caused these present to be executed and attested by their duly authorized
officers and their seals to be thereunto affixed on the day and year first
above written.
