ORDINANCE NO. M-10-2008
AN ORDINANCE GRANTING A VARIATION IN THE APPLICATION OF THE ZONING ORDINANCE OF
THE VILLAGE OF WINNETKA, COOK COUNTY, ILLINOIS (455 Sheridan)
WHEREAS, the Village of Winnetka is a home rule municipality in accordance with
Article VII, Section 6 of the Constitution of the State of Illinois of 1970,
pursuant to which it has the authority, except as limited by said Section 6 of
Article VII, to exercise any power and perform any function pertaining to the
government and affairs of the Village; and
WHEREAS, the Council of the Village of Winnetka (“Village Council”) find that
establishing standards for the use and development of lands and buildings
within the Village and establishing and applying criteria for variations from
those standards are matters pertaining to the affairs of the Village; and
WHEREAS, the property commonly known as 455 Sheridan Road, Winnetka, Illinois
(the “Subject Property”), is legally described as follows:
Lot 5 in Winnetka Beach Estates, a Subdivision of that part of Block 42 in
Charles E. Peck’s Subdivision of the Northeast Quarter of Section 20, and the
North Half of Fractional Section 21, Township 42 North, Range 13, East of the
Third Principal Meridian, lying North of the Northerly line of that part of
non-vacated Cherry Street, and South of the Northerly line of the South 10 feet
of Oak Street, and Easterly of the East line of Sheridan Road, all in Cook
County, Illinois,
WHEREAS, the Subject Property is located in the R-2 Zoning District provided in
Chapter 17.24 of the Winnetka Zoning Ordinance, Title 17 of the Winnetka
Village Code; and
WHEREAS, on March 3, 2008, the owners of the Subject Property filed an
application for a variation from the front yard setback requirements of Section
17.30.050 of the Winnetka Zoning Ordinance, to allow a front yard setback of
10.21 feet, whereas a minimum of 50 feet is required, resulting in a variation
of 38.79 feet (79.58%); and
WHEREAS, on March 10, 2008, on due notice thereof, the Zoning Board of Appeals
conducted a public hearing on the requested variation and recommended against
granting the variation by a vote of six to one; and
WHEREAS, at its April 15th Council Meeting, the Village Council discussed the
zoning variation application, and made the decision to uphold the
recommendation of the Zoning Board of Appeals; and
WHEREAS, at the April 15th Council Meeting, the applicants formally withdrew
their application for a front yard setback variation; and
WHEREAS, on April 30, 2008, the owners of the Subject Property filed an amended
application for the following variations from requirements of the Lot, Space,
Bulk and Yard Regulations for Single Family Residential Districts established
by Chapter 17.30 of the Zoning Ordinance: (a) a variation from the front yard
setback requirements of Section 17.30.050, to permit a front yard setback of
26.19 feet, whereas a minimum of 50 feet is required, resulting in a variation
of 23.81 feet (47.62%); (b) a variation from the garage provisions of Section
17.30.110 to allow a front-facing garage that is 38 feet wide, whereas the
maximum allowed is 22 feet, resulting in a variation of 16 feet (72.7%); and
(c) a variation from the garage restrictions of Section 17.30.110 to allow
three garage doors totaling 26.82 feet in width, whereas a maximum of two 9-
foot wide doors totaling 18 feet in width are permitted, resulting in a
variation of 8.82 feet (49%); and
WHEREAS, the variations are being requested to allow the construction of a new
single-family residence and attached three-car garage; and
WHEREAS, on May 12, 2008, on due notice thereof, the Zoning Board of Appeals
conducted a public hearing on the requested variations and, by the unanimous
vote of the 4 members then present, has reported to the Council recommending
that the requested variations be granted; and
WHEREAS, there are practical difficulties and particular hardships associated
with carrying out the strict application of the Zoning Ordinance with respect
to the Subject Property in that: (a) the Subject Property is an irregularly
shaped flag lot located on the east side of Sheridan Road, adjacent to Lake
Michigan; (b) because of its location adjacent to Lake Michigan, the Subject
Property is considered a through lot pursuant to Section 17.04.030 (T)(4) of
the Zoning Ordinance and, as such, is subject to two front yard setbacks; (c)
due to the location and configuration of the Subject Property, the Zoning
Administrator has designated the west property line of the “flag” portion of
the Subject Property as the front lot line, in accordance with Section
17.30.050 (C)(6) of the Zoning Ordinance; (d) building a new home in conformity
with the required 50-foot setback would necessitate pushing the home farther
east on the bluff, which would require removing three significant trees from
the east front yard; (e) the Winnetka Comprehensive Plan, Winnetka 2020
recommends against building homes too close to the lake bluff in order to
preserve its stability; (f) because the southern lot line juts north 15 degrees
at the 84.83-foot mark, strict observance of the front yard setback would
result in the construction of a home that would be wider at the western portion
of the Subject Property and that would be longer at the east, which would
interfere with neighboring properties’ views of the lake; and (g) it is not
reasonably practicable to construct a detached garage behind the proposed house
on the east side of the Subject Property without jeopardizing the stability of
the bluff, existing trees, and sightlines to the lake; and
WHEREAS, the Subject Property cannot yield a reasonable return if permitted to
be used only under the conditions allowed by the Zoning Ordinance in that: (a)
a three-car garage is a standard amenity in the immediate vicinity, given the
size of the lot and of the proposed new home; (b) a strict application of the
Zoning Ordinance would result in diminished use and enjoyment of the east front
yard; and (c) construction of buildings farther into the east portion of the
Subject Property can jeopardize the stability of the bluff, existing trees and
sightlines to the lake; and
WHEREAS, the requested variations will not alter the essential character of the
neighborhood because the proposed front-facing garage will not be visible from
the street, the house is designed to reduce the appearance of the front-facing
garage doors as viewed from the property immediately to the west, and the front
setback of house will be more in line with existing setbacks on homes on nearby
properties that are also located on the bluffs adjacent to the lake; and
WHEREAS, the requested variations will not impair an adequate supply of light
and air because there are no neighboring structures adjacent to the proposed
new construction, and the requested variations will actually preserve the
current light and air of neighboring properties; and
WHEREAS, the requested variations will not increase the hazard from fire and
other dangers to the Subject Property, as the proposed construction will comply
with all applicable building and fire protection codes; and
WHEREAS, the requested variations will not diminish the taxable value of land
and buildings throughout the Village, and the taxable value of the Subject
Property may be increased because of the proposed improvements; and
WHEREAS, the proposed construction will not contribute to congestion on the
public streets, as the property will continue to be used for single family
residential purposes; and
WHEREAS, there is no evidence that the requested variations will otherwise
impair the public health, safety, comfort, morals, and welfare of the
inhabitants of the Village; and
WHEREAS, the requested variations are in harmony with the general purpose and
intent of the Winnetka Zoning Ordinance, in that they allow the construction of
a new home that maintains the existing scale and appearance of the community,
preserves the stability of the bluffs and protects established trees and
landscaping.
NOW, THEREFORE, the Council of the Village of Winnetka do ordain as follows:
SECTION 1:  The foregoing recitals are hereby incorporated as the findings of
the Council of the Village of Winnetka, as if fully set forth herein.
SECTION 2: The following variations from the Lot, Space, Bulk and Yard
Regulations for Single Family Residential Districts established by Section
17.30 of the Winnetka Zoning Ordinance are hereby granted to the Subject
Property, commonly known as 455 Sheridan Road and located in the R-2 Single-
Family Residential District provided in Chapter 17.24 of the Winnetka Zoning
Ordinance, Title 17 of the Winnetka Village Code: (a) a variation from the
front yard setback requirements of Section 17.30.050, to permit a front yard
setback of 26.19 feet, whereas a minimum of 50 feet is required, resulting in a
variation of 23.81 feet (47.62%); (b) a variation from the garage regulations
of Section 17.30.110 to allow a front-facing garage that is 38 feet wide,
whereas the maximum allowed is 22 feet, resulting in a variation of 16 feet
(72.7%); and (c) a variation from the garage regulations in Section 17.30.110
to allow three front-facing garage doors totaling 26.82 feet in width, whereas
a maximum of two 9-foot wide doors with a total width of no more than 18 feet
is permitted, resulting in a variation of 8.82 feet (49%), all to allow the
construction of a new single-family residence and attached three-car garage, in
accordance with the plans and elevations submitted with the application for
variations.
SECTION 3: This Ordinance is passed by the Council of the Village of Winnetka
in the exercise of its home rule powers pursuant to Section 6 of Article VII of
the Illinois Constitution of 1970.
SECTION 4: This Ordinance shall take effect immediately upon its passage,
approval and posting as provided by law.
