ORDINANCE NO. M-11-2008
AN ORDINANCE GRANTING A VARIATION IN THE APPLICATION OF THE ZONING ORDINANCE OF
THE VILLAGE OF WINNETKA, COOK COUNTY, ILLINOIS (635 Hill)
WHEREAS, the Village of Winnetka is a home rule municipality in accordance with
Article VII, Section 6 of the Constitution of the State of Illinois of 1970,
pursuant to which it has the authority, except as limited by said Section 6 of
Article VII, to exercise any power and perform any function pertaining to the
government and affairs of the Village; and
WHEREAS, the Council of the Village of Winnetka (“Village Council”) find that
establishing standards for the use and development of lands and buildings
within the Village and establishing and applying criteria for variations from
those standards are matters pertaining to the affairs of the Village; and
WHEREAS, the property commonly known as 635 Hill Road, Winnetka, Illinois (the
“Subject Property”), is legally described as follows:
Lot 10 in Odman’s Subdivision of Lots 5, 6 and 7 in Block 3 in Garland’s
Addition to Winnetka, being a Subdivision of the North 120 acres of the
Southwest ¼ of Section 21, Township 42 North, Range 13, East of the Third
Principal Meridian, in Cook County, Illinois; and
WHEREAS, the Subject Property is located in the R-4 Zoning District provided in
Chapter 17.16 of the Winnetka Zoning Ordinance, Title 17 of the Winnetka
Village Code; and
WHEREAS, on May 7, 2008, the owner of the Subject Property filed an application
for a variation from the garage setback requirements of Section 17.30.110 of
Chapter 17.30 of the Zoning Ordinance, to permit a proposed addition to a
detached garage to observe an east side yard setback of 2.13 feet, whereas a
minimum of 8 feet is required, resulting in a variation of 5.87 feet (73.37%);
and;
WHEREAS, on June 9, 2008, on due notice thereof, the Zoning Board of Appeals
conducted a public hearing on the requested variations and, by the favorable
vote of 4 of the 5 members then present, has reported to the Council
recommending that the requested variations be granted; and
WHEREAS, there are practical difficulties associated with carrying out the
strict application of the Zoning Ordinance with respect to the Subject Property
in that: (a) the Subject Property is nearly three times as long as it is wide,
having a lot width of 80 feet and a lot depth of 231.34 feet; (b) the existing
two-car garage is not located in the rear quarter of the lot and has a legally
nonconforming east side setback of .98 feet; (c) the existing two-car garage is
located adjacent to the rear yard of the property immediately to the east; (d)
the proposed expansion of the garage will extend the length of the garage
deeper into the lot, into an area that adjoins the rear yards of the other two
properties that lie immediately to the east of the Subject Property; (e) the
three properties immediately to the east of the Subject Property all have
garages or accessory structures in close proximity to their rear lot lines; (f)
the proposed addition will replace a storage shed that is currently located
behind the garage; (g) although the proposed addition will extend the length of
the garage, the addition will be located behind the garage of one of the three
adjacent properties; and (h) constructing a larger garage in a conforming
location would require the removal of the existing garage and shifting the
construction further to the center of the Subject Property, although the
garages and accessory structures in the adjacent rear yards to the east do not
observe full side yards; and
WHEREAS, the Subject Property cannot yield a reasonable return if permitted to
be used only under the conditions allowed by the Zoning Ordinance, in that: (a)
constructing the addition in a conforming location would result in an
approximately 6-foot offset in the alignment of the side walls of the expanded
garage and would push the garage farther toward the center of the Subject
Property, which would reduce access to the open space at the rear of the
Subject Property and would affect the garage’s functional relationship to the
house; and
WHEREAS, the requested variation will not alter the essential character of the
neighborhood because the proposed garage addition will not affect the adjoining
properties, as it will be constructed at the rear of the existing garage, so
that: (a) the view of the garage, as seen from the property immediately to the
north, will not be substantially altered; (b) the view of the garage addition
from the three properties immediately to the east will be obscured by the
garages and accessory buildings located on those properties; and (c) the
addition will not be visible from Hill Street; and
WHEREAS, the requested variation will not impair an adequate supply of light
and air because the garage is one-story high and it will be located in close
proximity to the garages and accessory structures located in the adjoining rear
yards of the three properties immediately to the east of the Subject Property;
and
WHEREAS, the requested variation will not increase the hazard from fire and
other dangers to the Subject Property, as the proposed construction will comply
with all applicable building and fire protection codes; and
WHEREAS, there is no evidence that the requested variation will diminish the
taxable value of land and buildings throughout the Village, and the taxable
value of the Subject Property may be increased because of the proposed
improvement; and
WHEREAS, the proposed garage addition will not contribute to congestion on the
public streets, as it will increase the amount of enclosed, off-street parking
on the Subject Property; and
WHEREAS, there is no evidence that the requested variation will otherwise
impair the public health, safety, comfort, morals, and welfare of the
inhabitants of the Village; and
WHEREAS, the requested variation is in harmony with the general purpose and
intent of the Winnetka Zoning Ordinance, in that it will allow the expansion of
a structurally sound, existing accessory building while maintaining the
existing scale and appearance of the community and protecting established trees
and landscaping.
NOW, THEREFORE, the Council of the Village of Winnetka do ordain as follows:
SECTION 1:  The foregoing recitals are hereby incorporated as the findings of
the Council of the Village of Winnetka, as if fully set forth herein.
SECTION 2: The Subject Property, commonly known as 635 Hill Road, is hereby
granted a variation from the garage setback requirements of Section 17.30.110
of Chapter 17.30 of the Zoning Ordinance, to permit a proposed addition to a
detached garage to observe an east side yard setback of 2.13 feet, whereas a
minimum of 8 feet is required, resulting in a variation of 5.87 feet (73.37%),
said addition to be in accordance with the plans and elevations submitted with
the application for variation.
SECTION 3: This Ordinance is passed by the Council of the Village of Winnetka
in the exercise of its home rule powers pursuant to Section 6 of Article VII of
the Illinois Constitution of 1970.
SECTION 4: This Ordinance shall take effect immediately upon its passage,
approval and posting as provided by law.
PASSED this 5th day of August, 2008, pursuant to the following roll call vote:
AYES: Trustees Berger, Greable, Johnson, Poor and Rintz
NAYS: Trustee Behles
ABSENT: None
APPROVED this 5th day of August, 2008.
