ORDINANCE NO. M-8-2009
AN ORDINANCE DESIGNATING A LANDMARK PURSUANT TO CHAPTER 15.64 OF THE WINNETKA
VILLAGE CODE (507 Cedar Street)
 
   WHEREAS, the Village of Winnetka is a home rule municipality in accordance
with Article VII, Section 6 of the Constitution of the State of Illinois of
1970, pursuant to which it has the authority, except as limited by said Section
6 of Article VII, to exercise any power and perform any function pertaining to
the government and affairs of the Village; and
   WHEREAS, the Council of the Village of Winnetka (“Village Council”) find
that the identification, designation and preservation of buildings and
structures in the Village that are historically, culturally, and
architecturally significant, and the encouragement of the restoration and
rehabilitation of those buildings and structures are matters pertaining to the
affairs of the Village; and
   WHEREAS, the property commonly known as 507 Cedar Street, Winnetka,
Illinois, (“Subject Property”) is legally described as follows:
      Lot 1 in Schweibert’s Subdivision of the South 140 feet of the West 120
feet of Block 22 in Winnetka Subdivision of the North West ¼ of Section 21,
Township 42 North, Range 13, East of the Third Principal Meridian, in Cook
County, Illinois; and
   WHEREAS, the owner of the Subject Property has submitted an application
seeking designation of the Subject Property as a certified Village of Winnetka
landmark; and
   WHEREAS, the Council of the Village of Winnetka has enacted Chapter 15.64 of
Title 15 of the Winnetka Village Code, titled “Landmark Preservation,” for the
purposes of preserving, protecting, enhancing, rehabilitating and regulating
buildings, structures, objects, and places of historical, cultural or
architectural importance; and
   WHEREAS, pursuant to the provisions of Chapter 15.64 of the Winnetka Village
Code (the “Landmark Ordinance”) and notice duly published and sent, the
Landmark Preservation Commission conducted a public hearing on January 5, 2009,
to consider the application for certified landmark designation and unanimously
recommended that the residence on the Subject Property be designated a Winnetka
landmark; and
   WHEREAS, the Landmark Preservation Commission applied the Village’s System
for the Evaluation of Landmarks to the information received at the hearing and
gave the home, known as the Jane M. Tittle House, an overall score of 80.7 with
a rating of “Unique;” and
   WHEREAS, architectural type, style and period of the Jane M. Tittle House is
between “rare” and “extremely rare,” in that the house was constructed in 1909
in the Prairie School style, using a method of construction the Commission
found to be “rare;” and
   WHEREAS, the home is located on the Village Green, which the Commission
found created a significant association with historical cultural activities and
they further found the home to be an established or familiar visual feature;
and
   WHEREAS, the Commission found the home to have excellent design integrity
and to be in exceptional condition; and
   WHEREAS, pursuant to the findings entered at the January 5, 2009, meeting of
the Landmark Preservation Commission, the members then present concluded that
the residence located at 507 Cedar Street is unique and meets the criteria of
the Landmark Ordinance, and unanimously voted to recommend that it be
designated a Winnetka landmark; and
   WHEREAS, the Council of the Village of Winnetka have considered the
recommendation of the Landmark Preservation Commission and have determined that
it is in the best interest of the Village and its residents to accept the
findings and recommendation of the Commission and to establish the James M.
Tittle House located at 507 Cedar Street, as a designated landmark, because of
its significant style and design, its excellent structural condition and its
prominent location on the Village Green.
   NOW, THEREFORE, the Council of the Village of Winnetka do ordain as follows:
   SECTION 1 :   The foregoing recitals are hereby incorporated as the findings
of the Council of the Village of Winnetka, as if fully set forth herein.
   SECTION 2:   The residence located on the property at 507 Cedar Street,
permanent real estate index number 05-21-111-014-0000, is hereby designated a
certified landmark under Section 15.64.070 the Landmark Preservation Ordinance,
in accordance with the findings and recommendations of the Landmark
Preservation Commission.
   SECTION 3:   This Ordinance is passed by the Council of the Village of
Winnetka in the exercise of its home rule powers pursuant to Section 6 of
Article VII of the Illinois Constitution of 1970.
   SECTION 4:   This Ordinance shall take effect immediately upon its passage,
approval and posting as provided by law.
