ORDINANCE NO. M-10-2009
AN ORDINANCE GRANTING A SPECIAL USE PERMIT FOR THE CONSTRUCTION OF A SERVICE
CENTER FOR THE WINNETKA PARK DISTRICT (1390 Willow)
WHEREAS, the Village of Winnetka (“Village”) is a home rule municipality in
accordance with Article VII, Section 6 of the Constitution of the State of
Illinois of 1970, pursuant to which it has the authority, except as limited by
said Section 6 of Article VII, to exercise any power and perform any function
pertaining to the government and affairs of the Village; and
WHEREAS, the Council of the Village of Winnetka (“Village Council”) find that
establishing and applying standards for the use and development of lands and
buildings within the Village are matters pertaining to the affairs of the
Village; and
WHEREAS, the Village of Winnetka is the owner of the following described real
estate (the “Subject Property”), which is commonly known as 1390 Willow Road,
Winnetka, Illinois:
The Northeast ¼ of the Southeast ¼ (except the East 10.0 Acres thereof) of
Section 19, Township 42 North, Range 13 East of the Third Principal Meridian in
the Village of Winnetka, Cook County, Illinois; and
WHEREAS, the Subject Property is located in the R-2 Single-Family Residential
District provided in Chapter 17.24 of the Winnetka Zoning Ordinance, Title 17
of the Winnetka Village Code; and
WHEREAS, the Subject Property, which has a total area of 1,263,574 square feet,
is the location of the former Village landfill, which was closed in 1994; and
WHEREAS, the Subject Property is located along the south side of Willow Road,
opposite the Skokie Playfield and is bordered on the east, south and west by
open space owned by the Cook County forest Preserve District; and
WHEREAS, on August 21, 2001, the Council of the Village of Winnetka (“Village
Council”) passed Ordinance M-18-2001, granting a special use permit under
Sections 17.56.010 and 17.24.010(B)(3) of the Zoning Ordinance to amend earlier
special use permits to allow the renovation and expansion of the Public Works
and Water & Electric maintenance facilities and related parking on the Subject
Property; and
WHEREAS, the Subject Property is now the site of the Village’s Public Works and
Water & Electric Departments, and is improved with (i) buildings that house
department offices and maintenance facilities, as well as parking and service
bays for heavy vehicles and equipment; (ii) visitor and employee parking areas;
(iii) a dome for the storage of road salt; (iv) a firefighting training tower;
(v) municipal and emergency communications facilities; and (vi) the Village’s
yard waste transfer station; and
WHEREAS, the maintenance facility for the Water & Electric Department, the
firefighting training tower and the communications facilities on the Subject
Property are essential public uses, as defined in Section 17.04.030(E) of the
Zoning Ordinance, which are permitted uses in the R-2 Zoning District pursuant
to Section 17.24.020(D) of the Zoning Ordinance; and
WHEREAS, the remaining uses of the Subject Property are non-essential public
uses, as defined in Section 17.04.030(N) of the Zoning Ordinance, which are
allowed as special uses, pursuant to Ordinance M-18-2001 and Section 17.56.010
(B) of the Zoning Ordinance; and
WHEREAS, the existing buildings and facilities on the Subject Property are
located primarily in the northwest portion of the Subject Property; and
WHEREAS, the Winnetka Park District is a body corporate and politic of the
State of Illinois and operates a parks maintenance facility located at Pine
Street west of Hibbard Road; and
WHEREAS, the Winnetka Park District (“Applicant”) has filed an application to
amend the existing special use permit pursuant to Section 17.56.010(I) of the
Winnetka Zoning Ordinance, to allow the construction of a parks maintenance
facility in the southwest area of the Subject Property, on the lower plateau of
the former landfill, south of the existing asphalt access road behind the
Winnetka Public Works facility; and
WHEREAS, the Village Council finds that park facilities are non-essential
public uses, as defined in Section 17.04.030(N) of the Zoning Ordinance, and
are therefore permitted as special uses in the R-2 Single-Family Residential
District, pursuant to Section 17.56.010(B) of the Zoning Ordinance; and
WHEREAS, the proposed building would measure 40 feet by 220 feet with a seven-
foot canopy overhang along the east elevation and a portion of the south
elevation at the entrance of the building; and
WHEREAS, the building would contain offices, a conference room, locker rooms,
vehicle maintenance bays, general work bays and associated storage areas, and
would also have outdoor bulk storage bins, a dumpster area, and parking for the
offices; and
WHEREAS, the proposed new construction complies with all zoning bulk, lot
coverage and setback requirements; and
WHEREAS, the Director of Public Works has reviewed the traffic impact study
prepared by the Applicant’s traffic engineers and concurs with the conclusions
that (i) the relocation of the parks maintenance facilities will have minimal
effects on traffic in the area; (ii) no roadway operational changes are
necessary; (iii) the additional access locations and traffic volumes are
compatible with the existing patterns and volumes; and (iv) traffic operations
will remain essentially unchanged; and
WHEREAS, on February 10, 2009, pursuant to due notice thereof, the Zoning Board
of Appeals conducted a public hearing on the requested special use and, by the
unanimous vote of the six members of the Board then present, has reported to
the Council, recommending that the requested special use be granted; and
WHEREAS, on February 19, 2009, on due notice thereof, the Design Review Board
considered the proposed building plans and issued favorable comment on the
project; and
WHEREAS, on January 28, 2009, pursuant to due notice thereof, the Plan
Commission considered the special use application and by the unanimous vote of
the nine members then present, found that the proposed special use is
consistent with the Comprehensive Plan, Winnetka 2020, subject to the
conditions that the Park District: (i) will ensure that exterior site lighting
and interior building lighting are utilized in a manner that assures the
facility is unobtrusive and well hidden; (ii) will confer with Village Staff to
assure that runoff and detention requirements are met; and (iii) will inform
the Cook County Forest Preserve District of the construction plans, in light of
the Forest Preserve’s close proximity to the construction site; and
WHEREAS, the proposed special use is consistent with the Comprehensive Plan’s
goal to preserve or expand the quantity, quality and distribution of open space
and recreational opportunities, and to protect the Village’s natural features
and environmental resources in that it will locate the Park District
maintenance facilities in an unobtrusive location on open space that is not
suitable for recreational use or other general uses by the public; and
WHEREAS, the proposed special use is consistent with the Comprehensive Plan’s
objective to ensure that commercial, institutional and residential development
is appropriate to the character of, and minimizes the adverse impact on, its
surrounding neighborhood, in that the area on which the new facility will be
built is part of a larger parcel occupied by similar facilities owned and
operated by the Village and is not visible from single family residences in the
vicinity of the Subject Property; and
WHEREAS, the proposed special use is consistent with the Comprehensive Plan’s
objective to encourage organizations, schools, religious institutions,
businesses, and citizens in their efforts to beautify the Village, in that,
when the facility is built, it will be located, designed and landscaped so as
to be compatible with the Village’s facilities and to maintain the natural
landscape of the Subject Property; and
WHEREAS, the proposed special use is consistent with the Comprehensive Plan’s
objective to use high quality design and materials when constructing public
improvements; and
WHEREAS, the proposed special use is consistent with the Comprehensive Plan’s
goals and objectives (i) to preserve or expand the quantity, quality and
distribution of open space and recreational opportunities; (ii) to protect the
Village’s natural features and environmental resources; (iii) to support the
development of recreational facilities to meet the needs of residents of all
ages; and (iv) to encourage the preservation of open space inside and outside
the Village, in that the special use will allow the Park District to expand and
improve service facilities necessary to its operations while freeing up usable
parks space by avoiding the need either to expand the existing facility at Pine
Street or to locate a new facility on usable park space; and
WHEREAS, the proposed special use is consistent with the Comprehensive Plan’s
objective to engage in a public process that balances institutional goals and
minimizes any adverse impact to the character of the adjacent residential
neighborhood; and
WHEREAS, the proposed special use is consistent with the objective to foster
greater cooperation among all governmental institutions, in that its location
on the Subject Property is the result of intergovernmental cooperation between
the Village and the Park District; and
WHEREAS, the proposed Service Center facility is necessary to the operation of
the Winnetka Park District and the provision of services to Winnetka residents
in that the new facility will improve the effectiveness of the Park District
maintenance operations, which maintains the parks in the Village of Winnetka;
and
WHEREAS, the proposed Service Center facility will benefit the public health,
safety, comfort, morals and general welfare of the Village, in that the design
and construction of the Service Center will be completed according to all
applicable building codes, and will allow much of the Park District’s staff,
vehicles and equipment to be relocated from the existing Service Center in the
northeast corner of the Skokie Playfield, improving the effectiveness of Park
District maintenance operations and freeing space for recreational use, all
without interfering with the Village’s operations on the Subject Property; and
WHEREAS, the proposed Service Center facility will not be substantially
injurious to the use and enjoyment of other property in the immediate vicinity,
will not substantially diminish or impair property values in the immediate
vicinity, and will not impede the normal and orderly development or improvement
of other property in the immediate vicinity for uses permitted under applicable
zoning regulations because: (i) the Subject Property is not adjacent to any
single family residences, being opposite the Skokie Playfields, part of the
Winnetka Park District Golf Course and the Madsen Water Reservoir, and
immediately west of property owned by the Forest Preserve District of Cook
County; and (ii) the new Park District service center will be located on the
same site as the Village Public Works Yards, which is a comparable operation
that is an established presence in the neighborhood; and
WHEREAS, when constructed in accordance with the conditions imposed by this
ordinance, the existing parking, utilities, access roads, drainage and other
facilities necessary to the uses on the Subject Property will be enhanced; and
WHEREAS, the proposed Service Center facility will not alter the amount of
parking on, or the ingress or egress to, the Subject Property, nor will it have
a negative impact on vehicular or pedestrian traffic on the surrounding street
system, as access to the site will be from an existing driveway on Willow Road;
and
WHEREAS, adequate parking, utilities, access roads, drainage and other
facilities necessary to the existing special use already exist on the Subject
Property; and
WHEREAS, when constructed pursuant to the terms and conditions set forth in
this ordinance, the special use in all other respects conforms to the
applicable regulations of this and other Village ordinances and codes.
NOW, THEREFORE, the Council of the Village of Winnetka do ordain as follows:
SECTION 1:   The foregoing recitals are hereby incorporated as the findings of
the Council of the Village of Winnetka, as if fully set forth herein.
SECTION 2:   Pursuant to Sections 17.56.010 of the Winnetka Zoning Ordinance,
Title 17 of the Winnetka Village Code, a special use permit is hereby granted
with respect to the Subject Property, which is located in the R-2 Single-Family
Residential Zoning District, provided in the Winnetka Zoning Ordinance, Title
17 of the Winnetka Village Code and is commonly known as 1390 Willow Road and
the Public Works Yards, to allow the construction of a Service Center for the
parks maintenance operations of the Winnetka Park District, subject to the
terms and conditions hereinafter set forth.
SECTION 3:   The special use permit hereby granted is subject to the following
conditions:
A.   The special use shall be as defined in the Park District’s application and
plans submitted with the original application.
B.   The Park District shall enter into a long term lease for the area to be
occupied by the Park District facilities.
C.   The precise location of the Park District facilities and lease area shall
be staked out in cooperation with the Village prior to the issuance of any
construction permits, and the legal description and a corresponding survey
shall be incorporated into the lease between the Park District and the Village.
D.   The Park District will ensure that exterior site lighting and interior
building lighting are utilized in a manner that assures the facility is
unobtrusive and well hidden.
E.   The Park District will confer with Village Staff to assure that runoff and
detention requirements are met.
F.   The Park District will inform the Cook County Forest Preserve District of
the construction plans, in light of the Forest Preserve’s close proximity to
the construction site.
G.   The proposed construction shall commence within 12 months after the
effective date of this ordinance.
SECTION 4:   Pursuant to Section 17.56.010(G) of the Zoning Ordinance, the
stipulations, conditions and restrictions set forth in this ordinance as part
of the terms under which the special use is granted, may be modified or revised
from time to time by the Village Council following public notice and hearing,
using the same procedures set forth in the Zoning ordinance for processing the
original special use application.
SECTION 5:   This Ordinance is passed by the Council of the Village of Winnetka
in the exercise of its home rule powers pursuant to Section 6 of Article VII of
the Illinois Constitution of 1970.
SECTION 6:   This Ordinance shall take effect immediately upon its passage,
approval and posting as provided by law.
PASSED this 5th day of May, 2009, pursuant to the following roll call vote: 
AYES:    Trustees Greable, Johnson, Pedian, Poor, Rintz, Spinney
NAYS:    None
ABSENT: None
APPROVED this 5th day of May, 2009.
