ORDINANCE NO. M-13-2009
AN ORDINANCE GRANTING A VARIATION IN THE APPLICATION OF THE ZONING ORDINANCE OF
THE VILLAGE OF WINNETKA, COOK COUNTY, ILLINOIS (594 Elm)
WHEREAS, the Village of Winnetka is a home rule municipality in accordance with
Article VII, Section 6 of the Constitution of the State of Illinois of 1970,
pursuant to which it has the authority, except as limited by said Section 6 of
Article VII, to exercise any power and perform any function pertaining to the
government and affairs of the Village; and
WHEREAS, the Council of the Village of Winnetka (“Village Council”) find that
establishing standards for the use and development of lands and buildings
within the Village and establishing and applying criteria for variations from
those standards are matters pertaining to the affairs of the Village; and
WHEREAS, the property commonly known as 594 Elm Street, Winnetka, Illinois (the
“Subject Property”), is legally described as follows:
All that part of Block 22, lying East of a line 120 feet West of the West line
of Walnut Street and lying South of the South line of Elm Street and North of
the North line of Oak Street (except the South 290.42 feet thereof) in the
Village of Winnetka, in Sections 20 and 21, Township 42 North, Range 13, East
of the Third Principal Meridian, in Cook County, Illinois; and
WHEREAS, the Subject Property is located in the R-4 Zoning District provided in
Chapter 17.16 of the Winnetka Zoning Ordinance, Title 17 of the Winnetka
Village Code; and
WHEREAS, the Subject Property is improved with a single family residence that
was constructed in 1872 and was the first local landmark designated by the
Village of Winnetka; and
WHEREAS, on April 8, 2009, the owner of the Subject Property filed an
application for a variation from the garage restrictions of Section 17.30.110,
Chapter 17.30 of the Zoning Ordinance, to allow a below-grade, front-facing
attached two-car garage addition on the east portion of the home facing Walnut
Street; and
WHEREAS, on April 6, 2009, on due notice thereof, the Landmark Preservation
Commission completed its review of the proposed alteration to the Subject
Property, and, by the unanimous vote of the Commission, concluded that the
proposed alteration is appropriate to the preservation of the designated
landmark; and
WHEREAS, on May 11, 2009, on due notice thereof, the Zoning Board of Appeals
conducted a public hearing on the requested variation and, by the favorable
vote of 6 of the 7 members then present, has reported to the Council
recommending that the requested variations be granted; and
WHEREAS, there are practical difficulties associated with carrying out the
strict application of the Zoning Ordinance with respect to the Subject Property
in that: (a) the Subject Property is improved with a single family residence
which was constructed in 1872, approximately 50 years before the enactment of
the Winnetka Zoning Ordinance; (b) the Subject Property is a square-shaped
corner parcel bounded by Elm Street on the north and Walnut Street on the east,
which requires the observation of two front yards under the Zoning Ordinance;
(c) although the residence is oriented to face Elm Street and has an Elm Street
address, the Walnut Street frontage is slightly narrower and is therefore
treated as the front yard under the Zoning Ordinance; (d) the existing one-car
garage faces Walnut Street; and (e) replacement of the deteriorating garage
with a new detached garage in a conforming location would require a longer
driveway, thus increasing impermeable surface, and would require removing
several mature trees, which would have a significant impact on the appearance
and character of the Subject Property and the immediate neighborhood; and
WHEREAS, the Subject Property cannot yield a reasonable return if permitted to
be used only under the conditions allowed by the Zoning Ordinance, in that: (a)
the existing one-car garage is substandard; (b) a two-car garage is a typical
amenity found in homes throughout the Village; and (c) the construction of a
conforming garage would result in the removal of several trees, increase
impermeable surface and alter the character of the Subject Property; and
WHEREAS, the requested variation will not alter the essential character of the
neighborhood because the proposed addition is below grade level, has been found
by the Landmark Preservation Commission to be architecturally compatible with
the landmark residence, and will maintain the existing orientation of the
Subject Property and its access from Walnut Street; and
WHEREAS, the requested variation will not impair an adequate supply of light
and air because the proposed garage is below-grade; and
WHEREAS, the requested variation will not increase the hazard from fire and
other dangers to the Subject Property, as the proposed construction will comply
with all applicable building and fire protection codes; and
WHEREAS, the requested variation will not diminish the taxable value of land
and buildings throughout the Village, and the taxable value of the Subject
Property may be increased because of the proposed improvement; and
WHEREAS, the proposed construction will not contribute to congestion on the
public streets, as: (a) the entrance to the new garage will be located on the
less-travelled of the two street frontages of the Subject Property, (b) the new
two-car garage will provide additional off-street parking; and (c) the property
will continue to be used for single family residential purposes; and
WHEREAS, there is no evidence that the requested variation will otherwise
impair the public health, safety, comfort, morals, and welfare of the
inhabitants of the Village; and
WHEREAS, the requested variation is in harmony with the general purpose and
intent of the Winnetka Zoning Ordinance, in that it allows the renovation,
restoration and rehabilitation of a structurally sound designated landmark
residence, while maintaining the existing scale and appearance of the community
and protecting established trees and landscaping.
NOW, THEREFORE, the Council of the Village of Winnetka do ordain as follows:
SECTION 1:   The foregoing recitals are hereby incorporated as the findings of
the Council of the Village of Winnetka, as if fully set forth herein.
SECTION 2:   The Subject Property, commonly known as 594 Elm Street, and
located in the R-4 Single-Family Residential District provided in Chapter 17.16
of the Winnetka Zoning Ordinance, Title 17 of the Winnetka Village Code, is
hereby granted a variation from the garage restrictions of Section 17.30.110,
Chapter 17.30 of the Zoning Ordinance, to allow a below-grade, front-facing
attached two-car garage addition on the east portion of the home facing Walnut
Street, in accordance with the plans and elevations submitted with the
application for variations.
SECTION 3:   This Ordinance is passed by the Council of the Village of Winnetka
in the exercise of its home rule powers pursuant to Section 6 of Article VII of
the Illinois Constitution of 1970.
SECTION 4:   This Ordinance shall take effect immediately upon its passage,
approval and posting as provided by law.
PASSED this 16th day of June, 2009, pursuant to the following roll call vote: 
AYES:    Trustees Greable, Johnson, Pedian, Poor, Rintz, Spinney
NAYS:    None
ABSENT: None
APPROVED this 16th day of June, 2009.
   Signed:
   s/Jessica B. Tucker
   Village President
Countersigned:
s/Douglas G. Williams
Village Clerk
