ORDINANCE NO. M-14-2009
AN ORDINANCE AUTHORIZING THE LEASE OF VILLAGE PROPERTY TO THE WINNETKA PARK
DISTRICT FOR THE CONSTRUCTION AND OPERATION OF A SERVICE CENTER
WHEREAS, the Village of Winnetka (“Village”) is a home rule municipality in
accordance with Article VII, Section 6 of the Constitution of the State of
Illinois of 1970 and, pursuant thereto, has the authority, except as limited by
said Section 6 of Article VII, to exercise any power and perform any function
pertaining to the government and affairs of the Village, including the power to
regulate for the protection of the public health, safety and welfare; and
WHEREAS,  Village is the sole owner of certain real property in Winnetka,
Illinois, commonly known as 1390 Willow Road, on which there is currently
located the Village’s Public Works Facility, Landfill and other Village service
facilities; and
WHEREAS, the Winnetka Park District (“Park District”) is a body corporate and
politic, organized pursuant to the laws of the State of Illinois; and
WHEREAS, Village and Park District are Illinois units of local government
authorized by the Constitution and statutes of the State of Illinois to enter
into intergovernmental agreements, and to enter into agreements to lease real
property as lessor or lessee; and
WHEREAS, the Park District desires to lease a portion of the Village’s landfill
property for the construction and operation of a new parks service center; and
WHEREAS, the Village and Park District have negotiated mutually agreeable terms
to allow for the construction of a proposed parks service center, the terms of
which are set forth in Exhibit A to this Ordinance, which is incorporated
herein by reference as if fully set forth; and
WHEREAS, the Village and Park District have each determined that the Village’s
lease of a portion of the landfill property to the Park District for the
construction of a new service center is in the best interests of the Village’s
residents and other persons served by the Park District; and
WHEREAS, the Council of the Village of Winnetka find and determine that the
leasing of its property to the Winnetka Park District is a matter of the
government and affairs of the Village.
NOW THEREFORE, the Council of the Village of Winnetka do ordain as follows:
SECTION 1:   The foregoing recitals are hereby incorporated into this section
as the findings of the Council of the Village of Winnetka, as if fully set
forth herein.
SECTION 2:   The Council of the Village of Winnetka hereby approve the lease
titled “Lease Agreement between the Village of Winnetka and the Winnetka Park
District,” for the Park District’s construction and operation of a new service
facility on a portion of the Village’s former landfill, said lease agreement to
be substantially in the form attached hereto as Exhibit A and incorporated
herein by reference (the “Lease Agreement”).
SECTION 3:   The Village President and Village Clerk are hereby authorized and
directed to execute the Lease Agreement on behalf of the Village.
SECTION 4:   This Ordinance is passed by the Council of the Village of Winnetka
in the exercise of its home rule powers pursuant to Section 6 of Article VII of
the Illinois Constitution of 1970.
SECTION 5:   This Ordinance shall take effect immediately upon its passage,
approval and posting as provided by law.
PASSED this 18 th day of August, 2009, pursuant to the following roll call
vote: 
