ORDINANCE NO. M-17-2009
AN ORDINANCE AUTHORIZING THE DISPOSITION OF CERTAIN PERSONAL PROPERTY OWNED BY
THE VILLAGE OF WINNETKA
WHEREAS, Article VII, Section 10 of the Constitution of the State of Illinois,
and the Intergovernmental Cooperation Act, 220 ILCS 220/1, et seq., authorize
and encourage intergovernmental cooperation; and
WHEREAS, the Northwest Municipal Conference, is a regional council of
government that represents Illinois municipalities and townships located in
Cook, DuPage, Kane, Lake and McHenry Counties, and organizes joint municipal
auctions for the sale of surplus vehicles and equipment; and
WHEREAS, the Northwest Municipal Conference has scheduled a joint municipal
auction for the sale of surplus vehicles and equipment at 10:00 a.m., Saturday,
September 26, 2009, at the Village of Winnetka Public Works Facility, 1390
Willow Road, Winnetka, Illinois; and
WHEREAS, the Village of Winnetka owns the following described items of personal
property (the “Personal Property”) and has established a minimum value for each
such item of personal property as hereinafter described:
 
