Exhibit A
NOTICE OF PUBLIC HEARING VILLAGE OF WINNETKA PROPOSED SPECIAL SERVICE AREA
NUMBER 3
Trapp Lane Improvements
NOTICE IS HEREBY GIVEN that on May 18, 2010, at 7:30 p.m. in the Winnetka
Village Hall, 510 Green Bay Road, Winnetka, Illinois, a public hearing will be
held by the Village of Winnetka (“Village”) to consider forming a special
service area (the “Winnetka Special Service Area No. 3”) consisting of the real
property known by the property index numbers and the approximate common street
addresses described below (hereinafter collectively referred to as the
“Territory”):
P.I.N.        STREET ADDRESS
05-18-402-073 1274 Trapp Lane
05-18-402-056 1279 Trapp Lane
05-18-402-072 1284 Trapp Lane
05-18-402-040 1294 Trapp Lane
05-18-402-054 1299 Trapp Lane
05-18-402-039 1304 Trapp Lane
05-18-402-053 1309 Trapp Lane
05-18-402-049 1314 Trapp Lane
05-18-402-052 1319 Trapp Lane
05-18-402-048 1324 Trapp Lane
05-18-402-051 1329 Trapp Lane
05-18-402-047 1334 Trapp Lane
05-18-402-050 1339 Trapp Lane
05-18-402-076 1345 Trapp Lane
05-18-402-046 1350 Trapp Lane
05-18-402-075 1360 Trapp Lane
05-18-402-074 1368 Trapp Lane
05-18-402-043 1370 Trapp Lane
05-18-402-042 1372 Trapp Lane
05-18-402-077 1385 Trapp Lane
 
Winnetka Special Service Area No. 3 is to be established to provide certain
public services (the “Services”) to the Territory that will supplement the
services currently or customarily provided by the Village to the Territory, in
particular the installation of a new storm sewer and all appurtenances thereto,
the reconstruction and repaving of Trapp Lane including the construction of a
new cul-de-sac, and the furnishing of all necessary labor and materials in
connection therewith, and any other similar types of amenities and improvements
that shall be compatible with the proposed improved plan for the Territory. The
proposed Winnetka Special Service Area No. 3 is intended to improve stormwater
drainage to the Territory and to upgrade Trapp Lane to Village standards so
that Trapp Lane, which is currently a private roadway, can be dedicated to the
Village as a public right-of-way. The Services proposed to be provided in
Winnetka Special Service Area No. 3 are unique and in addition to the general
municipal services provided to the Village as a whole and will be for the
common interests and specific benefit of the Territory.
At the hearing, consideration shall also be given to borrowing an amount not to
exceed $631,895.00 (125% of the engineer’s estimate of project costs), to be
evidenced by general obligation bonds (the “Bonds”). The proceeds of the Bonds
shall be used to pay part of the costs of the proposed Winnetka Special Service
Area No. 3. The Bonds are to be retired over a period not to exceed 10 years
and are to bear interest at a rate not to exceed 5.00% per annum or the maximum
rate permitted by law. The Bonds, if issued, shall be retired by the levy of a
direct tax on all taxable real property within the Territory for a maximum
period of 10 years, to discharge the principal as it matures and the interest
thereon, and said tax shall be in addition to all other taxes presently levied
by any taxing district within the Territory.
All interested persons affected by the formation of the Winnetka Special
Service Area No. 3, including, but not limited to, all persons owning taxable
real property located within the Territory, will be given an opportunity to be
heard regarding the formation and the boundaries of the proposed Winnetka
Special Service Area No. 3, and will be given an opportunity to file objections
to the formation of Winnetka Special Service Area No. 3, the issuance of bonds,
and the related levy of taxes affecting the Winnetka Special Service Area No.
3.
The public hearing may be adjourned by the Village to another date without
further notice other than a motion to be entered upon the minutes of its
meeting fixing the time and place of its adjournment.
If a petition signed by at least 51 % of the electors residing within the
Territory and by at least 51% of the owners of record of the land included
within the Territory is filed with the Village Clerk within 60 days following
the final adjournment of the public hearing objecting to the establishment of
the proposed Winnetka Special Service Area No. 3, the enlargement thereof, the
levy or imposition of a tax or the issuance of the Bonds for the provision of
the Services to the Area, or to a proposed increase in the tax rate, then the
proposed Winnetka Special Service Area No. 3 may not be created or enlarged,
nor the tax levied or imposed, nor the rate increased, and the Bonds may not be
issued.
Dated this 22nd day of April, 2010.
s/Douglas G. Williams
Douglas G. Williams, Village Clerk
Village of Winnetka, Cook County, Illinois
