Posted: July 8, 2010
ORDINANCE NO. M-13-2010
AN ORDINANCE ESTABLISHING WINNETKA SPECIAL SERVICE AREA NO. 3 IN THE VILLAGE OF
WINNETKA (Trapp Lane Improvements)
WHEREAS, the Village of Winnetka (“Village”) is a home rule municipality in
accordance with Article VII, Section 6 of the Constitution of the State of
Illinois of 1970; and
WHEREAS, the Village has the authority to adopt ordinances and to promulgate
rules and regulations that pertain to its government and affairs that protect
the public health, safety and welfare of its citizens; and
WHEREAS, it is in the public interest that the area described in Exhibit A and
depicted on the map in Exhibit B (the “Area”), which exhibits are attached to
and made a part of this Ordinance, be established as Winnetka Special Service
Area No. 3 for the purposes set forth herein; and
WHEREAS, the Area is a single family residential area consisting of the
properties lying along a private road known as Trapp Lane, which Area
constitutes a compact and contiguous residential territory; and
WHEREAS, the owners of the properties in the Area have requested that the
corporate authorities (the “Village Council”) give consideration to the
establishment of a special service area in order to provide for the
construction of a storm sewer, the reconstruction and repaving of Trapp Lane,
the construction of a cul-de-sac at the terminus of Trapp Lane and the
construction of related appurtenances to the Area (the “Services”); and
WHEREAS, the Services proposed to be provided to the proposed special service
area will supplement services currently or customarily provided by the Village
to the Area, in particular in connection with the street and storm drainage
infrastructure, in that the proposed special service area is intended to
improve stormwater drainage to the Area and to upgrade Trapp Lane to Village
standards so that Trapp Lane, which is currently a private roadway, can be
dedicated to the Village as a public right-of-way; and
WHEREAS, the Services proposed to be provided to the Area are unique and in
addition to the general municipal services provided to the Village as a whole
and will be for the common interests and specific benefit of the Area; and
WHEREAS, a special service area has been proposed so that bonds or other duly
authorized financing instrument may be issued to meet the costs of the Services
for the Area, said bonds or financing instrument to be payable from taxes
levied on all taxable property within the Area, in addition to all other
Village taxes so levied; and
WHEREAS, the bonds or other duly authorized financing instrument proposed to be
issued for the purpose of paying the cost of providing the Services (“Bonds”)
shall be in an amount not to exceed $631,895.00 (125% of the estimated cost of
the Services) and shall be secured by the full faith and credit of the Area;
and
WHEREAS, the Bonds are to mature over a period of not to exceed 10 years from
the issuance thereof and shall bear interest at a rate or rates not to exceed
five per cent (5%) per annum or the maximum rate then permitted by law; and
WHEREAS, the Bonds are to be retired by the levy of a direct annual tax,
sufficient to pay the interest and principal on the Bonds as the same come due,
upon all taxable property within the Area for a period of not to exceed 10
years, and the tax levied for the retirement of the Bonds shall be unlimited as
to the rate or amount in addition to all other taxes permitted by law; and
WHEREAS, the establishment of the proposed special service area was proposed by
the Village Council pursuant to Ordinance M-6-2010, titled: “An Ordinance
Proposing the Establishment of the Village of Winnetka Special Service Area No.
3 in the Village of Winnetka and Providing for a Public Hearing and Other
Procedures in Connection Therewith,” adopted on April 6, 2010, and re-adopted
on reconsideration on April 20, 2010, and was considered at a public hearing
(the “Hearing”) held by the Village Council on May 18, 2010; and
WHEREAS, the Hearing was held pursuant to notice duly published at least
fifteen (15) days prior to the Hearing in the Winnetka Talk, a newspaper
published in the Winnetka area and being in general circulation in the Village
of Winnetka, and pursuant to notice by mail; and
WHEREAS, mailed notice of the Hearing was given by depositing said notice in
the United States mails addressed to the person or persons in whose name the
general taxes for the last preceding year were paid on each lot, block, tract
or parcel of land lying within the Area, not less than ten (10) days prior to
the time set for the public hearing, and in the event taxes for the last
preceding year were not paid, said notice was sent to the person or persons
last listed on the tax rolls prior to that year as the owner or owners of said
property; and
WHEREAS, said notices conformed in all respects to the requirements of the
Special Service Area Tax Law, 35 ILCS 200/27-5, et seq.; and
WHEREAS, at the Hearing, all interested persons, including all persons owning
taxable property within the Area, were given an opportunity to be heard on the
question of the creation of the special service area, the levy or imposition of
a tax in the Area and the issuance of bonds providing for special services, as
set forth in the notice of the Hearing, a copy of which is attached hereto as
Exhibit C and made a part of this Ordinance; and
WHEREAS, no petition signed by at least 51 % of the electors residing within
the Area and by at least 51% of the owners of record of the land included
within the Area has been filed with the Village Clerk within 60 days following
the final adjournment of the Hearing objecting to the establishment of the
proposed special service area, the enlargement thereof, the levy or imposition
of a tax or the issuance of the Bonds for the provision of the Services to the
Area, or to a proposed increase in the tax rate; and
WHEREAS, it is in the public interest of the Village of Winnetka that Winnetka
Special Service Area No. 3 be established in the Area and that the Services to
be provided to the Area be paid for by the issuance of the Bonds and the
related levy of a special tax against all property located within the Area; and
WHEREAS, pursuant to Section 2.04.040(D) of the Winnetka Village Code, the
members of the Village Council present on July 20, 2010, have unanimously
determined, by motion, that cause has been established that introduction and
initial posting of this Ordinance, as provided in Sections 2.04.040(A) and (B)
of the Village Code, do not in this instance serve the best interests of the
Village and should therefore be waived; and
WHEREAS, the Village Council, having given consideration to the proposal, deem
it advisable to initiate proceedings under the applicable laws of the State of
Illinois in connection with such proposal; and
WHEREAS, Article VII, Section 6(i) of the Illinois Constitution provides, in
pertinent part, that “the General Assembly may not deny or limit the power of
home rule units . . . to levy or impose additional taxes upon areas within
their boundaries in the manner provided by law for the provision of special
services to those areas and for the payment of debt incurred in order to
provide those special services.”
NOW, THEREFORE, the Council of the Village of Winnetka do ordain as follows:
SECTION 1:   The facts and statements contained in the preamble to this
Ordinance are found to be true and correct and are hereby incorporated into
this Ordinance by reference as the findings of the Council of the Village of
Winnetka, as if fully set forth herein.
SECTION 2:   The public hearing on the proposed special service area was
adjourned on May 18, 2010.
SECTION 3:   No petition signed by at least 51 % of the electors residing
within the Area and by at least 51% of the owners of record of the land
included within the Area has been filed with the Village Clerk within 60 days
following the final adjournment of the public hearing objecting to the
establishment of the proposed Winnetka Special Service Area No. 3, the
enlargement thereof, the levy or imposition of a tax or the issuance of the
Bonds for the provision of the Services to the Area, or to a proposed increase
in the tax rate.
SECTION 4:   That after considering the data, as presented at the public
hearing, the Village Council find that it is in the public interest and in the
interest of the Area, that Village of Winnetka Special Service Area No. 3, as
hereinafter described, be established.
SECTION 5:   A special service area to be known and designated as “Village of
Winnetka Special Service Area No. 3” (“SSA No. 3”) is hereby established and
shall consist of the territory legally described in Exhibit A, a copy of which
is attached hereto and is made a part of this Ordinance.
SECTION 6:   The territory of SSA No. 3 consists of the properties abutting
Trapp Lane, from the west side of Hibbard Road westward to the west terminus of
Trapp Lane on the west, which properties are known by the following permanent
property index numbers (“PIN”) and the approximate common street locations
described below:
P.I.N.        STREET ADDRESS
05-18-402-073 1274 Trapp Lane
05-18-402-056 1279 Trapp Lane
05-18-402-072 1284 Trapp Lane
05-18-402-040 1294 Trapp Lane
05-18-402-054 1299 Trapp Lane
05-18-402-039 1304 Trapp Lane
05-18-402-053 1309 Trapp Lane
05-18-402-049 1314 Trapp Lane
05-18-402-052 1319 Trapp Lane
05-18-402-048 1324 Trapp Lane
05-18-402-051 1329 Trapp Lane
05-18-402-047 1334 Trapp Lane
05-18-402-050 1339 Trapp Lane
05-18-402-076 1345 Trapp Lane
05-18-402-046 1350 Trapp Lane
05-18-402-075 1360 Trapp Lane
05-18-402-074 1368 Trapp Lane
05-18-402-043 1370 Trapp Lane
05-18-402-042 1372 Trapp Lane
05-18-402-077 1385 Trapp Lane
 
SECTION 7:    The purpose of the establishment of SSA No. 3 is to provide for
the construction of a storm sewer, the reconstruction and repaving of Trapp
Lane, the construction of a cul-de-sac at the terminus of Trapp Lane and the
construction of related appurtenances to the Area (the “Services”). All of the
Services will supplement services currently or customarily provided by the
Village to the Area, in particular in connection with the street and storm
drainage infrastructure, in that SSA No. 3 is intended to improve stormwater
drainage to the Area and to upgrade Trapp Lane to Village standards so that
Trapp Lane, which is currently a private roadway, can be dedicated to the
Village as a public right-of-way.
SECTION 8:   SSA No. 3 is also created so that bonds or such other financing
instrument as may be authorized by law may be issued to meet the costs of the
Services for SSA No. 3 and for the purposes aforesaid, said bonds or financing
instrument (the “Bonds”) to be payable from taxes levied on the property in the
Area, in addition to all other Village taxes so levied; provided, that the
Bonds shall not be issued in excess of the principal amount of $631,895.00; and
provided, that the Bonds shall be at an interest rate not to exceed 5.00% per
annum and shall be retired over a period not to exceed 10 years. The Bonds, if
issued, shall be retired by the levy of a direct tax on all taxable real
property within the Area to discharge the principal as it matures and the
interest thereon as it comes due, and said tax shall be in addition to all
other taxes presently levied by any taxing district within the Area.
SECTION 9:   SSA No. 3 shall terminate not later than the 10th anniversary of
the issuance of the Bonds, unless prior to such date the Village enacts an
ordinance extending the duration of SSA Area No. 3.
SECTION 10:   The Village Clerk is hereby directed to file a certified copy of
this Ordinance creating SSA No. 3, including Exhibits A, B and C, along with an
accurate map of the Area, with the County Clerk of Cook County no later than 60
days after the passage and approval of this Ordinance.
SECTION 11:   This Ordinance is passed by the Council of the Village of
Winnetka in the exercise of its home rule powers pursuant to Section 6 of
Article VII of the Illinois Constitution of 1970.
SECTION 12:   This Ordinance shall take effect immediately upon its passage,
approval and posting as provided by law.
PASSED this 20th day of July, 2010, pursuant to the following roll call vote: 
