ORDINANCE NO. M-15-2010
AN ORDINANCE AUTHORIZING THE DISPOSITION OF CERTAIN PERSONAL PROPERTY OWNED BY
THE VILLAGE OF WINNETKA
WHEREAS, Article VII, Section 10 of the Constitution of the State of Illinois,
and the Intergovernmental Cooperation Act, 220 ILCS 220/1, et seq., authorize
and encourage intergovernmental cooperation; and
WHEREAS, the Northwest Municipal Conference, is a regional council of
government that represents Illinois municipalities and townships located in
Cook, DuPage, Kane, Lake and McHenry Counties, and organizes joint municipal
auctions for the sale of surplus vehicles and equipment; and
WHEREAS, the Northwest Municipal Conference has scheduled a joint municipal
auction for the sale of surplus vehicles and equipment at 10:00 a.m., Saturday,
October 9, 2010, at the Village of Wheeling Public Works Facility, 77 Hintz
Road, Wheeling, Illinois; and
WHEREAS, the Village of Winnetka owns the following described items of personal
property (the “Personal Property”) and has established a minimum value for each
such item of personal property as hereinafter described:
 
Serial Number     Village ID Year Make         Model     Comments       Minimum
                                                                        Price
                                                         Stellar roll-
1FVXJLBB3TL704745 PW-25      1996 Freightliner FL 80     off Model 174- $30,000
                                                         20-65
1FDXK74CORVA14174 W&E-66     1994 Ford         F700      Versa-Lift     $5,000
                                                         VST4000
2FAFP71W45X156980 PD-441     2005 Ford         Crown Vic               $4,500
1FAFP53212G272573 PW-91      2002 Ford         Taurus                   $2,500
WHEREAS, the Council of the Village of Winnetka (“Village Council”) have
determined that it is no longer useful to, or in the best interests of, the
Village of Winnetka to retain said Personal Property and that said Personal
Property should be sold in the manner hereinafter provided; and
WHEREAS, the Village Manager of the Village of Winnetka has authorized the
Northwest Municipal Conference to advertise and obtain bids for the sale of the
items of Personal Property at the joint municipal auction to be conducted by
the Northwest Municipal Conference at 10:00 a.m., Saturday, October 9, 2010, at
the Village of Wheeling Public Works Facility, 77 Hintz Road, Wheeling,
Illinois, with the acceptance of any bids being subject to the approval of the
corporate authorities pursuant to a duly enacted ordinance; and
WHEREAS, the Village of Winnetka (“Village”) is a home rule municipality in
accordance with Article VII, Section 6 of the Constitution of the State of
Illinois of 1970, with the authority, except as limited by said Section 6 of
Article VII, to exercise any power and perform any function pertaining to the
government and affairs of the Village, including, but not limited to, the
powers to regulate for the protection of the public health, safety, morals and
welfare; and
WHEREAS, the Village Council find that the disposal of surplus personal
property owned by the Village, such as the surplus Personal Property described
in this Ordinance, is a matter pertaining to the affairs of the Village and
that the manner of disposal of such property pertains to the public health,
safety and general welfare of the Village and its citizens; and
WHEREAS, the Council of the Village of Winnetka, in the exercise of its home
rule powers pursuant to Section 6 of Article VII of the Illinois Constitution
of 1970, have determined that it is in the best interests of the Village and
its citizens to dispose of the said Personal Property in a manner consistent
with the provisions of Section 11-76-4 of the Illinois Municipal Code (65 ILCS
5/11-76-4), as more fully set forth in this Ordinance.
NOW, THEREFORE, the Council of the Village of Winnetka do ordain:
SECTION 1:   Pursuant to the Village's home rule authority, and consistent with
Section 11-76-4 of the Illinois Municipal Code 65 (ILCS 5/11-76-4), the Council
the Village of Winnetka find that the above-described Personal Property is no
longer necessary or useful to the Village of Winnetka and that the best
interests of the Village of Winnetka will be served by the sale of said
Personal Property as provided in this Ordinance.
SECTION 2:   Pursuant to the Village's home rule authority and consistent with
said Section 11-76-4, the Village Manager is hereby authorized to direct the
sale of the Personal Property at an auction to be conducted by the Northwest
Municipal Conference (“NWMC”) at 10:00 a.m., Saturday, October 9, 2010, at the
Village of Wheeling Public Works Facility, 77 Hintz Road, Winnetka, Illinois.
SECTION 3:   The Village Manager is further authorized to direct the NWMC to
advertise the sale of the Personal Property through area newspapers, direct
mailings, and such other channels as the NWMC deems appropriate prior to the
date of the auction.
SECTION 4:   The Village Manager is further authorized to direct the NWMC to
enter into an agreement for the sale of the Personal Property, whereby the
Personal Property shall be sold at the auction to the highest bidder or
bidders, according to the terms set forth in the Specifications for the Sale of
Vehicles and Equipment at Northwest Municipal Conference Auctions, which
specifications are attached hereto and made a part of this ordinance.
SECTION 5:   No bid shall be accepted for the sale of any item of the Personal
Property which is less than the minimum value of said item of personal property
as set forth in the preamble to this ordinance, unless the Village Manager, or
his designee, so authorizes at the time of the auction, and unless the highest
bid received for such item is less than the minimum value set forth in this
ordinance.
SECTION 6:   Upon payment in full of the auctioned price by the highest bidder
or bidders for any item of the Personal Property, the Village Manager is
authorized to direct the NWMC to convey and transfer the title and ownership of
said item of Personal Property to the highest bidder or bidders.
SECTION 7:   This Ordinance is passed by the Council of the Village of Winnetka
in the exercise of its home rule powers pursuant to Section 6 of Article VII of
the Illinois Constitution of 1970.
SECTION 8   This Ordinance shall take effect immediately upon its passage,
approval and posting as provided by law.
PASSED this 21st day of September, 2010, pursuant to the following roll call
