ORDINANCE NO. M-16-2010
AN ORDINANCE GRANTING A VARIATION IN THE APPLICATION OF THE ZONING ORDINANCE OF
THE VILLAGE OF WINNETKA, COOK COUNTY, ILLINOIS (245 Ridge)
WHEREAS, the Village of Winnetka is a home rule municipality in accordance with
Article VII, Section 6 of the Constitution of the State of Illinois of 1970,
pursuant to which it has the authority, except as limited by said Section 6 of
Article VII, to exercise any power and perform any function pertaining to the
government and affairs of the Village; and
WHEREAS, the Council of the Village of Winnetka (“Village Council”) find that
establishing standards for the use and development of lands and buildings
within the Village and establishing and applying criteria for variations from
those standards are matters pertaining to the affairs of the Village; and
WHEREAS, the property commonly known as 245 Ridge Avenue, Winnetka, Illinois
(the “Subject Property”), is legally described as follows:
The Southwest Quarter of Lot 5 (said property being particularly described as
the South 66 feet of the West 132 feet of said Lot 5 without including in this
measurement any portion of the street on the West of said Lot) in Block 2 in
Garland’s Addition to Winnetka, a subdivision of the North 120 acres of the
Southwest Quarter of Section 21, Township 42 North, Range 13, East of the Third
Principal Meridian, in Cook County, Illinois; and
WHEREAS, the Subject Property is located in the R-5 Zoning District provided in
Chapter 17.12 of the Winnetka Zoning Ordinance, Title 17 of the Winnetka
Village Code; and
WHEREAS, on September 30, 2010, the owner of the Subject Property filed an
application seeking variations from the 2.0-foot garage setback requirements of
Section 17.30.110(E) of the Zoning Ordinance to allow a new, two-car detached
garage to have (i) a rear yard setback of 0.33 feet, a variation of 1.67 feet
(83.5%), and (ii) a north side yard setback of 0.58 feet, a variation of 1.42
feet (71%); and
WHEREAS, on October 11, 2010, on due notice thereof, the Zoning Board of
Appeals conducted a public hearing on the requested variations, at which time
the applicant withdrew the request for the north side yard setback variation
and, by the unanimous vote of the six members then present, has reported to the
Council recommending that the requested rear yard setback variation be granted;
and
WHEREAS, there are practical difficulties and particular hardships associated
with carrying out the strict application of the Zoning Ordinance with respect
to the Subject Property in that: (a) the Subject Property is improved with a
single-family residence, constructed in 1906, prior to the enactment of the
original Zoning Ordinance; (b) the configuration of the Subject Property was
established no later than 1929, when what is now a nonconforming two-car garage
was constructed at the location where the existing garage now stands; (c) it is
not reasonably possible to relocate the driveway to the south side of the
Subject Property, as the entrances to the existing residence are on the north
side of the house; and (d) the garage cannot be shifted closer to the house,
because adequate space is required between the garage and the house to provide
a vehicle turnaround, as it is not reasonably possible to safely exit the
Subject Property by driving down the driveway in reverse; and
WHEREAS, the Subject Property cannot yield a reasonable return if permitted to
be used only under the conditions allowed by the Zoning Ordinance, in that: (a)
the existing, nonconforming garage is in dilapidated condition; (b) the
foundation of the current garage is at a low elevation, which is causing water
damage to the wood framed walls; and (c) a new garage cannot reasonably be
built in a conforming location because of the necessity to provide a vehicle
turnaround for safe exit from the Subject Property; and
WHEREAS, the requested variation will not alter the essential character of the
neighborhood because the proposed new garage will maintain the established
orientation of the Subject Property and will be comparable in size and design
to the garage it will replace; and
WHEREAS, the requested variation will not impair an adequate supply of light
and air because the relation of the rear yard to the adjoining property to the
east will not be changed and the north side yard setback will comply with the
applicable zoning regulations; and
WHEREAS, the requested variation will not increase the hazard from fire and
other dangers to the Subject Property, as: (a) the proposed construction will
comply with all applicable building and fire protection codes; and (b) the rear
setback of the garage will be slightly larger than the existing setback; and
WHEREAS, there is no evidence that the requested variation will diminish the
taxable value of land and buildings throughout the Village, and the replacement
of the existing, dilapidated garage is likely to increase the value of the
Subject Property; and
WHEREAS, the proposed construction will not contribute to congestion on the
public streets, as the property will continue to be used for single family
residential purposes and the new garage will preserve off-street parking; and
WHEREAS, there is no evidence that the requested variation will otherwise
impair the public health, safety, comfort, morals, and welfare of the
inhabitants of the Village; and
WHEREAS, the requested variation is in harmony with the general purpose and
intent of the Winnetka Zoning Ordinance, in that it allows the replacement of a
dilapidated existing building while maintaining the existing scale and
appearance of the community and protecting established trees and landscaping.
NOW, THEREFORE, the Council of the Village of Winnetka do ordain as follows:
SECTION 1:  The foregoing recitals are hereby incorporated as the findings of
the Council of the Village of Winnetka, as if fully set forth herein.
SECTION 2:   The Subject Property, commonly known as 245 Ridge Avenue in the
Village of Winnetka, and located in the R-5 Single-Family Residential District
provided in Chapter 17.12 of the Winnetka Zoning Ordinance, Title 17 of the
Winnetka Village Code, is hereby granted a variation of 1.67 feet (83.5%) from
the garage setback requirements of Section 17.30.110 of Chapter 17.30 of the
Zoning Ordinance to permit the construction of a new two-car detached garage
with a rear yard setback of 0.33 feet, rather than the required minimum rear
yard setback of 2 feet, in accordance with the plans and elevations submitted
with the application for variation, as amended by the drawings dated October
18, 2010.
SECTION 3:   The variation granted herein is conditioned upon the commencement
of the proposed construction within 12 months after the effective date of this
Ordinance. 
SECTION 4:   This Ordinance is passed by the Council of the Village of Winnetka
in the exercise of its home rule powers pursuant to Section 6 of Article VII of
the Illinois Constitution of 1970.
SECTION 5:   This Ordinance shall take effect immediately upon its passage,
approval and posting as provided by law.
PASSED this 7th day of December, 2010, pursuant to the following roll call
vote: 
AYES:    Trustees Greable, Johnson, Pedian, Rintz and Spinney
NAYS:    None
ABSENT:    Trustee Poor
APPROVED this 7th day of December, 2010
   Signed:
   s/Jessica Tucker
   Village President
Countersigned:
s/Robert M. Bahan
Village Clerk
Introduced: November 16, 2010
Posted: November 17, 2010
Passed and Approved: December 7, 2010
