ORDINANCE NO. M-17-2010
AN ORDINANCE GRANTING A VARIATION IN THE APPLICATION OF THE ZONING ORDINANCE OF
THE VILLAGE OF WINNETKA, COOK COUNTY, ILLINOIS (1110 Pine)
WHEREAS, the Village of Winnetka is a home rule municipality in accordance with
Article VII, Section 6 of the Constitution of the State of Illinois of 1970,
pursuant to which it has the authority, except as limited by said Section 6 of
Article VII, to exercise any power and perform any function pertaining to the
government and affairs of the Village; and
WHEREAS, the Council of the Village of Winnetka (“Village Council”) find that
establishing standards for the use and development of lands and buildings
within the Village and establishing and applying criteria for variations from
those standards are matters pertaining to the affairs of the Village; and
WHEREAS, the property commonly known as 1110 Pine Street, Winnetka, Illinois
(the “Subject Property”), is legally described as follows:
Lot 10 (except the East 6.0 feet thereof) in Block 2 in Groveland Addition to
Winnetka, being a subdivision in Section 20, Township 42 North, Range 13, East
of the Third Principal Meridian, in Cook County, Illinois; and
WHEREAS, the Subject Property is located in the R-5 Zoning District provided in
Chapter 17.12 of the Winnetka Zoning Ordinance, Title 17 of the Winnetka
Village Code; and
WHEREAS, on September 8, 2010, the owner of the Subject Property filed an
application seeking the following variations from requirements of the Lot,
Space, Bulk and Yard Regulations for Single Family Residential Districts
established by Chapter 17.30 of the Zoning Ordinance: (a) a variation from the
maximum building size limitations of Section 17.30.040 to permit a gross floor
area of 4,504.92 square feet, which exceeds the allowable maximum of 4,272.29
square feet, resulting in a variation of 232.63 square feet (5.44%); and (b) a
variation from the front (corner) setback requirements of Section 17.30.050 to
allow a west front yard setback of 8.47 feet, whereas a minimum of 20.1 feet is
required, resulting in a variation of 11.63 feet (57.86%), said variations
being for the purposes of allowing the conversion of the existing attached
garage into a family room, allowing the construction of a one-story addition to
add a mudroom and two-car attached garage adjacent to the family room, and
allowing the construction of a two-story addition to accommodate the
reconfiguration of the rear bedroom and the addition of a hallway; and
WHEREAS, on October 11, 2010, on due notice thereof, the Zoning Board of
Appeals conducted a public hearing on the requested variations and, by the
unanimous vote of the six members then present, has reported to the Council
recommending that the requested variations be granted; and
WHEREAS, there are practical difficulties associated with carrying out the
strict application of the Zoning Ordinance with respect to the Subject Property
in that: (a) the Subject Property is a corner lot located at the southeast
corner of Pine Street and Glendale Avenue and is therefore subject to front
setback requirements along both street frontages; (b) the Subject Property is
improved with a single-family residence, constructed in 1923, before the
enactment of the Winnetka Zoning Ordinance; (c) the existing home has an
attached garage, which is accessed from Glendale Avenue; (d) the home and
garage have a legally nonconforming west front yard setback of 6.97 feet; (e)
the rear of the Subject Property has a slope of approximately three feet and
the area becomes flooded after any significant rainfall; (f) because building a
detached garage in a conforming location in the rear of the Subject Property
would require another 11.63 linear feet of driveway and the construction of a
retaining wall, building a new garage in a conforming location would increase
impervious surface and block the natural flow of stormwater runoff, thereby
increasing the incidence of flooding; and (f) the rear of the Subject Property
has two mature trees which would have to be removed in order to construct a
detached garage in a conforming location; and
WHEREAS, the Subject Property cannot yield a reasonable return if permitted to
be used only under the conditions allowed by the Zoning Ordinance, because (i)
the existing residence lacks a family room and mudroom, which are considered
standard amenities in homes throughout the Village, (ii) the powder room is
undersized, and (iii) due to the interior configuration of the residence, the
only reasonable location for providing such standard amenities is in the area
where the attached garage is located; and
WHEREAS, the requested variations will not alter the essential character of the
neighborhood because: (a) the proposed addition will be no closer to the street
than the existing building; (b) the proposed addition will be an attached
garaged that will maintain the existing orientation of the residence and garage
to the street and will be designed to be consistent with the existing building;
(c) the proposed additions will have less visual impact than would a new,
detached garage, which would give the garage more prominence on the block face
and would require the removal of mature landscaping; and (d) the existing
double-wide garage door will be replaced with two conforming overhead doors;
and
WHEREAS, the requested variations will not impair an adequate supply of light
and air because: (a) the setback variation is along the Glendale Avenue street
frontage and the setback will be increased by 1.5 feet, thereby reducing the
amount of the existing nonconformity; and (b) the proposed additions be of a
conforming height; and
WHEREAS, the requested variations will not increase the hazard from fire and
other dangers to the Subject Property, as the proposed construction will comply
with all applicable building and fire protection codes; and
WHEREAS, the requested variations will not diminish the taxable value of land
and buildings throughout the Village, and the taxable value of the Subject
Property may be increased because of the proposed improvements; and
WHEREAS, the proposed construction will not contribute to congestion on the
public streets, as the property will continue to be used for single family
residential purposes and off-street parking will be maintained; and
WHEREAS, there is no evidence that the requested variations will otherwise
impair the public health, safety, comfort, morals, and welfare of the
inhabitants of the Village; and
WHEREAS, the requested variations are in harmony with the general purpose and
intent of the Winnetka Zoning Ordinance, in that they allow the renovation of a
structurally sound existing building while maintaining the existing scale and
appearance of the community and protecting established trees and landscaping.
NOW, THEREFORE, the Council of the Village of Winnetka do ordain as follows:
SECTION 1:   The foregoing recitals are hereby incorporated as the findings of
the Council of the Village of Winnetka, as if fully set forth herein.
SECTION 2:   The Subject Property, commonly known as 1110 Pine and located in
the R-5 Single-Family Residential District provided in Chapter 17.12 of the
Winnetka Zoning Ordinance, Title 17 of the Winnetka Village Code is hereby
granted the following variations from requirements of the Lot, Space, Bulk and
Yard Regulations for Single Family Residential Districts established by Chapter
17.30 of the Zoning Ordinance: (a) a variation from the maximum building size
limitations of Section 17.30.040 to permit a gross floor area of 4,504.92
square feet, which exceeds the allowable maximum of 4,272.29 square feet,
resulting in a variation of 232.63 square feet (5.44%), and (b) a variation
from the front (corner) setback requirements of Section 17.30.050 to allow a
west front yard setback of 8.47 feet, whereas a minimum of 20.1 feet is
required, resulting in a variation of 11.63 feet (57.86%), said variations
being for the purposes of allowing the conversion of the existing attached
garage into a family room, allowing the construction of a one-story addition to
add a mudroom and two-car attached garage adjacent to the family room, and
allowing the construction of a two-story addition to accommodate the
reconfiguration of the rear bedroom and the addition of a hallway, all in
accordance with the plans and elevations submitted with the application for
variations.
SECTION 3:   The variations granted herein are conditioned upon the
commencement of the proposed construction within 12 months after the effective
date of this Ordinance. 
SECTION 4:   This Ordinance is passed by the Council of the Village of Winnetka
in the exercise of its home rule powers pursuant to Section 6 of Article VII of
the Illinois Constitution of 1970.
SECTION 5:   This Ordinance shall take effect immediately upon its passage,
approval and posting as provided by law.
