ORDINANCE NO. M-10-2011
AN ORDINANCE AMENDING THE BOUNDARIES OF PROPOSED SPECIAL SERVICE AREA NO. 5 IN
THE VILLAGE OF WINNETKA
WHEREAS, the Village of Winnetka (“Village”) is a home rule municipality in
accordance with Article VII, Section 6 of the Constitution of the State of
Illinois of 1970; and
WHEREAS, the Village has the authority to adopt ordinances and to promulgate
rules and regulations that pertain to its government and affairs that protect
the public health, safety and welfare of its citizens; and
WHEREAS, on April 26, 2011, the Council of the Village of Winnetka (“Village
Council”) passed Ordinance M-3-2011, proposing the establishment of Winnetka
Special Service Area No. 5 for the purpose of constructing a storm sewer, a new
concrete alley and related appurtenances in the block bounded by Elm Street,
Oak Street, Glendale Avenue, and Rosewood Avenue, which Territory constitutes a
compact and contiguous residential territory; and
WHEREAS, as provided in Ordinance M-3-2011, and pursuant to due notice, the
Village Council convened a public hearing on proposed Special Service Area No.
5 on June 7, 2011, at which time the owners of certain properties at the edge
of the proposed territory requested that they be excluded from Special Service
Area No. 5 because they do not use the alley for access; and
WHEREAS, at the close of the hearing on June 7, 2011, the Village Council
determined that it would consider amending the boundaries of proposed Special
Service Area No. 5, provided the owners of the properties seeking to be
excluded agreed to pay, in full, one-half of the amount indentified in
Ordinance M-3-2011 as their share of the project costs, and provided that the
removal of the properties did not affect the contiguity of the proposed Special
Service Area No. 5; and
WHEREAS, pursuant to Section 27-35 of the Special Service Area Tax Law, 35 ILCS
200/27-35, the Village may delete area from the proposed special service area
at the public hearing or at the first regular meeting of the corporate
authorities following the public hearing, provided that the special service
area is still a contiguous area; and
WHEREAS, the first regular meeting of the Village Council after the public
hearing is June 21, 2011; and
WHEREAS, the owners of the parcels of property commonly known as 1110 Elm
Street, and 1111 Oak Street in the Village of Winnetka, Illinois, have paid, in
full, one-half of the amount indentified in Ordinance M-3-2011 as their share
of the project costs; and
WHEREAS, the deletion of the parcels of property commonly known as 1110 Elm
Street, and 1111 Oak Street in the Village of Winnetka, Illinois, from proposed
Special Service Area No. 5 will not affect the contiguity of the area.
NOW, THEREFORE, the Council of the Village of Winnetka do ordain as follows:
SECTION 1:   The facts and statements contained in the preamble to this
Ordinance are found to be true and correct and are hereby incorporated into
this Ordinance by reference as the findings of the Council of the Village of
Winnetka, as if fully set forth herein.
SECTION 2:   The Council of the Village of Winnetka further find that cause has
been presented, in accordance with Section 2.04.040 of the Winnetka Village
Code, for the Village Council to determine that requiring introduction and
initial posting of this ordinance will not, in this instance, serve the best
interests of the Village, in that: (i) Section 27-35 of the Special Service
Area Tax Law imposes a deadline for deleting territory from a proposed special
service area; (ii) the boundaries of the proposed Special Service Area No. 5
have been discussed both at public meetings of the Village Council, at the
public hearing on June 7, 2011, and in meetings between Village staff and the
owners of property within the proposed Special Service Area No. 5; (iii) the
deletion of the properties described below will allow all of the improvements
to proceed without affecting the contiguity of the proposed special service
area; and (iv) it is not possible to comply with both the statutory deadline
for deleting territory from the proposed special service area and the
introduction and posting requirements of Section 2.04.040 of the Village Code.
