WHEREAS, the Village of Winnetka is a home rule municipality in accordance with
Article VII, Section 6 of the Constitution of the State of Illinois of 1970 and
has the authority, except as limited by said Section 6 of Article VII, to
exercise any power and perform any function pertaining to the Village’s
government and affairs and to the public health, safety and welfare; and
WHEREAS, the Village Council finds that the disposal of surplus property owned
by the Village, such as the Surplus Property described in this Ordinance, is a
matter pertaining to the affairs of the Village and to the public health,
safety and general welfare; and
WHEREAS, the Village of Winnetka owns certain vehicles and equipment that have
been retired from service due to their scheduled replacement, obsolescence or
damage (the “Surplus Property”), which Surplus Property is described, and its
sale value estimated, in the following table:
