ORDINANCE NO. M-6-2014
AN ORDINANCE EXTENDING THE SPECIAL USE PERMIT AND VARIATION GRANTED PURSUANT TO
ORDINANCE M-7-2013 (925-931 Green Bay Road)
   WHEREAS, the Village of Winnetka ("Village") is a home rule municipality in
accordance with Article VII, Section 6 of the Constitution of the State of
Illinois of 1970 and, pursuant thereto, has the authority, except as limited by
said Section 6 of Article VII, to exercise any power and perform any function
pertaining to the government and affairs of the Village, including the power to
regulate for the protection of the public health, safety and welfare; and
   WHEREAS, the Village Council find that establishing standards for the use
and development of lands and buildings within the Village and establishing and
applying criteria for variations from those standards are matters pertaining to
the affairs of the Village; and
   WHEREAS, on June 18, 2013, the Village Council enacted Ordinance M-7-2013
("Ordinance"), granting a variation and special use for the following described
real estate (the "Subject Property"), which is commonly known as 925-931 Green
Bay Road:
   Lot 3 in Block 5 in Jared Gage's Subdivision in Section 17 and 8, Township
42 North, Range 13 East of the Third Principal Meridian, in Cook County,
Illinois;
   And also
   The southerly 50 feet of that part of the east half of the Northwest Quarter
of said Factional Section 17, described as follows: Commencing at the Northeast
corner of Lot 1 in Block 5 in Jared Gage's Subdivision aforesaid and running
thence Southeasterly along the Easterly line of Lots 1,2 and 3 in said Block 5,
a distance of 150 feet; thence running Easterly on a line of parallel with the
southerly line of Gage Street extended, a distance of 50 feet; thence
Northwesterly on a line parallel with the Easterly line of Lots 1,2 and 3
aforesaid, a distance of 150 feet to a point on the South line of Gage Street
extended, and thence Southwesterly to the point of beginning, in Cook County,
Illinois;
   And also
   Lots 4 and 5 in Block 5 in Jared Gage's Subdivision of part of Northwest
Quarter of Fractional Section 17 and part of the East half of the Southwest
Quarter of Fractional Section 8, all in Township 42 North, Range 13 East of the
Third Principal Meridian;
   And also
   The Southerly 18 feet of strip of land 50 feet wide and 168 feet long lying
Easterly of adjoining Lots 1, 2 and 3 and Northerly 18 feet of Lot 4 in Block 5
in Jared Gage's Subdivision aforesaid, all in Cook County, Illinois; and
   WHEREAS, the Ordinance granted a special use permit and variation to allow
the construction of a street-level parking lot on that portion of the Subject
Property known as 929 - 931 Green Bay Road ("Parcel 1"), with streetscape
amenities (collectively, the "Parking Lot"), as depicted in Owner's Exhibit E,
"Revised Site Plan," and Exhibit F, "Revised Arched Gateway Feature Concept,"
both prepared by The Lakota Group and dated April 18, 2013; and
   WHEREAS, the owner has been in negotiations with a potential tenant for the
Subject Property, but has not yet finalized the terms of a lease; and
   WHEREAS, the building on Parcel 1 contains two retail spaces, both of which
were under lease when it was purchased by the current owner; and
   WHEREAS, although the tenant of one of the retail spaces on Parcel 1 has
relocated, the other retail space remains occupied by a tenant whose lease does
not expire until February of 2015; and
   WHEREAS, the Owner has not yet begun construction of the proposed Parking
Lot and cannot begin such construction until the building on Parcel 1 has been
vacated and demolished; and
   WHEREAS, Section 4.B of the Ordinance provides that the special use and
variation granted by that Ordinance will expire if the construction of the
Parking Lot did not commence within 12 months after the effective date of the
Ordinance; and
   WHEREAS, Section 17.56.100(A) of the Winnetka Zoning Ordinance, Title 17 of
the Winnetka Village Code, provides that a special use permit shall become null
and void if the construction or occupancy for which the special use is granted
has not been "actively pursued" within one year and "completed and occupied"
within 18 months following the date of Village Council approval; and
   WHEREAS, Section 16.56.100 of the Winnetka Zoning Ordinance also provides
that the time limits can be extended by the Village Council, at its discretion,
following a written request to do so; and
   WHEREAS, the Owner has submitted a timely written request to extend the
special use and variation granted by the Ordinance to April 30, 2015, to allow
time (i) for the tenant in the building on Parcel 1 to move after the lease for
that space expires, and (ii) for the Owner to complete lease negotiations with
a new tenant for the Subject Property; and
   WHEREAS, the Village Council finds that, although construction of the
Parking Lot will not begin within 12 months after the grant of the special use
and variation, the Owner has actively pursued the work permitted by the
Ordinance; and
   WHEREAS, the Village Council finds that, although construction of Parking
Lot cannot be completed and occupied within 18 months after the grant of the
special use, the Owner has made reasonable efforts to pursue the work permitted
by the Ordinance, in that the Owner has (i) continued efforts to negotiate a
lease with a new tenant for the large commercial building on the Subject
Property, (ii) has relocated one of the retail tenants from Parcel 1, and (iii)
is continuing efforts to relocate the remaining tenant on Parcel 1; and
   WHEREAS, at the regular meeting of the Village Council on June 3, 2014, the
Village Council considered the Owner's written request for an extension and
directed staff to prepare an ordinance granting the requested extension; and
   WHEREAS, the Village Council meeting of June 17, 2014, was rescheduled for
June 24, 2014, making it impossible for the Council to take final action on the
Owner's extension request before June 18, 204; and
   WHEREAS, this Ordinance has been placed on the Village Council's agenda and
made available for public inspection at Village Hall and on the Village's web
site, in accordance with Sections 2.04.040 and 2.16.040 of the Winnetka Village
Code and applicable law.
   NOW, THEREFORE, BE IT ORDAINED by the Council of the Village of Winnetka as
follows:
   SECTION 1:   The foregoing recitals are hereby incorporated as the findings
of the Council of the Village of Winnetka, as if fully set forth herein.
   SECTION 2:   That, subject to the terms and conditions hereinafter set
forth, and pursuant to Section 17.56.100 of Chapter 17.56 of the Winnetka
Zoning Ordinance, Title 17 of the Winnetka Village Code, the special use permit
and variation granted by Ordinance M-7-2013 with respect to the Subject
Property, commonly known as 925 - 931 Green Bay Road and located in the C-
2 Retail Overlay Zoning District, is hereby extended from June 18, 2014, to and
including April 30, 2015.
   SECTION 3:   The extension hereby granted shall be subject to the following
conditions:
   A.   The construction of the Parking Lot shall commence no later than April
30, 2015.
   B.   The special use permit and variation granted by Ordinance M-7-2013 and
extended by this Ordinance shall expire if construction of the Parking Lot is
not commenced by April 30, 2015.
   C.   Any requests for further extensions of the special use and variation
granted by Ordinance M-7-2013 shall be treated as a new application and shall
be subject to public hearings before the Zoning Board of Appeals and such other
subordinate bodies as may be required by Chapters 17.56 and 17.60 of the
Winnetka Village Code at the time such new application is filed.
   SECTION 4:   Except as provided in Section 3 of this Ordinance, the terms
and conditions of Ordinance M-7-2013 shall remain in full force and effect.
   SECTION 5:   This Ordinance is passed by the Council of the Village of
Winnetka in the exercise of its home rule powers pursuant to Section 6 of
Article VII of the Illinois Constitution of 1970.
   SECTION 6:   This Ordinance shall take effect immediately upon its passage,
approval and posting as provided by law.
   PASSED this 24th day of June, 2014, pursuant to the following roll call
vote:
   AYES:    Trustees Braun, Fessler, Kates, Krucks, McCrary, Prodromos
   NAYS:    None
   ABSENT:    None
   APPROVED this 24th day of June, 2014.
