ORDINANCE NO. M-6-2016
AN ORDINANCE GRANTING A SPECIAL USE PERMIT AND VARIATIONS FROM THE WINNETKA
ZONING ORDINANCE FOR THE CONSTRUCTION OF IMPROVEMENTS AT SAINTS FAITH, HOPE,
AND CHARITY CHURCH
(150 and 191 Linden Street)
   WHEREAS, the Catholic Bishop of Chicago, an Illinois Corporation Sole
("Applicant"), is the record title owner of those parcels of real property
commonly known as 150 Linden Street (“150 Linden Property”) and 191 Linden
Street (“191 Linden Property”) in Winnetka, Illinois, and legally described in
Exhibit A attached to and, by this reference, made a part of this Ordinance
(collectively, “Subject Property”); and
   WHEREAS, the Subject Property is located within the R-3 Single Family
Residential Zoning District of the Village ("R-3 District"); and
   WHEREAS, the Subject Property is improved with buildings, structures, and
facilities used by the Saints Faith, Hope, and Charity Church (“Church”); and
   WHEREAS, the Applicant desires to construct: (i) a new, two-story building
on the 191 Linden Property for use as a parish center; (ii) a new,
approximately 27,000 square-foot synthetic turf athletic field and play area on
the 150 Linden Property; and (iii) modifications to existing parking and site
access improvements on the Subject Property (collectively, “Proposed
Improvements”); and
   WHEREAS, the Proposed Improvements include construction of (i) angled
parking spaces within the portion of the Linden Street right-of-way located
adjacent to, and to the east of, the 150 Linden Property (“Linden Parking
Spaces”), and (ii) a sidewalk open to public use on the portion of the 150
Linden Property located adjacent to, and to the west of, the Linden Street
right-of-way (“Linden Sidewalk”); and
   WHEREAS, pursuant to Section 17.20.020 of the Winnetka Zoning Ordinance
(“Zoning Ordinance”), the operation of a church is not permitted within the R-
3 District without a special use permit; and
   WHEREAS, pursuant to Section 17.56.090 of the Zoning Ordinance, no special
use may be enlarged or extended by structural alteration of a building or
structure without a special use permit; and
   WHEREAS, pursuant to Section 17.30.030 of the Zoning Ordinance, (i) the area
of roofed lot coverage on the Subject Property may not exceed 43,383.75 square
feet, and (ii) the area of impermeable surfaces on the Subject Property may not
exceed 27,093.5 square feet; and
   WHEREAS, pursuant to Section 17.30.040 of the Zoning Ordinance, the gross
floor area of buildings on the Subject Property may not exceed 41,728.05 square
feet; and
   WHEREAS, pursuant to Section 17.30.050 of the Zoning Ordinance, the front
and corner yard setbacks of the Subject Property may not exceed 40 feet,
respectively; and
   WHEREAS, pursuant to Section 17.30.070 of the Zoning Ordinance, the rear
yard setback of the Subject Property may not exceed 25 feet; and
   WHEREAS, pursuant to Section 17.30.100 of the Zoning Ordinance, the area of
each off-street parking space located on the Subject Property may not be less
than 180 square feet; and
   WHEREAS, the Applicant desires to construct the Proposed Improvements so
that: (i) the improvements on the 191 Linden Property will have (a) a roofed
lot coverage area of 54,662 square feet, in violation of Section 17.30.030 of
the Zoning Ordinance; (b) a gross floor area of 145,124 square feet, in
violation of Section 17.30.040 of the Zoning Ordinance; and (c) off-street
parking spaces with an area of 153.12 square feet per space, in violation of
Section 17.30.100 of the Zoning Ordinance; and (ii) the improvements on the 150
Linden Property will have (a) an impermeable surface area of 36,747 square
feet, in violation of Section 17.30.040 of the Zoning Ordinance; (b) a front
yard setback from Hill Road of 15 feet and a corner yard setback from Linden
Street of 20 feet, in violation of Section 17.30.050 of the Zoning Ordinance;
and (c) a rear yard setback of 20 feet from the north property line of the 150
Linden Property and of zero feet from Linden Street, in violation of Section
17.30.070 of the Zoning Ordinance; and
   WHEREAS, the Applicant filed an application for: (i) a special use permit
pursuant to Section 17.20.020 and Chapter 17.56 of the Zoning Ordinance to
allow expansion of the Church through construction of the Proposed Improvements
(“Special Use Permit”); and (ii) variations from (a) Section 17.30.030 of the
Zoning Ordinance to allow a roofed lot coverage area of 54,662 square feet on
the 191 Linden Property and an impermeable surface area of 36,747 square feet
on the 150 Linden Property; (b) Section 17.30.040 of the Zoning Ordinance to
allow a gross floor area of buildings on the 191 Linden Property of 145,124
square feet; (c) Section 17.30.050 of the Zoning Ordinance to allow a front
yard setback from Hill Road of 15 feet and a corner yard setback from Linden
Street of 20 feet on the 150 Linden Property; (d) Section 17.30.070 of the
Zoning Ordinance to allow a rear yard setback of 20 feet from the north
property line of the 150 Linden Property and zero feet from Linden Street on
the 150 Linden Property; and (e) Section 17.30.100 of the Zoning Ordinance to
allow off-street parking spaces with an area of 153.12 square feet per space on
the 191 Linden Property (collectively, “Variations”) (collectively, the Special
Use Permit and the Variations are the “Requested Relief”); and
   WHEREAS, on January 11, 2016, after due notice thereof, the Zoning Board of
Appeals (“ZBA”) conducted a public hearing on the Requested Relief and, by the
unanimous vote of the six members then present, recommended that the Council of
the Village of Winnetka (“Village Council”) approve the Requested Relief; and
   WHEREAS, pursuant to Chapter 17.60 and Chapter 17.56 of the Zoning
Ordinance, the ZBA heard evidence and made certain findings in support of
recommending approval of the Special Use Permit and the Variations,
respectively, which findings are set forth in the ZBA public hearing minutes
attached to and, by this reference, made a part of this Ordinance as Exhibit B;
and
   WHEREAS, on January 27, 2016, and February 24, 2016, after due notice
thereof, the Plan Commission held a public hearing to consider whether approval
of the Requested Relief is consistent with "Winnetka 2020," the Winnetka
comprehensive plan ("Comprehensive Plan"), and found, by the unanimous vote of
the eight members then present, that approval of the Requested Relief is
consistent with the Comprehensive Plan; and
   WHEREAS, on January 21, 2016, and February 18, 2016, after due notice
thereof, the Design Review Board held a public hearing to consider the
Requested Relief and, by the vote of four members in favor and one opposed,
recommended that the Village Council approve the Requested Relief; and
   WHEREAS, the Village Council has determined that approval of the proposed
Special Use Permit (i) is consistent with the Comprehensive Plan and (ii)
satisfies the standards for the approval of special use permits set forth in
Chapter 17.56 of the Zoning Ordinance; and
   WHEREAS, pursuant to Section 17.60.050 of the Zoning Ordinance, the Village
Council has determined that: (i) the Variations are in harmony with the general
purpose and intent of the Zoning Ordinance and are in accordance with general
or specific rules set forth in Chapter 17.60 of the Zoning Ordinance; and (ii)
there are practical difficulties or particular hardships in the way of carrying
out the strict letter of the provisions or regulations of the Zoning Ordinance
from which the Variations have been sought; and
   WHEREAS, the Village Council has determined that approval of the Requested
Relief for the construction of the Proposed Improvements on the Subject
Property is in the best interest of the Village and its residents;
   NOW, THEREFORE, the Council of the Village of Winnetka do ordain as follows:
   SECTION 1:   RECITALS. The foregoing recitals are hereby incorporated into
this section as the findings of the Village Council, as if fully set forth
herein.
   SECTION 2:   APPROVAL OF SPECIAL USE PERMIT. Subject to, and contingent
upon, the terms, conditions, restrictions, and provisions set forth in Section
4 of this Ordinance, and pursuant to Chapter 17.56 and Section 17.20.020 of the
Zoning Ordinance and the home rule powers of the Village, the Special Use
Permit is granted to allow expansion of the Church through construction of the
Proposed Improvements on the Subject Property.
   SECTION 3:   APPROVAL OF VARIATIONS. Subject to, and contingent upon, the
terms, conditions, restrictions, and provisions set forth in Section 4 of this
Ordinance, and pursuant to Chapter 17.60 of the Zoning Ordinance and the home
rule powers of the Village, the Variations are granted to allow construction of
the Proposed Improvements on the Subject Property.
   SECTION 4:   CONDITIONS. The Special Use Permit granted by Section 2 of this
Ordinance and the Variations granted by Section 3 of this Ordinance are subject
to, and contingent upon, compliance by the Applicant with the following
conditions:
   Commencement of Construction. The Applicant must commence the construction
of the Proposed Improvements no later than 12 months after the effective date
of this Ordinance.
   Compliance with Regulations. Except to the extent specifically provided
otherwise in this Ordinance, the development, use, and maintenance of the
Proposed Improvements on the Subject Property must comply at all times with all
applicable Village codes and ordinances, as they have been or may be amended
over time.
   Reimbursement of Village Costs. In addition to any other costs, payments,
fees, charges, contributions, or dedications required under applicable Village
codes, ordinances, resolutions, rules, or regulations, the Applicant must pay
to the Village, promptly upon presentation of a written demand or demands
therefor, of all fees, costs, and expenses incurred or accrued in connection
with the review, negotiation, preparation, consideration, and review of this
Ordinance. Payment of all such fees, costs, and expenses for which demand has
been made shall be made by a certified or cashier's check. Further, the
Applicant must pay upon demand all costs incurred by the Village for
publications and recordings required in connection with the aforesaid matters.
   License for Linden Parking Spaces. The Village will not issue building
permits for the Proposed Improvements unless and until the Applicant enters
into a license agreement with the Village, in substantially the form provided
by the Village and approved by the Village Council, authorizing the Applicant
to use and maintain a portion of the Linden Street right-of-way for the Linden
Parking Spaces.
   Easement for Linden Sidewalk. The Village will not issue building permits
for the Proposed Improvements unless and until the Applicant enters into an
easement agreement with the Village, in substantially the form provided by the
Village and approved by the Village Council, granting the Village and the
public an easement to use a portion of the 150 Linden Property for the Linden
Sidewalk.
   Compliance with Plans. The development, use, and maintenance of the Proposed
Improvements at the Subject Property must be in strict accordance with the
following documents and plans, except for minor changes and site work approved
by the Director of Community Development or the Director of Public Works
(within their respective permitting authority) in accordance with all
applicable Village codes, ordinances, and standards:
   1.   The Site Plan prepared by OKW Architects, consisting of two sheets, and
dated March 4, 2016, attached to and, by this reference, made a part of this
Ordinance as Exhibit C; and
   2.   The Ground Floor Plan prepared by OKW Architects, consisting of one
sheet, and dated March 4, 2016, attached to and, by this reference, made a part
of this Ordinance as Exhibit D; and
   3.   The Lower Level Plan prepared by OKW Architects, consisting of one
sheet, and dated March 4, 2016, attached to and, by this reference, made a part
of this Ordinance as Exhibit E; and
   4.   The Roof Plan prepared by OKW Architects, consisting of one sheet, and
dated March 4, 2016, attached to and, by this reference, made a part of this
Ordinance as Exhibit F; and
   5.   The Building Sections prepared by OKW Architects, consisting of one
sheet, and dated March 4, 2016, attached to and, by this reference, made a part
of this Ordinance as Exhibit G; and
   6.   The North Building Elevation prepared by OKW Architects, consisting of
one sheet, and dated March 4, 2016, attached to and, by this reference, made a
part of this Ordinance as Exhibit H; and
   7.   The East Building Elevation prepared by OKW Architects, consisting of
one sheet, and dated March 4, 2016, attached to and, by this reference, made a
part of this Ordinance as Exhibit I; and
   8.   The South Building Elevation prepared by OKW Architects, consisting of
one sheet, and dated March 4, 2016, attached to and, by this reference, made a
part of this Ordinance as Exhibit J; and
   9.   The Aerial Views prepared by OKW Architects, prepared by OKW
Architects, consisting of one sheet, and dated March 4, 2016, attached to and,
by this reference, made a part of this Ordinance as Exhibit K; and
   10.   The Street Views prepared by OKW Architects, consisting of one sheet,
and dated March 4, 2016, attached to and, by this reference, made a part of
this Ordinance as Exhibit L; and
   11.   The Site Amenities Plan – East Campus prepared by OKW Architects,
consisting of one sheet, and dated March 4, 2016, attached to and, by this
reference, made a part of this Ordinance as Exhibit M; and
   12.   The Lighting Plan prepared by OKW Architects, consisting of one sheet,
and dated March 4, 2016, attached to and, by this reference, made a part of
this Ordinance as Exhibit N; and
   13.   The Site Amenities Plan – West Campus prepared by OKW Architects,
consisting of one sheet, and dated March 4, 2016, attached to and, by this
reference, made a part of this Ordinance as Exhibit O; and
   14.   The Preliminary Landscape Plan prepared by OKW Architects, consisting
of one sheet, and dated March 4, 2016, attached to and, by this reference, made
a part of this Ordinance as Exhibit P; and
   15.   The Tree Preservation Plan prepared by OKW Architects, consisting of
one sheet, and dated March 4, 2016, attached to and, by this reference, made a
part of this Ordinance as Exhibit Q; and
   16.   The Preliminary Engineering Plan prepared by SpaceCo, Inc., consisting
of one sheet, and with a latest revision date of February 4, 2016, attached to
and, by this reference, made a part of this Ordinance as Exhibit R.
   SECTION 5:   RECORDATION; BINDING EFFECT. A copy of this Ordinance will be
recorded with the Cook County Recorder of Deeds. This Ordinance and the
privileges, obligations, and provisions contained herein inure solely to the
benefit of, and are binding upon, the Applicant and each of its heirs,
representatives, successors, and assigns.
   SECTION 6:   FAILURE TO COMPLY. Upon the failure or refusal of the Applicant
to comply with any or all of the conditions, restrictions, or provisions of
this Ordinance, in addition to all other remedies available to the Village, the
approvals granted in Sections 2 and 3 of this Ordinance may, at the sole
discretion of the Village Council, by ordinance duly adopted, be revoked and
become null and void; provided, however, that the Village Council may not so
revoke the approvals granted in Sections 2 and 3 of this Ordinance unless it
first provides the Applicant with two months advance written notice of the
reasons for revocation and an opportunity to be heard at a regular meeting of
the Village Council. In the event of revocation, the development and use of the
Subject Property will be governed solely by the regulations of the applicable
zoning district and the applicable provisions of the Zoning Ordinance, as the
same may, from time to time, be amended. Further, in the event of such
revocation, the Village Manager and Village Attorney are hereby authorized and
directed to bring such zoning enforcement action as may be appropriate under
the circumstances.
   SECTION 7:   AMENDMENT OF SPECIAL USE PERMIT. Any amendments to the
approvals granted in Sections 2 and 3 of this Ordinance that may be requested
by the Applicant after the effective date of this Ordinance may be granted only
pursuant to the procedures, and subject to the standards and limitations,
provided in the Zoning Ordinance.
   SECTION 8:   SEVERABILITY. If any provision of this Ordinance or part
thereof is held invalid by a court of competent jurisdiction, the remaining
provisions of this Ordinance shall remain in full force and effect, and shall
be interpreted, applied, and enforced so as to achieve, as near as may be, the
purpose and intent of this Ordinance to the greatest extent permitted by
applicable law.
   SECTION 9:   EFFECTIVE DATE.
   A.   This Ordinance will be effective only upon the occurrence of all of the
following events:
      1.   Passage by the Village Council in the manner required by law;
      2.   Publication in pamphlet form in the manner required by law; and
      3.   The filing by the Applicant with the Village Clerk of an
Unconditional Agreement and Consent in the form of Exhibit S attached to and,
by this reference, made a part of this Ordinance to accept and abide by each
and all of the terms, conditions, and limitations set forth in this Ordinance
and to indemnify the Village for any claims that may arise in connection with
the approval of this Ordinance.
   B.   In the event that the Applicant does not file with the Village Clerk a
fully executed copy of the unconditional agreement and consent described in
Section 9.A.3 of this Ordinance within 60 days after the date of passage of
this Ordinance by the Village Council, the Village Council shall have the
right, in its sole discretion, to declare this Ordinance null and void and of
no force or effect.
