ORDINANCE NO. M-10-2018
AN ORDINANCE AUTHORIZING THE DISPOSITION OF A SURPLUS VEHICLE OWNED BY THE
VILLAGE OF WINNETKA
WHEREAS, the Village of Winnetka ( “Village” ) is a home rule municipality in
accordance with Article VII, Section 6 of the Constitution of the State of
Illinois of 1970; and
WHEREAS, on February 20, 2018, pursuant to Resolution R-14-2018, the Village
Council authorized the purchase of a vehicle to replace a 2006 Ford Escape
Hybrid known as Public Works vehicle PW2 ( “Vehicle” ); and
WHEREAS, the Vehicle is no longer necessary or useful to the Village; and
WHEREAS, the Village Council desires to authorize the Village Manager to
dispose of Vehicle selling the vehicle at auction or in a manner to be
determined by the Village Manager; and
WHEREAS, the Village Council has determined that it is in the best interests of
the Village to authorize the Village Manager to dispose of the Vehicle as set
forth in this Ordinance;
NOW, THEREFORE, be it ordained by the Council of the Village of Winnetka as
follows:
SECTION 1:  RECITALS. The foregoing recitals are hereby incorporated as the
findings of the Village Council as if fully set forth herein.
SECTION 2: AUTHORIZATION TO DISPOSE OF VEHICLE. Pursuant to the Village’s home
rule authority, the Village Council hereby deems the Vehicle to be no longer
necessary or useful to, or for the best interests of, the Village, and hereby
authorizes the Village Manager, or his designee, to dispose of the Vehicle by
auction or in a manner to be determined by the Village Manager, in his
discretion.
SECTION 3: EXECUTION OF REQUIRED DOCUMENTATION.  The Village President and the
Village Clerk are hereby authorized to execute and attest, on behalf of the
Village, all documents necessary to complete the disposition of the Vehicle
authorized pursuant to Section 2 of this Ordinance.
SECTION 4: EFFECTIVE DATE. This Ordinance will be in full force and effect from
and after its passage, approval, and publication in the manner provided by law.
PASSED this 7th day of August, 2018, pursuant to the following roll call vote:
   AYES:      Trustees Cripe, Dearborn, Lanphier and President Rintz         
   NAYS:   None                              
   ABSENT:   Trustees Myers, Swierk and Wedner                  
APPROVED this 7th day of August, 2018.
                     Signed
                     s/Chris Rintz               
                     Village President
