Elm Street (“ Pre-Development Parking Lot Parcel ”); and
WHEREAS, the Developer (i) desires to acquire from the Village a portion of the
Pre-Development Parking Lot Parcel located to the east of the Developer’s Pre-
Development Property ( “Post-Development Transfer Parcel” ) (the Post-
Development Transfer Parcel, SB Winnetka Property, and SB One Property are,
collectively, the “Subject Property” ), (ii) develop on the Subject Property
three new mixed-use buildings for retail and residential uses and related on-
site improvements ( “Development” ), and (iii) convey to the Village a vertical
portion of the Subject Property; and
WHEREAS, as part of the exchange for the conveyance of the Post-Development
Transfer Parcel to the Developer, the Developer has agreed to reconstruct a
public parking lot ( “Parking Lot” ) on the portion of the Pre-Development
Parking Lot Parcel that the Village will retain ( “Post-Development Parking Lot
Parcel” ); and
   WHEREAS, Ordinance No. M-12-2018, adopted by the Village Council on October
16, 2018 ( "Ordinance" ), grants a special use permit, a certain variation from
the provisions of the Winnetka Zoning Ordinance, and a certificate of
appropriateness to permit the construction of Parking Lot on the Post-
Development Parking Lot Parcel; and
   WHEREAS, Section 10 of the Ordinance provides, among other things, that the
Ordinance will be of no force or effect unless and until the Developer has
filed, within 10 business days following the passage of the Ordinance, its
unconditional agreement and consent to accept and abide by each and all of the
terms, conditions, and limitations set forth in the Ordinance;
NOW, THEREFORE, the Developer does hereby agree and covenant as follows:
1.   The Developer does hereby unconditionally agree to accept, consent to, and
abide by each and all of the terms, conditions, limitations, restrictions, and
provisions of the Ordinance.
2.   The Developer acknowledges that public notices and hearings have been
properly given and held with respect to the adoption of the Ordinance, has
considered the possibility of the revocation provided for in the Ordinance, and
agrees not to challenge any such revocation on the grounds of any procedural
infirmity or a denial of any procedural right.
3.   The Developer acknowledges and agrees that the Village is not and will not
be, in any way, liable for any damages or injuries that may be sustained as a
result of the Village's grant of the variation, special use permit, or
certificate of appropriateness for the Post-Development Parking Lot Parcel or
its adoption of the Ordinance, and that the Village's approvals do not, and
will not, in any way, be deemed to insure the Developer against damage or
injury of any kind and at any time.
4.   The Developer does hereby agree to hold harmless and indemnify the
Village, the Village's corporate authorities, and all Village elected and
appointed officials, officers, employees, agents, representatives, and
attorneys, from any and all claims that may, at any time, be asserted against
any of such parties in connection with the Village's adoption of the Ordinance
granting the variation, special use permit, or certificate of appropriateness
for the Post-Development Parking Lot Parcel.
5.   The Developer hereby agrees to pay all expenses incurred by the Village in
defending itself with regard to any and all of the claims mentioned in this
Unconditional Agreement and Consent. These expenses will include all out-of-
pocket expenses, such as attorneys' and experts' fees, and will also include
the reasonable value of any services rendered by any employees of the Village.
 
