ORDINANCE NO. M-14-2021
AN ORDINANCE ACCEPTING THE TRANSFER OF REAL PROPERTY FROM THE BOARD OF
EDUCATION OF NEW TRIER TOWNSHIP HIGH SCHOOL DISTRICT NO. 203 PURSUANT TO THE
LOCAL GOVERNMENT PROPERTY TRANSFER ACT AND
DEDICATING ESSEX ROAD AS A PUBLIC RIGHT-OF-WAY
(Essex Road)
   WHEREAS, the Village is an Illinois home rule municipal corporation; and
   WHEREAS, the Local Government Property Transfer Act, 50 ILCS 605/0.01 et
seq. ( “Act” ), authorizes a municipality to transfer real property to another
municipality upon such terms as may be agreed by the corporate authorities of
the parties, subject to the requirements of the Act; and
   WHEREAS, the Village and Board of Education ( “Board” ) of New Trier
Township High School District No. 203 ( “School District” ) are municipalities
as defined in Section 1(c) of the Act, 50 ILCS 605/2; and
   WHEREAS, the Board of Education ( “Board” ) of New Trier Township High
School District No. 203 ( “School District” ), Cook County, Illinois, owns a
parcel of property ( “Property” ) known as Essex Road, which is legally
described in Exhibit A, attached hereto, and incorporated herein; and
   WHEREAS, the Village and Board have determined that it is in their best
interests and the best interests of their respective residents to transfer
ownership of the Property from the School District to the Village for public
purposes of the Village, including, without limitation, use of the Property as
a public right-of-way; and
   WHEREAS, the Village desires the School District to transfer the Property to
the Village pursuant to the terms and conditions of the Act and an
intergovernmental agreement attached hereto as Exhibit B ( “Agreement” ); and
   WHEREAS, the Village Council has determined that it is necessary,
appropriate, and in the best interests of the Village to acquire the Property
by transfer from the School District, according to the terms of this Ordinance
and the Agreement;
   NOW, THEREFORE, the Council of the Village of Winnetka does ordain as
follows: 
   SECTION 1:   RECITALS. The foregoing recitals are hereby incorporated into
this section as the findings of the Village Council, as if fully set forth
herein. 
   SECTION 2:   APPROVAL OF AGREEMENT. The Village Council hereby: (i) approves
the Agreement in substantially the form attached as Exhibit B and in a final
form approved by the Village Attorney; and (ii) authorizes the Village
President and Village Manager to take such further actions as may be necessary
to carry out and comply with the Agreement.
   SECTION 3:   AUTHORIZATION TO EXECUTE AGREEMENT. The Village Council hereby
authorizes and directs the Village President and the Village Clerk to execute
and attest, respectively, on behalf of the Village: (i) the final Agreement;
and (ii) any documents necessary to effectuate the transfer of the Property to
the Village in accordance with and pursuant to the terms of the Agreement.
   SECTION 4:   DELIVERY OF ORDINANCE. The Village Clerk is hereby authorized
and directed to deliver a certified copy of this Ordinance to the Board, in
care of the School District’s Superintendent.
   SECTION 5:   DEDICATION OF PROPERTY. Upon the receipt by the Village of a
quit claim deed executed in accordance and pursuant to the satisfaction of the
terms and conditions of the Agreement, the Village President and Village Clerk
are hereby authorized and directed to execute and record against the Property
with the Cook County Clerk Recording Division a plat of dedication in
substantially the form attached as Exhibit C and in a final form approved by
the Village Attorney.
   SECTION 6:   EFFECTIVE DATE. This Ordinance will be in full force and effect
from and after its passage and approval in the manner provided by law.
