EXHIBIT K

UNCONDITIONAL AGREEMENT AND CONSENT
 
TO:   The Village of Winnetka, Illinois ( “Village” ):
WHEREAS, RIC (Winnetka Lincoln) LLC, an Illinois limited liability company (“
Owner ”) is the owner of the properties commonly known as 714-716 Elm Street,
718-732 Elm Street, 736 Elm Street, 740 Elm Street, 511 Lincoln Avenue, and 515
Lincoln Avenue (collectively, “Property” ), which Property is legally described
in Exhibit A attached to this Unconditional Agreement and Consent; and
WHEREAS, the Property is generally located on the southeast corner of Elm
Street and Lincoln Avenue in Winnetka, and is located in the C-2 General Retail
Commercial District and C-2 Overlay District under the; and
WHEREAS, the Property is required to be developed as a planned development in
accordance with Chapter 17.58 of the “Winnetka Zoning Ordinance,” as amended
( “Zoning Code” ); and
   WHEREAS, Ordinance No. M-01-2024, adopted by the Village Council on
_________ __, 2024 ("Ordinance"), grants the Owner approval of its preliminary
development plan and certain exceptions and modifications from provisions of
the Zoning Ordinance to permit Owner to construct and develop a four story
mixed-use building; related parking improvements; and related on-site and off-
site streetscape, landscape, and other public and private improvements
( “Zoning Approvals” ); and
 WHEREAS, Section 15 of the Ordinance provides, among other things, that the
Ordinance will be of no force or effect unless and until the Owner has filed,
within 10 days following the passage of the Ordinance, its unconditional
agreement and consent to accept and abide by each and all of the terms,
conditions, and limitations set forth in the Ordinance;
NOW, THEREFORE, the Owner hereby agrees and covenants as follows:
1.   The Owner hereby unconditionally agrees to accept, consent to, and abide
by each and all of the terms, conditions, limitations, restrictions, and
provisions of the Ordinance.
2.   The Owner acknowledges that public notices and hearings have been properly
given and held with respect to the adoption of the Ordinance and the Zoning
Approvals, has considered the possibility of the revocation provided for in the
Ordinance, and agrees not to challenge any such revocation on the grounds of
any procedural infirmity or a denial of any procedural right.
3.   The Owner acknowledges and agrees that the Village is not and will not be,
in any way, liable for any damages or injuries that may be sustained as a
result of the Village’s granting of the Zoning Approvals or its adoption of the
Ordinance, and that the Village’s approval of the Zoning Approvals does not,
and will not, in any way, be deemed to insure the Owner against damage or
injury of any kind and at any time.
4.   The Owner hereby agrees to hold harmless and indemnify the Village, the
Village’s corporate authorities, and all Village elected and appointed
officials, officers, employees, agents, representatives, and attorneys, from
any and all claims that may, at any time, be asserted against any of such
parties in connection with the Village’s adoption of the Ordinance.
 
IN WITNESS WHEREOF, the Parties have hereunto set their hands on the date first
above written.
 
 
 RIC (ONE WINNETKA) LLC, an Illinois limited liability company
 By: Romspen (Reomaster) Holdings, Inc, a Delaware corporation, its Manager
