EXHIBIT J
License Agreement
TEMPORARY CONSTRUCTION LICENSE AGREEMENT
(Elm Street Parking Lot)
 
   THIS TEMPORARY CONSTRUCTION LICENSE AGREEMENT (“ License Agreement ”) is
made as of this __ day of_________________, 2025, by and between MDG WINNETKA
ONE, LP, an Illinois limited partnership (“ Owner ”) and the VILLAGE OF
WINNETKA, an Illinois home rule municipal corporation (“ Village ”).
   NOW THEREFORE, in consideration of the recitals, mutual covenants, and
agreements set forth herein and other good and valuable consideration, the
receipt and sufficiency of which are hereby acknowledged, the parties do hereby
mutually agree as follows:
SECTION 1.   RECITALS.
A.   Owner is the owner of the properties commonly known as 714-716 Elm Street,
718-732 Elm Street, 736 Elm Street, 740 Elm Street, 511 Lincoln Avenue, and 515
Lincoln Avenue (collectively, “Development Property”), which Development
Property is legally described in Exhibit A attached hereto and incorporated
herein by this reference.
B.   The Development Property is adjacent to and contiguous with a parking lot
owned by the Village located on Elm Street (“Elm Street Parking Lot”), which is
depicted on Exhibit B attached hereto and incorporated herein by this
reference.
C.   Owner desires to demolish the existing buildings on the Development
Property and construct a new four-story mixed-use building with ground floor
commercial space and 59 apartments on the upper level, and related on-site
improvements, including a new ground level parking lot with 39 parking spaces
and an underground parking lot with 111 parking spaces (collectively,
"Development'”).
D.   Due to the density of the Development, Owner has requested that the
Village grant Owner, its contractors, subcontractors, and suppliers a license
to use the portion of the Elm Street Parking Lot designated in Exhibit B
(“Licensed Area”) for the installation of a temporary transformer and for a
construction safety zone, such safety zone shall be fenced off and kept free
from use during demolition of the existing adjacent building on the Development
Property and during portions of the vertical construction of the Development
(collectively, “Licensed Activities”).
E.   Owner and Village desire to make and execute this License Agreement to
grant the Owner a license to conduct the Licensed Activities, and only the
Licensed Activities, within the portion of the Elm Street Parking Lot and
obligate Owner to undertake certain indemnification obligations with respect to
the aforementioned Licensed Activities as more particularly set forth herein;
SECTION 2.   GRANT AND TERM OF LICENSE.
A.   Grant of License. Subject to the terms and conditions set forth in this
License Agreement, the Village hereby grants to the Owner, and the Owner hereby
accepts, a non-exclusive revocable license, for the benefit of the Development
Property, for the Licensed Activities within the Licensed Area (“License”).
Owner may erect construction fencing to secure the Licensed Area during the
term of the License from unlawful entry and to secure the safety of the general
public, which the location, size, and type of fencing must be approved by the
Village’s Director of Community Development. During the extended periods of
time where the Owner does not need to use the safety zone in the Licensed Area,
the Owner must remove the fence from the Elm Street Parking Lot, allowing the
Village to resume the use of the parking spaces for public parking spaces.
B.   Owner’s Obligation to Restore. Owner will make any necessary repairs to
the Licensed Premises damaged by Owner, its subcontractors, suppliers, agents
or employees, to ensure the Elm Street Parking Lot, including the Licensed
Premises, is able to be used for parking, until the Elm Street Parking Lot is
reconstructed.
C.   Limitation of Interest.  Except for the License granted in Subsection A,
Owner does not and will not have any legal, beneficial, or equitable interest,
whether by adverse possession or prescription or otherwise, in any portion of
the Elm Street Parking Lot, or any other Village-owned property or right-of-
way. Specifically, and without limitation of the foregoing, the Owner
acknowledges and agrees that nothing in this License Agreement is to be
interpreted to provide a license to Owner to alter any Village-owned right-of-
way or the Elm Street Parking Lot in any way other than as specifically
provided for herein.
D.   Reservation of Rights. The Village hereby reserves the right to use the
Elm Street Parking Lot, including the Licensed Area, in any manner that will
not prevent, impede, or interfere in any way with the exercise by Owner of the
rights granted pursuant to this License Agreement. The Village will have the
right to grant other non-exclusive licenses or easements, including, without
limitation, licenses or easements for utility purposes, over, along, upon, or
across the Elm Street Parking Lot. The Village further reserves its right of
full and normal access to the Elm Street Parking Lot for the maintenance of any
existing or future utility located thereon.
E.   Liens. Owner hereby represents and warrants that it will take all
necessary action to keep all portions of the Elm Street Parking Lot and all
other property owned by the Village free and clear of all liens, claims, and
demands, including without limitation mechanic's liens, in connection with any
work performed by Owner or its agents.
F.   Term. The License granted pursuant to this Section 2.A will expire upon
the expiration, revoking, or termination of Owner’s building permit for the
Development.
G.   Indemnity. Owner agrees to indemnify, defend, save and hold harmless the
Village from and against any and all liability, claims, judgments, loss, cost,
damage or expense (collectively, “Claims”) suffered or incurred by the Village,
including without limitation reasonable attorneys’ and experts’ fees and court
costs, due to third party claims for personal injury, death, or property damage
caused by any activities of the Owner or its employees, agents, Owners, tenants
or invitees in the Elm Street Parking Lot, including the construction,
existence, use, operation, repair, maintenance and replacement of the
Development and not caused by the sole negligence of the Village. Owner will
maintain a commercial general liability policy with limits of $2,000,000 per
occurrence and general aggregate, the limits of which may be met by a
combination of primary and umbrella or excess policies. The Village of Winnetka
is to be included as an additional insured as regards claims arising from the
Owner’s use of the Elm Street Parking Lot and shall be named as a cancellation
notice recipient on the commercial general liability policy. Owner must provide
the Village with a copy of the insurance certificate for the commercial general
liability policy prior to installation of the temporary transformer and
construction fencing as well as any amendments or renewals to the policy.
H.   Entire Agreement. This License Agreement supplements that certain
Development Agreement which was approved by the Village’s Village Council on
April 2, 2024 by the adoption of Resolution No. R-25, 2024 (“Development
Agreement”) and various easement agreements entered into by the Owner and the
Village pertaining to the Development. The provisions of this License Agreement
are not meant to supersede but to supplement those agreements. In the event of
a conflict, the provisions of the Development Agreement will control.
I.   Counterparts. This License Agreement may be executed in counterparts, each
of which shall be deemed to be an original and all of which shall together
constitute one and the same instrument.
J.   Governing Law. This License Agreement shall be interpreted in accordance
with the laws of the State of Illinois.
