Street from 30 feet to 19.5 feet, requiring a variation of 10.5 feet; and
WHEREAS, the Owner filed an application for: (i) approval of a final plat of
subdivision for the Proposed Subdivision (“Final Plat”); (ii) a special use
permit to allow the Proposed Subdivision which consolidation results in a lot
that is greater than two times the minimum required lot size by 24,909 square
feet and minimum average lot width for a corner lot by 30 feet in the R-
5 District pursuant to Chapter 17.56 of the Zoning Ordinance and Section
16.12.010.D.10 of the Village Code (“Special Use Permit”); (iii) variations
from Sections 17.30.030.A, 17.30.040, and 17.30.050 of the Zoning Ordinance to
permit the construction of the Proposed Additions and Improvements
(collectively, the “Variations” ); (iv) an amendment to the Original Special
Use Permit pursuant to Sections 17.12.020 and Chapter 17.56 of the Zoning
Ordinance to allow the construction and operation of the Proposed Additions and
Improvements on the Subject Property within the R-5 District ( “Special Use
Permit Amendment” ); and (v) a certificate of appropriateness pursuant to
Section 15.40.010 of the Winnetka Village Code (“Village Code”) (the Final
Plat, Special Use Permit, Variations, Special Use Permit Amendment, and
Certificate of Appropriateness are, collectively, the “Requested Relief” ); and
   WHEREAS, Ordinance M-06-2025, adopted by the Village Council on June 3, 2025
( “Ordinance” ), approved the Requested Relief; and
 
   WHEREAS, Section 14 of the Ordinance provides, among other things, that the
Ordinance will be of no force or effect unless and until the Owner has filed,
within 60 days following the passage of the Ordinance, its unconditional
agreement and consent to accept and abide by each and all of the terms,
conditions, and limitations set forth in the Ordinance;
 
 
   NOW, THEREFORE, the Owner does hereby agree and covenant as follows:
1.   The Owner hereby unconditionally agrees to accept, consent to, and abide by each and
all of the terms, conditions, limitations, restrictions, and provisions of the Ordinance.
2.   The Owner acknowledges that public notices and hearings have been properly given and
held with respect to the adoption of the Ordinance, has considered the possibility of the
revocation provided for in the Ordinance, and agrees not to challenge any such revocation
on the grounds of any procedural infirmity or a denial of any procedural right.
3.   The Owner acknowledges and agrees that the Village is not and will not be, in any
way, liable for any damages or injuries that may be sustained as a result of the Village’s
grant of the Variation for the Subject Property or its adoption of the Ordinance, and that
the Village’s approvals do not, and will not, in any way, be deemed to insure the Owner
against damage or injury of any kind and at any time.
4.   The Owner hereby agrees to hold harmless and indemnify the Village, the Village’s
corporate authorities, and all Village elected and appointed officials, officers,
employees, agents, representatives, and attorneys, from any and all claims that may, at
any time, be asserted against any of such parties in connection with the Village’s
adoption of the Ordinance granting the Variation for the Subject Property.
5.   The Owner hereby agrees to pay all expenses incurred by the Village in defending
itself with regard to any and all of the claims mentioned in this Unconditional Agreement
and Consent. These expenses will include all out-of-pocket expenses, such as attorneys’
and experts’ fees, and will also include the reasonable value of any services rendered by
any employees of the Village.
