ORDINANCE NO. MC-203-98
AN ORDINANCE IMPOSING A MUNICIPAL TELECOMUNICATIONS TAX
WHEREAS, Section 8-11-17 of the Illinois Municipal Code, 65 ILCS 5/8-11-117,
authorizes the Council of the Village of Winnetka to impose a tax on the
privilege of sending or receiving intrastate and interstate telecommunications
by persons within the Village of Winnetka at a rate not to exceed 5% of the
gross charge for such telecommunications purchased from a retailer; and
WHEREAS, the Council of the Village of Winnetka desires to impose such a tax to
the extent authorized by the Illinois Municipal Code.
NOW THEREFORE, the Council of the Village of Winnetka do ordain as follows:
SECTION 1: Chapter 33 of the Winnetka Village Code, entitled “Occupation Taxes”
is hereby amended by adding a new Section 33.05, which shall be entitled,
“Municipal Telecommunications Tax,” and shall provide as follows:
33.05   MUNICIPAL TELECOMMUNICATIONS TAX.
   (a)   Imposed; Rate. A tax is hereby imposed on any or all of the following
acts or privileges:
      1.   The act or privilege of originating in the Village or receiving in
the Village intrastate telecommunications by a person at a rate not to exceed
5% of the gross charge for such telecommunications purchased at retail from a
retailer by the person.
      2.   The act or privilege of originating in the Village or receiving in
the Village interstate telecommunications by a person for such
telecommunications purchased at retail from a retailer by the person. To
prevent actual multi-state taxation of the act or privilege that is subject to
taxation under this subparagraph, any taxpayer shall be allowed a credit
against any tax imposed under this subparagraph, in the manner and to the
extent provided in 65 ILCS 5/8-11-17(a)(2).
      The tax imposed under this section shall be at a rate of 5% of the gross
charge for such service purchased at retail by the person being taxed, and
shall be charged, collected and remitted to the Village in accordance with the
provisions of 65 ILCS 5/8-11-17 and all subsections thereto. The tax imposed
under this section shall not be imposed to the extent the act or privilege may
not, under the Constitution and statutes of the United States, be made the
subject of taxation by the Village.
   (b)   Report to be Filed. Every retailer required by this ordinance to
charge, collect and remit the tax imposed by this section shall file with the
Village, on or before the last calendar day of each month, a report for the
previous calendar month of all gross receipts subject to the tax imposed by
this section, the amount of the tax imposed, the amount of the commission which
the retailer has retained as reimbursement for the expense of collecting the
tax, and the amount of tax remitted to the Village.
   (c)   Time of Payment. At the time the report required by this section is
filed, the retailer filing the report shall pay to the Village the amount of
tax imposed for the previous calendar month pursuant to this section, less the
commission permitted by 65 ILCS 5/8-11-(b) as reimbursement for collecting the
tax.
   (d)   Nature of Tax. The tax imposed by this section is a tax on the acts
and privileges described herein and shall be in addition to, not in lieu of,
the payment of money or the furnishing of products or services to the Village
by the retailer as compensation for the use of the Village=s streets, alleys,
utility poles, utility easements or other public places used by the retailer in
for the installation or maintenance of its equipment or for the operation of
its business.
   (e)   Definitions. For the purpose of the taxes authorized by this section,
the following terms shall be defined as in 65 ILCS 5/8-11-17(c): amount paid,
gross charge, interstate telecommunications, intrastate telecommunications,
person, purchase at retail, retailer, retailer maintaining a place of business
in this State, sale at retail, service address, taxpayer, telecommunications.
   (f)   Exceptions for Resellers. If a person, who originates or receives
telecommunications in the Village claims to be a reseller of such
telecommunications, the person shall apply to the Village for a resale number.
The applicant shall state facts which will show the Village why the applicant
is not liable for tax under this section on any of the purchases subject to the
tax, and shall furnish such additional information as the Village may
reasonably require. Upon approval of the application, the Village shall assign
a resale number to the applicant and shall certify such number to the
applicant. The Village may cancel any number which is obtained through
misrepresentation, which is used to send or receive any telecommunications tax-
free when such actions in fact are not for resale, or which no longer applies
because of the persons having discontinued the making of resales.
   (g)   Penalties. Any taxpayer who fails to make a return, or who makes a
fraudulent return, or who willfully violates any other provision of this
section shall be subject to a fine of not less than one hundred dollars ($100)
nor more than seven hundred fifty dollars ($750), and in addition shall be
liable in a civil action for the amount of tax due, plus interest and costs.
SECTION 2: This ordinance shall be in full force and effect from and after its
passage, approval, and posting.
   PASSED and approved this 17th day of March, 1998.
AYES:      Trustees Derning, Duhl, Hilton, Lanphier, Lien and Meuer
