Posted: March 18, 1998
ORDINANCE NO. MC-204-98
AN ORDINANCE AMENDING THE PROVISIONS OF CHAPTER 12 OF THE WINNETKA VILLAGE CODE
PERTAINING TO GASOLINE - POWERED LEAF BLOWERS
WHEREAS, Section 11-60-2 of the Illinois Municipal Code authorizes
municipalities to define, prevent and abate nuisances; and
WHEREAS, the Village Council have previously enacted paragraph 20 of
subparagraph (d) of Section 12.02 of the Winnetka Village Code to declare that
the use of gasoline-powered leaf blowers at certain times is a public nuisance;
and
WHEREAS, a question has arisen as to whether electric leaf blowers connected to
portable gasoline-powered generators are gasoline-powered leaf blowers for
purposes of said Section 12.02(d)20; and
WHEREAS, it has been and continues to be the intent of the Village Council to
include any leaf-blowers powered by gasoline, whether directly or indirectly,
within the scope of said Section 12.02(d)20; and
WHEREAS, the Village Council desire to amend Section 12.02(d)20 to clarify that
the term “gasoline-powered leaf blowers” includes electric leaf blowers
connected to portable gasoline-powered electric generators.
NOW, THEREFORE, the Council of the Village of Winnetka do ordain as follows:
SECTION 1: That the recitals stated in the foregoing preamble to this Ordinance
are adopted by the Council of the Village of Winnetka as its findings.
SECTION 2: Paragraph 20 of Subsection (d), of Section 12.02 of Chapter 12 of
the Winnetka Village Code “Nuisances”, is amended to provide as follows:
   20.   The use of any gasoline-powered leaf blower, whether backpack-mounted,
wheel-mounted or hand held, which include electric leaf blowers connected to
portable gasoline-powered electric generators, between June 1 and October 1 of
each year. From October 1 of any year through June 1 of the next year, the use
of any such leaf blowers before the hour of 8:00 a.m. and after the hour of 7:
00 p.m. on Mondays through Fridays, inclusive, and before the hours of 9:00
a.m. and after 6:00 p.m. on Saturdays, Sundays and holidays. In the event of a
storm or other emergency, upon determining that it is in the best interests of
the safety and welfare of the village to use gasoline-powered leaf blowers in
clean-up or restoration activities, the village manager may waive the
enforcement of the foregoing restrictions. Nothing in this paragraph shall be
construed to deem lawn maintenance activities on golf courses or on publicly
owned properties as nuisances, whenever conducted.
SECTION 13 : This Ordinance shall take effect immediately upon passage,
approval and posting.
   ADOPTED this 7th day of April, 1998, pursuant to the following roll call
vote:
AYES:      Trustees Derning, Hilton, Lanphier, Lien and Meuer
NAYS:   None
ABSENT:   Trustee Duhl
Signed:
s/s Louise A. Holland
Village President
Countersigned:
s/s Douglas G. Williams
Village Clerk
Introduced: March 17, 1998
Posted: March 18, 1998
Passed and Approved: April 7, 1998
Posted: April 8, 1998
ORDINANCE NO. MC-205-98 (not adopted)
ORDINANCE NO. MC-206-98
AN ORDINANCE AMENDING THE BUILDING CODE AND FIRE PREVENTION CODE AS THEY
PERTAIN TO SMOKE DETECTORS
THE COUNCIL OF THE VILLAGE OF WINNETKA do ordain:
SECTION 1 : Subsection (f), “Dwelling Code Exclusions,” of Section 23.39,
“Building Code, Mechanical Code, Dwelling Code and Energy Code,” of the
Winnetka Building Code, Chapter 23 of the Winnetka Village Code, is hereby
amended by adding a new paragraphs 8, which shall provide as follows:
      8.   Section 316, Smoke Detectors.
SECTION 2: Section 26.04, “Automatic Alarm and Fire Detection System
Requirements; Telephone Alarms,” of Chapter 26 of the Winnetka Village Code,
“Fire Prevention,” is hereby amended by changing its title to read: “Automatic
Alarm and Fire Detection System Requirements; Telephone Alarms; Smoke
Detectors.”
SECTION 3: Subsection (a) of Section 26.04, “Automatic Alarm and Fire Detection
System Requirements; Telephone Alarms; Smoke Detectors,” of Chapter 26 of the
Winnetka Village Code, “Fire Prevention,” is hereby amended to provide as
follows:
   (a)   An automatic alarm and fire detection system installed in accordance
with the standards set forth in NFPA Publication 72, National Fire Alarm Code,
1996 Edition, shall be installed in any building used for an occupancy
described in subsections (a) through (g) of Section 26.17 of this Chapter and
with respect to which the installation of an automatic fire extinguisher system
is not required by reason of a specific exception provided in Section 26.17.
SECTION 4: Section 26.04, “Automatic Alarm and Fire Detection System
Requirements; Telephone Alarms; Smoke Detectors,” of Chapter 26 of the Winnetka
Village Code, “Fire Prevention,” is hereby amended by adding a new subsection
(d), which shall provide as follows:
   (d)   Residential smoke detectors shall be supplied and installed in
accordance with the “Illinois Smoke Detector Act,” 425 ILCS 60/1, et seq.,
except that an approved smoke detector shall also be installed in each sleeping
room. As used in the Illinois Smoke Detector Act, the term “substantially
remodelled” shall mean the installation of new electrical wiring throughout the
dwelling unit regardless of the cost of such wiring, and any work to repair,
restore, renovate, remodel or increase the size of a dwelling unit if the cost
of such work exceeds 50% of the value of the existing dwelling unit.
Notwithstanding any exceptions stated in the Illinois Smoke Detector Act to the
contrary, the smoke detectors required for any newly constructed addition to a
dwelling unit shall be permanently wired into the addition’s AC power line, and
if more than one detector is required to be installed in the addition the
detectors shall be wired so that the actuation of one detector will actuate all
the detectors in the addition.  
SECTION 5 :   This Ordinance shall take effect immediately upon passage,
approval and posting.
   ADOPTED this 5th day of May, 1998, pursuant to the following roll call vote:
AYES:      Trustees Derning, Hilton, Lanphier, and Lien
NAYS:   None
ABSENT:   Trustees Duhl and Meuer
Signed:
s/s Louise A. Holland
Village President
Countersigned:
s/s Douglas G. Williams
Village Clerk
Introduced: April 21, 1998
Posted: April 22, 1998
Passed and Approved: May 5, 1998
