ORDINANCE NO. MC-207-98
ORDINANCE AMENDING CHAPTER 41 OF THE WINNETKA VILLAGE CODE TO CLARIFY THE
AUTHORITY OF THE VILLAGE MANAGER AS IT PERTAINS TO PARKING REGULATIONS
WHEREAS, the Council of the Village of Winnetka have previously enacted
ordinances which authorize the Village Manager to impose parking restrictions
on village streets and in village off-street parking facilities; and
WHEREAS, the Council of the Village of Winnetka desire to clarify that the
scope of that authority includes requiring permits for parking on public
streets, establishing categories of parking permits and limiting use of village
owned parking lots to certain classifications of users,
NOW THEREFORE, the Council of the Village of Winnetka do ordain as follows:
SECTION 1:  That the recitals stated in the foregoing preamble to this
Ordinance are adopted by the Council of the Village of Winnetka as its
findings.
SECTION 2:  Subsection (b) of section 41.22, “Parking Authority of Village
Manager,” of Chapter 41 of the Winnetka Village Code, “Traffic”, is hereby
amended to provide as follows:
   (b)   Restricted Parking on Certain Streets. The village manager may
designate either side, or both sides, or any portion of either side, of any
street as a restricted parking area, which restrictions may include such
limitations as the duration of parking, the requirement of permits, and the
time of day parking is permitted or restricted. The village manager shall
determine the time of the day any such parking restriction shall be effective
as well as the duration of time allowed for continuous vehicular parking, and
shall cause appropriate signs to be erected and maintained in such areas
designating the effective time of day of such parking restriction as well as
the duration of time that continuous vehicular parking is allowed. Such
designation shall be evidenced by the physical presence of such signs or
legends or notices on or near the parking lane of the streets or portions
thereof where such restrictions are to be effective. When such signs are
erected, no person shall park a vehicle in violation of this section.
SECTION 3 : Subsection (a) of section 41.26, “Parking in Village Off-Street
Parking Lots or Facilities,” of Chapter 41 of the Winnetka Village Code,
“Traffic”, is hereby amended to provide as follows:
   (a)   The village manager may restrict the parking of vehicles in any
village off-street parking lot or lots or facility or facilities to certain
hours of the day or night or to certain days of the week and restrict the
duration of continuous parking therein; limit authorized parking to residents
of the village and to vehicles bearing a village motor license; restrict
authorized parking to persons parking for a particular purpose or purposes
including, but not limited to parking for commuters, employees of local
businesses, students and school staff; and impose restrictions based upon any
combination of the foregoing authorized restrictions or limitations.
SECTION 4 : This Ordinance shall take effect immediately upon passage, approval
and posting.
   ADOPTED this 19th day of May, 1998, pursuant to the following roll call
vote:
AYES:      Trustees Derning, Duhl, Hilton, Lanphier, and Meuer
NAYS:   None
ABSENT:   Trustee Lien
Signed:
s/s Louise A. Holland
Village President
Countersigned:
s/s Douglas G. Williams
Village Clerk
Introduced: May 5, 1998
Posted: May 6, 1998
Passed and Approved: May 19, 1998
