ORDINANCE NO. MC-210-98
AN ORDINANCE IMPOSING A MORATORIUM ON THE ISSUANCE OF CERTAIN BUILDING PERMITS
AND THE PROCESSING OF APPLICATIONS FOR ZONING RELIEF IN THE C-1 COMMERCIAL
ZONING DISTRICT
WHEREAS, the Village of Winnetka is in the process of developing a twenty year
comprehensive plan, which has been the subject of extensive work by the
Winnetka Plan Commission, with the assistance of a planning consultant retained
by the Village in 1997; and
WHEREAS, the work of the Plan Commission, assisted by the Village’s planning
consultant, has resulted in preliminary goals and objectives for the Indian
Hill business district which, if accepted by the Village Council, could lead to
amendments to development standards and types of uses permitted in the C-1
(Limited Retail) Commercial Zoning District, which is located in Indian Hill;
and
WHEREAS, on February 3, 1998, the council of the Village of Winnetka adopted
ordinance number MC-200-98, which amended the building height and parking
regulations for the C-1 and C-2 zoning districts; and
WHEREAS, the Village of Winnetka is considering proposals for consultant
services assistance in developing design standards for commercial and multi-
family zoning districts; and
WHEREAS, the Council of the Village of Winnetka have determined that
redevelopment of property within the C-1 Zoning Districts prior to the
completion of the final plan for that district, by issuing demolition or
building permits, by rezoning property or by granting special uses or
variations to allow the construction of new buildings or the expansion of
existing buildings, could hinder the ability of the Village of Winnetka to
implement the plan; and
WHEREAS, the Council of the Village of Winnetka have further determined that it
is in the best interests of the Village and its residents that the status quo
of the C-1 Zoning District be preserved and that any further applications for
demolition permits, building permits, or zoning relief to allow the
redevelopment of any property in the C-1 (Limited Retail) Zoning District
through the demolition or expansion of any existing building or the
construction of any new building not be processed until the Village has had the
opportunity to receive, consider, and act on the pending studies and reports as
they pertain to the C-1 (Limited Retail) Commercial Zoning District; and
WHEREAS, the Council of the Village of Winnetka have determined that it will
take approximately six months for the Village Council to receive, consider and
begin acting on the final recommendations of the Plan Commission regarding the
Indian Hill business district; and
WHEREAS, on August 18, 1998, on due notice thereof, the Winnetka Village
Council, sitting as a Committee of the Whole, conducted a public hearing to
consider the imposition of a moratorium on the processing of applications for
zoning relief, demolition permits, or building permits for new buildings or
building expansions in the C-1 (Limited Retail) Commercial Zoning Districts.
NOW, THEREFORE, the Council of the Village of Winnetka do ordain:
SECTION 1: That the foregoing preambles to this ordinance are hereby adopted by
the Council of the Village of Winnetka as its findings, as if fully set forth
herein.
SECTION 2: That pending the Plan Commission’s completion of its final
recommendations pertaining to the Indian Hill business district and the Village
Council’s consideration of those recommendations and enactment of any resulting
amendments to the Zoning Ordinance, the Department of Community Development is
hereby directed not to process any applications for zoning relief, demolition
permits, or building permits for new buildings or building expansions in the C-
1 (Limited Retail) Commercial Zoning Districts of the Village.
SECTION 3: That the moratorium on development in the C-1 (Limited Retail)
Commercial Zoning District imposed pursuant to Section 2 of this ordinance
shall expire 6 months after the date of the adoption of this ordinance.
SECTION 4: That this Ordinance shall be in full force and effect from and after
its passage, approval, and posting.
Passed and approved this 18th day of August, 1998.
