         c.    Up to 64 square feet of the aggregate floor area of all bay
windows and chimneys that form part of the exterior building line;
         d.    The floor area under any dormer that is no more than 6 feet wide
and is set in at least 3.5 feet from the gable end walls, provided that the
total width of all dormers does not exceed 25% of the length of the roof on
which they area located.
         e.    The first 50 square feet of the aggregate floor area of a
detached storage shed, playhouse, walled enclosures for refuse containers or
swimming pool equipment, or similar enclosed structures, provided they are
located in the rear quarter of the lot.
      5.    Notwithstanding the foregoing, any zoning lot consisting of a
single, legal, nonconforming lot that has a lot area of less than 7,260 square
feet as the result of the acquisition or condemnation of a portion of the rear
yard of the lot for a public purpose, shall be entitled to an additional 400
square feet of gross floor area on the lot, provided that such additional floor
area permitted by this paragraph shall be in lieu of, and not in addition to,
the additional floor area permitted pursuant to subparagraph 4a of this
subsection.
      6.    Maximum FAR. Notwithstanding the allowances and exclusions
permitted in the foregoing paragraphs, under no circumstances shall the
resulting FAR for any lot exceed 0.50 (50%).
SECTION 62: That subsection (h), “Set Back,” of Section 22.07A of the Winnetka
Zoning Ordinance, R-1 Single-Family Residential District Regulations, Chapter
22 of the Winnetka Village Code, is hereby amended by changing the second
paragraph to provide as follows:
   On corner lots, there shall be a minimum corner yard set back equal to the
set back established in the preceding paragraph, except that the regulation
shall not reduce the width of the buildable area as measured from the minimum
required side yard to less than 60 percent of the average width of the lot, and
shall not reduce the length of the buildable area as measured from the minimum
required rear yard to less than 50 percent of the maximum depth of the lot.
SECTION 63: That Section 22.07A of the Winnetka Zoning Ordinance, R-1 Single-
Family Residential District Regulations, Chapter 22 of the Winnetka Village
Code, is hereby amended by adding a new subsection (q) “Garages,” which shall
provide as follows:
   (q)    Garages.
      1.   Front-facing Garage Doors. Garage door widths may not exceed 33
percent of the lot width or 18 feet, whichever is less, provided that no
individual door shall extend more than 9 feet when facing the front yard. (MC-
160-96) (08/16/96)
      2.   Width of Attached Garages. No attached garage with garage doors that
face a front yard or corner yard shall exceed the greater of 50 percent of the
front building line or 22 feet.
      3.   Location of Attached Garages. An attached garage shall be permitted
as the lowest story of the principal building provided that the garage doors
are not a part of the front building elevation of the principal building.
SECTION 64: That Section 22.15, “Exceptions,” of the Winnetka Zoning Ordinance,
Chapter 22 of the Winnetka Village Code, is hereby amended to provide as
follows:
22.15   EXCEPTIONS.
   The foregoing requirements shall be subject to the following exceptions:
   (a)    Permitted Obstructions in Required Yards and Courts. The following
buildings and other structures shall not be considered to be obstructions when
located in the required yards or courts specified:
      1.    In all required yards and required inner and outer courts:
         a.    Open patios, terraces and steps with associated landings below
the first floor level and which are not roofed over;
         b.    Temporary awnings and temporary canopies with temporary
supports, whether or not above open terraces or patios;
         c.    Cornices, sills, belt course, eaves, gutters, downspouts and
ornamental features projecting 18 inches or less into a yard;
         d.    Chimneys and flues projecting 18 inches or less into a yard and
not exceeding in the aggregate 7 feet in length;
         e.    Statuary;
         f.    Flag poles;
         g.    Signs permitted under the Winnetka Village Code, as amended;
         h.    Driveways;
         i.    Fences, walls, arbors and trellises not exceeding 6-1/2 feet
above natural grade (except that fences, walls, arbors and trellises not
exceeding 8 feet above natural grade may be erected and maintained if they are
located along the contiguous rear or side lot lines between commercial and
single-family or multiple-family residential zoning districts) and not
extending within 10 feet of the intersection of a driveway and sidewalk or
within 25 feet of the intersection of the street line of two intersecting
streets unless the visibility at right angles to the surface of such fence or
wall be reduced by not more than 10 percent;
         j.    Poles, towers, conduits, vaults, pipelines, laterals or any
similar distribution equipment of a public utility nature, whether municipal or
investor-owned;
         k.    Bay windows projecting 24 inches or less into a required front
yard, and bay windows projecting 18 inches or less into any other required
yard, provided such bay window shall not exceed 7 feet in length and no more
than one bay window may encroach upon a side yard. (MC-157-96) (4/2/96)
      2.    In required side yards:
         a.    Exterior doorway entrances, roofed but not enclosed, projecting
3-1/2 feet or less into a yard and having a horizontal projected area within
the yard of 50 square feet or less;
         b.    Accessory buildings, but only that portion lying within the rear
25 percent of the depth of the lot;
         c.    Decks and/or air conditioning units, provided that a minimum
side yard of 6 feet is maintained within the R-5, R-4 and R-3 Single-Family
Residential District and 12 feet in the R-2 Single-Family Residential District
(decks and/or air conditioning units shall not be considered to be permitted
obstructions in any district other than the aforesaid single-family residential
districts);
         d.    Open parking areas (including a parking slab) not covered by a
roof or roof structure, temporary or permanent, and not surrounded by a fence
or wall exceeding 6-1/2 feet in height.
         e.    In-ground swimming pools that are accessory uses to single-
family family residences located in the R-5, R-4, R-3 or R-2 Single-Family
Residential Districts, provided that a minimum side yard of 6 feet is
maintained in the R-5, R-4 and R-3 Single-Family Residential Districts and that
a minimum side yard of 12 feet is maintained in the R-2 Single-Family
Residential Districts. (MC-178-97) (4/8/97)
      3.    In required front yards and corner yard:
         a.    Exterior doorway entrances, roofed but not enclosed and having a
horizontal projected area within the yard of 60 square feet or less;
         b.    Basketball standards. (MC-157-96) (4/2/96)
         c.    Where an average front set back applies, front porches may
extend up to 8 feet into the average set back, provided that any extension into
the minimum set back shall not exceed the limits established in subparagraph a,
above.
      4.    In required rear yards:
         a.    Accessory buildings;
         b.    Gym and play equipment;
         c.    Swimming pools;
         d.    Tennis courts;
         e.    Open parking areas (including a parking slab) not covered by a
roof or roof structure, temporary or permanent, and not surrounded by a fence
or wall exceeding 6-1/2 feet in height.
         f.    Satellite receiving dishes, provided that they comply with all
other applicable regulations of the zoning districts in which they are located.
(MC-157-96) (4/2/96)
SECTION 65: That all zoning interpretations that conflict with or are otherwise
inconsistent with the provisions of this Ordinance are hereby rescinded.
SECTION 66: The several provisions and regulations of this ordinance are hereby
declared to be severable. If any court of competent jurisdiction declares any
provision or regulation of this ordinance to be invalid, such declaration shall
not affect the validity of any other provision or regulation of this ordinance
not specifically included in the court's decision. If any court of competent
jurisdiction declares any provision or regulation of this ordinance to be
invalid as applied to any particular case or individual, such declaration shall
not affect the application of such provision or regulation to any other case or
individual not specifically included in the court's decision.
SECTION 67: This Ordinance shall take effect immediately upon passage, approval
and posting, or May 1, 1999 whichever is later.
   ADOPTED this 20th day of April, 1999, pursuant to the following roll call
vote:
   AYES: Trustees Derning, Meuer, Lanphier, Lien, Hilton, Duhl
