ORDINANCE NO. MC-222-99 (Void)
ORDINANCE NO. MC-223-99
AN ORDINANCE AMENDING CHAPTERS 9 AND 23 OF THE WINNETKA VILLAGE CODE
ESTABLISHING A POLICY TO REQUIRE THE INSTALLATION OF TEMPORARY ELECTRIC
SERVICES
WHEREAS, electric power is necessary for the construction of new buildings and
remodeling where the electric service has been removed; and
WHEREAS, Village staff has observed both the use of electric generators and the
use of electric extension cords connected to neighboring properties as means of
providing electricity at construction sites; and
WHEREAS, the unauthorized use of electricity from other properties constitutes
theft of electricity; and
WHEREAS, the noise caused by electric generators to provide electric service
disturbs the tranquility of the neighborhood and constitutes a nuisance; and
WHEREAS, requiring a temporary supply of electricity to construction sites will
eliminate both the nuisance caused by electric generators and the unauthorized
use of electric service; and
WHEREAS, the Village Council have determined that it is in the best interest of
the Village of Winnetka that all construction sites have utility provided
electric service on site; and
NOW, THEREFORE, be it resolved by the Council of the Village of Winnetka as
follows:
SECTION 1: That the foregoing recitals are hereby adopted by the Council of the
Village of Winnetka as its findings.
SECTION 2: That Chapter 9 of the Winnetka Village Code, “Electric Service,” is
hereby amended by adding a new Section 9.20, which shall be entitled,
“Electricity At Construction Sites,” and shall provide as follows:
9.20   ELECTRICITY AT CONSTRUCTION SITES.
   Except as provided in Section 23.22 of the Winnetka Building Code,
electrical service for all construction sites shall be provided through a
temporary electric service connection the Village’s electric distribution
system. Temporary electric service shall be billed at the rate applicable to
the use specified in the building permit. The use of electric generators and
the drawing of electricity from adjoining properties is expressly prohibited.
SECTION 3: That Section 22, “Construction Noise,” of the Winnetka Building
Code, Chapter 23 of the Winnetka Village Code, is hereby amended to provide as
follows:
   (a)    Permitted Hours of Construction. In addition to the provisions of
this code relating to nuisances, and without limiting any other provision of
this code, it shall be unlawful for any person to permit or engage in any
construction activity, or to operate or permit the operation of power equipment
such as any pile driver, power shovel, pneumatic hammer or derrick, or to
operate or permit the operation of any motor vehicles in relation to any such
activities at any location in the village, before 9:00 a.m. and after 6:00 p.m.
on any Saturday, Sunday, or holiday, or before 7:00 a.m. and after 7:00 p.m. on
all other days, except as hereinafter provided.
   (b)    Electric Generators. Except for public works projects being performed
on or in any public right-of-way by or on behalf of the Village or another
governmental entity, the use of portable electric generators in construction
activity at any time is prohibited.
   (c)    Exceptions. The director or the director=s designee may issue a
written permit temporarily allowing either work during an otherwise prohibited
time or the use of a portable electric generator if the director or the
director=s designee finds that an emergency exists or that such work is
necessary to correct or prevent an unsafe condition, or if the village manager
determines that such work is necessary to preserve or protect the public
health, safety or welfare, provided that any such temporary permit shall be
granted only for a specified scope of work and for the period of time that the
emergency or other circumstance giving rise to the need for such permit
continues. The director or director’s designee may issue a written permit
allowing the use of a portable electric generator during permitted working
hours for no more than 5 days if the director or director’s designee find that
the construction activity requires the temporary disconnection of service from
the Village’s electric distribution system.
   (d)   Penalties. In addition to any other penalties provided in this code, a
violation of this section shall constitute a sufficient basis for the
revocation of any permit issued under the provisions of this code.
SECTION 4: This Ordinance shall take effect immediately upon passage, approval
and posting.
   ADOPTED this 6th day of April, 1999, pursuant to the following roll call
vote:
AYES:      Trustees Derning, Duhl, Hilton, Lanphier, Lien and Meuer
NAYS:   None
ABSENT:   None
Signed:
s/s Louise A. Holland
Village President
Countersigned:
s/s Douglas G. Williams
Village Clerk
Introduced: March 2, 1999
Posted: March 3, 199
Passed and Approved: April 6, 1999
Posted: April 7, 1999
ORDINANCE NO. MC-224-99 (Void)
ORDINANCE NO. MC-225-99
AN ORDINANCE AMENDING SECTION 41.18 OF THE WINNETKA VILLAGE CODE AS IT PERTAINS
TO PROHIBITED PARKING
WHEREAS, citations for violations of the parking regulations of the Winnetka
Village Code are issued and tracked through a computerized process; and
WHEREAS, citations for violations of parking regulations in the Illinois Motor
Vehicle Code must be issued and tracked manually; and
WHEREAS, the Council of the Village of Winnetka have determined that parking on
public sidewalks and parking so as to obstruct sidewalks and driveways should
be prohibited by the Winnetka Village Code in order to facilitate the issuance
and processing of citations for such violations as well to assure the accuracy
of the Village’s records.
NOW, THEREFORE, the Council of the Village of Winnetka do ordain as follows:
SECTION 1: That the foregoing recitals are hereby incorporated as the findings
of the Council of the Village of Winnetka, as if fully set forth herein.
SECTION 2: That Section 41.18, “Prohibited Parking,” of Chapter 41 of the
Winnetka Village Code, “Traffic,” is hereby amended by adding new subsections
(f) and (g), which shall provide as follows:
   (f)    Obstruction of Sidewalks. No person shall park a vehicle, whether on
public or private property, so as to encroach upon or otherwise obstruct any
portion of a sidewalk or parkway, unless the sidewalk has been marked and
signed as a permitted parking area.
   (g)    Obstruction of Driveways. No person shall park a vehicle whether on
public or private property, so as to encroach upon or otherwise obstruct access
to a public or private driveway.
SECTION 3: This Ordinance shall take effect immediately upon passage, approval
and posting.
   ADOPTED this 16th day of March, 1999, pursuant to the following roll call
vote:
AYES:      Trustees Derning, Hilton, Lanphier, Lien and Meuer
NAYS:   None
ABSENT:   Trustee Duhl
Signed:
s/s Louise A. Holland
Village President
Countersigned:
s/s Douglas G. Williams
Village Clerk
Introduced: March 2, 1999
Posted: March 3, 1999
Passed and Approved: March 16, 199
