ORDINANCE NO. MC-227-99
AN ORDINANCE AMENDING CHAPTER 1 OF THE WINNETKA VILLAGE CODE BY ADDING
PROVISIONS PERTAINING TO DELINQUENT ACCOUNTS
WHEREAS, the Finance Director has reported instances in which persons and
businesses with delinquent accounts have requested issuance, grant or renewal
of permits, licenses and other privileges, notwithstanding such delinquent
accounts; and
WHEREAS, the Finance Director has requested that the Council clarify its policy
regarding delinquent accounts and the effect of delinquent accounts on the
issuance, grant or renewal of permits, licenses and privileges to persons with
delinquent accounts; and
WHEREAS, the Council of the Village of Winnetka find that delinquent accounts
increase the Village’s administrative costs, often result in the loss of
revenues, and unfairly shift the burden of paying for the cost of providing
special services and privileges from the person or business that directly
benefits from the permit, license, privilege or service, to all other residents
and businesses in the Village.
NOW, THEREFORE, the Council of the Village of Winnetka do ordain as follows:
SECTION 1: That the foregoing recitals are hereby incorporated as the findings
of the Council of the Village of Winnetka, as if fully set forth herein.
SECTION 2: That Chapter 1 of the Winnetka Village Code, “General Provisions,”
is hereby amended by adding a new Section 1.16, which shall be entitled,
“Delinquent Accounts,” and shall provide as follows:
1.16   DELINQUENT ACCOUNTS.
   (a) Delinquent Account Defined. For purposes of this section, any account
that is not current and for which the person owing the account has not entered
into an enforceable payment plan pursuant to Section 1.16(c), below, shall be
considered to be a delinquent account. Such accounts shall include, but not be
limited to, accounts with unpaid water and electric fees, accounts with unpaid
fees for false alarms, accounts with unpaid parking tickets, accounts with
unpaid license or permit fees, and accounts with unpaid late fees or collection
charges.
   (b) Collection Charge. Unless otherwise specifically provided in this Code,
a collection charge shall be added to any delinquent account. The amount of the
collection charge shall be established by the village manager, upon the
recommendation of the director of finance, in an amount sufficient to recover
the Village’s costs of carrying and collecting the debt.
   (c) Payment Plan. The finance director is hereby authorized to enter into an
enforceable payment plan providing for the full payment of a delinquent
account, after consideration of the following factors based upon information
available from current Village records or provided by the customer or
applicant:
      1.   The size of the past due account; and
      2.   The ability of the customer or applicant to pay; and
      3.   The payment history of the customer or applicant; and
      4.   The reason for the outstanding indebtedness; and
      5.   Any other relevant factors relating to the circumstances of the
customer’s or applicant’s service.
   All payment plans shall be noted in the Village’s records of the customer’s
account. Any payment plan for a delinquent account of $1,000 or more shall be
in writing, with a copy provided to the applicant or customer. No payment plan
may be for a term of more than twelve months. All payment plans shall require
the timely payment of all future bills on the account and may require payment
of a deposit to secure such future payments.
   (d)    Effect of Delinquent Accounts. The Village may deny the issuance,
grant or renewal of any license, permit or privilege to any person who has a
delinquent account with the Village.
   (e)    Exceptions. Nothing in this section shall be construed as imposing
limitations or conditions on the provision of police and fire services within
the corporate limits of the Village.
SECTION 3: This Ordinance shall take effect immediately upon passage, approval
and posting.
   ADOPTED this 6th day of July 1999, pursuant to the following roll call vote:
AYES:      Trustees Aquilino, Derning, Hilton, Lien and Powell
NAYS:   None
