ORDINANCE NO. MC-1-2000
AN ORDINANCE ADOPTING THE COMPREHENSIVE RECODIFICATION OF THE WINNETKA VILLAGE
CODE
WHEREAS, the Book Publishing Company, Seattle, Washington, has compiled,
edited, indexed, and published a codification of the permanent and general
ordinances of the Village of Winnetka, Illinois; and
WHEREAS, there are now on file in the office of the Village Clerk, for public
inspection, three copies of a document entitled, “Winnetka Village Code of
1999, A Codification of the General Ordinances of the Village of Winnetka,
Illinois.”
THE COUNCIL OF THE VILLAGE OF WINNETKA do ordain:
SECTION 1: That the Winnetka Village Code, passed by the Village Council on
November 3, 1992, and approved by the Village President on the same date, as
amended, is hereby comprehensively amended to read as set forth in the
“Winnetka Village Code of 1999, A Codification of the General Ordinances of the
Village of Winnetka, Illinois,” as set forth in printed pamphlet form attached
hereto. Said “Winnetka Village Code of 1999, A Codification of the General
Ordinances of the Village of Winnetka, Illinois,” is hereby adopted as the
Winnetka Village Code and is hereby ordered to be published in such pamphlet
form and shall be received as evidence of the passage and legal publication of
such Code in all courts and places without further proof thereof.
SECTION 2: That Chapter 1.01 of the Winnetka Village Code of 1999, entitled
“Code Adoption,” is hereby amended by adding the following sections 1.01.010
through 1.01.060, which shall provide as follows:
1.01.010   Title; Citation; Reference.  
   This code of ordinances shall be known and cited as the “Winnetka Village
Code” and it shall be sufficient to refer to said code as the “Winnetka Village
Code” in any prosecution for the violation of any provision of this code or in
any proceeding at law or equity. It is sufficient to designate any ordinance
adding to, amending, correcting or repealing all or any part or portion of this
code as an addition to, amendment to, correction or repeal of the “Winnetka
Village Code.” References may be made to the titles, chapters, sections and
subsections of the “Winnetka Village Code” and such references shall apply to
those titles, chapters, sections or subsections as they appear in the code.
1.01.020   Amendments.
   All additions and amendments to this code are hereby incorporated in this
code so that a reference to this code as the “Winnetka Village Code” or to any
portion thereof, or to any ordinance of the Village of Winnetka codified
herein, the reference shall apply to all amendments, corrections and additions
heretofore, now or hereafter made.
1.01.030   Repealer; Title, chapter and section headings.  
Title, chapter and section headings contained in this code shall not be deemed
to govern, limit, modify or in any manner affect the scope, meaning or intent
of the provisions of any title, chapter or section in this code.
1.01.040   Reference to specific ordinances.  
The provisions of this code shall not in any manner affect matters of record
which refer to, or are otherwise connected with ordinances which are therein
specifically designated by number or otherwise and which are included within
the code, but such reference shall be construed to apply to the corresponding
provisions contained within this code.
1.01.050   Effect of code on past actions and obligations.  
The adoption of this code does not affect prosecutions for ordinance violations
committed prior to the effective date of this code, does not waive any fee or
penalty due and unpaid on the effective date of this code, and does not affect
the validity of any bond or cash deposit posted, filed or deposited pursuant to
the requirements of any ordinance.
1.01.060   References to prior code.  
References in Village forms, documents and regulations to the chapters and
sections of the former Village Code shall be construed to apply to the
corresponding provisions contained within this code.
SECTION 3: That this ordinance shall be in full force and effect from and after
its passage, approval and posting.
   Passed and approved this 18th day of January, 2000, by the Council of the
Village of Winnetka:
