ORDINANCE NO. MC-10-2000
AN ORDINANCE AMENDING CHAPTER 10.28 OF THE WINNETKA VILLAGE CODE TO REGULATE
TRUCK TRAFFIC
WHEREAS, Article III, Section 4, Paragraph Fifth of the Village Charter grants
the Village Council the power to enact ordinances “to declare what shall be a
nuisance and to prevent or remove the same, and punish the authors thereof;”
and
WHEREAS, Article III, Section 4, Paragraph Sixth of the Village Charter confers
on the Village Council the “exclusive power and control over streets within the
Village;” and
WHEREAS, Article III, Section 4, Paragraph Twenty-second of the Village Charter
grants power to the Village Council to “pass, publish, amend and repeal all
ordinances, rules and police regulations necessary and proper for the
government and good order of [the] Village and to enforce the observance of all
such ordinances;” and
WHEREAS, Section 15-316(c) of the Illinois Motor Vehicle Code, 625 ILCS 5/15-
316(c) authorizes municipalities to enact ordinances prohibiting the operation
of trucks or other commercial vehicles, or imposing limitations as to the
weight thereof, on designated highways under their jurisdiction; and
WHEREAS, the Village has received an increasing number of complaints of truck
traffic on residential streets during nighttime hours; and
WHEREAS, the Village Council have determined that the noises and fumes and
vibrations caused by heavy trucks at night time constitutes a nuisance,
disturbs the peace of the community and unreasonably interferes with the rights
of the Village’s residents to the quiet enjoyment of their property during the
night; and
WHEREAS, the Village Council have determined that it is necessary and proper to
protect the public health, safety and welfare by prohibiting trucks and
commercial vehicles from using streets under the jurisdiction of the Village
during certain nighttime hours.
NOW THEREFORE, the Council of the Village of Winnetka do ordain as follows:
SECTION 1:   The foregoing recitals are hereby incorporated as the findings of
the Council of the Village of Winnetka, as if fully set forth herein.
SECTION 2:   Chapter 10.28, “Miscellaneous Vehicle and Traffic Regulations,” of
Title 10 of the Winnetka Village Code, “Vehicles and Traffic,” is amended by
adding a new section 10.28.100, which shall provide as follows:
10.28.100   Truck Traffic
   A.    It is unlawful for any person to operate any truck or other commercial
vehicle having a gross weight in excess of two and one-half (2 ½) tons on any
street under the jurisdiction of the Village, between the hours of midnight and
5:00 a.m. However, any truck or other commercial vehicle having a gross weight
in excess of two and one-half (2 ½) tons carrying goods, merchandise or other
articles to or from any commercial premises within the Village may enter upon
such street, solely for the purpose of delivering or receiving goods,
merchandise or other articles at a commercial premises within the Village;
provided that, there is no other route available on which truck traffic is
permitted during those hours and that the truck travels on such street for the
shortest distance necessary to travel to or from the commercial premises in the
Village or to or from a route on which truck traffic is permitted. In doing so,
the driver of the vehicle shall proceed no further than is necessary for such
purpose upon any street upon which trucks are prohibited.
   B.    The provisions of this section do not apply to:
      1.   any fire or emergency apparatus owned or operated by the Village or
any other governmental body;
      2.   any vehicle owned or operated by or on behalf of the Village.
      3.   any vehicle operated under the terms of a special permit issued
under Section 15-301 et seq. of the Illinois Vehicle Code.
SECTION 3:   This Ordinance shall take effect immediately upon passage,
approval and posting and upon the posting of signs in the manner required by
the Illinois Motor Vehicle Code.
   ADOPTED this 2nd day of January, 2001, pursuant to the following roll call
vote:
AYES:      Trustees Aquilino, Brower, Lien, Powell, Presser and Woodbury
NAYS:   None
ABSENT:   None
Signed:
s/s Louise A. Holland
Village President
Countersigned:
s/s Douglas G. Williams
Village Clerk
