ORDINANCE NO. MC-8-2001
AN ORDINANCE AMENDING THE STORMWATER DETENTION REQUIREMENTS OF CHAPTER 15.32 OF
THE WINNETKA VILLAGE CODE BY RESTRICTING THE LOCATIONS OF RETAINING WALLS
WHEREAS, the Village of Winnetka participates in the National Flood Insurance
Program administered by the Federal Emergency Management Agency (“FEMA”), and
WHEREAS, on August 7, 2001, the Council of the Village of Winnetka enacted
Ordinance MC-5-2001, which amended the Flood Hazard Protection Regulations of
Chapter 15.68 of the Winnetka Village Code to establish criteria, consistent
with the regulations and technical bulletin published by FEMA for the
construction of basements in residential buildings on property currently
located in the flood fringe areas; and
WHEREAS, in the course of considering MC-5-2001, the Council of the Village of
Winnetka determined that using retaining walls to construct compensatory
storage areas for surface water drainage and stormwater run-off may, in some
instances, create an additional hazard for adjoining properties; and
WHEREAS, the Council of the Village of Winnetka have determined that it is in
the best interests of the public safety and welfare of the Village, its
residents and property owners to amend the standards for the issuance of
building permits to limit the location of retaining walls used as a means of
providing compensatory storage areas for surface water drainage and stormwater
run-off.
NOW, THEREFORE, the Council of the Village of Winnetka do ordain as follows:
SECTION 1: The foregoing recitals are hereby incorporated as the findings of
the Council of the Village of Winnetka, as if fully set forth herein.
SECTION 2: Subsection G of Section 15.32.080, “Criteria for permit approval,”
of Chapter 15.32 of the Winnetka Village Code, “Construction Permits,” is
amended to provide as follows:
   G.   Drainage of Surface Water. To diminish or remove any adverse impact of
surface water drainage and stormwater run-off on adjacent property, no new
building or other structure, or any addition thereto, shall be constructed in
such a manner as to cause the rate of surface water run-off, whether during or
following construction, to be greater than the rate of surface water run-off
immediately prior to such construction. No building permit shall be issued
unless and until the Director of Public works determines that the applicant has
provided for the proper control and drainage of surface water and stormwater
run-off, by connecting to available storm sewers or by using drainage swales,
detention areas or such other forms of water control mechanism as may be
approved by the Director of Public Works. When compensatory storage or
stormwater detention is required to be provided on site, the required storage
area or detention basin may be constructed with the use of retaining walls,
provided that retaining walls shall not be permitted along the sides of the
storage area or basin nearest to the property line.
SECTION 3: This Ordinance shall take effect immediately upon its passage,
approval and posting.
   ADOPTED this 21st day of August, 2001, pursuant to the following roll call
vote:
AYES:      Trustees Aquilino, Brower, Greenough, Powell, Presser and Woodbury
NAYS:   None
ABSENT:   None
Signed:
s/s Michael F. Duhl
Village President
Countersigned:
s/s Douglas G. Williams
Village Clerk
