ORDINANCE NO. MC-12-2001
AN ORDINANCE AMENDING THE RESIDENCY REQUIREMENTS FOR CHIEF OF POLICE
WHEREAS, Section 2.60.030(A) of the Winnetka Village Code requires the Chief of
Police to become a resident of the Village within 120 days after being
appointed; and
WHEREAS, the Council of the Village of Winnetka find that, due to rising
housing costs within the Village, the residency requirements may prevent
otherwise qualified candidates for Chief of Police from submitting their names
for consideration; and
WHEREAS, the Council of the Village of Winnetka find that, while desirable,
having the Chief of Police reside in the Village is not essential to the
performance of the duties of that position.
NOW, THEREFORE, the Council of the Village of Winnetka do ordain as follows:
SECTION 1: That the foregoing recitals are hereby incorporated as the findings
of the Council of the Village of Winnetka, as if fully set forth herein.
SECTION 2:  Subsection A of Section 2.60.030, “Chief of Police,” of Chapter
2.60, “Police Department,” of the Winnetka Village Code, is hereby amended to
provide as follows:
   A.   Creation; Appointment. There is created the office of Chief of Police,
an administrative office of the Village. The Chief of Police shall be appointed
by the Village Manager, and shall not be subject to the Board of Fire and
Police Commissioners created by this code. The Chief of Police need not be a
resident of the Village.
SECTION 3: This Ordinance shall take effect immediately upon passage, approval
and posting.
   ADOPTED this 20th day of November, 2001, pursuant to the following roll call
vote:
AYES:      Trustees Aquilino, Brower, Greenough, Powell, Presser and Woodbury
NAYS:   None
ABSENT:   None
