ORDINANCE NO. MC-1-2002
AN ORDINANCE AMENDING THE OFFICIAL ZONING MAP OF THE VILLAGE OF WINNETKA TO
REZONE THE PROPERTY AT 705 OAK STREET FROM B-1 MULTI-FAMILY RESIDENTIAL TO R-
5 SINGLE FAMILY RESIDENTIAL
WHEREAS, there has been presented to the Council of the Village of Winnetka,
Cook County, Illinois, the request of the owner of the following described real
estate (the “Subject Property”):
   PARCEL 1: THE EAST 25 FEET OF LOT 4, LOT 5 ( EXCEPT THE EAST 160 FEET AS
MEASURED ON THE NORTH AND SOUTH LINES THEREOF ) AND LOT 6 ( EXCEPT THE EAST 160
FEET AS MEASURED ON THE NORTH AND SOUTH LINES THEREOF ) IN PROUTY HOMESTEAD
SUBDIVISION OF ALL OF BLOCKS 24 AND 25, LYING NORTHEASTERLY OF THE RIGHT OF WAY
OF THE CHICAGO AND MILWAUKEE ELECTRIC RAILROAD ( EXCEPT THE NORTH 211 FEET OF
SAID BLOCK 24, ALSO THE WEST 3 FEET OF THE NORTH 211 FEET OF SAID BLOCK 24 ),
ALL IN WINNETKA, A SUBDIVISION BY CHARLES E. PECK OF THE NORTHEAST ¼ OF SECTION
20 AND THE FRACTIONAL NORTH ½ OF FRACTIONAL SECTION 21, ALL IN TOWNSHIP 42
NORTH, RANGE 13, EAST OF THE THIRD PRINCIPAL MERIDIAN, IN COOK COUNTY,
ILLINOIS.
commonly known as 705 Oak Street, Winnetka, Illinois, for an amendment to the
Official Village of Winnetka Zoning Map, to rezone the Subject Property from B-
1 Multi-Family Residential District to R-5 Single Family Residential District,
pursuant to Section 17.72.040 of the Winnetka Village Code; and
WHEREAS, on December 16, 2001, pursuant to the direction of the Village Council
and on due notice thereof, the Plan Commission conducted a public hearing on
the requested rezoning and by the unanimous vote of the 7 members then present,
has reported to the Council recommending that the requested rezoning from B-
1 Multi-Family Residential to R-5 Single Family Residential be granted; and
WHEREAS, the Subject Property is located on the north side of Oak Street
between Lincoln Avenue and Maple Street; and
WHEREAS, the two parcels of property that adjoin the east lot line of the
Subject Property are zoned R-4 Single Family Residential and are improved with
single family residences; and
WHEREAS, the property that adjoins the Subject Property to the west is zoned B-
2 Multi-Family Residential and is improved with a multi-family residential
building; and
WHEREAS, the property adjoining the north lot line of the Subject Property is
zoned R-4 Single Family Residential and is the site of the Hadley School for
the Blind; and
WHEREAS, the properties on the block face opposite the Subject Property consist
of: (a) a townhouse development in a B-1 Multi-Family Residential Zoning
District; (b) a small commercial building located on a parcel zoned C-2 General
Retail; and (c) a large parcel that is the site of the Christ Church chapel and
other church buildings, with the western portion of the parcel being zoned B-
1 Multi-Family Residential and the east portion, at the southwest corner of Oak
and Maple Streets, being zoned R-4 Single Family Residential; and
WHEREAS, the Subject Property is improved with a single family residence that
serves as the residence for the President of the Hadley School; and
WHEREAS, the use of the Subject Property for the existing single family
residence is a legal, nonconforming use that is well established in the
neighborhood; and
WHEREAS, the Hadley School proposes to replace the existing single family
residence on the Subject Property with a new single family residence, which
will continue to be used as the residence of the President of the Hadley
School; and
WHEREAS, although the established use of the Subject Property is for a single
family residence, single family residences are not permitted uses within the B-
1 Zoning District and the proposed replacement of the single family structure
cannot be accomplished without rezoning the Subject Property; and
WHEREAS, the proposed rezoning will maintain the existing land use pattern on
the block face, including the decreasing intensity of use of land from B-
2 Multi-Family at the west end of the block face to R-4 Single Family
residences at the east end of the block face; and
WHEREAS, the Subject Property has a lot area of 11,484 square feet and meets
the zoning requirements for the R-5 Zoning District; and
WHEREAS, the proposed development plan submitted by the Hadley School is a
reasonable use of the Subject Property and is reasonably necessary to the
promotion of the public health, safety and general welfare of the Village, in
that it maintains the existing land use patterns in the immediate vicinity and
provides a use of the Subject Property that is consistent with Winnetka 2020,
the Winnetka Comprehensive Plan; and
WHEREAS, the Subject Property is not a desirable location for multiple family
development, which would result in increasing the intensity of use adjacent to
the single family residences immediately to the east of the Subject Property;
and
WHEREAS, on November 15, 2001, pursuant to procedures prescribed by the
Winnetka Zoning Ordinance, the Design Review Board reviewed and provided
favorable comment on the plans for the proposed new residence.
NOW, THEREFORE, the Council of the Village of Winnetka do ordain as follows:
SECTION 1 : The foregoing recitals are hereby incorporated as the findings of
the Council of the Village of Winnetka, as if fully set forth herein.
SECTION 2:  The Official Village of Winnetka Zoning Map provided for in Section
17.08.010(B) of the Winnetka Zoning Ordinance is hereby amended by rezoning the
Subject Property, commonly known as 705 Oak Street in the Village of Winnetka,
from B-1 Multi-Family Residential District to R-5 Single Family Residential
District.
SECTION 3: This Ordinance shall take effect immediately upon passage, approval
and posting.
