ORDINANCE NO. MC-2-2002 (not adopted)
ORDINANCE NO. MC-3-2002
AN ORDINANCE AMENDING CHAPTER 10.12 OF THE WINNETKA VILLAGE CODE AS IT PERTAINS
TO MOTOR VEHICLE CLASSIFICATIONS AND LICENSE FEES
WHEREAS, Section 10.12.010 of the Winnetka Village Code requires all persons
residing or having a principal place of business in the Village of Winnetka to
obtain a motor vehicle license from the Village for any vehicle that is used on
any street, avenue or alley in the Village; and
WHEREAS, under Section 10.12.030 of the Winnetka Village Code, local
governmental vehicles are considered to be Class H vehicles; and
WHEREAS, the Council of the Village of Winnetka find that applying the local
licensing requirement to vehicles owned by the Village of Winnetka is not
warranted, because of the amount of time it takes to update each vehicle’s
license each year, the vehicle information that is recorded as part of the
local licensing process duplicates vehicle records already maintained by the
Village in the ordinary course of business, and the license fee merely
reallocates Village funds rather than generating any revenue to cover the
Village’s administrative costs.
NOW, THEREFORE, the Council of the Village of Winnetka do ordain as follows:
SECTION 1: That the foregoing recitals are hereby incorporated as the findings
of the Council of the Village of Winnetka, as if fully set forth herein.
SECTION 2: That Section 10.12.010, “License required,” of Chapter 10.12 of the
Winnetka Village Code, “Vehicle Licenses,” is hereby amended to provide as
follows:
Section 10.12.010   License required.
   It is unlawful for any person residing or having his or her principal place
of business within the Village to use or cause or permit any of his or her
agents or employees to use any motor vehicle upon the streets, avenues or
alleys of the Village, unless such motor vehicle is licensed as provided in
this chapter. The licensing requirements of this chapter shall not apply to any
motor vehicles owned and operated by the Village of Winnetka or any of its
departments. (Prior code §42.01)
SECTION 3: That Section 10.12.030, “Classification--Fees,” of Chapter 10.12 of
the Winnetka Village Code, “Vehicle Licenses,” is hereby amended to provide as
follows:
Section 10.12.030   Classification--Fees.
   Classification of vehicles for licenses required by this chapter shall be as
follows:
 
Class A: motor vehicles of thirty-five (35) horsepower or less for
         noncommercial purposes
Class B: motor vehicles of more than thirty-five (35) horsepower for
         noncommercial purposes
Class C: commercial vehicles for conveying loads of one ton or less and
         automobiles used for commercial purposes
Class D: taxicabs
Class E: commercial vehicles for carrying loads of over one ton
Class F: motorcycles
Class H: local governmental (does not include placePlaceTypeVillage of
         PlaceNameWinnetka vehicles)
 
   The horsepower rating of motor vehicles shall be determined in accordance
with the standard rating prescribed by the Secretary of State of Illinois for
the state registration of motor vehicles under the Illinois Vehicle Code.
   License fees for each class of license shall be as set from time to time by
resolution of the Village Council. (Prior code §42.03)
SECTION 4:   This Ordinance shall take effect immediately upon passage,
approval and posting.
   ADOPTED this 19th day of March, 2001, pursuant to the following roll call
vote:
AYES:      Trustees Aquilino, Brower, Greenough, Powell, Presser and Woodbury
NAYS:   None
ABSENT:   None
Signed:
s/s Michael F. Duhl
Village President
Countersigned:
s/s Douglas G. Williams
Village Clerk
